{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SVfSHcwjP6EK5zK47kaP2j","type":"tool_result","content":"/*!\nmy-3D2dge module STORY v0.85.1: dialogue as data, flags and values, a quest log and emote balloons\nhttps://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge (MIT License)\nLoads after: the full engine or the agent edition. Needs: no other module.\n\nA JRPG's or an adventure's talk (Dragon Quest, Chrono Trigger, Zelda): conversations written as data and run through an\nE.Dialog (its markup and portraits), remembering what was said and done.\n- const story = new E.Story(game, { people: { elder: { name: 'ELDER', portrait: rig, at: npc } }, nodes, vars, on:\n  { gift(story, step) {...} }, dialog }). people: who speaks (portrait, full engine: a Humanoid or a function (g, x, y, size); at:\n  anything with x, y, z, and h its height, a balloon floats over); dialog: the E.Dialog it talks through (else its own:\n  story.talk); on: the game's handlers for events.\n- nodes: { id: [step, ...] }: the steps run in order, and a step with if runs only when its condition holds.\n  - { who, say: 'text' | [pages], choices: [{ text, if, goto, ...actions }] }: a line in the box (markup, {$name}\n    from vars); a choice's actions run when it is picked, then its goto, else the next step.\n  - { goto: 'id' } jumps; { end: true } stops; { wait: seconds } pauses.\n  - actions, on any step or choice: set: 'flag' | { key: value }; add: { gold: -50 }; quest: [id, title, text]; done:\n    id; emote: '!' | '?' | 'heart' | 'dots' | 'note' (over who's at); event: 'name' (calls on[name](story, step), after\n    the line on a step that speaks; with wait: true the story holds until story.resume(): the game's scene, a shop).\n  - conditions: 'flag' (set and truthy), '!flag', 'gold >= 50' (== != < <= > >=, a number or a word), 'quest:id'\n    (taken), 'done:id' (finished), an array (all of them), or a function (story) => true or false.\n- story.run(id, { onDone }) starts a node (stopping any other). In update: if (story.update(dt)) return; (true while it\n  runs: play waits); in draw: story.draw(r) (the box and the balloons). story.running; story.node: the node's id.\n- story.vars: every flag and value ({$name} in a line reads them); story.set(key, value = true), get(key) (a dotted\n  path), test(condition).\n- Quests: story.quest(id, title, text), story.done(id); story.quests: [{ id, title, text, done }] in the order taken.\n- story.emote(target, kind, seconds = 1.5): a balloon over anything with x, y, z (h: its height).\n- A visual novel: story.log (what was said and chosen: { who, name, text }, for a backlog), story.auto (seconds a page\n  stays before it turns), story.skip (pages type and turn at once; choices wait).\n- story.state() and story.restore(state): its vars and quests as JSON, for a save (game.saves' data, full engine).\n\n```js story\nconst E = My3D2dge, game = new E.Game({ headless: true });\nconst story = new E.Story(game, { vars: { gold: 30, hero: 'ROWAN' }, nodes: {\n  elder: [{ if: 'helping', goto: 'thanks' }, { who: 'elder', say: 'Will you help us, {$hero}?', choices: [\n    { text: 'Yes', set: 'helping', quest: ['cave', 'The cave', 'Clear the cave north of town'] }, { text: 'No', goto: 'bye' }] },\n    { add: { gold: 20 } }],\n  thanks: [{ say: 'Thank you!' }, { if: 'gold >= 50', done: 'cave' }],\n  bye: [{ say: 'Farewell.' }] } });\ngame.start({ update(dt) { story.update(dt); }, draw(r) { story.draw(r); } });\nconst press = n => { for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) { game.input.tap('confirm'); game.advance(.5); } };\nstory.run('elder'); press(2);   // the line types out, then the first choice: Yes\nif (!story.get('helping') || story.get('gold') !== 50 || story.quests[0].id !== 'cave' || story.running) throw new Error('the quest taken');\nstory.run('elder'); press(2);\nif (!story.quests[0].done || !story.test('done:cave')) throw new Error('the quest done');\n```\nRules: keep the nodes as data (a game's script is an event); put story.state() in the game's save and restore it on a\nload; one story per game, its talk the only box on screen.\n*/\n(function (E) {\n'use strict';\nif (!E) throw new Error('my-3D2dge module STORY: load engine/my-3d2dge.js (or the agent edition) first');\n\n/* =============================================================================\n * STORY  conversations as data run through a Dialog, flags and values, quests, emote balloons\n * ========================================================================== */\nconst { px } = E;\nconst HEART = E.sprite(['.R.R.', 'RRRRR', 'RRRRR', '.RRR.', '..R..'], { R: '#e8384a' });\nclass Story {\n  /** new E.Story(game, { people, nodes, vars, on, dialog }): the talk of a game (the manual above) */\n  constructor(game, o = {}) {\n    /** game: its game; people: who speaks, by id ({ name, portrait, at }); nodes: the conversations by id (lists of\n     *  steps); on: the game's event handlers by name */\n    this.game = game; this.people = o.people || {}; this.nodes = o.nodes || {}; this.on = Object.assign({}, o.on);\n    /** vars: every flag and value (a line's {$name} reads them) */\n    this.vars = Object.assign({}, o.vars);\n    /** talk: the E.Dialog it speaks through */\n    this.talk = o.dialog || new E.Dialog(game); this.talk.vars = this.vars;\n    /** quests: the quest log, in the order taken ({ id, title, text, done }) */\n    this.quests = [];\n    /** log: what was said and chosen, oldest first ({ who, name, text }, the last 200: a visual novel's backlog) */\n    this.log = [];\n    /** auto: seconds a page shows before it turns by itself (0: it waits for the player); skip: pages type at once and\n     *  turn at once (choices still wait) */\n    this.auto = 0; this.skip = false;\n    /** running: a node runs; node: its id */\n    this.running = false; this.node = null;\n    this._steps = null; this._i = 0; this._wait = 0; this._held = false; this._then = null; this._pick = null; this._done = null; this._balloons = [];\n  }\n  /** start node id (stopping any other); o.onDone(story) when it ends */\n  run(id, o = {}) {\n    if (!this.nodes[id]) { E.warn('story:' + id, 'E.Story: no node \"' + id + '\"'); return this; }\n    if (this.talk.open) this.talk.close();\n    this.running = true; this.node = id; this._steps = this.nodes[id]; this._i = 0; this._wait = 0; this._held = false; this._then = null; this._pick = null; this._done = o.onDone || null;\n    this._next(); return this;\n  }\n  /** stop the node running (its box closes; onDone isn't called) */\n  stop() { this.running = false; this.node = null; this._done = null; if (this.talk.open) this.talk.close(); }\n  /** after an event with wait: true, go on (to the choice's goto, or the next step) */\n  resume() { if (!this._held) return; this._held = false; const g = this._then; this._then = null; if (g && !this._jump(g)) return; this._next(); }\n  // the steps until one waits (a line, a pause, a held event) or the node ends\n  _next() {\n    while (this.running) {\n      const s = this._steps[this._i++];\n      if (!s) return this._end();\n      if (s.if !== undefined && !this.test(s.if)) continue;\n      if (s.say !== undefined) return this._say(s);   // (its event, goto and a choice's run when the box closes)\n      this._act(s); if (!this.running) return;\n      if (this._fire(s, s.goto)) return;\n      if (s.goto && !this._jump(s.goto)) return;\n      if (!s.event && s.wait > 0) { this._wait = s.wait; return; }\n    }\n  }\n  _say(s) {\n    const p = this.people[s.who] || {}, ch = s.choices && s.choices.filter(c => c.if === undefined || this.test(c.if));\n    this._act(s); if (!this.running) return;\n    const name = s.name || p.name || '', note = e => { this.log.push(e); if (this.log.length > 200) this.log.shift(); };\n    for (const t of [].concat(s.say)) note({ who: s.who || null, name, text: t });\n    if (this._speed === undefined) this._speed = this.talk.speed;\n    this.talk.speed = this.skip ? 1e6 : this._speed;\n    this.talk.say(s.say, { name, portrait: p.portrait, auto: this.skip ? .08 : this.auto || undefined, choices: ch && ch.length ? ch.map(c => c.text) : null, onChoice: i => { this._pick = ch[i]; note({ who: 'choice', name: '', text: ch[i].text }); }, onDone: () => this._after(s) });\n  }\n  _after(s) {\n    const c = this._pick; this._pick = null;\n    if (c) { this._act(c); if (!this.running || this._fire(c, c.goto)) return; if (c.goto) { if (this._jump(c.goto)) this._next(); return; } }\n    if (this._fire(s, s.goto)) return;\n    if (s.goto && !this._jump(s.goto)) return;\n    this._next();\n  }\n  // a step's or a choice's event: true when the story stops here (it ended, or holds till resume(), then goes to then)\n  _fire(s, then) {\n    if (!s.event) return false;\n    const f = this.on[s.event];\n    if (f) try { f(this, s); } catch (e) { this.game.fail('story event \"' + s.event + '\"', e); }\n    else E.warn('story:on:' + s.event, 'E.Story: no handler for event \"' + s.event + '\" (on: { ' + s.event + '(story, step) {...} })');\n    if (!this.running) return true;\n    if (s.wait) { this._held = true; this._then = then || null; return true; }\n    return false;\n  }\n  _jump(id) {\n    if (!this.nodes[id]) { E.warn('story:' + id, 'E.Story: no","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e2aa65a8-ee1a-45c4-b8e6-f96cf188e23d","uuid":"cdbd28cf-5869-4bcc-b36b-47e8f9589cf7","timestamp":"2026-11-03T18:03:53.972Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"/*!\nmy-3D2dge module STORY v0.85.1: dialogue as data, flags and values, a quest log and emote balloons\nhttps://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge (MIT License)\nLoads after: the full engine or the agent edition. Needs: no other module.\n\nA JRPG's or an adventure's talk (Dragon Quest, Chrono Trigger, Zelda): conversations written as data and run through an\nE.Dialog (its markup and portraits), remembering what was said and done.\n- const story = new E.Story(game, { people: { elder: { name: 'ELDER', portrait: rig, at: npc } }, nodes, vars, on:\n  { gift(story, step) {...} }, dialog }). people: who speaks (portrait, full engine: a Humanoid or a function (g, x, y, size); at:\n  anything with x, y, z, and h its height, a balloon floats over); dialog: the E.Dialog it talks through (else its own:\n  story.talk); on: the game's handlers for events.\n- nodes: { id: [step, ...] }: the steps run in order, and a step with if runs only when its condition holds.\n  - { who, say: 'text' | [pages], choices: [{ text, if, goto, ...actions }] }: a line in the box (markup, {$name}\n    from vars); a choice's actions run when it is picked, then its goto, else the next step.\n  - { goto: 'id' } jumps; { end: true } stops; { wait: seconds } pauses.\n  - actions, on any step or choice: set: 'flag' | { key: value }; add: { gold: -50 }; quest: [id, title, text]; done:\n    id; emote: '!' | '?' | 'heart' | 'dots' | 'note' (over who's at); event: 'name' (calls on[name](story, step), after\n    the line on a step that speaks; with wait: true the story holds until story.resume(): the game's scene, a shop).\n  - conditions: 'flag' (set and truthy), '!flag', 'gold >= 50' (== != < <= > >=, a number or a word), 'quest:id'\n    (taken), 'done:id' (finished), an array (all of them), or a function (story) => true or false.\n- story.run(id, { onDone }) starts a node (stopping any other). In update: if (story.update(dt)) return; (true while it\n  runs: play waits); in draw: story.draw(r) (the box and the balloons). story.running; story.node: the node's id.\n- story.vars: every flag and value ({$name} in a line reads them); story.set(key, value = true), get(key) (a dotted\n  path), test(condition).\n- Quests: story.quest(id, title, text), story.done(id); story.quests: [{ id, title, text, done }] in the order taken.\n- story.emote(target, kind, seconds = 1.5): a balloon over anything with x, y, z (h: its height).\n- A visual novel: story.log (what was said and chosen: { who, name, text }, for a backlog), story.auto (seconds a page\n  stays before it turns), story.skip (pages type and turn at once; choices wait).\n- story.state() and story.restore(state): its vars and quests as JSON, for a save (game.saves' data, full engine).\n\n```js story\nconst E = My3D2dge, game = new E.Game({ headless: true });\nconst story = new E.Story(game, { vars: { gold: 30, hero: 'ROWAN' }, nodes: {\n  elder: [{ if: 'helping', goto: 'thanks' }, { who: 'elder', say: 'Will you help us, {$hero}?', choices: [\n    { text: 'Yes', set: 'helping', quest: ['cave', 'The cave', 'Clear the cave north of town'] }, { text: 'No', goto: 'bye' }] },\n    { add: { gold: 20 } }],\n  thanks: [{ say: 'Thank you!' }, { if: 'gold >= 50', done: 'cave' }],\n  bye: [{ say: 'Farewell.' }] } });\ngame.start({ update(dt) { story.update(dt); }, draw(r) { story.draw(r); } });\nconst press = n => { for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) { game.input.tap('confirm'); game.advance(.5); } };\nstory.run('elder'); press(2);   // the line types out, then the first choice: Yes\nif (!story.get('helping') || story.get('gold') !== 50 || story.quests[0].id !== 'cave' || story.running) throw new Error('the quest taken');\nstory.run('elder'); press(2);\nif (!story.quests[0].done || !story.test('done:cave')) throw new Error('the quest done');\n```\nRules: keep the nodes as data (a game's script is an event); put story.state() in the game's save and restore it on a\nload; one story per game, its talk the only box on screen.\n*/\n(function (E) {\n'use strict';\nif (!E) throw new Error('my-3D2dge module STORY: load engine/my-3d2dge.js (or the agent edition) first');\n\n/* =============================================================================\n * STORY  conversations as data run through a Dialog, flags and values, quests, emote balloons\n * ========================================================================== */\nconst { px } = E;\nconst HEART = E.sprite(['.R.R.', 'RRRRR', 'RRRRR', '.RRR.', '..R..'], { R: '#e8384a' });\nclass Story {\n  /** new E.Story(game, { people, nodes, vars, on, dialog }): the talk of a game (the manual above) */\n  constructor(game, o = {}) {\n    /** game: its game; people: who speaks, by id ({ name, portrait, at }); nodes: the conversations by id (lists of\n     *  steps); on: the game's event handlers by name */\n    this.game = game; this.people = o.people || {}; this.nodes = o.nodes || {}; this.on = Object.assign({}, o.on);\n    /** vars: every flag and value (a line's {$name} reads them) */\n    this.vars = Object.assign({}, o.vars);\n    /** talk: the E.Dialog it speaks through */\n    this.talk = o.dialog || new E.Dialog(game); this.talk.vars = this.vars;\n    /** quests: the quest log, in the order taken ({ id, title, text, done }) */\n    this.quests = [];\n    /** log: what was said and chosen, oldest first ({ who, name, text }, the last 200: a visual novel's backlog) */\n    this.log = [];\n    /** auto: seconds a page shows before it turns by itself (0: it waits for the player); skip: pages type at once and\n     *  turn at once (choices still wait) */\n    this.auto = 0; this.skip = false;\n    /** running: a node runs; node: its id */\n    this.running = false; this.node = null;\n    this._steps = null; this._i = 0; this._wait = 0; this._held = false; this._then = null; this._pick = null; this._done = null; this._balloons = [];\n  }\n  /** start node id (stopping any other); o.onDone(story) when it ends */\n  run(id, o = {}) {\n    if (!this.nodes[id]) { E.warn('story:' + id, 'E.Story: no node \"' + id + '\"'); return this; }\n    if (this.talk.open) this.talk.close();\n    this.running = true; this.node = id; this._steps = this.nodes[id]; this._i = 0; this._wait = 0; this._held = false; this._then = null; this._pick = null; this._done = o.onDone || null;\n    this._next(); return this;\n  }\n  /** stop the node running (its box closes; onDone isn't called) */\n  stop() { this.running = false; this.node = null; this._done = null; if (this.talk.open) this.talk.close(); }\n  /** after an event with wait: true, go on (to the choice's goto, or the next step) */\n  resume() { if (!this._held) return; this._held = false; const g = this._then; this._then = null; if (g && !this._jump(g)) return; this._next(); }\n  // the steps until one waits (a line, a pause, a held event) or the node ends\n  _next() {\n    while (this.running) {\n      const s = this._steps[this._i++];\n      if (!s) return this._end();\n      if (s.if !== undefined && !this.test(s.if)) continue;\n      if (s.say !== undefined) return this._say(s);   // (its event, goto and a choice's run when the box closes)\n      this._act(s); if (!this.running) return;\n      if (this._fire(s, s.goto)) return;\n      if (s.goto && !this._jump(s.goto)) return;\n      if (!s.event && s.wait > 0) { this._wait = s.wait; return; }\n    }\n  }\n  _say(s) {\n    const p = this.people[s.who] || {}, ch = s.choices && s.choices.filter(c => c.if === undefined || this.test(c.if));\n    this._act(s); if (!this.running) return;\n    const name = s.name || p.name || '', note = e => { this.log.push(e); if (this.log.length > 200) this.log.shift(); };\n    for (const t of [].concat(s.say)) note({ who: s.who || null, name, text: t });\n    if (this._speed === undefined) this._speed = this.talk.speed;\n    this.talk.speed = this.skip ? 1e6 : this._speed;\n    this.talk.say(s.say, { name, portrait: p.portrait, auto: this.skip ? .08 : this.auto || undefined, choices: ch && ch.length ? ch.map(c => c.text) : null, onChoice: i => { this._pick = ch[i]; note({ who: 'choice', name: '', text: ch[i].text }); }, onDone: () => this._after(s) });\n  }\n  _after(s) {\n    const c = this._pick; this._pick = null;\n    if (c) { this._act(c); if (!this.running || this._fire(c, c.goto)) return; if (c.goto) { if (this._jump(c.goto)) this._next(); return; } }\n    if (this._fire(s, s.goto)) return;\n    if (s.goto && !this._jump(s.goto)) return;\n    this._next();\n  }\n  // a step's or a choice's event: true when the story stops here (it ended, or holds till resume(), then goes to then)\n  _fire(s, then) {\n    if (!s.event) return false;\n    const f = this.on[s.event];\n    if (f) try { f(this, s); } catch (e) { this.game.fail('story event \"' + s.event + '\"', e); }\n    else E.warn('story:on:' + s.event, 'E.Story: no handler for event \"' + s.event + '\" (on: { ' + s.event + '(story, step) {...} })');\n    if (!this.running) return true;\n    if (s.wait) { this._held = true; this._then = then || null; return true; }\n    return false;\n  }\n  _jump(id) {\n    if (!this.nodes[id]) { E.warn('story:' + id, 'E.Story: no","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01SVfSHcwjP6EK5zK47kaP2j","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CggSDjqwRtABbChFDTn8X","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014dQeGvPgX57ksvMohAWKKE","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"D=/tmp/wireplan-research-516709/engine/dist/handoff; grep -n \"game.saves\\|saves\\.\\|E.Clock\\|clock\\.\\|E.Suspicion\\|mind\\.\\|r.sightCone\\|splitScreen\\|viewports\\|E.Shell\\|ui\\.\\(show\\|hud\\|toast\\|tutorial\\|back\\|hide\\)\" $D/API-INDEX.md | cut -c1-260 | head -60","description":"Search engine index for saves, clock, suspicion, split screen, shell"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1112,"cache_read_input_tokens":213553,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1112,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e2aa65a8-ee1a-45c4-b8e6-f96cf188e23d","uuid":"c6815702-32ca-4277-9d02-6569e6385ff4","timestamp":"2026-11-03T18:03:55.480Z","request_id":"req_011CggSDiybzcqxznhPTQYLc","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_014dQeGvPgX57ksvMohAWKKE":{"command":"D=/tmp/wireplan-research-516709/engine/dist/handoff; grep -n \"game.saves\\|saves\\.\\|E.Clock\\|clock\\.\\|E.Suspicion\\|mind\\.\\|r.sightCone\\|splitScreen\\|viewports\\|E.Shell\\|ui\\.\\(show\\|hud\\|toast\\|tutorial\\|back\\|hide\\)\" $D/API-INDEX.md | cut -c1-260 | head -60","description":"Search engine index for saves, clock, suspicion, split screen, shell"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014dQeGvPgX57ksvMohAWKKE","type":"tool_result","content":"80:- 1000 17d. Perception; E.Suspicion: suspicion\n88:- 1161 21d. Shell; E.Shell: shell\n105:- 1675 Module strategy: real-time strategy and simulation: selection, orders, armies, production, resources, placement, fog, AI; a day clock, needs, overlays (engine/modules/strategy.js); E.Clock: clock, E.Strategy: strategy\n332:- `input.names = null` †: the actions' names on the Controls screen ({ attack: 'Sword' }; false hides one from rebinding: the game's menu.controls); onBindings(b): called with the player's new bindings (the game saves and applies them)\n431:- `r.sightCone(obs, o = {})` †: an observer's view on the ground: a dithered fan fov wide (radians) about its facing, out to range, cut short where the map hides a body's chest (map.ray, the height rules), draped over the ground below. o: { range: 120, fov\n495:- `game.saves()` †: game.saves: the save slots (section 10k), made when first read\n501:- `game.splitScreen(n, o = {})` †: split the screen into n viewports (2 to 4; 0 or 1: one screen again), o: { layout: 'auto' (side by side on a wide screen, stacked on a tall one; a grid for 3 or 4) | 'columns' | 'rows' | 'grid', follow: [targets], z: 16, \n510:- `game.viewports` †: a split screen's viewports ({ i, x, y, w, h, cam, focus(x, y, z), follow(target, { z }): game.splitScreen), or [] on one screen\n545:- `game.shell = null` †: the E.Shell over this game (an HTML interface: screens and HUD), or null\n617:- `new E.Saves(game, o) → saves` †: game.saves (made when first read): o is menu.saves ({ slots, version, migrate, write, read })\n618:- `saves.any` †: is there any save to load (a title's Continue)?\n619:- `saves.autosave(o)` †: save to the autosave (what write() gives)\n620:- `saves.copy(from, to)` †: copy a slot's save onto another (over what is there); false when the first is empty\n621:- `saves.erase(slot)` †: erase a slot\n622:- `saves.get(slot)` †: a slot's save as it is stored, checked: null when empty; { slot, damaged: true } when it can't be read; { newer: true } from a newer version of the game; else { slot, data, place, level, time, at (the date saved), version }\n623:- `saves.latest()` †: the most recent save that loads, or null (a title's Continue loads it)\n624:- `saves.list()` †: every slot, the autosave first: [{ slot, empty, place, level, time, at, damaged, newer }] (a menu's rows)\n625:- `saves.load(slot)` †: load a slot: its data brought up to this version (migrate), played set from it, read(save) called. Returns the save ({ data, place, level, time, slot }), or null when the slot is empty, damaged or from a newer version\n626:- `saves.save(slot, o)` †: save to a slot (0.., or 'auto'): o ({ data, place, level }) or what write() gives. Returns true when it is kept (in storage, or for the visit when storage is blocked: blocked tells), false when there was nothing to save\n627:- `saves.show(mode = 'load', done)` †: open the standard save screen over the game (E.Shell's): 'save' (to a slot) or 'load'; done(save) after a load or a save. False without a menu (a headless game, menu: false)\n628:- `saves.blocked = false` †: storage refused a save (they last for the visit)\n629:- `saves.canSave = true` †: the pause menu offers Save (a JRPG turns it off away from save points)\n630:- `saves.game` †: its game\n631:- `saves.migrate` †: an older version's data brought up to this one (or null: kept as it is)\n632:- `saves.played = 0` †: seconds played in the game's scenes (paused time and titles left out), saved with each save and set by a load\n633:- `saves.read` †: what a load does with { data, place, level, time, slot }\n634:- `saves.slots` †: how many slots besides the autosave (3)\n635:- `saves.version` †: the game's version of its data (1), saved with each save\n636:- `saves.write` †: what a save holds ({ data, place, level })\n1002:- `new E.Suspicion(o = {}) → suspicion`: new E.Suspicion({ rise, decay, notice, search, alert, forget }): a guard's mind (its fields, below, are its options). Its level rises while it sees the target (faster the more exposed and nearer), decays while it d\n1057:- `game.audio.music(song, o = {})`: Loop a song (or play once with { loop: false }). song = { bpm: 120, steps: 4, tracks: [ { wave: 'square', vol: .2, notes: 'C5 - E5 - G5 - . . | ...' }, one token per step { wave: 'triangle', notes: 'C3 . C3 . G2 . G2 .'\n1163:- `new E.Shell(game, o = {}) → shell`: new E.Shell(game, { theme, screens: { name: spec }, settings: { items, onChange(settings, key) }, store: 'shell-settings', meters: .125, standard: true }): an HTML interface over the game (see the section's header)\n1164:- `new E.Shell({ theme })`: CSS variables (ink, paper, accent, muted, danger, line, font, titleFont)\n1165:- `new E.Shell({ screens })`: specs ui.show(name) starts from (the pause screen follows game.paused; screens: { pause: false } leaves it out)\n1166:- `new E.Shell({ settings })`: settings.items: the game's own settings, { key, label, type: 'toggle' | 'slider' | 'select', min, max, step, options, value } (kept in game.settings, beside the standard ones)\n1167:- `new E.Shell({ store, meters })`: store: where an older version saved them; meters: meters per world unit for distances\n1168:- `new E.Shell({ standard })`: false leaves out the standard menu (the pause screen's Settings, Controls, Full screen and Quit, and the settings' groups)\n1605:- `world.shellMap()`: the explored map for E.Shell's minimap: game.shell.hud({ minimap: world.shellMap() }) (a cell a square, the save and boss rooms marked, the hero's cell)\n1677:- `new E.Clock(o = {}) → clock` †: new E.Clock({ day: 240 (real seconds of game time a day), hour: 8 (to start at) })\n1678:- `clock.hour` †: the hour (0..23)\n1679:- `clock.label()` †: 'DAY 2 14:30'\n1680:- `clock.light()` †: the light by the hour: { ambient (.12 at night .. 1 at noon), color (the sky's tint: blue night, warm dawn and dusk) }\n1681:- `clock.minute` †: the minute (0..59)\n1682:- `clock.night` †: true from 20:00 to 6:00\n1683:- `clock.update(dt)` †: run it by dt seconds of game time\n1684:- `clock.day = 1` †: the day (1, 2, ...)\n1685:- `clock.length` †: seconds a day\n1686:- `clock.t` †: hours since the first midnight\n1695:- `strategy.minimap(colors = {})` †: E.Shell's minimap spec: the map, the fog, the camera's view, the units seen as dots by side, a click moving the camera","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e2aa65a8-ee1a-45c4-b8e6-f96cf188e23d","uuid":"85051609-211a-41d9-ab45-465c64ac43d1","timestamp":"2026-11-03T18:03:55.544Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"80:- 1000 17d. Perception; E.Suspicion: suspicion\n88:- 1161 21d. Shell; E.Shell: shell\n105:- 1675 Module strategy: real-time strategy and simulation: selection, orders, armies, production, resources, placement, fog, AI; a day clock, needs, overlays (engine/modules/strategy.js); E.Clock: clock, E.Strategy: strategy\n332:- `input.names = null` †: the actions' names on the Controls screen ({ attack: 'Sword' }; false hides one from rebinding: the game's menu.controls); onBindings(b): called with the player's new bindings (the game saves and applies them)\n431:- `r.sightCone(obs, o = {})` †: an observer's view on the ground: a dithered fan fov wide (radians) about its facing, out to range, cut short where the map hides a body's chest (map.ray, the height rules), draped over the ground below. o: { range: 120, fov\n495:- `game.saves()` †: game.saves: the save slots (section 10k), made when first read\n501:- `game.splitScreen(n, o = {})` †: split the screen into n viewports (2 to 4; 0 or 1: one screen again), o: { layout: 'auto' (side by side on a wide screen, stacked on a tall one; a grid for 3 or 4) | 'columns' | 'rows' | 'grid', follow: [targets], z: 16, \n510:- `game.viewports` †: a split screen's viewports ({ i, x, y, w, h, cam, focus(x, y, z), follow(target, { z }): game.splitScreen), or [] on one screen\n545:- `game.shell = null` †: the E.Shell over this game (an HTML interface: screens and HUD), or null\n617:- `new E.Saves(game, o) → saves` †: game.saves (made when first read): o is menu.saves ({ slots, version, migrate, write, read })\n618:- `saves.any` †: is there any save to load (a title's Continue)?\n619:- `saves.autosave(o)` †: save to the autosave (what write() gives)\n620:- `saves.copy(from, to)` †: copy a slot's save onto another (over what is there); false when the first is empty\n621:- `saves.erase(slot)` †: erase a slot\n622:- `saves.get(slot)` †: a slot's save as it is stored, checked: null when empty; { slot, damaged: true } when it can't be read; { newer: true } from a newer version of the game; else { slot, data, place, level, time, at (the date saved), version }\n623:- `saves.latest()` †: the most recent save that loads, or null (a title's Continue loads it)\n624:- `saves.list()` †: every slot, the autosave first: [{ slot, empty, place, level, time, at, damaged, newer }] (a menu's rows)\n625:- `saves.load(slot)` †: load a slot: its data brought up to this version (migrate), played set from it, read(save) called. Returns the save ({ data, place, level, time, slot }), or null when the slot is empty, damaged or from a newer version\n626:- `saves.save(slot, o)` †: save to a slot (0.., or 'auto'): o ({ data, place, level }) or what write() gives. Returns true when it is kept (in storage, or for the visit when storage is blocked: blocked tells), false when there was nothing to save\n627:- `saves.show(mode = 'load', done)` †: open the standard save screen over the game (E.Shell's): 'save' (to a slot) or 'load'; done(save) after a load or a save. False without a menu (a headless game, menu: false)\n628:- `saves.blocked = false` †: storage refused a save (they last for the visit)\n629:- `saves.canSave = true` †: the pause menu offers Save (a JRPG turns it off away from save points)\n630:- `saves.game` †: its game\n631:- `saves.migrate` †: an older version's data brought up to this one (or null: kept as it is)\n632:- `saves.played = 0` †: seconds played in the game's scenes (paused time and titles left out), saved with each save and set by a load\n633:- `saves.read` †: what a load does with { data, place, level, time, slot }\n634:- `saves.slots` †: how many slots besides the autosave (3)\n635:- `saves.version` †: the game's version of its data (1), saved with each save\n636:- `saves.write` †: what a save holds ({ data, place, level })\n1002:- `new E.Suspicion(o = {}) → suspicion`: new E.Suspicion({ rise, decay, notice, search, alert, forget }): a guard's mind (its fields, below, are its options). Its level rises while it sees the target (faster the more exposed and nearer), decays while it d\n1057:- `game.audio.music(song, o = {})`: Loop a song (or play once with { loop: false }). song = { bpm: 120, steps: 4, tracks: [ { wave: 'square', vol: .2, notes: 'C5 - E5 - G5 - . . | ...' }, one token per step { wave: 'triangle', notes: 'C3 . C3 . G2 . G2 .'\n1163:- `new E.Shell(game, o = {}) → shell`: new E.Shell(game, { theme, screens: { name: spec }, settings: { items, onChange(settings, key) }, store: 'shell-settings', meters: .125, standard: true }): an HTML interface over the game (see the section's header)\n1164:- `new E.Shell({ theme })`: CSS variables (ink, paper, accent, muted, danger, line, font, titleFont)\n1165:- `new E.Shell({ screens })`: specs ui.show(name) starts from (the pause screen follows game.paused; screens: { pause: false } leaves it out)\n1166:- `new E.Shell({ settings })`: settings.items: the game's own settings, { key, label, type: 'toggle' | 'slider' | 'select', min, max, step, options, value } (kept in game.settings, beside the standard ones)\n1167:- `new E.Shell({ store, meters })`: store: where an older version saved them; meters: meters per world unit for distances\n1168:- `new E.Shell({ standard })`: false leaves out the standard menu (the pause screen's Settings, Controls, Full screen and Quit, and the settings' groups)\n1605:- `world.shellMap()`: the explored map for E.Shell's minimap: game.shell.hud({ minimap: world.shellMap() }) (a cell a square, the save and boss rooms marked, the hero's cell)\n1677:- `new E.Clock(o = {}) → clock` †: new E.Clock({ day: 240 (real seconds of game time a day), hour: 8 (to start at) })\n1678:- `clock.hour` †: the hour (0..23)\n1679:- `clock.label()` †: 'DAY 2 14:30'\n1680:- `clock.light()` †: the light by the hour: { ambient (.12 at night .. 1 at noon), color (the sky's tint: blue night, warm dawn and dusk) }\n1681:- `clock.minute` †: the minute (0..59)\n1682:- `clock.night` †: true from 20:00 to 6:00\n1683:- `clock.update(dt)` †: run it by dt seconds of game time\n1684:- `clock.day = 1` †: the day (1, 2, ...)\n1685:- `clock.length` †: seconds a day\n1686:- `clock.t` †: hours since the first midnight\n1695:- `strategy.minimap(colors = {})` †: E.Shell's minimap spec: the map, the fog, the camera's view, the units seen as dots by side, a click moving the camera","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_014dQeGvPgX57ksvMohAWKKE","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
