{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CggUNk26dWjgEVud1DEhf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Part 1 written (header, contents, game summary, genre/perspective, architecture, controls/UX, core field systems). Now part 2: investigation systems and the crew-side corner."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":22826,"cache_read_input_tokens":373365,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":22826,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e2aa65a8-ee1a-45c4-b8e6-f96cf188e23d","uuid":"590b34c9-9966-498c-a9fa-cd20982590f1","timestamp":"2026-11-03T18:32:28.642Z","request_id":"req_011CggUNjBz921zCx9sMzV2G"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CggUNk26dWjgEVud1DEhf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01PW6XJGiddgWmkquQA9n88F","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat >> /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-105319/work/PLAN.md <<'EOF'\n---\n\n## 6. Investigation systems\n\n### 6.0 The Annex (hub scene) and the car\nThe detail's office is a converted records room above the city impound lot, 22×10 cells (App. B). Dana walks it in iso. **Stations** are interactables, lit only when the current beat allows them:\n\n| Station | What it does |\n|---|---|\n| **The Board** (north wall, bullpen) | Opens the Board screen (§6.1). The wall shape redraws its pinned cards and strings from STATE, so progress shows in the world too |\n| **Lt. Navarre's office** (glass, east) | Briefings (story nodes), the **ops choice** of the episode (§6.7), the Major's phone calls. Shows the Brass gauge |\n| **Wire room** (west door) | The wire scene (§6.6), only while a line is up |\n| **Evidence cage** (south-west) | Evidence viewer: photos large, items, decoded pages; also the cipher (§6.3) when a pager is in evidence |\n| **Coffee** (south-east) | Talk to whoever is on break: hints (the `hints` setting), flavor, relationship lines |\n| **Hal's bench** | Hal fixing a 1962 Zenith radio: wire tips, voice-ID practice |\n| **Ren's desk** | Photo prints come out here (flavor); van requests |\n| **Stairs** (south exit) | Leave for the next field beat → **car scene** |\n\n**Car scene:** Dana and Lou in a beige Chevy Lumina, as a side view of a city-night `E.Backdrop` scrolling (parallax by time), the car body drawn as a `px` silhouette with the two of them in the windows. It runs 1-3 short topics (E.Story with choices: \"the case\", \"Lou's daughter\", \"the Orioles\", \"Felton\"). It's skippable with ○ after the first line. It replaces free driving and carries character beats the way the show's car conversations do.\n\n### 6.1 The Board (14-board.js)\n- **Model:** `slots` by tier, `cards` (people, phones, places, vehicles, businesses) and `links` (string between cards). Each slot has `needs` (facts). Facts come from photos (★Face → `face:<id>`), reads (`obs:<id>:<role>`), informants (`name:<id>`, `stmt:<id>:<fact>`), intercepts and decoded pages (`num:<phone>:<person>`) and plates (`plate:harstad`).\n- **Tiers and slots:**\n  - **THE CORNER:** Lieutenant (Tee), Muscle (Rook), Stash (Corey), Money (Dink), Runner (Tavon), Lookout ×2 (Pigeon, Lil Moe).\n  - **THE PACKAGE:** Courier (Dale), Supplier front (Harstad Auto Parts), Re-up spot (Arundel Gas → the garage).\n  - **THE MONEY:** Boss (Easy), Driver (Lonnie), Front (Mama B's), Count (Thursday after close).\n  - **PHONES** column: P1, P2, P3, pager clone, burners B1-B5.\n- **Interaction** (DOM corkboard, 10-ft sized: at most 8 cards visible per tier page, L1/R1 change tier):\n  - Select a card (✕/click), then a slot or another card (✕/click): pin it or tie a string. Mouse drag-and-drop works too. □ unpins. △ inspects (a polaroid big, with its facts).\n  - **Validation:** a pin succeeds only if the card has the slot's needed fact. Otherwise Szabo says why not (\"Says who? Get me something that puts him on the stash.\"). Nothing is lost.\n  - Correct pins and links add Case points (§6.7) and play a pin-push sound.\n  - An unknown person shows as a silhouette card with \"?\". Easy's slot shows \"?\" until Ep3 (name) and Ep5 (face).\n- **Board tutorial** (Ep1): pin 4 faces, assign roles, and tie Tee to P1 if you photographed his payphone call.\n\n### 6.2 Notebook (15-notebook.js; Create / Tab)\nTabs with L1/R1, at most 6 items each:\n- **Objectives:** current and optional, plain sentences.\n- **Map:** the neighborhood at 1 px per 2 units, with markers (objective, payphones, known places, last-seen target) and a legend.\n- **People:** cards with portrait, name/alias, role, notes.\n- **Evidence:** polaroids and items.\n- **Phones:** known numbers, what they are, decoded pages.\n- **Case:** Case strength bar, Major's patience, estimated street heat (\"Calm / Wary / Spooked / Gone dark\"), Legal risk, episode stats.\n\n### 6.3 Pager cipher (16-cipher.js; App. C)\n- **The crew's code:** \"turn the pad\". Each digit is replaced by the digit that sits in its place after the keypad is turned a quarter-turn clockwise (`1→7 2→4 3→1 4→8 5→5 6→2 7→9 8→6 9→3 0→0`).\n- **Format:** pages are `<encoded callback> <crew code> <sender id>`. Crew codes are sent in the clear (vocabulary from Corey and intercepts): `11` package ready · `22` call me at the usual phone · `33` the count · `44` need product · `55` all clear · `77` police around · `99` stop everything. Sender ids: Tee 07, Rook 13, Pigeon 14, Corey 21, Easy's people 00.\n- **Decoder UI:** a big 3×4 keypad on the left and the encoded digits on the right. L1/R1 (or click the arrows) **turn the keypad** 90° at a time, and the decoded digits update live by position. When the decoded number matches a number Dana knows (notebook Phones), it locks with \"MATCH: Suds City payphone\" and becomes evidence `page:<n>` (Case +3). △ toggles a hint: Corey's line \"It's the phone... you turn it.\"\n- **Code flip (Ep3):** at Heat ≥ 50 after the robbery, Tee switches to counter-clockwise (the inverse). Old decodes stop matching (\"NO MATCH ×3\"). It's a **known-plaintext** puzzle: a page arrives right after Tee is overheard saying \"call me at the laundry\". The player turns the pad the other way until it matches P2. Hal: \"They didn't change the lock. They just turned the key the other way.\"\n\n### 6.4 The box: interrogation (17-box.js; App. E)\n- **Scene:** `brawler` view of a small room: table, two chairs, one-way glass, a buzzing fluorescent light (flicker light plus a 120 Hz hum). The suspect sits (sit pose). Dana and Lou stand or sit.\n- **DOM side panel:** the suspect's **Resolve** (100 → 0), **Fear** (0 → 100) and a clock (\"Booking wants him at Central in 20 min\" = 12 exchanges). Each is a bar with a word, with no color-only meaning.\n- **Each exchange,** choose an approach. The four sit on a face-button diamond drawn in the dialog area (glyph + verb; keys 1-4; hover/click):\n  - **△ Show evidence:** opens a 6-card evidence picker. Relevant evidence = a big Resolve drop. Irrelevant = Resolve +10 (\"That's a picture of a corner, Detective.\").\n  - **□ Bluff:** \"Your boy already told us…\". Succeeds only if the bluffed fact is known on the Board (Resolve −25). Otherwise Resolve +20 and Trust −1.\n  - **○ Lean on him:** Resolve −12, Fear +15.\n  - **✕ Offer a way out:** Fear −15, Resolve −8. Right after a Lean (Lou plays bad cop, you play good cop) it combos: an extra Resolve −20 and Trust +1.\n- **Beats:** 3 info beats per suspect, unlocked at Resolve thresholds and/or specific evidence. Each adds facts to the Board.\n- **Lawyer:** Fear ≥ 80 → \"I want a lawyer.\" The session ends and you keep what you have.\n- **Flip:** when beat 3 is reached and Fear ≤ 60, a fourth approach appears: **\"Work for us\"**. Accept → CI flag (with consequences later).\n- **Kitchen variant (Ep4, Pigeon at Miss Odessa's table):**\n  - Meters: **Trust** (0 → 100) and **Fear**.\n  - Approaches: △ *Be honest* (+Trust if Board facts back it), □ *Promise* (+Trust now; broken promises cost later), ○ *Push* (+Fear, risky), ✕ *Listen* (small +Trust, lets him talk; Odessa approves).\n  - Goal: Trust ≥ 70 → he agrees to tell Dana when the count moves (Path B enabler). Push twice → Odessa ends it.\n- **Lines:** every approach × Resolve band (high/mid/low) has 2 variants per side. That's about 40 lines per suspect, written in App. E style.\n\n### 6.5 Paper: affidavit and the judge (18-paper.js; App. F)\n- **Affidavit screen:** a typed document (typewriter keys sound as text appears) with a section per **target line** (e.g., P1, P2, pager clone).\n  - Each line takes up to 3 evidence cards from the evidence locker. **Probable-cause points:**\n\n    | Evidence | Points |\n    |---|---|\n    | ACT photo tied to that number | 2 |\n    | Decoded page showing the number | 2 |\n    | Intercept or observation log of a crew member using it | 1 |\n    | Informant statement | 1 (counts only with a direct item) |\n    | Seizure | 1 |\n    | Face ID linking the user to the Board | 1 |\n\n  - A line needs **≥ 4 points including at least one direct item** (ACT photo or page).\n- **Necessity section:** checkboxes for techniques tried: *Physical surveillance*, *Confidential informant*, *Undercover purchase*, *Search warrant*, *Grand jury subpoena*. Only what STATE says you did is true. Ticking a technique you didn't use is **perjury**: hidden until the judge asks. It's a real choice: an honest affidavit with fewer ticks is weaker but safe.\n- **Chambers (judge cross-examination):** Judge Halloway (crossword in hand) asks **3 questions**, chosen from App. F's pool: the weakest lines first, then any false necessity tick (always asked if present).\n  - Each question offers 3-4 answers, built from your evidence and statements. The right answers cite the right item.\n  - A wrong answer strikes that line. A caught lie denies everything: Brass −15, Legal +30, and Vance is furious.\n  - Signed lines go up for 30 days.\n  - All lines struck → denied (Brass −10). The mission runner then offers a short field beat to get one more item (any ACT photo at a payphone), and you resubmit.\n\n### 6.6 The wire room (19-wire.js; App. D) — the signature system\n- **Layout:** the room on the left 38% of the screen (canvas: Hal at the reel-to-reel, which turns while recording, a green CRT, a radiator that clanks) and three DOM panels on the right, switched with L1/R1:\n  - **LIVE:** the current call. Line and number, time, speakers (`UNKNOWN MALE 1` until identified), an animated speech-energy strip, and the transcript typing in sync with the voice.\n  - **LOG:** recorded pertinent calls; replay any of them.\n  - **PAGER:** clone-pager pages, plus the cipher.\n- **A shift** is a scheduled list of calls on a session clock (e.g., 16:00 → 23:00). One game hour passes in about 45 s; hold **R2 / Shift** to fast-forward silence ×4. About 8-10 calls per session, each 15-45 s of speech. Voices go through the phone filter (§11.3).\n- **Minimization (the law).**\n  - On every call you may listen for the first **8 s** (difficulty 6-10 s) to judge pertinence.\n  - If it's **non-pertinent** (family, food, a citizen on a public payphone), press **□ MINIMIZE** before the window ends. Listening past it on a non-pertinent call adds **Legal +4 per second**.\n  - While minimized: the audio cuts, the transcript shows \"— minimized —\" and the reels stop. You may **spot-check (□ again) for 3 s once every 10 s** to catch a call that turns pertinent, then keep listening if it did.\n  - Minimizing a pertinent call loses whatever is said while minimized.\n- **Logging:** press **✕ LOG** while a key line is spoken (or up to 2 s after) to log it. That becomes evidence `int:<call>:<line>` (Case +4). Key lines aren't highlighted unless `hints` is on and difficulty is Rookie. Logging a line that isn't key does nothing (\"Hal: Write that down if you want, it ain't evidence.\").\n- **Voice ID:** **△ ID** opens a strip of known voiceprints: people Dana heard talk in person (dialogue and barks record them in STATE) and confirmed IDs. A voiceprint is a 16-bar glyph generated from the voice profile (App. I). Matching the current speaker's glyph links the number to the person (Case +2, Board fact) for every call from now on. A wrong pick only gets \"Listen to the vowels.\"\n- **Live pages** arrive on the clone pager (a beep and a toast). Decode them in PAGER (§6.3).\n- **Session result screen:** pertinent calls logged, intel unlocked, minimization record, Legal change. This feeds the Director. If **Legal ≥ 100**, the judge pulls the wire: the rest of the session is skipped, a fallback beat has Dana get the missing intel the hard way (a field observation), and Brass −20.\n\n### 6.7 Meters and ops choices (20-meters.js)\n| Meter | Range / start | Up | Down | Effects |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **Brass** (Major's patience) | 0-100 / 60 | Arrests and seizures: Corey +10, Rook gun stop +15, sweep +25, raid +40; Sunday package +10 | Each episode start without new stats −10; affidavit denied −10; perjury −15; wire pulled −20; tail retries −5; corner gone dark −15 | **0 → the detail is shut down** (game over → retry the beat from its autosave, or take the Shut Down ending). Below 30 in Ep5 locks Path B |\n| **Heat** (crew wariness) | 0-100 / 10 | Made +15; van burned +10; Corey arrest +10; seizure +15; sweep +20; wall-off stop +5; confronting Sunday +30; Tee's interlude choices ±10 | −5 per episode; good discipline as Tee is the reverse (higher Heat means a tighter crew) | ≥30: a 3rd lookout and customer screening. ≥50: code flip and payphone rotation. ≥70: more `lookBack`s in tails (+50%). ≥90: corner goes dark for a day (Brass −15) |\n| **Legal** | 0-100 / 0 | Minimization violations; perjury +30; an illegal search (searching a person without cause in a field beat) +15 | −10 per episode | 100 → the wire is pulled; it also lowers the conviction lines in the endings |\n| **Case** | 0+ / 0 | Faces +2, reads +1, ACT +5, statements +2, pages +3, intercepts +4, voice IDs +2, plate +5, seizure +5, Easy ACT +20 | never | Bands at the end: low < 60, mid 60-119, high ≥ 120 → sentences in the montage |\n\n**Ops choice** (one per episode, Navarre's office, 2-3 cards with consequences spelled out):\n\n| Ep | Choice |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | *Ask for the van (Ren)* vs *Ask for overtime (more wire hours later)* |\n| 2 | *Use Pockets* vs *Pay for a second informant* (Fund −$100) |\n| 3 | **Give the Major bodies (sweep)** vs **Hold the line** |\n| 4 | *Burner subpoenas: rush (Legal +10, faster)* vs *by the book (Brass −5)* |\n| 5 | **Dope on the table** vs **Follow the money** |\n\n---\n\n## 7. The corner: crew side (09-corner.js)\n\n### 7.1 CornerSim (one system for story, interludes, versus and attract)\n**Roles** (each an Agent with a role brain):\n- **lieutenant:** oversees, collects cash, uses payphones and the pager.\n- **muscle:** stands near the money; deals with trouble.\n- **stash:** guards the stash spot and fetches product.\n- **money:** takes cash from customers.\n- **runner:** carries product from stash to customer.\n- **tout:** calls out the brand, steers customers.\n- **lookout ×1-3:** watchers on roofs, corners and bikes.\n\n**Places:**\n- **post** (sidewalk cells 30,31-30,34, beside the corner vacant)\n- **stash** (one of the stash spots: vacant 1412 inside 27,36 · trash can by the basketball court gate 26,49 · wheel well of a dead Buick on Gaither 32,40)\n- **handoff spot** (alley mouth 29,42 or the vacant's side 30,35)\n- **payphones** P1/P2/P3 (App. A)\n- **re-up drop** (Arundel Gas → the garage in Ep4-5)\n\n**A sale:**\n1. A customer arrives (spawn at the map edge, walks to the tout area).\n2. **Money exchange** with the money man (2 s, act `sale-money`).\n3. The money man signals the runner (a hand sign).\n4. The runner walks to the stash and back (or the stash keeper hands it out at the vacant door, act `stash-access`).\n5. **Product handoff** at the handoff spot (1.5 s, act `sale-product`).\n6. The customer leaves.\n\n$10 a vial, and a customer buys 1-3.\n\n**Rates:**\n- Customer arrivals: Poisson λ = 0.12/s base (story), 0.25/s (versus); × night 1.2; × package freshness (1.2 fresh → 0.8 stale); × 0 while shut down.\n- The money man walks the cash to the lieutenant every $300 (act `count-handoff`).\n- Re-up needed when the stash < 30 vials (versus: < 20).\n\n**Shutdown** (\"5-0!\"): triggered by any lookout reaching `alert` on police, a patrol car or knockers in view, or a call (player Tee or bot).\n- Touts go quiet, sales freeze, runners stash what they carry, and everyone switches to innocent idles (dice, phone, lean).\n- \"All clear\" after 20 s with no police in any lookout's view (versus: after the player calls it).\n- Customers waiting during a shutdown leave after 15 s.\n\n**Ledger** (invariant tests): `vials_start − vials_sold − vials_seized = vials_now` and `cash_taken = cash_banked + cash_on_money + cash_seized`.\n\n### 7.2 Police pressure (for crew-side play, versus and attract)\n- **Patrol car:** a sedan shape drives a lane loop (Ridley → Gaither → Dunmore → Abbott) at 70 u/s every 60-90 s, with a light bar off. It triggers shutdowns when seen.\n- **Knockers:** an unmarked car stops; 2 officers jump out and frisk the nearest crew member carrying product or cash. Seized if not stashed in time.\n- **Detectives** (AI plainclothes in interludes/attract, players in versus) behave like civilians but linger and raise cameras (a visible tell: the camera-raise pose for 0.6 s before a shot).\n\n### 7.3 Playing Tee (interludes)\n- **Controls:** same movement as Dana. **✕** talks and gives a context order (\"Wake up, Pigeon\", \"Count it again\", \"Walk with me\").\n- **Hold △/Q for the order wheel** (canvas radial around Tee; stick or mouse selects; release issues):\n  - *Shut it down* (5-0)\n  - *Open up*\n  - *Move the stash* (pick a spot)\n  - *Post up* (send a lookout to a spot chosen with the reticle)\n- **Watch (L2/RMB)** works for Tee too: he can study people. A suspicious read reveals undercover cops and the van, and lets you call them out.\n- **Pager and code card** (Create/Tab): incoming pages, and a keypad to send pages. **The code card shows Tee's plaintext and the encoded result side by side.** An observant player can learn the cipher from the crew side. That's dramatic irony on purpose; the police side still needs evidence (Corey's statement) to use it legally.\n- **Payphones:** walk up and ✕, then dial on a keypad with real DTMF tones (697/770/852/941 × 1209/1336/1477 Hz).\n- **The count** at the end of the shift: an animated tally (bills flick, a running total), compared with the target, then the episode's interlude choice.\n- **Shortfall:** missing the target sets `teeShort`. Easy's scenes get colder and Tee's ending changes. There's no game over.\n\n### 7.4 Interludes (all at night, 4-6 min, CornerSim running)\n| # | After | Target | Events (scripted on the sim) | Choice at the end (flags) |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| I1 | Ep1 | $2,400 | Tutorial; Dutch is $2 short (let it slide / turn him away / let Rook handle it); a patrol drive-by (call 5-0 in time); Pigeon asleep on the roof; page the re-up with the code card; Rook and Tee talk about Felton (\"who told you his name?\" → the 911 leak thread) | Dutch: `goodwill±`, `discipline±` |\n| I2 | Ep2 | $2,800 | Corey locked up; choose a new stash spot (3 options: near/risky, far/safe, slow/safe); re-up via a **payphone choice P1/P2/P3**. Tapped phones = more intel for Dana in Ep3; untapped P3 → Ep3 starts with Hal amending (Brass −5); knockers jump out | Corey: bail him out / let him sit / \"Rook wants to send a message\" (danger flag on Corey) |\n| I3 | Ep3 | $3,600 | Easy's summons at Mama B's back room (scene: Easy, Lonnie, Tee); double shift with Pigeon promoted to runner; the van event (if burned); Sunday's hearse rolls by (panic shutdown); Rook missing if arrested | **Who takes the loss?** Tee / Corey / Pigeon (`lossOn`) |\n| I4 | Ep4 | $3,000 | Burner handout at the basketball court; Tee spots Dana's car (dramatic irony); Lonnie's message about the count | **Canary trap?** Feed Corey a fake re-up time (yes/no). If yes and Corey is a CI → Corey exposed in Ep5 (a rescue objective in Path A/B) |\n| I5 | Ep5 | none | Path A: Central Booking, Easy's lawyer visits. Path B: dawn on the corner | A: take the weight / talk. B: run / stay |\n\n### 7.5 Barks\nShort speech bubbles (`E.font` on a small box over the head, 2.5 s) with Animalese voice, from a data table per role and state:\n- tout: \"Overtime! Got that Overtime!\", \"Orange tops, orange tops!\"\n- lookout warning: \"Five-oh!\", \"Hoppers up!\", two-tone whistle\n- customers: \"Y'all open?\", \"Lemme get two.\"\n- civilians: small talk, Orioles, the heat, the bus being late\n\nIntel barks (eavesdrop) carry facts: \"Re-up at four, the old gas station.\" / \"Pigeon, get your little ass back on that roof.\"\n\nEOF\nwc -c /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-105319/work/PLAN.md","description":"Append investigation and corner sections to PLAN.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":22826,"cache_read_input_tokens":373365,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":22826,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e2aa65a8-ee1a-45c4-b8e6-f96cf188e23d","uuid":"1980830b-fa2f-4570-bc39-dd804541ca8d","timestamp":"2026-11-03T18:33:53.446Z","request_id":"req_011CggUNjBz921zCx9sMzV2G","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01PW6XJGiddgWmkquQA9n88F":{"command":"cat >> /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-105319/work/PLAN.md <<'EOF'\n---\n\n## 6. Investigation systems\n\n### 6.0 The Annex (hub scene) and the car\nThe detail's office is a converted records room above the city impound lot, 22×10 cells (App. B). Dana walks it in iso. **Stations** are interactables, lit only when the current beat allows them:\n\n| Station | What it does |\n|---|---|\n| **The Board** (north wall, bullpen) | Opens the Board screen (§6.1). The wall shape redraws its pinned cards and strings from STATE, so progress shows in the world too |\n| **Lt. Navarre's office** (glass, east) | Briefings (story nodes), the **ops choice** of the episode (§6.7), the Major's phone calls. Shows the Brass gauge |\n| **Wire room** (west door) | The wire scene (§6.6), only while a line is up |\n| **Evidence cage** (south-west) | Evidence viewer: photos large, items, decoded pages; also the cipher (§6.3) when a pager is in evidence |\n| **Coffee** (south-east) | Talk to whoever is on break: hints (the `hints` setting), flavor, relationship lines |\n| **Hal's bench** | Hal fixing a 1962 Zenith radio: wire tips, voice-ID practice |\n| **Ren's desk** | Photo prints come out here (flavor); van requests |\n| **Stairs** (south exit) | Leave for the next field beat → **car scene** |\n\n**Car scene:** Dana and Lou in a beige Chevy Lumina, as a side view of a city-night `E.Backdrop` scrolling (parallax by time), the car body drawn as a `px` silhouette with the two of them in the windows. It runs 1-3 short topics (E.Story with choices: \"the case\", \"Lou's daughter\", \"the Orioles\", \"Felton\"). It's skippable with ○ after the first line. It replaces free driving and carries character beats the way the show's car conversations do.\n\n### 6.1 The Board (14-board.js)\n- **Model:** `slots` by tier, `cards` (people, phones, places, vehicles, businesses) and `links` (string between cards). Each slot has `needs` (facts). Facts come from photos (★Face → `face:<id>`), reads (`obs:<id>:<role>`), informants (`name:<id>`, `stmt:<id>:<fact>`), intercepts and decoded pages (`num:<phone>:<person>`) and plates (`plate:harstad`).\n- **Tiers and slots:**\n  - **THE CORNER:** Lieutenant (Tee), Muscle (Rook), Stash (Corey), Money (Dink), Runner (Tavon), Lookout ×2 (Pigeon, Lil Moe).\n  - **THE PACKAGE:** Courier (Dale), Supplier front (Harstad Auto Parts), Re-up spot (Arundel Gas → the garage).\n  - **THE MONEY:** Boss (Easy), Driver (Lonnie), Front (Mama B's), Count (Thursday after close).\n  - **PHONES** column: P1, P2, P3, pager clone, burners B1-B5.\n- **Interaction** (DOM corkboard, 10-ft sized: at most 8 cards visible per tier page, L1/R1 change tier):\n  - Select a card (✕/click), then a slot or another card (✕/click): pin it or tie a string. Mouse drag-and-drop works too. □ unpins. △ inspects (a polaroid big, with its facts).\n  - **Validation:** a pin succeeds only if the card has the slot's needed fact. Otherwise Szabo says why not (\"Says who? Get me something that puts him on the stash.\"). Nothing is lost.\n  - Correct pins and links add Case points (§6.7) and play a pin-push sound.\n  - An unknown person shows as a silhouette card with \"?\". Easy's slot shows \"?\" until Ep3 (name) and Ep5 (face).\n- **Board tutorial** (Ep1): pin 4 faces, assign roles, and tie Tee to P1 if you photographed his payphone call.\n\n### 6.2 Notebook (15-notebook.js; Create / Tab)\nTabs with L1/R1, at most 6 items each:\n- **Objectives:** current and optional, plain sentences.\n- **Map:** the neighborhood at 1 px per 2 units, with markers (objective, payphones, known places, last-seen target) and a legend.\n- **People:** cards with portrait, name/alias, role, notes.\n- **Evidence:** polaroids and items.\n- **Phones:** known numbers, what they are, decoded pages.\n- **Case:** Case strength bar, Major's patience, estimated street heat (\"Calm / Wary / Spooked / Gone dark\"), Legal risk, episode stats.\n\n### 6.3 Pager cipher (16-cipher.js; App. C)\n- **The crew's code:** \"turn the pad\". Each digit is replaced by the digit that sits in its place after the keypad is turned a quarter-turn clockwise (`1→7 2→4 3→1 4→8 5→5 6→2 7→9 8→6 9→3 0→0`).\n- **Format:** pages are `<encoded callback> <crew code> <sender id>`. Crew codes are sent in the clear (vocabulary from Corey and intercepts): `11` package ready · `22` call me at the usual phone · `33` the count · `44` need product · `55` all clear · `77` police around · `99` stop everything. Sender ids: Tee 07, Rook 13, Pigeon 14, Corey 21, Easy's people 00.\n- **Decoder UI:** a big 3×4 keypad on the left and the encoded digits on the right. L1/R1 (or click the arrows) **turn the keypad** 90° at a time, and the decoded digits update live by position. When the decoded number matches a number Dana knows (notebook Phones), it locks with \"MATCH: Suds City payphone\" and becomes evidence `page:<n>` (Case +3). △ toggles a hint: Corey's line \"It's the phone... you turn it.\"\n- **Code flip (Ep3):** at Heat ≥ 50 after the robbery, Tee switches to counter-clockwise (the inverse). Old decodes stop matching (\"NO MATCH ×3\"). It's a **known-plaintext** puzzle: a page arrives right after Tee is overheard saying \"call me at the laundry\". The player turns the pad the other way until it matches P2. Hal: \"They didn't change the lock. They just turned the key the other way.\"\n\n### 6.4 The box: interrogation (17-box.js; App. E)\n- **Scene:** `brawler` view of a small room: table, two chairs, one-way glass, a buzzing fluorescent light (flicker light plus a 120 Hz hum). The suspect sits (sit pose). Dana and Lou stand or sit.\n- **DOM side panel:** the suspect's **Resolve** (100 → 0), **Fear** (0 → 100) and a clock (\"Booking wants him at Central in 20 min\" = 12 exchanges). Each is a bar with a word, with no color-only meaning.\n- **Each exchange,** choose an approach. The four sit on a face-button diamond drawn in the dialog area (glyph + verb; keys 1-4; hover/click):\n  - **△ Show evidence:** opens a 6-card evidence picker. Relevant evidence = a big Resolve drop. Irrelevant = Resolve +10 (\"That's a picture of a corner, Detective.\").\n  - **□ Bluff:** \"Your boy already told us…\". Succeeds only if the bluffed fact is known on the Board (Resolve −25). Otherwise Resolve +20 and Trust −1.\n  - **○ Lean on him:** Resolve −12, Fear +15.\n  - **✕ Offer a way out:** Fear −15, Resolve −8. Right after a Lean (Lou plays bad cop, you play good cop) it combos: an extra Resolve −20 and Trust +1.\n- **Beats:** 3 info beats per suspect, unlocked at Resolve thresholds and/or specific evidence. Each adds facts to the Board.\n- **Lawyer:** Fear ≥ 80 → \"I want a lawyer.\" The session ends and you keep what you have.\n- **Flip:** when beat 3 is reached and Fear ≤ 60, a fourth approach appears: **\"Work for us\"**. Accept → CI flag (with consequences later).\n- **Kitchen variant (Ep4, Pigeon at Miss Odessa's table):**\n  - Meters: **Trust** (0 → 100) and **Fear**.\n  - Approaches: △ *Be honest* (+Trust if Board facts back it), □ *Promise* (+Trust now; broken promises cost later), ○ *Push* (+Fear, risky), ✕ *Listen* (small +Trust, lets him talk; Odessa approves).\n  - Goal: Trust ≥ 70 → he agrees to tell Dana when the count moves (Path B enabler). Push twice → Odessa ends it.\n- **Lines:** every approach × Resolve band (high/mid/low) has 2 variants per side. That's about 40 lines per suspect, written in App. E style.\n\n### 6.5 Paper: affidavit and the judge (18-paper.js; App. F)\n- **Affidavit screen:** a typed document (typewriter keys sound as text appears) with a section per **target line** (e.g., P1, P2, pager clone).\n  - Each line takes up to 3 evidence cards from the evidence locker. **Probable-cause points:**\n\n    | Evidence | Points |\n    |---|---|\n    | ACT photo tied to that number | 2 |\n    | Decoded page showing the number | 2 |\n    | Intercept or observation log of a crew member using it | 1 |\n    | Informant statement | 1 (counts only with a direct item) |\n    | Seizure | 1 |\n    | Face ID linking the user to the Board | 1 |\n\n  - A line needs **≥ 4 points including at least one direct item** (ACT photo or page).\n- **Necessity section:** checkboxes for techniques tried: *Physical surveillance*, *Confidential informant*, *Undercover purchase*, *Search warrant*, *Grand jury subpoena*. Only what STATE says you did is true. Ticking a technique you didn't use is **perjury**: hidden until the judge asks. It's a real choice: an honest affidavit with fewer ticks is weaker but safe.\n- **Chambers (judge cross-examination):** Judge Halloway (crossword in hand) asks **3 questions**, chosen from App. F's pool: the weakest lines first, then any false necessity tick (always asked if present).\n  - Each question offers 3-4 answers, built from your evidence and statements. The right answers cite the right item.\n  - A wrong answer strikes that line. A caught lie denies everything: Brass −15, Legal +30, and Vance is furious.\n  - Signed lines go up for 30 days.\n  - All lines struck → denied (Brass −10). The mission runner then offers a short field beat to get one more item (any ACT photo at a payphone), and you resubmit.\n\n### 6.6 The wire room (19-wire.js; App. D) — the signature system\n- **Layout:** the room on the left 38% of the screen (canvas: Hal at the reel-to-reel, which turns while recording, a green CRT, a radiator that clanks) and three DOM panels on the right, switched with L1/R1:\n  - **LIVE:** the current call. Line and number, time, speakers (`UNKNOWN MALE 1` until identified), an animated speech-energy strip, and the transcript typing in sync with the voice.\n  - **LOG:** recorded pertinent calls; replay any of them.\n  - **PAGER:** clone-pager pages, plus the cipher.\n- **A shift** is a scheduled list of calls on a session clock (e.g., 16:00 → 23:00). One game hour passes in about 45 s; hold **R2 / Shift** to fast-forward silence ×4. About 8-10 calls per session, each 15-45 s of speech. Voices go through the phone filter (§11.3).\n- **Minimization (the law).**\n  - On every call you may listen for the first **8 s** (difficulty 6-10 s) to judge pertinence.\n  - If it's **non-pertinent** (family, food, a citizen on a public payphone), press **□ MINIMIZE** before the window ends. Listening past it on a non-pertinent call adds **Legal +4 per second**.\n  - While minimized: the audio cuts, the transcript shows \"— minimized —\" and the reels stop. You may **spot-check (□ again) for 3 s once every 10 s** to catch a call that turns pertinent, then keep listening if it did.\n  - Minimizing a pertinent call loses whatever is said while minimized.\n- **Logging:** press **✕ LOG** while a key line is spoken (or up to 2 s after) to log it. That becomes evidence `int:<call>:<line>` (Case +4). Key lines aren't highlighted unless `hints` is on and difficulty is Rookie. Logging a line that isn't key does nothing (\"Hal: Write that down if you want, it ain't evidence.\").\n- **Voice ID:** **△ ID** opens a strip of known voiceprints: people Dana heard talk in person (dialogue and barks record them in STATE) and confirmed IDs. A voiceprint is a 16-bar glyph generated from the voice profile (App. I). Matching the current speaker's glyph links the number to the person (Case +2, Board fact) for every call from now on. A wrong pick only gets \"Listen to the vowels.\"\n- **Live pages** arrive on the clone pager (a beep and a toast). Decode them in PAGER (§6.3).\n- **Session result screen:** pertinent calls logged, intel unlocked, minimization record, Legal change. This feeds the Director. If **Legal ≥ 100**, the judge pulls the wire: the rest of the session is skipped, a fallback beat has Dana get the missing intel the hard way (a field observation), and Brass −20.\n\n### 6.7 Meters and ops choices (20-meters.js)\n| Meter | Range / start | Up | Down | Effects |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **Brass** (Major's patience) | 0-100 / 60 | Arrests and seizures: Corey +10, Rook gun stop +15, sweep +25, raid +40; Sunday package +10 | Each episode start without new stats −10; affidavit denied −10; perjury −15; wire pulled −20; tail retries −5; corner gone dark −15 | **0 → the detail is shut down** (game over → retry the beat from its autosave, or take the Shut Down ending). Below 30 in Ep5 locks Path B |\n| **Heat** (crew wariness) | 0-100 / 10 | Made +15; van burned +10; Corey arrest +10; seizure +15; sweep +20; wall-off stop +5; confronting Sunday +30; Tee's interlude choices ±10 | −5 per episode; good discipline as Tee is the reverse (higher Heat means a tighter crew) | ≥30: a 3rd lookout and customer screening. ≥50: code flip and payphone rotation. ≥70: more `lookBack`s in tails (+50%). ≥90: corner goes dark for a day (Brass −15) |\n| **Legal** | 0-100 / 0 | Minimization violations; perjury +30; an illegal search (searching a person without cause in a field beat) +15 | −10 per episode | 100 → the wire is pulled; it also lowers the conviction lines in the endings |\n| **Case** | 0+ / 0 | Faces +2, reads +1, ACT +5, statements +2, pages +3, intercepts +4, voice IDs +2, plate +5, seizure +5, Easy ACT +20 | never | Bands at the end: low < 60, mid 60-119, high ≥ 120 → sentences in the montage |\n\n**Ops choice** (one per episode, Navarre's office, 2-3 cards with consequences spelled out):\n\n| Ep | Choice |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | *Ask for the van (Ren)* vs *Ask for overtime (more wire hours later)* |\n| 2 | *Use Pockets* vs *Pay for a second informant* (Fund −$100) |\n| 3 | **Give the Major bodies (sweep)** vs **Hold the line** |\n| 4 | *Burner subpoenas: rush (Legal +10, faster)* vs *by the book (Brass −5)* |\n| 5 | **Dope on the table** vs **Follow the money** |\n\n---\n\n## 7. The corner: crew side (09-corner.js)\n\n### 7.1 CornerSim (one system for story, interludes, versus and attract)\n**Roles** (each an Agent with a role brain):\n- **lieutenant:** oversees, collects cash, uses payphones and the pager.\n- **muscle:** stands near the money; deals with trouble.\n- **stash:** guards the stash spot and fetches product.\n- **money:** takes cash from customers.\n- **runner:** carries product from stash to customer.\n- **tout:** calls out the brand, steers customers.\n- **lookout ×1-3:** watchers on roofs, corners and bikes.\n\n**Places:**\n- **post** (sidewalk cells 30,31-30,34, beside the corner vacant)\n- **stash** (one of the stash spots: vacant 1412 inside 27,36 · trash can by the basketball court gate 26,49 · wheel well of a dead Buick on Gaither 32,40)\n- **handoff spot** (alley mouth 29,42 or the vacant's side 30,35)\n- **payphones** P1/P2/P3 (App. A)\n- **re-up drop** (Arundel Gas → the garage in Ep4-5)\n\n**A sale:**\n1. A customer arrives (spawn at the map edge, walks to the tout area).\n2. **Money exchange** with the money man (2 s, act `sale-money`).\n3. The money man signals the runner (a hand sign).\n4. The runner walks to the stash and back (or the stash keeper hands it out at the vacant door, act `stash-access`).\n5. **Product handoff** at the handoff spot (1.5 s, act `sale-product`).\n6. The customer leaves.\n\n$10 a vial, and a customer buys 1-3.\n\n**Rates:**\n- Customer arrivals: Poisson λ = 0.12/s base (story), 0.25/s (versus); × night 1.2; × package freshness (1.2 fresh → 0.8 stale); × 0 while shut down.\n- The money man walks the cash to the lieutenant every $300 (act `count-handoff`).\n- Re-up needed when the stash < 30 vials (versus: < 20).\n\n**Shutdown** (\"5-0!\"): triggered by any lookout reaching `alert` on police, a patrol car or knockers in view, or a call (player Tee or bot).\n- Touts go quiet, sales freeze, runners stash what they carry, and everyone switches to innocent idles (dice, phone, lean).\n- \"All clear\" after 20 s with no police in any lookout's view (versus: after the player calls it).\n- Customers waiting during a shutdown leave after 15 s.\n\n**Ledger** (invariant tests): `vials_start − vials_sold − vials_seized = vials_now` and `cash_taken = cash_banked + cash_on_money + cash_seized`.\n\n### 7.2 Police pressure (for crew-side play, versus and attract)\n- **Patrol car:** a sedan shape drives a lane loop (Ridley → Gaither → Dunmore → Abbott) at 70 u/s every 60-90 s, with a light bar off. It triggers shutdowns when seen.\n- **Knockers:** an unmarked car stops; 2 officers jump out and frisk the nearest crew member carrying product or cash. Seized if not stashed in time.\n- **Detectives** (AI plainclothes in interludes/attract, players in versus) behave like civilians but linger and raise cameras (a visible tell: the camera-raise pose for 0.6 s before a shot).\n\n### 7.3 Playing Tee (interludes)\n- **Controls:** same movement as Dana. **✕** talks and gives a context order (\"Wake up, Pigeon\", \"Count it again\", \"Walk with me\").\n- **Hold △/Q for the order wheel** (canvas radial around Tee; stick or mouse selects; release issues):\n  - *Shut it down* (5-0)\n  - *Open up*\n  - *Move the stash* (pick a spot)\n  - *Post up* (send a lookout to a spot chosen with the reticle)\n- **Watch (L2/RMB)** works for Tee too: he can study people. A suspicious read reveals undercover cops and the van, and lets you call them out.\n- **Pager and code card** (Create/Tab): incoming pages, and a keypad to send pages. **The code card shows Tee's plaintext and the encoded result side by side.** An observant player can learn the cipher from the crew side. That's dramatic irony on purpose; the police side still needs evidence (Corey's statement) to use it legally.\n- **Payphones:** walk up and ✕, then dial on a keypad with real DTMF tones (697/770/852/941 × 1209/1336/1477 Hz).\n- **The count** at the end of the shift: an animated tally (bills flick, a running total), compared with the target, then the episode's interlude choice.\n- **Shortfall:** missing the target sets `teeShort`. Easy's scenes get colder and Tee's ending changes. There's no game over.\n\n### 7.4 Interludes (all at night, 4-6 min, CornerSim running)\n| # | After | Target | Events (scripted on the sim) | Choice at the end (flags) |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| I1 | Ep1 | $2,400 | Tutorial; Dutch is $2 short (let it slide / turn him away / let Rook handle it); a patrol drive-by (call 5-0 in time); Pigeon asleep on the roof; page the re-up with the code card; Rook and Tee talk about Felton (\"who told you his name?\" → the 911 leak thread) | Dutch: `goodwill±`, `discipline±` |\n| I2 | Ep2 | $2,800 | Corey locked up; choose a new stash spot (3 options: near/risky, far/safe, slow/safe); re-up via a **payphone choice P1/P2/P3**. Tapped phones = more intel for Dana in Ep3; untapped P3 → Ep3 starts with Hal amending (Brass −5); knockers jump out | Corey: bail him out / let him sit / \"Rook wants to send a message\" (danger flag on Corey) |\n| I3 | Ep3 | $3,600 | Easy's summons at Mama B's back room (scene: Easy, Lonnie, Tee); double shift with Pigeon promoted to runner; the van event (if burned); Sunday's hearse rolls by (panic shutdown); Rook missing if arrested | **Who takes the loss?** Tee / Corey / Pigeon (`lossOn`) |\n| I4 | Ep4 | $3,000 | Burner handout at the basketball court; Tee spots Dana's car (dramatic irony); Lonnie's message about the count | **Canary trap?** Feed Corey a fake re-up time (yes/no). If yes and Corey is a CI → Corey exposed in Ep5 (a rescue objective in Path A/B) |\n| I5 | Ep5 | none | Path A: Central Booking, Easy's lawyer visits. Path B: dawn on the corner | A: take the weight / talk. B: run / stay |\n\n### 7.5 Barks\nShort speech bubbles (`E.font` on a small box over the head, 2.5 s) with Animalese voice, from a data table per role and state:\n- tout: \"Overtime! Got that Overtime!\", \"Orange tops, orange tops!\"\n- lookout warning: \"Five-oh!\", \"Hoppers up!\", two-tone whistle\n- customers: \"Y'all open?\", \"Lemme get two.\"\n- civilians: small talk, Orioles, the heat, the bus being late\n\nIntel barks (eavesdrop) carry facts: \"Re-up at four, the old gas station.\" / \"Pigeon, get your little ass back on that roof.\"\n\nEOF\nwc -c /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-105319/work/PLAN.md","description":"Append investigation and corner sections to PLAN.md"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PW6XJGiddgWmkquQA9n88F","type":"tool_result","content":"64430 /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-105319/work/PLAN.md","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e2aa65a8-ee1a-45c4-b8e6-f96cf188e23d","uuid":"fff29ced-07e2-4766-b608-ad55d557871f","timestamp":"2026-11-03T18:33:53.556Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"64430 /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-105319/work/PLAN.md","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-105319/work/PLAN.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":447,"oldLines":3,"newStart":447,"newLines":203,"lines":[" 4. **Search:** 4 suspicious spots (car trunk, ceiling tile, toolbox, false wall). Two hold the stash, picked from a seed. Clue decals: plaster dust under the false wall, a ladder under the ceiling tile."," 5. **Results:** the package, cash and gun are seized. The press-conference cutscene follows (§8.7)."," ","+---","+","+## 6. Investigation systems","+","+### 6.0 The Annex (hub scene) and the car","+The detail's office is a converted records room above the city impound lot, 22×10 cells (App. B). Dana walks it in iso. **Stations** are interactables, lit only when the current beat allows them:","+","+| Station | What it does |","+|---|---|","+| **The Board** (north wall, bullpen) | Opens the Board screen (§6.1). The wall shape redraws its pinned cards and strings from STATE, so progress shows in the world too |","+| **Lt. Navarre's office** (glass, east) | Briefings (story nodes), the **ops choice** of the episode (§6.7), the Major's phone calls. Shows the Brass gauge |","+| **Wire room** (west door) | The wire scene (§6.6), only while a line is up |","+| **Evidence cage** (south-west) | Evidence viewer: photos large, items, decoded pages; also the cipher (§6.3) when a pager is in evidence |","+| **Coffee** (south-east) | Talk to whoever is on break: hints (the `hints` setting), flavor, relationship lines |","+| **Hal's bench** | Hal fixing a 1962 Zenith radio: wire tips, voice-ID practice |","+| **Ren's desk** | Photo prints come out here (flavor); van requests |","+| **Stairs** (south exit) | Leave for the next field beat → **car scene** |","+","+**Car scene:** Dana and Lou in a beige Chevy Lumina, as a side view of a city-night `E.Backdrop` scrolling (parallax by time), the car body drawn as a `px` silhouette with the two of them in the windows. It runs 1-3 short topics (E.Story with choices: \"the case\", \"Lou's daughter\", \"the Orioles\", \"Felton\"). It's skippable with ○ after the first line. It replaces free driving and carries character beats the way the show's car conversations do.","+","+### 6.1 The Board (14-board.js)","+- **Model:** `slots` by tier, `cards` (people, phones, places, vehicles, businesses) and `links` (string between cards). Each slot has `needs` (facts). Facts come from photos (★Face → `face:<id>`), reads (`obs:<id>:<role>`), informants (`name:<id>`, `stmt:<id>:<fact>`), intercepts and decoded pages (`num:<phone>:<person>`) and plates (`plate:harstad`).","+- **Tiers and slots:**","+  - **THE CORNER:** Lieutenant (Tee), Muscle (Rook), Stash (Corey), Money (Dink), Runner (Tavon), Lookout ×2 (Pigeon, Lil Moe).","+  - **THE PACKAGE:** Courier (Dale), Supplier front (Harstad Auto Parts), Re-up spot (Arundel Gas → the garage).","+  - **THE MONEY:** Boss (Easy), Driver (Lonnie), Front (Mama B's), Count (Thursday after close).","+  - **PHONES** column: P1, P2, P3, pager clone, burners B1-B5.","+- **Interaction** (DOM corkboard, 10-ft sized: at most 8 cards visible per tier page, L1/R1 change tier):","+  - Select a card (✕/click), then a slot or another card (✕/click): pin it or tie a string. Mouse drag-and-drop works too. □ unpins. △ inspects (a polaroid big, with its facts).","+  - **Validation:** a pin succeeds only if the card has the slot's needed fact. Otherwise Szabo says why not (\"Says who? Get me something that puts him on the stash.\"). Nothing is lost.","+  - Correct pins and links add Case points (§6.7) and play a pin-push sound.","+  - An unknown person shows as a silhouette card with \"?\". Easy's slot shows \"?\" until Ep3 (name) and Ep5 (face).","+- **Board tutorial** (Ep1): pin 4 faces, assign roles, and tie Tee to P1 if you photographed his payphone call.","+","+### 6.2 Notebook (15-notebook.js; Create / Tab)","+Tabs with L1/R1, at most 6 items each:","+- **Objectives:** current and optional, plain sentences.","+- **Map:** the neighborhood at 1 px per 2 units, with markers (objective, payphones, known places, last-seen target) and a legend.","+- **People:** cards with portrait, name/alias, role, notes.","+- **Evidence:** polaroids and items.","+- **Phones:** known numbers, what they are, decoded pages.","+- **Case:** Case strength bar, Major's patience, estimated street heat (\"Calm / Wary / Spooked / Gone dark\"), Legal risk, episode stats.","+","+### 6.3 Pager cipher (16-cipher.js; App. C)","+- **The crew's code:** \"turn the pad\". Each digit is replaced by the digit that sits in its place after the keypad is turned a quarter-turn clockwise (`1→7 2→4 3→1 4→8 5→5 6→2 7→9 8→6 9→3 0→0`).","+- **Format:** pages are `<encoded callback> <crew code> <sender id>`. Crew codes are sent in the clear (vocabulary from Corey and intercepts): `11` package ready · `22` call me at the usual phone · `33` the count · `44` need product · `55` all clear · `77` police around · `99` stop everything. Sender ids: Tee 07, Rook 13, Pigeon 14, Corey 21, Easy's people 00.","+- **Decoder UI:** a big 3×4 keypad on the left and the encoded digits on the right. L1/R1 (or click the arrows) **turn the keypad** 90° at a time, and the decoded digits update live by position. When the decoded number matches a number Dana knows (notebook Phones), it locks with \"MATCH: Suds City payphone\" and becomes evidence `page:<n>` (Case +3). △ toggles a hint: Corey's line \"It's the phone... you turn it.\"","+- **Code flip (Ep3):** at Heat ≥ 50 after the robbery, Tee switches to counter-clockwise (the inverse). Old decodes stop matching (\"NO MATCH ×3\"). It's a **known-plaintext** puzzle: a page arrives right after Tee is overheard saying \"call me at the laundry\". The player turns the pad the other way until it matches P2. Hal: \"They didn't change the lock. They just turned the key the other way.\"","+","+### 6.4 The box: interrogation (17-box.js; App. E)","+- **Scene:** `brawler` view of a small room: table, two chairs, one-way glass, a buzzing fluorescent light (flicker light plus a 120 Hz hum). The suspect sits (sit pose). Dana and Lou stand or sit.","+- **DOM side panel:** the suspect's **Resolve** (100 → 0), **Fear** (0 → 100) and a clock (\"Booking wants him at Central in 20 min\" = 12 exchanges). Each is a bar with a word, with no color-only meaning.","+- **Each exchange,** choose an approach. The four sit on a face-button diamond drawn in the dialog area (glyph + verb; keys 1-4; hover/click):","+  - **△ Show evidence:** opens a 6-card evidence picker. Relevant evidence = a big Resolve drop. Irrelevant = Resolve +10 (\"That's a picture of a corner, Detective.\").","+  - **□ Bluff:** \"Your boy already told us…\". Succeeds only if the bluffed fact is known on the Board (Resolve −25). Otherwise Resolve +20 and Trust −1.","+  - **○ Lean on him:** Resolve −12, Fear +15.","+  - **✕ Offer a way out:** Fear −15, Resolve −8. Right after a Lean (Lou plays bad cop, you play good cop) it combos: an extra Resolve −20 and Trust +1.","+- **Beats:** 3 info beats per suspect, unlocked at Resolve thresholds and/or specific evidence. Each adds facts to the Board.","+- **Lawyer:** Fear ≥ 80 → \"I want a lawyer.\" The session ends and you keep what you have.","+- **Flip:** when beat 3 is reached and Fear ≤ 60, a fourth approach appears: **\"Work for us\"**. Accept → CI flag (with consequences later).","+- **Kitchen variant (Ep4, Pigeon at Miss Odessa's table):**","+  - Meters: **Trust** (0 → 100) and **Fear**.","+  - Approaches: △ *Be honest* (+Trust if Board facts back it), □ *Promise* (+Trust now; broken promises cost later), ○ *Push* (+Fear, risky), ✕ *Listen* (small +Trust, lets him talk; Odessa approves).","+  - Goal: Trust ≥ 70 → he agrees to tell Dana when the count moves (Path B enabler). Push twice → Odessa ends it.","+- **Lines:** every approach × Resolve band (high/mid/low) has 2 variants per side. That's about 40 lines per suspect, written in App. E style.","+","+### 6.5 Paper: affidavit and the judge (18-paper.js; App. F)","+- **Affidavit screen:** a typed document (typewriter keys sound as text appears) with a section per **target line** (e.g., P1, P2, pager clone).","+  - Each line takes up to 3 evidence cards from the evidence locker. **Probable-cause points:**","+","+    | Evidence | Points |","+    |---|---|","+    | ACT photo tied to that number | 2 |","+    | Decoded page showing the number | 2 |","+    | Intercept or observation log of a crew member using it | 1 |","+    | Informant statement | 1 (counts only with a direct item) |","+    | Seizure | 1 |","+    | Face ID linking the user to the Board | 1 |","+","+  - A line needs **≥ 4 points including at least one direct item** (ACT photo or page).","+- **Necessity section:** checkboxes for techniques tried: *Physical surveillance*, *Confidential informant*, *Undercover purchase*, *Search warrant*, *Grand jury subpoena*. Only what STATE says you did is true. Ticking a technique you didn't use is **perjury**: hidden until the judge asks. It's a real choice: an honest affidavit with fewer ticks is weaker but safe.","+- **Chambers (judge cross-examination):** Judge Halloway (crossword in hand) asks **3 questions**, chosen from App. F's pool: the weakest lines first, then any false necessity tick (always asked if present).","+  - Each question offers 3-4 answers, built from your evidence and statements. The right answers cite the right item.","+  - A wrong answer strikes that line. A caught lie denies everything: Brass −15, Legal +30, and Vance is furious.","+  - Signed lines go up for 30 days.","+  - All lines struck → denied (Brass −10). The mission runner then offers a short field beat to get one more item (any ACT photo at a payphone), and you resubmit.","+","+### 6.6 The wire room (19-wire.js; App. D) — the signature system","+- **Layout:** the room on the left 38% of the screen (canvas: Hal at the reel-to-reel, which turns while recording, a green CRT, a radiator that clanks) and three DOM panels on the right, switched with L1/R1:","+  - **LIVE:** the current call. Line and number, time, speakers (`UNKNOWN MALE 1` until identified), an animated speech-energy strip, and the transcript typing in sync with the voice.","+  - **LOG:** recorded pertinent calls; replay any of them.","+  - **PAGER:** clone-pager pages, plus the cipher.","+- **A shift** is a scheduled list of calls on a session clock (e.g., 16:00 → 23:00). One game hour passes in about 45 s; hold **R2 / Shift** to fast-forward silence ×4. About 8-10 calls per session, each 15-45 s of speech. Voices go through the phone filter (§11.3).","+- **Minimization (the law).**","+  - On every call you may listen for the first **8 s** (difficulty 6-10 s) to judge pertinence.","+  - If it's **non-pertinent** (family, food, a citizen on a public payphone), press **□ MINIMIZE** before the window ends. Listening past it on a non-pertinent call adds **Legal +4 per second**.","+  - While minimized: the audio cuts, the transcript shows \"— minimized —\" and the reels stop. You may **spot-check (□ again) for 3 s once every 10 s** to catch a call that turns pertinent, then keep listening if it did.","+  - Minimizing a pertinent call loses whatever is said while minimized.","+- **Logging:** press **✕ LOG** while a key line is spoken (or up to 2 s after) to log it. That becomes evidence `int:<call>:<line>` (Case +4). Key lines aren't highlighted unless `hints` is on and difficulty is Rookie. Logging a line that isn't key does nothing (\"Hal: Write that down if you want, it ain't evidence.\").","+- **Voice ID:** **△ ID** opens a strip of known voiceprints: people Dana heard talk in person (dialogue and barks record them in STATE) and confirmed IDs. A voiceprint is a 16-bar glyph generated from the voice profile (App. I). Matching the current speaker's glyph links the number to the person (Case +2, Board fact) for every call from now on. A wrong pick only gets \"Listen to the vowels.\"","+- **Live pages** arrive on the clone pager (a beep and a toast). Decode them in PAGER (§6.3).","+- **Session result screen:** pertinent calls logged, intel unlocked, minimization record, Legal change. This feeds the Director. If **Legal ≥ 100**, the judge pulls the wire: the rest of the session is skipped, a fallback beat has Dana get the missing intel the hard way (a field observation), and Brass −20.","+","+### 6.7 Meters and ops choices (20-meters.js)","+| Meter | Range / start | Up | Down | Effects |","+|---|---|---|---|---|","+| **Brass** (Major's patience) | 0-100 / 60 | Arrests and seizures: Corey +10, Rook gun stop +15, sweep +25, raid +40; Sunday package +10 | Each episode start without new stats −10; affidavit denied −10; perjury −15; wire pulled −20; tail retries −5; corner gone dark −15 | **0 → the detail is shut down** (game over → retry the beat from its autosave, or take the Shut Down ending). Below 30 in Ep5 locks Path B |","+| **Heat** (crew wariness) | 0-100 / 10 | Made +15; van burned +10; Corey arrest +10; seizure +15; sweep +20; wall-off stop +5; confronting Sunday +30; Tee's interlude choices ±10 | −5 per episode; good discipline as Tee is the reverse (higher Heat means a tighter crew) | ≥30: a 3rd lookout and customer screening. ≥50: code flip and payphone rotation. ≥70: more `lookBack`s in tails (+50%). ≥90: corner goes dark for a day (Brass −15) |","+| **Legal** | 0-100 / 0 | Minimization violations; perjury +30; an illegal search (searching a person without cause in a field beat) +15 | −10 per episode | 100 → the wire is pulled; it also lowers the conviction lines in the endings |","+| **Case** | 0+ / 0 | Faces +2, reads +1, ACT +5, statements +2, pages +3, intercepts +4, voice IDs +2, plate +5, seizure +5, Easy ACT +20 | never | Bands at the end: low < 60, mid 60-119, high ≥ 120 → sentences in the montage |","+","+**Ops choice** (one per episode, Navarre's office, 2-3 cards with consequences spelled out):","+","+| Ep | Choice |","+|---|---|","+| 1 | *Ask for the van (Ren)* vs *Ask for overtime (more wire hours later)* |","+| 2 | *Use Pockets* vs *Pay for a second informant* (Fund −$100) |","+| 3 | **Give the Major bodies (sweep)** vs **Hold the line** |","+| 4 | *Burner subpoenas: rush (Legal +10, faster)* vs *by the book (Brass −5)* |","+| 5 | **Dope on the table** vs **Follow the money** |","+","+---","+","+## 7. The corner: crew side (09-corner.js)","+","+### 7.1 CornerSim (one system for story, interludes, versus and attract)","+**Roles** (each an Agent with a role brain):","+- **lieutenant:** oversees, collects cash, uses payphones and the pager.","+- **muscle:** stands near the money; deals with trouble.","+- **stash:** guards the stash spot and fetches product.","+- **money:** takes cash from customers.","+- **runner:** carries product from stash to customer.","+- **tout:** calls out the brand, steers customers.","+- **lookout ×1-3:** watchers on roofs, corners and bikes.","+","+**Places:**","+- **post** (sidewalk cells 30,31-30,34, beside the corner vacant)","+- **stash** (one of the stash spots: vacant 1412 inside 27,36 · trash can by the basketball court gate 26,49 · wheel well of a dead Buick on Gaither 32,40)","+- **handoff spot** (alley mouth 29,42 or the vacant's side 30,35)","+- **payphones** P1/P2/P3 (App. A)","+- **re-up drop** (Arundel Gas → the garage in Ep4-5)","+","+**A sale:**","+1. A customer arrives (spawn at the map edge, walks to the tout area).","+2. **Money exchange** with the money man (2 s, act `sale-money`).","+3. The money man signals the runner (a hand sign).","+4. The runner walks to the stash and back (or the stash keeper hands it out at the vacant door, act `stash-access`).","+5. **Product handoff** at the handoff spot (1.5 s, act `sale-product`).","+6. The customer leaves.","+","+$10 a vial, and a customer buys 1-3.","+","+**Rates:**","+- Customer arrivals: Poisson λ = 0.12/s base (story), 0.25/s (versus); × night 1.2; × package freshness (1.2 fresh → 0.8 stale); × 0 while shut down.","+- The money man walks the cash to the lieutenant every $300 (act `count-handoff`).","+- Re-up needed when the stash < 30 vials (versus: < 20).","+","+**Shutdown** (\"5-0!\"): triggered by any lookout reaching `alert` on police, a patrol car or knockers in view, or a call (player Tee or bot).","+- Touts go quiet, sales freeze, runners stash what they carry, and everyone switches to innocent idles (dice, phone, lean).","+- \"All clear\" after 20 s with no police in any lookout's view (versus: after the player calls it).","+- Customers waiting during a shutdown leave after 15 s.","+","+**Ledger** (invariant tests): `vials_start − vials_sold − vials_seized = vials_now` and `cash_taken = cash_banked + cash_on_money + cash_seized`.","+","+### 7.2 Police pressure (for crew-side play, versus and attract)","+- **Patrol car:** a sedan shape drives a lane loop (Ridley → Gaither → Dunmore → Abbott) at 70 u/s every 60-90 s, with a light bar off. It triggers shutdowns when seen.","+- **Knockers:** an unmarked car stops; 2 officers jump out and frisk the nearest crew member carrying product or cash. Seized if not stashed in time.","+- **Detectives** (AI plainclothes in interludes/attract, players in versus) behave like civilians but linger and raise cameras (a visible tell: the camera-raise pose for 0.6 s before a shot).","+","+### 7.3 Playing Tee (interludes)","+- **Controls:** same movement as Dana. **✕** talks and gives a context order (\"Wake up, Pigeon\", \"Count it again\", \"Walk with me\").","+- **Hold △/Q for the order wheel** (canvas radial around Tee; stick or mouse selects; release issues):","+  - *Shut it down* (5-0)","+  - *Open up*","+  - *Move the stash* (pick a spot)","+  - *Post up* (send a lookout to a spot chosen with the reticle)","+- **Watch (L2/RMB)** works for Tee too: he can study people. A suspicious read reveals undercover cops and the van, and lets you call them out.","+- **Pager and code card** (Create/Tab): incoming pages, and a keypad to send pages. **The code card shows Tee's plaintext and the encoded result side by side.** An observant player can learn the cipher from the crew side. That's dramatic irony on purpose; the police side still needs evidence (Corey's statement) to use it legally.","+- **Payphones:** walk up and ✕, then dial on a keypad with real DTMF tones (697/770/852/941 × 1209/1336/1477 Hz).","+- **The count** at the end of the shift: an animated tally (bills flick, a running total), compared with the target, then the episode's interlude choice.","+- **Shortfall:** missing the target sets `teeShort`. Easy's scenes get colder and Tee's ending changes. There's no game over.","+","+### 7.4 Interludes (all at night, 4-6 min, CornerSim running)","+| # | After | Target | Events (scripted on the sim) | Choice at the end (flags) |","+|---|---|---|---|---|","+| I1 | Ep1 | $2,400 | Tutorial; Dutch is $2 short (let it slide / turn him away / let Rook handle it); a patrol drive-by (call 5-0 in time); Pigeon asleep on the roof; page the re-up with the code card; Rook and Tee talk about Felton (\"who told you his name?\" → the 911 leak thread) | Dutch: `goodwill±`, `discipline±` |","+| I2 | Ep2 | $2,800 | Corey locked up; choose a new stash spot (3 options: near/risky, far/safe, slow/safe); re-up via a **payphone choice P1/P2/P3**. Tapped phones = more intel for Dana in Ep3; untapped P3 → Ep3 starts with Hal amending (Brass −5); knockers jump out | Corey: bail him out / let him sit / \"Rook wants to send a message\" (danger flag on Corey) |","+| I3 | Ep3 | $3,600 | Easy's summons at Mama B's back room (scene: Easy, Lonnie, Tee); double shift with Pigeon promoted to runner; the van event (if burned); Sunday's hearse rolls by (panic shutdown); Rook missing if arrested | **Who takes the loss?** Tee / Corey / Pigeon (`lossOn`) |","+| I4 | Ep4 | $3,000 | Burner handout at the basketball court; Tee spots Dana's car (dramatic irony); Lonnie's message about the count | **Canary trap?** Feed Corey a fake re-up time (yes/no). If yes and Corey is a CI → Corey exposed in Ep5 (a rescue objective in Path A/B) |","+| I5 | Ep5 | none | Path A: Central Booking, Easy's lawyer visits. Path B: dawn on the corner | A: take the weight / talk. B: run / stay |","+","+### 7.5 Barks","+Short speech bubbles (`E.font` on a small box over the head, 2.5 s) with Animalese voice, from a data table per role and state:","+- tout: \"Overtime! Got that Overtime!\", \"Orange tops, orange tops!\"","+- lookout warning: \"Five-oh!\", \"Hoppers up!\", two-tone whistle","+- customers: \"Y'all open?\", \"Lemme get two.\"","+- civilians: small talk, Orioles, the heat, the bus being late","+","+Intel barks (eavesdrop) carry facts: \"Re-up at four, the old gas station.\" / \"Pigeon, get your little ass back on that roof.\"","+"]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-105319/work/PLAN.md"]}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01PW6XJGiddgWmkquQA9n88F","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
