{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CggUWxKVxJ7Mj4rahN8vW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01S713NtZqJ9LH7Zm9q7x7vV","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat >> /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-105319/work/PLAN.md <<'EOF'\n---\n\n## 8. Story mode: The Case\n\n### 8.1 Setting\n- **Place and time:** **Penn Row**, a fictional neighborhood in West Baltimore, **October 2004**. Pagers, payphones and the first throwaway cell phones. Use the real city, invent the streets and places:\n  - **Ridley Avenue** (the main drag), **Gaither Street** (the corner at Gaither & Ridley), **Dunmore**, **Abbott** and **Harlow** Streets.\n  - Shops: **Gaither Market** (corner store), **Suds City** (laundromat), **Ridley Wireless & Pager** (sells the burners), **Mama B's Soul Food** (Easy's front), **Ridley Check Cashing**, **Fades & Grades** (barbershop), **Abbott Liquors**, **Ridley Carryout**.\n  - Also: **Greater Hope Baptist Church**, **the Delancey Courts** (low-rise projects), **Arundel Gas** (closed station), **the garage behind the Courts**.\n- **The crew's product:** **Overtime** (orange-top vials). A rival brand, **Hurricane**, is only talked about.\n- **The detail:** officially \"Special Detail 9\", which everyone calls *the detail*. Its office is **the Annex**, above the city impound lot.\n- **Real things stay generic:** \"Central Booking\", \"the courthouse\", \"the Western District\". All phone numbers use the fictional `555-01xx` block.\n\n### 8.2 Cast (all original; App. I has voices, §12.4 has colors)\n| id | Name | Who | Look (Humanoid options) |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| dana | **Det. Dana Whitlock**, 34 | Player. Western District narcotics, grew up three blocks off Ridley; her mother Gloria still lives there. Patient, watchful, dry; takes it personally | heroic 1.25, hair short, coat (brown leather), cream sweater, jeans |\n| lou | **Det. Louis \"Lou\" Szabo**, 52 | Partner. Exiled from Homicide for embarrassing a deputy commissioner. Smokes, Orioles, his father's sayings; very good in the box | heroic 1.25, bald, tan trench, hunch .15 |\n| hal | **Det. Harold \"Hal\" Pettiford**, 61 | Thirteen years in the pawn unit, Army Signal Corps. Fixes tube radios at his desk; runs the wire room with infinite patience | heroic 1.2, gray hair, brown cardigan, hunch .2 |\n| ren | **Officer Renata \"Ren\" Ocasio**, 26 | On loan from Southwest patrol. Digital camera, laptop, drives the van; talks fast | heroic 1.15, ponytail, navy hoodie |\n| navarre | **Lt. Gilbert \"Gil\" Navarre**, 45 | Runs the detail. Careful careerist with a conscience; an old rumor follows him | heroic 1.25, shirt and burgundy tie |\n| pruitt | **Maj. Leland Pruitt**, 55 | District commander. Lives for the stat sheet | bulky 1.3, navy uniform coat, gold trim, cap |\n| ostrowski | **Deputy Commissioner Raymond Ostrowski** | The politics (speakerphone, press conference) | bulky 1.3, dark suit |\n| vance | **ASA Corinne Vance**, 38 | Prosecutor who shepherds the affidavit; sharp, impatient | heroic 1.2, long hair pulled back, charcoal suit |\n| halloway | **Judge Abner Halloway**, 68 | Signs or refuses the wire. Crosswords, bow tie, reads every log | heroic 1.2, white hair, black robe, hunch .25 |\n| easy | **Darnell \"Easy\" Booker**, 39 | The boss. Never on the corner, never on a phone. Owns Mama B's and the check-cashing store. Soft-spoken, frightening | heroic 1.3, black leather coat |\n| lonnie | **Lonnie Fitch**, 45 | Easy's driver and voice on the phone | bulky 1.25, gray cap |\n| tee | **Terrence \"Tee\" Mabry**, 24 | Lieutenant; the second playable character. Reads business books; the counter-surveillance brain | heroic 1.25, black fitted cap, white tee, jeans, **wheat Timberlands** |\n| rook | **Ricky \"Rook\" Batts**, 27 | Muscle; volatile | bulky 1.35, black do-rag, black hoodie, **black Air Force 1s, red swoosh** |\n| corey | **Corey \"Stash\" Lyle**, 19 | Stash keeper; nervous, stammers; flip candidate | heroic 1.15, gray hood up, **duct-taped Nikes**, hunch .25 |\n| pigeon | **Junior \"Pigeon\" Hollis**, 14 | Roof lookout; keeps pigeons on his grandmother's roof; comics. The heart of the story | heroic 1.0, red hoodie, **light-up sneakers** (blink while he runs) |\n| moe | **Maurice \"Lil Moe\" Dorsey**, 13 | Bike lookout | heroic 1.0, green cap, yellow tee, bike |\n| dink | **Darius \"Dink\" Pratt**, 16 | Money man | heroic 1.1, blue jersey |\n| tavon | **Tavon Gibbs**, 17 | Runner/tout | heroic 1.15, black puffy coat, red band |\n| pockets | **Wesley \"Pockets\" Gaines**, 47 | Informant and addict. Sells loosies and batteries from a baby stroller. Never looks at faces, knows everyone by their **shoes** | heroic 1.15, army jacket, old red cap, hunch .3, stroller shape |\n| odessa | **Miss Odessa Tillman**, 70 | Pigeon's grandmother, church usher, sits on her stoop; calls Dana \"Dana Lynn\" | heroic 1.1, gray hair, plum housedress, hunch .2 |\n| sunday | **Royal \"Sunday\" Odom**, 52 | Stick-up man with a code: never on Sunday, never a citizen, never a child. Drives an old **hearse** | heroic 1.25, flat cap, fishing vest |\n| dale | **Dale Kucharski**, 50s | Courier; drives the **Harstad Auto Parts** box truck | bulky 1.25, red company cap, work shirt |\n| harstad | **Glenn Harstad**, 57 | The connect (Dundalk). Montage teaser only | heroic 1.25, navy blazer |\n| felton | **Cornelius Felton**, 66 | Retired MTA bus driver who called in the corner. Murdered in the cold open (seen only under a sheet; a photo on his stoop memorial) | |\n| others | Officers Dukes and Kowalczyk (patrol), knockers, civilians, \"Dutch\" (a customer), Gloria Whitlock (phone only), State Senator Marian Ocheltree (montage) | | |\n\n### 8.3 Episode 1: EYES ON (~15 min)\nEpigraph: *\"Everybody on that corner is working. Question is, who's signing the checks.\"* (Lou Szabo)\n\n| # | Beat | Where | What happens / mechanics | Exit, flags |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1.1 | **Cold open** | field, 05:40, rain | Police tape at 1407 Gaither, two patrol cars with light bars (red/blue lights), Felton under a sheet on his stoop, candles and flowers. Dana walks in (move tutorial). Talk to Officer Dukes, then Lou (Homicide primary), then Miss Odessa across the street. She won't talk (\"I got a grandbaby to raise.\"), and the camera drifts up to Pigeon on her roof with his birds, watching. Optional: read the cards on the stoop | Lou: \"This ain't a whodunit, Dana. It's a who-cares.\" |\n| 1.2 | Card | | WIRETAP logo sting, then \"Episode 1: Eyes On\" and the epigraph | |\n| 1.3 | **Briefing** | Annex | Navarre assembles the detail (introductions in App. G). The Sun ran Felton's photo; the Deputy Commissioner wants \"six weeks, one corner, arrests\". Brass gauge appears. Stations: Board (empty: tutorial arrow), Evidence cage (take the camera: 30 shots; Fund $200), Coffee (Lou). Ops choice 1 | Car scene |\n| 1.4 | **Eyes on** | field, 15:00-17:30, overcast | **Required:** ★Face photos of Tee, Rook, Corey and Pigeon; read 2 roles; meet Pockets in the alley behind Gaither Market (pay $20, show photos, match shoes to names: App. G). **Optional:** an ★Act photo of a sale; Tee's call at P1 (16:10, then every 12 game minutes). Pockets also drops \"Dre broke his ankle jumping the fence at the old Arundel station\". It's needed in Ep3 and logged in the notebook. Tutorials as each first happens: Watch, Photo, Blend, Cover, Heat, Made, Eavesdrop | Back to the Chevy |\n| 1.5 | **Board** | Annex | Board tutorial: pin faces, assign roles, tie Tee to P1 if photographed. Pruitt calls Navarre (speaker): \"I've got a dead taxpayer on page one and a detail with no arrests.\" | Autosave |\n| 1.6 | **Interlude I1** | field, night, as Tee | §7.4 | flags |\n\n### 8.4 Episode 2: PAPER (~15 min)\nEpigraph: *\"A judge doesn't care what you know. He cares what you can write down.\"* (ASA Corinne Vance)\n\n| # | Beat | Where | What happens / mechanics | Exit, flags |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 2.1 | Card | | | |\n| 2.2 | Briefing | Annex | Vance explains what a wire needs (numbers, probable cause, necessity). Hal: \"They don't carry cell phones. Payphones and pagers.\" Ops choice 2 | Car scene |\n| 2.3 | **Payphones** | field, 11:00-13:00, day | Read the number plates on P1, P2 and P3 (interact; reading in a watcher's view counts as loitering). ★Act payphone photos (Tee at P1, Tavon at P2 on schedules). Then Navarre on the radio: the knockers are rolling on the corner to grab the stash kid with the pager. **Corey bolts → CHASE** (tutorial: sprint, vault, tackle, cuff), ditch and search | Corey in custody (+ package if found) |\n| 2.4 | **The box** | box | Corey (App. E): B1 who he works for (Tee), B2 the code hint (\"you turn it\"), B3 the stash (1412 vacant, behind the radiator). Flip offer | `coreyCI`, facts |\n| 2.5 | **Cipher** | Evidence cage | Decode Corey's pager memory (5 pages, App. C). Matches P1/P2/P3; 555-0174 stays unknown (later Harstad) | evidence |\n| 2.6 | **Affidavit** | Annex | Lines for P1, P2 and the pager clone (+P3 if supported). Necessity honesty | |\n| 2.7 | **Chambers** | chambers | Halloway, 3 questions (App. F). Signed: \"You're up. Thirty days. Minimize, Detective. I read the logs.\" Denied: an extra field beat (one more ★Act payphone photo), then resubmit | `wireUp` |\n| 2.8 | **Interlude I2** | Tee | Includes the payphone choice that shapes Ep3 | flags |\n\n### 8.5 Episode 3: UP (~18 min)\nEpigraph: *\"You don't listen to a phone. You listen to a man getting comfortable.\"* (Hal Pettiford)\n\n| # | Beat | Where | What happens / mechanics | Exit, flags |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 3.1 | Card | | | |\n| 3.2 | **We're up** | Annex | Hal's wire tutorial (minimize, spot-check, log, ID, pages, fast-forward) | |\n| 3.3 | **Session 1** | wire, 16:00-23:00 | Calls S1-1…S1-10 (App. D). The re-up riddle: \"the place where Dre messed up his ankle\" → pick the place on the notebook map (Arundel Gas). If Pockets' line was missed, Hal suggests finding Pockets (a 1-minute field beat at the bus stop) | `reupSpot` |\n| 3.4 | **The van** | field, 15:30-16:30, next day | Ren drives. Choose a spot (V1 Harlow curb, V2 Ridley east, V3 lot gap); van heat (§5.2); long lens (48 shots). Photograph the **Harstad box truck** (logo + plate), **Dale** (★Act re-up handoff with Tavon) and Pigeon circling on a bike. Then **Sunday's hearse**: he robs Tavon of the package at gunpoint, quick, no shots (act `robbery`, photographable). **Dilemma:** *Stay on the eye* (Sunday on the Board; violence follows) / *Call it in anonymously* (patrol rolls up, Sunday escapes, Heat +20) / *Go in yourself* (stand-off dialogue; Sunday leaves the package: \"I don't do police, Detective. Police do me.\" Van burned, Heat +30, Brass +10) | `dilemma` |\n| 3.5 | **The Major** | Annex | Pruitt in person. **Ops choice 3:** *Give him bodies* (sweep: Brass +25, Heat +20, P1 line goes dead) vs *Hold the line* (Brass −20). Board: THE PACKAGE tier (plate → Harstad Auto Parts; 555-0174 matches) | `sweep` |\n| 3.6 | **Session 2** | wire, 20:00-01:00 | Calls S2-1…S2-8. Rook asks for \"a hammer\" → **threat to life:** *Let it ride* vs *Wall-off stop* (a patrol car stops Rook's Monte Carlo for a broken taillight, finds the gun, arrests him: Brass +15, Heat +5; Rook in the box, 3 lines: \"Lawyer.\"). Lonnie: \"He wants to see you. Mama B's.\" → THE MONEY tier gets \"Boss ?\" and Mama B's. **Code flip** if Heat ≥ 50 | `wallOff`, `rookFree` |\n| 3.7 | **Interlude I3** | Tee | Easy's scene at Mama B's; who takes the loss | `lossOn` |\n\n### 8.6 Episode 4: DRY CLEANING (~15 min)\nEpigraph: *\"Smart ain't never being seen. Smart is being boring when they look.\"* (Terrence Mabry)\n\n| # | Beat | Where | What happens / mechanics | Exit, flags |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 4.1 | Card | | | |\n| 4.2 | Quiet lines | Annex | The payphones went dead: \"Throwaways.\" Hal explains burners: bought for cash, used a week, thrown in the harbor. Plan: tail Tee to the handout, get the packaging, subpoena the carrier. Ops choice 4. Gloria calls: \"Somebody was asking about you at the market.\" | Car scene |\n| 4.3 | **The tail** | field, 20:00, rain | Tee's dry-cleaning route (App. J `teeDry`) with Lou hand-offs (§5.5). Ends at the basketball court: Tee hands phones to the crew (read = observation `burners`) | checkpoint |\n| 4.4 | **Trash** | field, 21:30, rain | The alley behind Ridley Wireless (§5.7): find the bag with 12 phone boxes | `serials` |\n| 4.5 | **Kitchen** | Odessa's kitchen (box scene variant, warm light) | Pigeon at the table, Odessa at the stove (§6.4 kitchen) | `pigeonTrust` |\n| 4.6 | Numbers | Annex | The subpoena returns B1-B5. Halloway amends by phone (\"Same rules, Detective.\"). Pin burners to people | |\n| 4.7 | **Session 3** | wire, 6 calls (App. D) | The count is Thursdays at Mama B's after close; Friday's truck goes to \"the garage behind the Courts\". Tee mentions Dana's mother → choice: *call your mother* (`momSafe`: she goes to her sister's in the county) / *stay on the wire* | |\n| 4.8 | **Interlude I4** | Tee | The canary trap | `canary` |\n\n### 8.7 Episode 5: THE COUNT (~15-20 min)\nEpigraph: *\"Every week the money gets counted. Every week somebody comes up short.\"* (Darnell \"Easy\" Booker)\n\n| # | Beat | Where | What happens / mechanics |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 5.1 | Card | | |\n| 5.2 | **Two ways** | Annex | Pruitt, with Ostrowski on speakerphone: \"Friday. Dope on the table, cameras rolling.\" Navarre lays out both paths. **Ops choice 5:** **A, Dope on the table** (raid the garage, Friday 21:00) or **B, Follow the money** (Thursday's count at Mama B's). B needs Brass ≥ 30 and either (`coreyCI` and Corey not exposed) or `pigeonTrust` ≥ 70; otherwise its card says why it's locked |\n| 5.3A | **Raid** | field, Friday 21:00 | §5.8. If the canary trap exposed Corey, first a **60-second rescue:** Rook holds Corey in the 1412 vacant (sprint there; Rook flees from police; there's no fight). Late means Corey disappears |\n| 5.4A | **Press conference** | outside the garage | A table with dope, guns and cash. Pruitt and Ostrowski at the mic, camera flashes, the detail at the back. Ostrowski: \"a major blow to the drug trade in West Baltimore.\" Lou: \"Major blow. They'll be open by Monday.\" |\n| 5.3B | **The count** | field, Thursday 22:30 | Tail the count runner (Pigeon if he trusts Dana and tells her the route: easier; otherwise Tavon) to Mama B's back door. Lonnie's car circles (a moving headlight cone = an observer). Then the vacant roof and the long lens (§5.7): ★★★ Easy in the act |\n| 5.4B | **The morning after** | Annex | Navarre: the detail is disbanded anyway (\"The Deputy wanted a podium, not a case file.\"). Vance takes the file to a grand jury: \"Eighteen months, Detective. If you're lucky.\" |\n| 5.5 | **Interlude I5** | Tee | A: Central Booking; Easy's lawyer: \"Easy says your mother's rent is paid through spring.\" Take the weight / talk. B: dawn on the corner. Run / stay |\n| 5.6 | **Montage → credits** | | §8.8. Then the credits roll (names, plus \"Inspired by The Wire (2002-2008)\") → title. All episodes unlock in Episode select |\n\n**Shut Down** at any point (Brass 0) → the `shutdown` scene: Navarre packing boxes: \"Detail 9 is disbanded, effective Monday.\" Choose *Retry from the last autosave* or *See how it ends* (the Shut Down montage).\n\n### 8.8 Endings and montage\n- **Three paths:** A (raid), B (money) or Shut Down. Each montage is 9-11 cards, picked by rules over the flags (App. G).\n- **Fixed cards** (the game goes on):\n  - \"The corner at Gaither & Ridley: open for business by Monday.\"\n  - \"Maj. Leland Pruitt: promoted to Colonel.\"\n  - \"Hal Pettiford: kept the wire room. Nobody told him to leave.\"\n- **Variable cards:**\n  - Tee: by I5 choice and Case band\n  - Easy: by path\n  - Pigeon (3 fates): by `lossOn`, `pigeonTrust`, Path B runner and `rookFree`\n  - Corey (3 fates): `coreyCI`, `canary`, rescue\n  - Rook: `wallOff`, `rookDrew`\n  - Sunday: `dilemma`\n  - Dana: by path\n  - Lou, Ren, Navarre\n- **The teaser** always runs last: \"Glenn Harstad: guest of honor at State Senator Marian Ocheltree's harbor fundraiser.\" Then **TO BE CONTINUED**.\n- **How a card is shown:** a live vignette (camera on a POI, characters posed, letterboxed 2.35:1), caption at the bottom, 6 s each, crossfade, the `montage` song (App. H).\n\n### 8.9 Episode select and saves\n- **Saves:** `game.saves` slots (3 + autosave). Autosave at every beat start.\n- **Title menu:** CONTINUE (latest), NEW CASE, EPISODES (unlocked), THE GAME, SETTINGS, ABOUT & CREDITS.\n- **Episode select** starts an episode from a **canonical state** (STATE presets in data):\n  - Ep2: 4 faces with names; Heat 20, Brass 55.\n  - Ep3: wire up on P1, P2 and the pager clone; `coreyCI` false; Brass 50.\n  - Ep4: dilemma \"stay\", sweep false, `wallOff` true, Heat 45.\n  - Ep5: burners known, `pigeonTrust` 75, Brass 45.\n- **Restarting:** the pause menu offers *Restart this part* (the beat's autosave) and *Episode select*.\n\n---\n\n## 9. Versus mode and online play: THE GAME (50-versus.js, 51-net.js)\n\n### 9.1 The round\n- **Sides:** *The Corner* (crew) vs *The Detail* (police) on the **versus zone** of the same map (cells 18-50 × 16-44: Ridley between Abbott and Harlow, Gaither, the two alleys, the Courts lane). Barricades and police tape block the zone's edge (blocked floor cells, sawhorse shapes). AI civilians walk through; detectives look like civilians.\n- **Length:** 5:00 (local setup: 3, 5 or 8 min).\n- **Outcome:**\n  - **Detail win:** Evidence reaches **100** (immediate).\n  - **Corner win:** at time-up, Count ≥ **$3,000** and Evidence < 100.\n  - **Draw:** neither (\"The game goes on\").\n- **Seats:** side of seat *i* = `(i + round) % 2 === 0 ? 'corner' : 'detail'`, so players alternate sides between rounds. With 1 player: Detail vs bot Corner. With 3: two on one side.\n  - Corner players take the **Lieutenant** first, then the **Runner**. Detail players are **Detectives** (up to 2).\n  - Bots fill every empty crew role (always) and empty detective slots (to at least 1 detective).\n\n| Corner actions | Detail actions |\n|---|---|\n| **Lieutenant:** watch people (L2/RMB); **call out** a person (△/Q while watching). A detective → **burned** 25 s (their photos score 0, they're outlined red for the Corner, and AI lookouts track them). A civilian → −$200 and customers avoid the corner for 10 s; cooldown 15 s. **Shut it down / open up** (□/F). Move the stash (✕ at the stash, pick a spot). **Re-up** at a payphone (✕, 2 s) when the stash < 20 → a car drops the package in 20 s, which the Runner must fetch | **Photos** (L2 + R2 / RMB + LMB): first ★Face of each crew member +4; ★Act +12 (max 2 per crew member). Photo of the **stash** in use +25 (+15 again after it moves). **Tap a payphone** (✕, 4 s, unseen) → each Corner re-up call from it +10. **Jump-out** (△/Q while watching, once per round): patrol frisks the target 8 s later. Carrying → seizure +20 and the Corner loses what was carried; clean → −10 |\n| **Runner:** pick up product at the stash (✕), hand off to a waiting customer (✕), ditch (○) if a cop closes in (lost product) | **Blend** (□/F) and cover activities work as in story. AI lookouts build suspicion on detectives (§5.2); full = auto-burn |\n\n- **Bots:**\n  - **Corner bot:** the CornerSim role brains, plus a lieutenant brain. It shuts down when any lookout reaches `search`. It calls out the person with the highest *observed* suspicion score once that passes 0.8 (from behaviors it can see: lingering, camera raises, following the runner). It re-ups at the payphone it hasn't seen tampered with. It moves the stash after a stash photo it noticed.\n  - **Detective bot:** picks vantage points (data list of 12), photographs the next sale it sees, moves when its heat passes 0.5, sometimes tails the runner, and taps a payphone when no crew is within 120 units.\n  - Bots may cheat a little on perception (they read exact act windows). They're for filling seats, not balance.\n- **Personal score:** Detail = the evidence they earned. Corner = the count they handled ÷ 10 + correct call-outs × 20.\n- **Results screen:** outcome, then per player: photos, burns, call-outs, count. Awards (*Eyes On*: most ★Act; *Made You*: first correct call-out; *Clean Hands*: Corner player never seized; *Paper Trail*: most tap points).\n\n### 9.2 Local play (\"on its own\")\n- **Setup screen** (DOM): P1 side, *P2: press ✕ on a second controller or Enter on the keyboard's right half* (`game.allowJoin({ max: 2 })`), round length, Start.\n- **1 human:** vs bots.\n- **2 humans:** split screen with `game.splitScreen(2, { follow: [c1, c2], layout: 'auto' })`. Each viewport draws its own HUD on the canvas inside `r.viewport` (E.Shell's HUD is single-screen, so versus uses a canvas HUD). Then `scene.hud(r)` draws the timer and the shared Count/Evidence bar at the top.\n- **Caveat:** hidden identity can be peeked at on one screen. Accept it locally; online it's truly hidden.\n- **Same code path:** local play runs the same `VersusSim` through `LocalTransport` (this copy is the host; all players are local).\n\n### 9.3 AI Hub: shared-world (AI Hub Session Protocol v1, client 1.4.0)\n**Tags** (in `<head>`, after the client script):\n```html\n<meta name=\"hub:session\" content=\"1\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-players\" content=\"1-4\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-mode\" content=\"shared-world\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-minutes\" content=\"6\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-goal\" content=\"Cops: build a 100-point case. Corner: make $3,000 unseen.\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-howto\" content=\"Move: stick/WASD · Watch: L2/RMB · Photo: R2/LMB · Act: ✕/E · Call out: △/Q\">\n```\n**Flow** (99-start.js):\n```js\nif (window.AIHub && AIHub.active) {                      // straight into the round: no title, attract or menus\n  game.start({ scenes, scene: 'hubWait', boot });        // 'Connecting…' (no prompts)\n  const info = await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'shared-world', seats: [1, 4] });   // the hub's own card (no card: true)\n  if (!info) game.go('title');                           // no hub after all: the normal game\n  else { await Versus.buildRound(info); AIHub.ready(); } // roster from AIHub.rng('roster'); sides from seats + info.round\n}\nAIHub.on('start', () => Versus.countdown());             // overlay: role card + 3-2-1 until AIHub.time() >= 0\n```\n- **Host authority** (`info.isHost`): the host copy runs `VersusSim`: NPCs, crew AI, bots, rules, scoring, the timer (from `AIHub.time()`).\n- **Every copy moves its own character locally** (no input lag) and reports it. The host trusts positions inside a speed check.\n- **Other copies render snapshots** with 150 ms interpolation.\n- **Messages:**\n  - Host → all, unreliable, 10 Hz: `{t:'s', at, tl, ev, cn, ph, p:[[id,x,y,f,st,fl],…], n:[[nid,x,y,f,st],…]}`.\n    - x, y are integers (world units); f is facing quantized 0-63; st is an animation code (0 idle, 1 walk, 2 run, 3 crouch, 4 watch, 5 act, 6 down, 7 sit, 8 phone, 9 bike); fl is flags (burned, carrying, shut).\n    - **Keep each message under 1,100 bytes.** If the NPC list makes it bigger, send NPCs in two alternating halves (5 Hz each).\n  - Host → all, reliable, on events: `{t:'e', k:'photo'|'burn'|'callout'|'tap'|'jump'|'seize'|'stash'|'reup'|'shut'|'open'|'sale', …}` (sounds, toasts, particles).\n  - Client → host, unreliable, 10 Hz: `{t:'me', at, x, y, f, st, w, ax, ay}` (w = watching; ax, ay = the aimed world point).\n  - Client → host, reliable: `{t:'act', k:'photo', target, q, at}` · `{k:'callout', target}` · `{k:'tap', phone}` · `{k:'jump', target}` · `{k:'shut'|'open'|'stash'|'reup'|'pickup'|'handoff'|'ditch', …}`.\n  - Budget: host 10 snapshots + under 5 events per second (< 20/s); clients 10 + a few.\n- **Validation on the host:**\n  - Positions are clamped to `maxSpeed × elapsed × 1.5` and to walkable cells.\n  - A photo claim needs: the target exists, is within 240 units of the claimer, and `map.sight` is clear on the host. If ★Act is claimed, the host's 1-second act history must show an act within 600 ms.\n  - Call-outs are checked against the true identity.\n- **Events:**\n  - `leave` → that player's character becomes a bot on the same side; the round goes on.\n  - The host leaving voids the round (the hub sends `end` `host-left`) → show \"Round cancelled\".\n  - `time-up` → the host finishes at once with the timer-end outcome.\n  - `end` → stop input (controllers to null), stop music and effects, show our results under the hub's. After `end`, send nothing.\n- **Server** (`AIHub.server`): the host has no local player. It runs the sim and shows a spectator camera (`cam.frame` over all players). No audio, no input.\n- **Finish** (host only, once):\n  - `standings`: winners `[[winning side ids],[losing side ids]]`; draw `[[all ids]]`. Only hub player ids, never bots.\n  - `scores`: personal scores.\n  - `stats`: `{id:{Photos, Burns, Count}}`.\n  - `awards`.\n- **Session rules:**\n  - No other network use.\n  - No `alert`/`confirm`/`prompt`, no new windows.\n  - Pause doesn't stop the host: the versus scene is `pausable: false` in a session. Options opens a non-pausing overlay with Settings/Controls (`game.menu('settings')`) while the character's input is suppressed.\n  - `menu.quit: false` and no restart items.\n  - While Create (Pad8) is held, ignore Options.\n- **Randomness:** the host never uses `Math.random` for the sim. Shared rolls come from `AIHub.rng(label)`, and the roster from `AIHub.rng('roster')`, so every copy builds identical NPC rigs.\n\n---\n\n## 10. Attract mode (52-attract.js)\n- **Trigger:** 10 s with no input (keys, mouse buttons, mouse moves over 6 px, wheel, touches, gamepad buttons, or axes past 0.3) on **title, main menu, episode select or versus setup**. Settings, About and Controls don't count (a player may be reading).\n- **Exit:** any input → back to the title, and the idle timer resets. On touch-only devices, a tap → the notice panel.\n- **The reel:** a looping playlist of vignettes, each a real system running with bot controllers. Bots may cheat: no suspicion, unlimited film, teleports, scripted perfect actions.\n  - **Overlay:** letterbox bars, a **DEMO** badge, a small WIRETAP logo, a caption, and a blinking \"Press any button\" built from the current device's glyph.\n\n| # | s | Vignette | Bot does |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | 12 | **THE CORNER**: night, rain, CornerSim full; the camera turns 90° twice | Nothing: customers, touts, lookouts |\n| 2 | 10 | **EYES ON**: Dana on the bus-stop bench | Enter Watch, aim at the next sale, snap ★★★, polaroid slides in |\n| 3 | 10 | **THE TAIL**: Tee's route | Dana tails; Tee looks back; Dana takes cover in a doorway; hand-off to Lou |\n| 4 | 9 | **THE CHASE**: Corey bolts | Sprint, vault the court fence, tackle, cuff |\n| 5 | 10 | **THE WIRE**: wire room | Grandma call → MINIMIZE; pertinent call → LOG; a page decodes with a keypad turn |\n| 6 | 7 | **THE BOARD**: corkboard | Cards fly onto slots; red string ties Tee to P1 |\n| 7 | 8 | **THE BOX**: Corey | Lean → Offer a way out → beat unlocked |\n| 8 | 10 | **THE GAME**: versus, split screen, bots | A call-out burns a detective; a stash photo |\n| 9 | 8 | **THE COUNT**: Tee's tally | Bills flick, the total ticks up, then the title card |\n\n- **Implementation:** each entry is `{ id, seconds, setup(), tick(dt), caption }`. `setup()` loads a mission/scene with `attract: true`: no saves, no tutorials, no autosave, quieter music, no HUD prompts. The attract scene owns the clock and calls `game.go` for the next entry with a short dissolve.\n\nEOF\nwc -c /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-105319/work/PLAN.md","description":"Append story, versus/online and attract sections to PLAN.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9176,"cache_read_input_tokens":396191,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":9176,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e2aa65a8-ee1a-45c4-b8e6-f96cf188e23d","uuid":"847c12c3-e8e8-4332-93eb-d425e59690ce","timestamp":"2026-11-03T18:37:14.782Z","request_id":"req_011CggUWwth5jHciH5YjK17o","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01S713NtZqJ9LH7Zm9q7x7vV":{"command":"cat >> /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-105319/work/PLAN.md <<'EOF'\n---\n\n## 8. Story mode: The Case\n\n### 8.1 Setting\n- **Place and time:** **Penn Row**, a fictional neighborhood in West Baltimore, **October 2004**. Pagers, payphones and the first throwaway cell phones. Use the real city, invent the streets and places:\n  - **Ridley Avenue** (the main drag), **Gaither Street** (the corner at Gaither & Ridley), **Dunmore**, **Abbott** and **Harlow** Streets.\n  - Shops: **Gaither Market** (corner store), **Suds City** (laundromat), **Ridley Wireless & Pager** (sells the burners), **Mama B's Soul Food** (Easy's front), **Ridley Check Cashing**, **Fades & Grades** (barbershop), **Abbott Liquors**, **Ridley Carryout**.\n  - Also: **Greater Hope Baptist Church**, **the Delancey Courts** (low-rise projects), **Arundel Gas** (closed station), **the garage behind the Courts**.\n- **The crew's product:** **Overtime** (orange-top vials). A rival brand, **Hurricane**, is only talked about.\n- **The detail:** officially \"Special Detail 9\", which everyone calls *the detail*. Its office is **the Annex**, above the city impound lot.\n- **Real things stay generic:** \"Central Booking\", \"the courthouse\", \"the Western District\". All phone numbers use the fictional `555-01xx` block.\n\n### 8.2 Cast (all original; App. I has voices, §12.4 has colors)\n| id | Name | Who | Look (Humanoid options) |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| dana | **Det. Dana Whitlock**, 34 | Player. Western District narcotics, grew up three blocks off Ridley; her mother Gloria still lives there. Patient, watchful, dry; takes it personally | heroic 1.25, hair short, coat (brown leather), cream sweater, jeans |\n| lou | **Det. Louis \"Lou\" Szabo**, 52 | Partner. Exiled from Homicide for embarrassing a deputy commissioner. Smokes, Orioles, his father's sayings; very good in the box | heroic 1.25, bald, tan trench, hunch .15 |\n| hal | **Det. Harold \"Hal\" Pettiford**, 61 | Thirteen years in the pawn unit, Army Signal Corps. Fixes tube radios at his desk; runs the wire room with infinite patience | heroic 1.2, gray hair, brown cardigan, hunch .2 |\n| ren | **Officer Renata \"Ren\" Ocasio**, 26 | On loan from Southwest patrol. Digital camera, laptop, drives the van; talks fast | heroic 1.15, ponytail, navy hoodie |\n| navarre | **Lt. Gilbert \"Gil\" Navarre**, 45 | Runs the detail. Careful careerist with a conscience; an old rumor follows him | heroic 1.25, shirt and burgundy tie |\n| pruitt | **Maj. Leland Pruitt**, 55 | District commander. Lives for the stat sheet | bulky 1.3, navy uniform coat, gold trim, cap |\n| ostrowski | **Deputy Commissioner Raymond Ostrowski** | The politics (speakerphone, press conference) | bulky 1.3, dark suit |\n| vance | **ASA Corinne Vance**, 38 | Prosecutor who shepherds the affidavit; sharp, impatient | heroic 1.2, long hair pulled back, charcoal suit |\n| halloway | **Judge Abner Halloway**, 68 | Signs or refuses the wire. Crosswords, bow tie, reads every log | heroic 1.2, white hair, black robe, hunch .25 |\n| easy | **Darnell \"Easy\" Booker**, 39 | The boss. Never on the corner, never on a phone. Owns Mama B's and the check-cashing store. Soft-spoken, frightening | heroic 1.3, black leather coat |\n| lonnie | **Lonnie Fitch**, 45 | Easy's driver and voice on the phone | bulky 1.25, gray cap |\n| tee | **Terrence \"Tee\" Mabry**, 24 | Lieutenant; the second playable character. Reads business books; the counter-surveillance brain | heroic 1.25, black fitted cap, white tee, jeans, **wheat Timberlands** |\n| rook | **Ricky \"Rook\" Batts**, 27 | Muscle; volatile | bulky 1.35, black do-rag, black hoodie, **black Air Force 1s, red swoosh** |\n| corey | **Corey \"Stash\" Lyle**, 19 | Stash keeper; nervous, stammers; flip candidate | heroic 1.15, gray hood up, **duct-taped Nikes**, hunch .25 |\n| pigeon | **Junior \"Pigeon\" Hollis**, 14 | Roof lookout; keeps pigeons on his grandmother's roof; comics. The heart of the story | heroic 1.0, red hoodie, **light-up sneakers** (blink while he runs) |\n| moe | **Maurice \"Lil Moe\" Dorsey**, 13 | Bike lookout | heroic 1.0, green cap, yellow tee, bike |\n| dink | **Darius \"Dink\" Pratt**, 16 | Money man | heroic 1.1, blue jersey |\n| tavon | **Tavon Gibbs**, 17 | Runner/tout | heroic 1.15, black puffy coat, red band |\n| pockets | **Wesley \"Pockets\" Gaines**, 47 | Informant and addict. Sells loosies and batteries from a baby stroller. Never looks at faces, knows everyone by their **shoes** | heroic 1.15, army jacket, old red cap, hunch .3, stroller shape |\n| odessa | **Miss Odessa Tillman**, 70 | Pigeon's grandmother, church usher, sits on her stoop; calls Dana \"Dana Lynn\" | heroic 1.1, gray hair, plum housedress, hunch .2 |\n| sunday | **Royal \"Sunday\" Odom**, 52 | Stick-up man with a code: never on Sunday, never a citizen, never a child. Drives an old **hearse** | heroic 1.25, flat cap, fishing vest |\n| dale | **Dale Kucharski**, 50s | Courier; drives the **Harstad Auto Parts** box truck | bulky 1.25, red company cap, work shirt |\n| harstad | **Glenn Harstad**, 57 | The connect (Dundalk). Montage teaser only | heroic 1.25, navy blazer |\n| felton | **Cornelius Felton**, 66 | Retired MTA bus driver who called in the corner. Murdered in the cold open (seen only under a sheet; a photo on his stoop memorial) | |\n| others | Officers Dukes and Kowalczyk (patrol), knockers, civilians, \"Dutch\" (a customer), Gloria Whitlock (phone only), State Senator Marian Ocheltree (montage) | | |\n\n### 8.3 Episode 1: EYES ON (~15 min)\nEpigraph: *\"Everybody on that corner is working. Question is, who's signing the checks.\"* (Lou Szabo)\n\n| # | Beat | Where | What happens / mechanics | Exit, flags |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1.1 | **Cold open** | field, 05:40, rain | Police tape at 1407 Gaither, two patrol cars with light bars (red/blue lights), Felton under a sheet on his stoop, candles and flowers. Dana walks in (move tutorial). Talk to Officer Dukes, then Lou (Homicide primary), then Miss Odessa across the street. She won't talk (\"I got a grandbaby to raise.\"), and the camera drifts up to Pigeon on her roof with his birds, watching. Optional: read the cards on the stoop | Lou: \"This ain't a whodunit, Dana. It's a who-cares.\" |\n| 1.2 | Card | | WIRETAP logo sting, then \"Episode 1: Eyes On\" and the epigraph | |\n| 1.3 | **Briefing** | Annex | Navarre assembles the detail (introductions in App. G). The Sun ran Felton's photo; the Deputy Commissioner wants \"six weeks, one corner, arrests\". Brass gauge appears. Stations: Board (empty: tutorial arrow), Evidence cage (take the camera: 30 shots; Fund $200), Coffee (Lou). Ops choice 1 | Car scene |\n| 1.4 | **Eyes on** | field, 15:00-17:30, overcast | **Required:** ★Face photos of Tee, Rook, Corey and Pigeon; read 2 roles; meet Pockets in the alley behind Gaither Market (pay $20, show photos, match shoes to names: App. G). **Optional:** an ★Act photo of a sale; Tee's call at P1 (16:10, then every 12 game minutes). Pockets also drops \"Dre broke his ankle jumping the fence at the old Arundel station\". It's needed in Ep3 and logged in the notebook. Tutorials as each first happens: Watch, Photo, Blend, Cover, Heat, Made, Eavesdrop | Back to the Chevy |\n| 1.5 | **Board** | Annex | Board tutorial: pin faces, assign roles, tie Tee to P1 if photographed. Pruitt calls Navarre (speaker): \"I've got a dead taxpayer on page one and a detail with no arrests.\" | Autosave |\n| 1.6 | **Interlude I1** | field, night, as Tee | §7.4 | flags |\n\n### 8.4 Episode 2: PAPER (~15 min)\nEpigraph: *\"A judge doesn't care what you know. He cares what you can write down.\"* (ASA Corinne Vance)\n\n| # | Beat | Where | What happens / mechanics | Exit, flags |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 2.1 | Card | | | |\n| 2.2 | Briefing | Annex | Vance explains what a wire needs (numbers, probable cause, necessity). Hal: \"They don't carry cell phones. Payphones and pagers.\" Ops choice 2 | Car scene |\n| 2.3 | **Payphones** | field, 11:00-13:00, day | Read the number plates on P1, P2 and P3 (interact; reading in a watcher's view counts as loitering). ★Act payphone photos (Tee at P1, Tavon at P2 on schedules). Then Navarre on the radio: the knockers are rolling on the corner to grab the stash kid with the pager. **Corey bolts → CHASE** (tutorial: sprint, vault, tackle, cuff), ditch and search | Corey in custody (+ package if found) |\n| 2.4 | **The box** | box | Corey (App. E): B1 who he works for (Tee), B2 the code hint (\"you turn it\"), B3 the stash (1412 vacant, behind the radiator). Flip offer | `coreyCI`, facts |\n| 2.5 | **Cipher** | Evidence cage | Decode Corey's pager memory (5 pages, App. C). Matches P1/P2/P3; 555-0174 stays unknown (later Harstad) | evidence |\n| 2.6 | **Affidavit** | Annex | Lines for P1, P2 and the pager clone (+P3 if supported). Necessity honesty | |\n| 2.7 | **Chambers** | chambers | Halloway, 3 questions (App. F). Signed: \"You're up. Thirty days. Minimize, Detective. I read the logs.\" Denied: an extra field beat (one more ★Act payphone photo), then resubmit | `wireUp` |\n| 2.8 | **Interlude I2** | Tee | Includes the payphone choice that shapes Ep3 | flags |\n\n### 8.5 Episode 3: UP (~18 min)\nEpigraph: *\"You don't listen to a phone. You listen to a man getting comfortable.\"* (Hal Pettiford)\n\n| # | Beat | Where | What happens / mechanics | Exit, flags |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 3.1 | Card | | | |\n| 3.2 | **We're up** | Annex | Hal's wire tutorial (minimize, spot-check, log, ID, pages, fast-forward) | |\n| 3.3 | **Session 1** | wire, 16:00-23:00 | Calls S1-1…S1-10 (App. D). The re-up riddle: \"the place where Dre messed up his ankle\" → pick the place on the notebook map (Arundel Gas). If Pockets' line was missed, Hal suggests finding Pockets (a 1-minute field beat at the bus stop) | `reupSpot` |\n| 3.4 | **The van** | field, 15:30-16:30, next day | Ren drives. Choose a spot (V1 Harlow curb, V2 Ridley east, V3 lot gap); van heat (§5.2); long lens (48 shots). Photograph the **Harstad box truck** (logo + plate), **Dale** (★Act re-up handoff with Tavon) and Pigeon circling on a bike. Then **Sunday's hearse**: he robs Tavon of the package at gunpoint, quick, no shots (act `robbery`, photographable). **Dilemma:** *Stay on the eye* (Sunday on the Board; violence follows) / *Call it in anonymously* (patrol rolls up, Sunday escapes, Heat +20) / *Go in yourself* (stand-off dialogue; Sunday leaves the package: \"I don't do police, Detective. Police do me.\" Van burned, Heat +30, Brass +10) | `dilemma` |\n| 3.5 | **The Major** | Annex | Pruitt in person. **Ops choice 3:** *Give him bodies* (sweep: Brass +25, Heat +20, P1 line goes dead) vs *Hold the line* (Brass −20). Board: THE PACKAGE tier (plate → Harstad Auto Parts; 555-0174 matches) | `sweep` |\n| 3.6 | **Session 2** | wire, 20:00-01:00 | Calls S2-1…S2-8. Rook asks for \"a hammer\" → **threat to life:** *Let it ride* vs *Wall-off stop* (a patrol car stops Rook's Monte Carlo for a broken taillight, finds the gun, arrests him: Brass +15, Heat +5; Rook in the box, 3 lines: \"Lawyer.\"). Lonnie: \"He wants to see you. Mama B's.\" → THE MONEY tier gets \"Boss ?\" and Mama B's. **Code flip** if Heat ≥ 50 | `wallOff`, `rookFree` |\n| 3.7 | **Interlude I3** | Tee | Easy's scene at Mama B's; who takes the loss | `lossOn` |\n\n### 8.6 Episode 4: DRY CLEANING (~15 min)\nEpigraph: *\"Smart ain't never being seen. Smart is being boring when they look.\"* (Terrence Mabry)\n\n| # | Beat | Where | What happens / mechanics | Exit, flags |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 4.1 | Card | | | |\n| 4.2 | Quiet lines | Annex | The payphones went dead: \"Throwaways.\" Hal explains burners: bought for cash, used a week, thrown in the harbor. Plan: tail Tee to the handout, get the packaging, subpoena the carrier. Ops choice 4. Gloria calls: \"Somebody was asking about you at the market.\" | Car scene |\n| 4.3 | **The tail** | field, 20:00, rain | Tee's dry-cleaning route (App. J `teeDry`) with Lou hand-offs (§5.5). Ends at the basketball court: Tee hands phones to the crew (read = observation `burners`) | checkpoint |\n| 4.4 | **Trash** | field, 21:30, rain | The alley behind Ridley Wireless (§5.7): find the bag with 12 phone boxes | `serials` |\n| 4.5 | **Kitchen** | Odessa's kitchen (box scene variant, warm light) | Pigeon at the table, Odessa at the stove (§6.4 kitchen) | `pigeonTrust` |\n| 4.6 | Numbers | Annex | The subpoena returns B1-B5. Halloway amends by phone (\"Same rules, Detective.\"). Pin burners to people | |\n| 4.7 | **Session 3** | wire, 6 calls (App. D) | The count is Thursdays at Mama B's after close; Friday's truck goes to \"the garage behind the Courts\". Tee mentions Dana's mother → choice: *call your mother* (`momSafe`: she goes to her sister's in the county) / *stay on the wire* | |\n| 4.8 | **Interlude I4** | Tee | The canary trap | `canary` |\n\n### 8.7 Episode 5: THE COUNT (~15-20 min)\nEpigraph: *\"Every week the money gets counted. Every week somebody comes up short.\"* (Darnell \"Easy\" Booker)\n\n| # | Beat | Where | What happens / mechanics |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 5.1 | Card | | |\n| 5.2 | **Two ways** | Annex | Pruitt, with Ostrowski on speakerphone: \"Friday. Dope on the table, cameras rolling.\" Navarre lays out both paths. **Ops choice 5:** **A, Dope on the table** (raid the garage, Friday 21:00) or **B, Follow the money** (Thursday's count at Mama B's). B needs Brass ≥ 30 and either (`coreyCI` and Corey not exposed) or `pigeonTrust` ≥ 70; otherwise its card says why it's locked |\n| 5.3A | **Raid** | field, Friday 21:00 | §5.8. If the canary trap exposed Corey, first a **60-second rescue:** Rook holds Corey in the 1412 vacant (sprint there; Rook flees from police; there's no fight). Late means Corey disappears |\n| 5.4A | **Press conference** | outside the garage | A table with dope, guns and cash. Pruitt and Ostrowski at the mic, camera flashes, the detail at the back. Ostrowski: \"a major blow to the drug trade in West Baltimore.\" Lou: \"Major blow. They'll be open by Monday.\" |\n| 5.3B | **The count** | field, Thursday 22:30 | Tail the count runner (Pigeon if he trusts Dana and tells her the route: easier; otherwise Tavon) to Mama B's back door. Lonnie's car circles (a moving headlight cone = an observer). Then the vacant roof and the long lens (§5.7): ★★★ Easy in the act |\n| 5.4B | **The morning after** | Annex | Navarre: the detail is disbanded anyway (\"The Deputy wanted a podium, not a case file.\"). Vance takes the file to a grand jury: \"Eighteen months, Detective. If you're lucky.\" |\n| 5.5 | **Interlude I5** | Tee | A: Central Booking; Easy's lawyer: \"Easy says your mother's rent is paid through spring.\" Take the weight / talk. B: dawn on the corner. Run / stay |\n| 5.6 | **Montage → credits** | | §8.8. Then the credits roll (names, plus \"Inspired by The Wire (2002-2008)\") → title. All episodes unlock in Episode select |\n\n**Shut Down** at any point (Brass 0) → the `shutdown` scene: Navarre packing boxes: \"Detail 9 is disbanded, effective Monday.\" Choose *Retry from the last autosave* or *See how it ends* (the Shut Down montage).\n\n### 8.8 Endings and montage\n- **Three paths:** A (raid), B (money) or Shut Down. Each montage is 9-11 cards, picked by rules over the flags (App. G).\n- **Fixed cards** (the game goes on):\n  - \"The corner at Gaither & Ridley: open for business by Monday.\"\n  - \"Maj. Leland Pruitt: promoted to Colonel.\"\n  - \"Hal Pettiford: kept the wire room. Nobody told him to leave.\"\n- **Variable cards:**\n  - Tee: by I5 choice and Case band\n  - Easy: by path\n  - Pigeon (3 fates): by `lossOn`, `pigeonTrust`, Path B runner and `rookFree`\n  - Corey (3 fates): `coreyCI`, `canary`, rescue\n  - Rook: `wallOff`, `rookDrew`\n  - Sunday: `dilemma`\n  - Dana: by path\n  - Lou, Ren, Navarre\n- **The teaser** always runs last: \"Glenn Harstad: guest of honor at State Senator Marian Ocheltree's harbor fundraiser.\" Then **TO BE CONTINUED**.\n- **How a card is shown:** a live vignette (camera on a POI, characters posed, letterboxed 2.35:1), caption at the bottom, 6 s each, crossfade, the `montage` song (App. H).\n\n### 8.9 Episode select and saves\n- **Saves:** `game.saves` slots (3 + autosave). Autosave at every beat start.\n- **Title menu:** CONTINUE (latest), NEW CASE, EPISODES (unlocked), THE GAME, SETTINGS, ABOUT & CREDITS.\n- **Episode select** starts an episode from a **canonical state** (STATE presets in data):\n  - Ep2: 4 faces with names; Heat 20, Brass 55.\n  - Ep3: wire up on P1, P2 and the pager clone; `coreyCI` false; Brass 50.\n  - Ep4: dilemma \"stay\", sweep false, `wallOff` true, Heat 45.\n  - Ep5: burners known, `pigeonTrust` 75, Brass 45.\n- **Restarting:** the pause menu offers *Restart this part* (the beat's autosave) and *Episode select*.\n\n---\n\n## 9. Versus mode and online play: THE GAME (50-versus.js, 51-net.js)\n\n### 9.1 The round\n- **Sides:** *The Corner* (crew) vs *The Detail* (police) on the **versus zone** of the same map (cells 18-50 × 16-44: Ridley between Abbott and Harlow, Gaither, the two alleys, the Courts lane). Barricades and police tape block the zone's edge (blocked floor cells, sawhorse shapes). AI civilians walk through; detectives look like civilians.\n- **Length:** 5:00 (local setup: 3, 5 or 8 min).\n- **Outcome:**\n  - **Detail win:** Evidence reaches **100** (immediate).\n  - **Corner win:** at time-up, Count ≥ **$3,000** and Evidence < 100.\n  - **Draw:** neither (\"The game goes on\").\n- **Seats:** side of seat *i* = `(i + round) % 2 === 0 ? 'corner' : 'detail'`, so players alternate sides between rounds. With 1 player: Detail vs bot Corner. With 3: two on one side.\n  - Corner players take the **Lieutenant** first, then the **Runner**. Detail players are **Detectives** (up to 2).\n  - Bots fill every empty crew role (always) and empty detective slots (to at least 1 detective).\n\n| Corner actions | Detail actions |\n|---|---|\n| **Lieutenant:** watch people (L2/RMB); **call out** a person (△/Q while watching). A detective → **burned** 25 s (their photos score 0, they're outlined red for the Corner, and AI lookouts track them). A civilian → −$200 and customers avoid the corner for 10 s; cooldown 15 s. **Shut it down / open up** (□/F). Move the stash (✕ at the stash, pick a spot). **Re-up** at a payphone (✕, 2 s) when the stash < 20 → a car drops the package in 20 s, which the Runner must fetch | **Photos** (L2 + R2 / RMB + LMB): first ★Face of each crew member +4; ★Act +12 (max 2 per crew member). Photo of the **stash** in use +25 (+15 again after it moves). **Tap a payphone** (✕, 4 s, unseen) → each Corner re-up call from it +10. **Jump-out** (△/Q while watching, once per round): patrol frisks the target 8 s later. Carrying → seizure +20 and the Corner loses what was carried; clean → −10 |\n| **Runner:** pick up product at the stash (✕), hand off to a waiting customer (✕), ditch (○) if a cop closes in (lost product) | **Blend** (□/F) and cover activities work as in story. AI lookouts build suspicion on detectives (§5.2); full = auto-burn |\n\n- **Bots:**\n  - **Corner bot:** the CornerSim role brains, plus a lieutenant brain. It shuts down when any lookout reaches `search`. It calls out the person with the highest *observed* suspicion score once that passes 0.8 (from behaviors it can see: lingering, camera raises, following the runner). It re-ups at the payphone it hasn't seen tampered with. It moves the stash after a stash photo it noticed.\n  - **Detective bot:** picks vantage points (data list of 12), photographs the next sale it sees, moves when its heat passes 0.5, sometimes tails the runner, and taps a payphone when no crew is within 120 units.\n  - Bots may cheat a little on perception (they read exact act windows). They're for filling seats, not balance.\n- **Personal score:** Detail = the evidence they earned. Corner = the count they handled ÷ 10 + correct call-outs × 20.\n- **Results screen:** outcome, then per player: photos, burns, call-outs, count. Awards (*Eyes On*: most ★Act; *Made You*: first correct call-out; *Clean Hands*: Corner player never seized; *Paper Trail*: most tap points).\n\n### 9.2 Local play (\"on its own\")\n- **Setup screen** (DOM): P1 side, *P2: press ✕ on a second controller or Enter on the keyboard's right half* (`game.allowJoin({ max: 2 })`), round length, Start.\n- **1 human:** vs bots.\n- **2 humans:** split screen with `game.splitScreen(2, { follow: [c1, c2], layout: 'auto' })`. Each viewport draws its own HUD on the canvas inside `r.viewport` (E.Shell's HUD is single-screen, so versus uses a canvas HUD). Then `scene.hud(r)` draws the timer and the shared Count/Evidence bar at the top.\n- **Caveat:** hidden identity can be peeked at on one screen. Accept it locally; online it's truly hidden.\n- **Same code path:** local play runs the same `VersusSim` through `LocalTransport` (this copy is the host; all players are local).\n\n### 9.3 AI Hub: shared-world (AI Hub Session Protocol v1, client 1.4.0)\n**Tags** (in `<head>`, after the client script):\n```html\n<meta name=\"hub:session\" content=\"1\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-players\" content=\"1-4\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-mode\" content=\"shared-world\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-minutes\" content=\"6\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-goal\" content=\"Cops: build a 100-point case. Corner: make $3,000 unseen.\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-howto\" content=\"Move: stick/WASD · Watch: L2/RMB · Photo: R2/LMB · Act: ✕/E · Call out: △/Q\">\n```\n**Flow** (99-start.js):\n```js\nif (window.AIHub && AIHub.active) {                      // straight into the round: no title, attract or menus\n  game.start({ scenes, scene: 'hubWait', boot });        // 'Connecting…' (no prompts)\n  const info = await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'shared-world', seats: [1, 4] });   // the hub's own card (no card: true)\n  if (!info) game.go('title');                           // no hub after all: the normal game\n  else { await Versus.buildRound(info); AIHub.ready(); } // roster from AIHub.rng('roster'); sides from seats + info.round\n}\nAIHub.on('start', () => Versus.countdown());             // overlay: role card + 3-2-1 until AIHub.time() >= 0\n```\n- **Host authority** (`info.isHost`): the host copy runs `VersusSim`: NPCs, crew AI, bots, rules, scoring, the timer (from `AIHub.time()`).\n- **Every copy moves its own character locally** (no input lag) and reports it. The host trusts positions inside a speed check.\n- **Other copies render snapshots** with 150 ms interpolation.\n- **Messages:**\n  - Host → all, unreliable, 10 Hz: `{t:'s', at, tl, ev, cn, ph, p:[[id,x,y,f,st,fl],…], n:[[nid,x,y,f,st],…]}`.\n    - x, y are integers (world units); f is facing quantized 0-63; st is an animation code (0 idle, 1 walk, 2 run, 3 crouch, 4 watch, 5 act, 6 down, 7 sit, 8 phone, 9 bike); fl is flags (burned, carrying, shut).\n    - **Keep each message under 1,100 bytes.** If the NPC list makes it bigger, send NPCs in two alternating halves (5 Hz each).\n  - Host → all, reliable, on events: `{t:'e', k:'photo'|'burn'|'callout'|'tap'|'jump'|'seize'|'stash'|'reup'|'shut'|'open'|'sale', …}` (sounds, toasts, particles).\n  - Client → host, unreliable, 10 Hz: `{t:'me', at, x, y, f, st, w, ax, ay}` (w = watching; ax, ay = the aimed world point).\n  - Client → host, reliable: `{t:'act', k:'photo', target, q, at}` · `{k:'callout', target}` · `{k:'tap', phone}` · `{k:'jump', target}` · `{k:'shut'|'open'|'stash'|'reup'|'pickup'|'handoff'|'ditch', …}`.\n  - Budget: host 10 snapshots + under 5 events per second (< 20/s); clients 10 + a few.\n- **Validation on the host:**\n  - Positions are clamped to `maxSpeed × elapsed × 1.5` and to walkable cells.\n  - A photo claim needs: the target exists, is within 240 units of the claimer, and `map.sight` is clear on the host. If ★Act is claimed, the host's 1-second act history must show an act within 600 ms.\n  - Call-outs are checked against the true identity.\n- **Events:**\n  - `leave` → that player's character becomes a bot on the same side; the round goes on.\n  - The host leaving voids the round (the hub sends `end` `host-left`) → show \"Round cancelled\".\n  - `time-up` → the host finishes at once with the timer-end outcome.\n  - `end` → stop input (controllers to null), stop music and effects, show our results under the hub's. After `end`, send nothing.\n- **Server** (`AIHub.server`): the host has no local player. It runs the sim and shows a spectator camera (`cam.frame` over all players). No audio, no input.\n- **Finish** (host only, once):\n  - `standings`: winners `[[winning side ids],[losing side ids]]`; draw `[[all ids]]`. Only hub player ids, never bots.\n  - `scores`: personal scores.\n  - `stats`: `{id:{Photos, Burns, Count}}`.\n  - `awards`.\n- **Session rules:**\n  - No other network use.\n  - No `alert`/`confirm`/`prompt`, no new windows.\n  - Pause doesn't stop the host: the versus scene is `pausable: false` in a session. Options opens a non-pausing overlay with Settings/Controls (`game.menu('settings')`) while the character's input is suppressed.\n  - `menu.quit: false` and no restart items.\n  - While Create (Pad8) is held, ignore Options.\n- **Randomness:** the host never uses `Math.random` for the sim. Shared rolls come from `AIHub.rng(label)`, and the roster from `AIHub.rng('roster')`, so every copy builds identical NPC rigs.\n\n---\n\n## 10. Attract mode (52-attract.js)\n- **Trigger:** 10 s with no input (keys, mouse buttons, mouse moves over 6 px, wheel, touches, gamepad buttons, or axes past 0.3) on **title, main menu, episode select or versus setup**. Settings, About and Controls don't count (a player may be reading).\n- **Exit:** any input → back to the title, and the idle timer resets. On touch-only devices, a tap → the notice panel.\n- **The reel:** a looping playlist of vignettes, each a real system running with bot controllers. Bots may cheat: no suspicion, unlimited film, teleports, scripted perfect actions.\n  - **Overlay:** letterbox bars, a **DEMO** badge, a small WIRETAP logo, a caption, and a blinking \"Press any button\" built from the current device's glyph.\n\n| # | s | Vignette | Bot does |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | 12 | **THE CORNER**: night, rain, CornerSim full; the camera turns 90° twice | Nothing: customers, touts, lookouts |\n| 2 | 10 | **EYES ON**: Dana on the bus-stop bench | Enter Watch, aim at the next sale, snap ★★★, polaroid slides in |\n| 3 | 10 | **THE TAIL**: Tee's route | Dana tails; Tee looks back; Dana takes cover in a doorway; hand-off to Lou |\n| 4 | 9 | **THE CHASE**: Corey bolts | Sprint, vault the court fence, tackle, cuff |\n| 5 | 10 | **THE WIRE**: wire room | Grandma call → MINIMIZE; pertinent call → LOG; a page decodes with a keypad turn |\n| 6 | 7 | **THE BOARD**: corkboard | Cards fly onto slots; red string ties Tee to P1 |\n| 7 | 8 | **THE BOX**: Corey | Lean → Offer a way out → beat unlocked |\n| 8 | 10 | **THE GAME**: versus, split screen, bots | A call-out burns a detective; a stash photo |\n| 9 | 8 | **THE COUNT**: Tee's tally | Bills flick, the total ticks up, then the title card |\n\n- **Implementation:** each entry is `{ id, seconds, setup(), tick(dt), caption }`. `setup()` loads a mission/scene with `attract: true`: no saves, no tutorials, no autosave, quieter music, no HUD prompts. The attract scene owns the clock and calls `game.go` for the next entry with a short dissolve.\n\nEOF\nwc -c /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-105319/work/PLAN.md","description":"Append story, versus/online and attract sections to PLAN.md"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01S713NtZqJ9LH7Zm9q7x7vV","type":"tool_result","content":"91594 /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-105319/work/PLAN.md\n[This command modified 1 file you've previously read: PLAN.md. Call Read before editing.]","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e2aa65a8-ee1a-45c4-b8e6-f96cf188e23d","uuid":"4ab995fe-ab0a-4397-b6d6-f631c240bcad","timestamp":"2026-11-03T18:37:14.887Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"91594 /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-105319/work/PLAN.md","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"staleReadFileStateHint":"[This command modified 1 file you've previously read: PLAN.md. Call Read before editing.]","bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-105319/work/PLAN.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":647,"oldLines":3,"newStart":647,"newLines":252,"lines":[" "," Intel barks (eavesdrop) carry facts: \"Re-up at four, the old gas station.\" / \"Pigeon, get your little ass back on that roof.\""," ","+---","+","+## 8. Story mode: The Case","+","+### 8.1 Setting","+- **Place and time:** **Penn Row**, a fictional neighborhood in West Baltimore, **October 2004**. Pagers, payphones and the first throwaway cell phones. Use the real city, invent the streets and places:","+  - **Ridley Avenue** (the main drag), **Gaither Street** (the corner at Gaither & Ridley), **Dunmore**, **Abbott** and **Harlow** Streets.","+  - Shops: **Gaither Market** (corner store), **Suds City** (laundromat), **Ridley Wireless & Pager** (sells the burners), **Mama B's Soul Food** (Easy's front), **Ridley Check Cashing**, **Fades & Grades** (barbershop), **Abbott Liquors**, **Ridley Carryout**.","+  - Also: **Greater Hope Baptist Church**, **the Delancey Courts** (low-rise projects), **Arundel Gas** (closed station), **the garage behind the Courts**.","+- **The crew's product:** **Overtime** (orange-top vials). A rival brand, **Hurricane**, is only talked about.","+- **The detail:** officially \"Special Detail 9\", which everyone calls *the detail*. Its office is **the Annex**, above the city impound lot.","+- **Real things stay generic:** \"Central Booking\", \"the courthouse\", \"the Western District\". All phone numbers use the fictional `555-01xx` block.","+","+### 8.2 Cast (all original; App. I has voices, §12.4 has colors)","+| id | Name | Who | Look (Humanoid options) |","+|---|---|---|---|","+| dana | **Det. Dana Whitlock**, 34 | Player. Western District narcotics, grew up three blocks off Ridley; her mother Gloria still lives there. Patient, watchful, dry; takes it personally | heroic 1.25, hair short, coat (brown leather), cream sweater, jeans |","+| lou | **Det. Louis \"Lou\" Szabo**, 52 | Partner. Exiled from Homicide for embarrassing a deputy commissioner. Smokes, Orioles, his father's sayings; very good in the box | heroic 1.25, bald, tan trench, hunch .15 |","+| hal | **Det. Harold \"Hal\" Pettiford**, 61 | Thirteen years in the pawn unit, Army Signal Corps. Fixes tube radios at his desk; runs the wire room with infinite patience | heroic 1.2, gray hair, brown cardigan, hunch .2 |","+| ren | **Officer Renata \"Ren\" Ocasio**, 26 | On loan from Southwest patrol. Digital camera, laptop, drives the van; talks fast | heroic 1.15, ponytail, navy hoodie |","+| navarre | **Lt. Gilbert \"Gil\" Navarre**, 45 | Runs the detail. Careful careerist with a conscience; an old rumor follows him | heroic 1.25, shirt and burgundy tie |","+| pruitt | **Maj. Leland Pruitt**, 55 | District commander. Lives for the stat sheet | bulky 1.3, navy uniform coat, gold trim, cap |","+| ostrowski | **Deputy Commissioner Raymond Ostrowski** | The politics (speakerphone, press conference) | bulky 1.3, dark suit |","+| vance | **ASA Corinne Vance**, 38 | Prosecutor who shepherds the affidavit; sharp, impatient | heroic 1.2, long hair pulled back, charcoal suit |","+| halloway | **Judge Abner Halloway**, 68 | Signs or refuses the wire. Crosswords, bow tie, reads every log | heroic 1.2, white hair, black robe, hunch .25 |","+| easy | **Darnell \"Easy\" Booker**, 39 | The boss. Never on the corner, never on a phone. Owns Mama B's and the check-cashing store. Soft-spoken, frightening | heroic 1.3, black leather coat |","+| lonnie | **Lonnie Fitch**, 45 | Easy's driver and voice on the phone | bulky 1.25, gray cap |","+| tee | **Terrence \"Tee\" Mabry**, 24 | Lieutenant; the second playable character. Reads business books; the counter-surveillance brain | heroic 1.25, black fitted cap, white tee, jeans, **wheat Timberlands** |","+| rook | **Ricky \"Rook\" Batts**, 27 | Muscle; volatile | bulky 1.35, black do-rag, black hoodie, **black Air Force 1s, red swoosh** |","+| corey | **Corey \"Stash\" Lyle**, 19 | Stash keeper; nervous, stammers; flip candidate | heroic 1.15, gray hood up, **duct-taped Nikes**, hunch .25 |","+| pigeon | **Junior \"Pigeon\" Hollis**, 14 | Roof lookout; keeps pigeons on his grandmother's roof; comics. The heart of the story | heroic 1.0, red hoodie, **light-up sneakers** (blink while he runs) |","+| moe | **Maurice \"Lil Moe\" Dorsey**, 13 | Bike lookout | heroic 1.0, green cap, yellow tee, bike |","+| dink | **Darius \"Dink\" Pratt**, 16 | Money man | heroic 1.1, blue jersey |","+| tavon | **Tavon Gibbs**, 17 | Runner/tout | heroic 1.15, black puffy coat, red band |","+| pockets | **Wesley \"Pockets\" Gaines**, 47 | Informant and addict. Sells loosies and batteries from a baby stroller. Never looks at faces, knows everyone by their **shoes** | heroic 1.15, army jacket, old red cap, hunch .3, stroller shape |","+| odessa | **Miss Odessa Tillman**, 70 | Pigeon's grandmother, church usher, sits on her stoop; calls Dana \"Dana Lynn\" | heroic 1.1, gray hair, plum housedress, hunch .2 |","+| sunday | **Royal \"Sunday\" Odom**, 52 | Stick-up man with a code: never on Sunday, never a citizen, never a child. Drives an old **hearse** | heroic 1.25, flat cap, fishing vest |","+| dale | **Dale Kucharski**, 50s | Courier; drives the **Harstad Auto Parts** box truck | bulky 1.25, red company cap, work shirt |","+| harstad | **Glenn Harstad**, 57 | The connect (Dundalk). Montage teaser only | heroic 1.25, navy blazer |","+| felton | **Cornelius Felton**, 66 | Retired MTA bus driver who called in the corner. Murdered in the cold open (seen only under a sheet; a photo on his stoop memorial) | |","+| others | Officers Dukes and Kowalczyk (patrol), knockers, civilians, \"Dutch\" (a customer), Gloria Whitlock (phone only), State Senator Marian Ocheltree (montage) | | |","+","+### 8.3 Episode 1: EYES ON (~15 min)","+Epigraph: *\"Everybody on that corner is working. Question is, who's signing the checks.\"* (Lou Szabo)","+","+| # | Beat | Where | What happens / mechanics | Exit, flags |","+|---|---|---|---|---|","+| 1.1 | **Cold open** | field, 05:40, rain | Police tape at 1407 Gaither, two patrol cars with light bars (red/blue lights), Felton under a sheet on his stoop, candles and flowers. Dana walks in (move tutorial). Talk to Officer Dukes, then Lou (Homicide primary), then Miss Odessa across the street. She won't talk (\"I got a grandbaby to raise.\"), and the camera drifts up to Pigeon on her roof with his birds, watching. Optional: read the cards on the stoop | Lou: \"This ain't a whodunit, Dana. It's a who-cares.\" |","+| 1.2 | Card | | WIRETAP logo sting, then \"Episode 1: Eyes On\" and the epigraph | |","+| 1.3 | **Briefing** | Annex | Navarre assembles the detail (introductions in App. G). The Sun ran Felton's photo; the Deputy Commissioner wants \"six weeks, one corner, arrests\". Brass gauge appears. Stations: Board (empty: tutorial arrow), Evidence cage (take the camera: 30 shots; Fund $200), Coffee (Lou). Ops choice 1 | Car scene |","+| 1.4 | **Eyes on** | field, 15:00-17:30, overcast | **Required:** ★Face photos of Tee, Rook, Corey and Pigeon; read 2 roles; meet Pockets in the alley behind Gaither Market (pay $20, show photos, match shoes to names: App. G). **Optional:** an ★Act photo of a sale; Tee's call at P1 (16:10, then every 12 game minutes). Pockets also drops \"Dre broke his ankle jumping the fence at the old Arundel station\". It's needed in Ep3 and logged in the notebook. Tutorials as each first happens: Watch, Photo, Blend, Cover, Heat, Made, Eavesdrop | Back to the Chevy |","+| 1.5 | **Board** | Annex | Board tutorial: pin faces, assign roles, tie Tee to P1 if photographed. Pruitt calls Navarre (speaker): \"I've got a dead taxpayer on page one and a detail with no arrests.\" | Autosave |","+| 1.6 | **Interlude I1** | field, night, as Tee | §7.4 | flags |","+","+### 8.4 Episode 2: PAPER (~15 min)","+Epigraph: *\"A judge doesn't care what you know. He cares what you can write down.\"* (ASA Corinne Vance)","+","+| # | Beat | Where | What happens / mechanics | Exit, flags |","+|---|---|---|---|---|","+| 2.1 | Card | | | |","+| 2.2 | Briefing | Annex | Vance explains what a wire needs (numbers, probable cause, necessity). Hal: \"They don't carry cell phones. Payphones and pagers.\" Ops choice 2 | Car scene |","+| 2.3 | **Payphones** | field, 11:00-13:00, day | Read the number plates on P1, P2 and P3 (interact; reading in a watcher's view counts as loitering). ★Act payphone photos (Tee at P1, Tavon at P2 on schedules). Then Navarre on the radio: the knockers are rolling on the corner to grab the stash kid with the pager. **Corey bolts → CHASE** (tutorial: sprint, vault, tackle, cuff), ditch and search | Corey in custody (+ package if found) |","+| 2.4 | **The box** | box | Corey (App. E): B1 who he works for (Tee), B2 the code hint (\"you turn it\"), B3 the stash (1412 vacant, behind the radiator). Flip offer | `coreyCI`, facts |","+| 2.5 | **Cipher** | Evidence cage | Decode Corey's pager memory (5 pages, App. C). Matches P1/P2/P3; 555-0174 stays unknown (later Harstad) | evidence |","+| 2.6 | **Affidavit** | Annex | Lines for P1, P2 and the pager clone (+P3 if supported). Necessity honesty | |","+| 2.7 | **Chambers** | chambers | Halloway, 3 questions (App. F). Signed: \"You're up. Thirty days. Minimize, Detective. I read the logs.\" Denied: an extra field beat (one more ★Act payphone photo), then resubmit | `wireUp` |","+| 2.8 | **Interlude I2** | Tee | Includes the payphone choice that shapes Ep3 | flags |","+","+### 8.5 Episode 3: UP (~18 min)","+Epigraph: *\"You don't listen to a phone. You listen to a man getting comfortable.\"* (Hal Pettiford)","+","+| # | Beat | Where | What happens / mechanics | Exit, flags |","+|---|---|---|---|---|","+| 3.1 | Card | | | |","+| 3.2 | **We're up** | Annex | Hal's wire tutorial (minimize, spot-check, log, ID, pages, fast-forward) | |","+| 3.3 | **Session 1** | wire, 16:00-23:00 | Calls S1-1…S1-10 (App. D). The re-up riddle: \"the place where Dre messed up his ankle\" → pick the place on the notebook map (Arundel Gas). If Pockets' line was missed, Hal suggests finding Pockets (a 1-minute field beat at the bus stop) | `reupSpot` |","+| 3.4 | **The van** | field, 15:30-16:30, next day | Ren drives. Choose a spot (V1 Harlow curb, V2 Ridley east, V3 lot gap); van heat (§5.2); long lens (48 shots). Photograph the **Harstad box truck** (logo + plate), **Dale** (★Act re-up handoff with Tavon) and Pigeon circling on a bike. Then **Sunday's hearse**: he robs Tavon of the package at gunpoint, quick, no shots (act `robbery`, photographable). **Dilemma:** *Stay on the eye* (Sunday on the Board; violence follows) / *Call it in anonymously* (patrol rolls up, Sunday escapes, Heat +20) / *Go in yourself* (stand-off dialogue; Sunday leaves the package: \"I don't do police, Detective. Police do me.\" Van burned, Heat +30, Brass +10) | `dilemma` |","+| 3.5 | **The Major** | Annex | Pruitt in person. **Ops choice 3:** *Give him bodies* (sweep: Brass +25, Heat +20, P1 line goes dead) vs *Hold the line* (Brass −20). Board: THE PACKAGE tier (plate → Harstad Auto Parts; 555-0174 matches) | `sweep` |","+| 3.6 | **Session 2** | wire, 20:00-01:00 | Calls S2-1…S2-8. Rook asks for \"a hammer\" → **threat to life:** *Let it ride* vs *Wall-off stop* (a patrol car stops Rook's Monte Carlo for a broken taillight, finds the gun, arrests him: Brass +15, Heat +5; Rook in the box, 3 lines: \"Lawyer.\"). Lonnie: \"He wants to see you. Mama B's.\" → THE MONEY tier gets \"Boss ?\" and Mama B's. **Code flip** if Heat ≥ 50 | `wallOff`, `rookFree` |","+| 3.7 | **Interlude I3** | Tee | Easy's scene at Mama B's; who takes the loss | `lossOn` |","+","+### 8.6 Episode 4: DRY CLEANING (~15 min)","+Epigraph: *\"Smart ain't never being seen. Smart is being boring when they look.\"* (Terrence Mabry)","+","+| # | Beat | Where | What happens / mechanics | Exit, flags |","+|---|---|---|---|---|","+| 4.1 | Card | | | |","+| 4.2 | Quiet lines | Annex | The payphones went dead: \"Throwaways.\" Hal explains burners: bought for cash, used a week, thrown in the harbor. Plan: tail Tee to the handout, get the packaging, subpoena the carrier. Ops choice 4. Gloria calls: \"Somebody was asking about you at the market.\" | Car scene |","+| 4.3 | **The tail** | field, 20:00, rain | Tee's dry-cleaning route (App. J `teeDry`) with Lou hand-offs (§5.5). Ends at the basketball court: Tee hands phones to the crew (read = observation `burners`) | checkpoint |","+| 4.4 | **Trash** | field, 21:30, rain | The alley behind Ridley Wireless (§5.7): find the bag with 12 phone boxes | `serials` |","+| 4.5 | **Kitchen** | Odessa's kitchen (box scene variant, warm light) | Pigeon at the table, Odessa at the stove (§6.4 kitchen) | `pigeonTrust` |","+| 4.6 | Numbers | Annex | The subpoena returns B1-B5. Halloway amends by phone (\"Same rules, Detective.\"). Pin burners to people | |","+| 4.7 | **Session 3** | wire, 6 calls (App. D) | The count is Thursdays at Mama B's after close; Friday's truck goes to \"the garage behind the Courts\". Tee mentions Dana's mother → choice: *call your mother* (`momSafe`: she goes to her sister's in the county) / *stay on the wire* | |","+| 4.8 | **Interlude I4** | Tee | The canary trap | `canary` |","+","+### 8.7 Episode 5: THE COUNT (~15-20 min)","+Epigraph: *\"Every week the money gets counted. Every week somebody comes up short.\"* (Darnell \"Easy\" Booker)","+","+| # | Beat | Where | What happens / mechanics |","+|---|---|---|---|","+| 5.1 | Card | | |","+| 5.2 | **Two ways** | Annex | Pruitt, with Ostrowski on speakerphone: \"Friday. Dope on the table, cameras rolling.\" Navarre lays out both paths. **Ops choice 5:** **A, Dope on the table** (raid the garage, Friday 21:00) or **B, Follow the money** (Thursday's count at Mama B's). B needs Brass ≥ 30 and either (`coreyCI` and Corey not exposed) or `pigeonTrust` ≥ 70; otherwise its card says why it's locked |","+| 5.3A | **Raid** | field, Friday 21:00 | §5.8. If the canary trap exposed Corey, first a **60-second rescue:** Rook holds Corey in the 1412 vacant (sprint there; Rook flees from police; there's no fight). Late means Corey disappears |","+| 5.4A | **Press conference** | outside the garage | A table with dope, guns and cash. Pruitt and Ostrowski at the mic, camera flashes, the detail at the back. Ostrowski: \"a major blow to the drug trade in West Baltimore.\" Lou: \"Major blow. They'll be open by Monday.\" |","+| 5.3B | **The count** | field, Thursday 22:30 | Tail the count runner (Pigeon if he trusts Dana and tells her the route: easier; otherwise Tavon) to Mama B's back door. Lonnie's car circles (a moving headlight cone = an observer). Then the vacant roof and the long lens (§5.7): ★★★ Easy in the act |","+| 5.4B | **The morning after** | Annex | Navarre: the detail is disbanded anyway (\"The Deputy wanted a podium, not a case file.\"). Vance takes the file to a grand jury: \"Eighteen months, Detective. If you're lucky.\" |","+| 5.5 | **Interlude I5** | Tee | A: Central Booking; Easy's lawyer: \"Easy says your mother's rent is paid through spring.\" Take the weight / talk. B: dawn on the corner. Run / stay |","+| 5.6 | **Montage → credits** | | §8.8. Then the credits roll (names, plus \"Inspired by The Wire (2002-2008)\") → title. All episodes unlock in Episode select |","+","+**Shut Down** at any point (Brass 0) → the `shutdown` scene: Navarre packing boxes: \"Detail 9 is disbanded, effective Monday.\" Choose *Retry from the last autosave* or *See how it ends* (the Shut Down montage).","+","+### 8.8 Endings and montage","+- **Three paths:** A (raid), B (money) or Shut Down. Each montage is 9-11 cards, picked by rules over the flags (App. G).","+- **Fixed cards** (the game goes on):","+  - \"The corner at Gaither & Ridley: open for business by Monday.\"","+  - \"Maj. Leland Pruitt: promoted to Colonel.\"","+  - \"Hal Pettiford: kept the wire room. Nobody told him to leave.\"","+- **Variable cards:**","+  - Tee: by I5 choice and Case band","+  - Easy: by path","+  - Pigeon (3 fates): by `lossOn`, `pigeonTrust`, Path B runner and `rookFree`","+  - Corey (3 fates): `coreyCI`, `canary`, rescue","+  - Rook: `wallOff`, `rookDrew`","+  - Sunday: `dilemma`","+  - Dana: by path","+  - Lou, Ren, Navarre","+- **The teaser** always runs last: \"Glenn Harstad: guest of honor at State Senator Marian Ocheltree's harbor fundraiser.\" Then **TO BE CONTINUED**.","+- **How a card is shown:** a live vignette (camera on a POI, characters posed, letterboxed 2.35:1), caption at the bottom, 6 s each, crossfade, the `montage` song (App. H).","+","+### 8.9 Episode select and saves","+- **Saves:** `game.saves` slots (3 + autosave). Autosave at every beat start.","+- **Title menu:** CONTINUE (latest), NEW CASE, EPISODES (unlocked), THE GAME, SETTINGS, ABOUT & CREDITS.","+- **Episode select** starts an episode from a **canonical state** (STATE presets in data):","+  - Ep2: 4 faces with names; Heat 20, Brass 55.","+  - Ep3: wire up on P1, P2 and the pager clone; `coreyCI` false; Brass 50.","+  - Ep4: dilemma \"stay\", sweep false, `wallOff` true, Heat 45.","+  - Ep5: burners known, `pigeonTrust` 75, Brass 45.","+- **Restarting:** the pause menu offers *Restart this part* (the beat's autosave) and *Episode select*.","+","+---","+","+## 9. Versus mode and online play: THE GAME (50-versus.js, 51-net.js)","+","+### 9.1 The round","+- **Sides:** *The Corner* (crew) vs *The Detail* (police) on the **versus zone** of the same map (cells 18-50 × 16-44: Ridley between Abbott and Harlow, Gaither, the two alleys, the Courts lane). Barricades and police tape block the zone's edge (blocked floor cells, sawhorse shapes). AI civilians walk through; detectives look like civilians.","+- **Length:** 5:00 (local setup: 3, 5 or 8 min).","+- **Outcome:**","+  - **Detail win:** Evidence reaches **100** (immediate).","+  - **Corner win:** at time-up, Count ≥ **$3,000** and Evidence < 100.","+  - **Draw:** neither (\"The game goes on\").","+- **Seats:** side of seat *i* = `(i + round) % 2 === 0 ? 'corner' : 'detail'`, so players alternate sides between rounds. With 1 player: Detail vs bot Corner. With 3: two on one side.","+  - Corner players take the **Lieutenant** first, then the **Runner**. Detail players are **Detectives** (up to 2).","+  - Bots fill every empty crew role (always) and empty detective slots (to at least 1 detective).","+","+| Corner actions | Detail actions |","+|---|---|","+| **Lieutenant:** watch people (L2/RMB); **call out** a person (△/Q while watching). A detective → **burned** 25 s (their photos score 0, they're outlined red for the Corner, and AI lookouts track them). A civilian → −$200 and customers avoid the corner for 10 s; cooldown 15 s. **Shut it down / open up** (□/F). Move the stash (✕ at the stash, pick a spot). **Re-up** at a payphone (✕, 2 s) when the stash < 20 → a car drops the package in 20 s, which the Runner must fetch | **Photos** (L2 + R2 / RMB + LMB): first ★Face of each crew member +4; ★Act +12 (max 2 per crew member). Photo of the **stash** in use +25 (+15 again after it moves). **Tap a payphone** (✕, 4 s, unseen) → each Corner re-up call from it +10. **Jump-out** (△/Q while watching, once per round): patrol frisks the target 8 s later. Carrying → seizure +20 and the Corner loses what was carried; clean → −10 |","+| **Runner:** pick up product at the stash (✕), hand off to a waiting customer (✕), ditch (○) if a cop closes in (lost product) | **Blend** (□/F) and cover activities work as in story. AI lookouts build suspicion on detectives (§5.2); full = auto-burn |","+","+- **Bots:**","+  - **Corner bot:** the CornerSim role brains, plus a lieutenant brain. It shuts down when any lookout reaches `search`. It calls out the person with the highest *observed* suspicion score once that passes 0.8 (from behaviors it can see: lingering, camera raises, following the runner). It re-ups at the payphone it hasn't seen tampered with. It moves the stash after a stash photo it noticed.","+  - **Detective bot:** picks vantage points (data list of 12), photographs the next sale it sees, moves when its heat passes 0.5, sometimes tails the runner, and taps a payphone when no crew is within 120 units.","+  - Bots may cheat a little on perception (they read exact act windows). They're for filling seats, not balance.","+- **Personal score:** Detail = the evidence they earned. Corner = the count they handled ÷ 10 + correct call-outs × 20.","+- **Results screen:** outcome, then per player: photos, burns, call-outs, count. Awards (*Eyes On*: most ★Act; *Made You*: first correct call-out; *Clean Hands*: Corner player never seized; *Paper Trail*: most tap points).","+","+### 9.2 Local play (\"on its own\")","+- **Setup screen** (DOM): P1 side, *P2: press ✕ on a second controller or Enter on the keyboard's right half* (`game.allowJoin({ max: 2 })`), round length, Start.","+- **1 human:** vs bots.","+- **2 humans:** split screen with `game.splitScreen(2, { follow: [c1, c2], layout: 'auto' })`. Each viewport draws its own HUD on the canvas inside `r.viewport` (E.Shell's HUD is single-screen, so versus uses a canvas HUD). Then `scene.hud(r)` draws the timer and the shared Count/Evidence bar at the top.","+- **Caveat:** hidden identity can be peeked at on one screen. Accept it locally; online it's truly hidden.","+- **Same code path:** local play runs the same `VersusSim` through `LocalTransport` (this copy is the host; all players are local).","+","+### 9.3 AI Hub: shared-world (AI Hub Session Protocol v1, client 1.4.0)","+**Tags** (in `<head>`, after the client script):","+```html","+<meta name=\"hub:session\" content=\"1\">","+<meta name=\"hub:session-players\" content=\"1-4\">","+<meta name=\"hub:session-mode\" content=\"shared-world\">","+<meta name=\"hub:session-minutes\" content=\"6\">","+<meta name=\"hub:session-goal\" content=\"Cops: build a 100-point case. Corner: make $3,000 unseen.\">","+<meta name=\"hub:session-howto\" content=\"Move: stick/WASD · Watch: L2/RMB · Photo: R2/LMB · Act: ✕/E · Call out: △/Q\">","+```","+**Flow** (99-start.js):","+```js","+if (window.AIHub && AIHub.active) {                      // straight into the round: no title, attract or menus","+  game.start({ scenes, scene: 'hubWait', boot });        // 'Connecting…' (no prompts)","+  const info = await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'shared-world', seats: [1, 4] });   // the hub's own card (no card: true)","+  if (!info) game.go('title');                           // no hub after all: the normal game","+  else { await Versus.buildRound(info); AIHub.ready(); } // roster from AIHub.rng('roster'); sides from seats + info.round","+}","+AIHub.on('start', () => Versus.countdown());             // overlay: role card + 3-2-1 until AIHub.time() >= 0","+```","+- **Host authority** (`info.isHost`): the host copy runs `VersusSim`: NPCs, crew AI, bots, rules, scoring, the timer (from `AIHub.time()`).","+- **Every copy moves its own character locally** (no input lag) and reports it. The host trusts positions inside a speed check.","+- **Other copies render snapshots** with 150 ms interpolation.","+- **Messages:**","+  - Host → all, unreliable, 10 Hz: `{t:'s', at, tl, ev, cn, ph, p:[[id,x,y,f,st,fl],…], n:[[nid,x,y,f,st],…]}`.","+    - x, y are integers (world units); f is facing quantized 0-63; st is an animation code (0 idle, 1 walk, 2 run, 3 crouch, 4 watch, 5 act, 6 down, 7 sit, 8 phone, 9 bike); fl is flags (burned, carrying, shut).","+    - **Keep each message under 1,100 bytes.** If the NPC list makes it bigger, send NPCs in two alternating halves (5 Hz each).","+  - Host → all, reliable, on events: `{t:'e', k:'photo'|'burn'|'callout'|'tap'|'jump'|'seize'|'stash'|'reup'|'shut'|'open'|'sale', …}` (sounds, toasts, particles).","+  - Client → host, unreliable, 10 Hz: `{t:'me', at, x, y, f, st, w, ax, ay}` (w = watching; ax, ay = the aimed world point).","+  - Client → host, reliable: `{t:'act', k:'photo', target, q, at}` · `{k:'callout', target}` · `{k:'tap', phone}` · `{k:'jump', target}` · `{k:'shut'|'open'|'stash'|'reup'|'pickup'|'handoff'|'ditch', …}`.","+  - Budget: host 10 snapshots + under 5 events per second (< 20/s); clients 10 + a few.","+- **Validation on the host:**","+  - Positions are clamped to `maxSpeed × elapsed × 1.5` and to walkable cells.","+  - A photo claim needs: the target exists, is within 240 units of the claimer, and `map.sight` is clear on the host. If ★Act is claimed, the host's 1-second act history must show an act within 600 ms.","+  - Call-outs are checked against the true identity.","+- **Events:**","+  - `leave` → that player's character becomes a bot on the same side; the round goes on.","+  - The host leaving voids the round (the hub sends `end` `host-left`) → show \"Round cancelled\".","+  - `time-up` → the host finishes at once with the timer-end outcome.","+  - `end` → stop input (controllers to null), stop music and effects, show our results under the hub's. After `end`, send nothing.","+- **Server** (`AIHub.server`): the host has no local player. It runs the sim and shows a spectator camera (`cam.frame` over all players). No audio, no input.","+- **Finish** (host only, once):","+  - `standings`: winners `[[winning side ids],[losing side ids]]`; draw `[[all ids]]`. Only hub player ids, never bots.","+  - `scores`: personal scores.","+  - `stats`: `{id:{Photos, Burns, Count}}`.","+  - `awards`.","+- **Session rules:**","+  - No other network use.","+  - No `alert`/`confirm`/`prompt`, no new windows.","+  - Pause doesn't stop the host: the versus scene is `pausable: false` in a session. Options opens a non-pausing overlay with Settings/Controls (`game.menu('settings')`) while the character's input is suppressed.","+  - `menu.quit: false` and no restart items.","+  - While Create (Pad8) is held, ignore Options.","+- **Randomness:** the host never uses `Math.random` for the sim. Shared rolls come from `AIHub.rng(label)`, and the roster from `AIHub.rng('roster')`, so every copy builds identical NPC rigs.","+","+---","+","+## 10. Attract mode (52-attract.js)","+- **Trigger:** 10 s with no input (keys, mouse buttons, mouse moves over 6 px, wheel, touches, gamepad buttons, or axes past 0.3) on **title, main menu, episode select or versus setup**. Settings, About and Controls don't count (a player may be reading).","+- **Exit:** any input → back to the title, and the idle timer resets. On touch-only devices, a tap → the notice panel.","+- **The reel:** a looping playlist of vignettes, each a real system running with bot controllers. Bots may cheat: no suspicion, unlimited film, teleports, scripted perfect actions.","+  - **Overlay:** letterbox bars, a **DEMO** badge, a small WIRETAP logo, a caption, and a blinking \"Press any button\" built from the current device's glyph.","+","+| # | s | Vignette | Bot does |","+|---|---|---|---|","+| 1 | 12 | **THE CORNER**: night, rain, CornerSim full; the camera turns 90° twice | Nothing: customers, touts, lookouts |","+| 2 | 10 | **EYES ON**: Dana on the bus-stop bench | Enter Watch, aim at the next sale, snap ★★★, polaroid slides in |","+| 3 | 10 | **THE TAIL**: Tee's route | Dana tails; Tee looks back; Dana takes cover in a doorway; hand-off to Lou |","+| 4 | 9 | **THE CHASE**: Corey bolts | Sprint, vault the court fence, tackle, cuff |","+| 5 | 10 | **THE WIRE**: wire room | Grandma call → MINIMIZE; pertinent call → LOG; a page decodes with a keypad turn |","+| 6 | 7 | **THE BOARD**: corkboard | Cards fly onto slots; red string ties Tee to P1 |","+| 7 | 8 | **THE BOX**: Corey | Lean → Offer a way out → beat unlocked |","+| 8 | 10 | **THE GAME**: versus, split screen, bots | A call-out burns a detective; a stash photo |","+| 9 | 8 | **THE COUNT**: Tee's tally | Bills flick, the total ticks up, then the title card |","+","+- **Implementation:** each entry is `{ id, seconds, setup(), tick(dt), caption }`. `setup()` loads a mission/scene with `attract: true`: no saves, no tutorials, no autosave, quieter music, no HUD prompts. The attract scene owns the clock and calls `game.go` for the next entry with a short dissolve.","+"]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-105319/work/PLAN.md"]}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01S713NtZqJ9LH7Zm9q7x7vV","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
