{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CggUmnwrBv9q42PYpGVc4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01NggFuotUhAPe1sdYxWjvZM","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat >> /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-105319/work/PLAN.md <<'EOF'\n---\n\n## 11. Audio (03-audio.js): all written in code\n\n### 11.1 Music (engine `game.audio.music`, scores in App. H)\n| Song | Plays | Layers (start `on: false`, faded with `audio.layer(name, vol, fade)`) |\n|---|---|---|\n| `theme` (84 bpm, A minor) | title, menus, about, credits, episode cards (as a `sting` of its last 2 bars) | — |\n| `field` (92 bpm, D minor) | field missions as Dana | `tension` while any observer is at `notice`+ toward Dana; `pulse` at `search`; `alarm`+`stab` for 8 s after MADE |\n| `corner` (95 bpm, G minor) | interludes as Tee; diegetic: also from a parked car's open door during Ep1-2 nights (volume by distance) | `lead` while the count is ahead of target pace |\n| `wire` (70 bpm, E minor) | wire room, evidence cage | `pulse` while a pertinent call is live |\n| `chase` (132 bpm) | foot chase, raid reactions, the 60-s rescue | — |\n| `montage` (68 bpm) | epilogue montage, Shut Down | — |\n| `versus` (104 bpm, C minor) | versus rounds | `pressure` at Evidence ≥ 50; `clock` in the last 60 s; `cash` at Count ≥ $2,000 |\n\n- **Stings** (`audio.sting`, `{ at: 'beat' }`):\n  - `made`: square A4 F4 D4, 0.12 s each\n  - `photoGood`: triangle E5 then B5\n  - `casePoint`: triangle C5 E5 G5 arp\n  - `beatDone`: the theme's last bar\n- **Ducking:** call `audio.duck(true)` while dialogue voices play.\n- **Field realism:** music volume in field missions is 0.6× the setting, so the ambience carries the street.\n\n### 11.2 Sound effects (`audio.define(name, voice)`; engine voice format)\n| Name | Recipe |\n|---|---|\n| `shutter` | `[{wave:'noise',freq:3000,dur:.03,vol:.25},{wave:'square',freq:1800,to:900,dur:.05,vol:.08}]`, then `whirr` `{wave:'saw',freq:220,to:320,dur:.18,vol:.04}` after 40 ms |\n| `pager` | three `{wave:'square',freq:'A6',dur:.07,vol:.1}` 110 ms apart, preceded by `{wave:'square',freq:'E6',dur:.07}` |\n| `dtmf_<d>` | two sines at the DTMF row/column pair (697/770/852/941 × 1209/1336/1477 Hz), 0.12 s, vol .08 |\n| `dialtone` / `ringback` | 350+440 Hz sines (loop); 440+480 Hz, 2 s on / 4 s off |\n| `phonering` | `{wave:'square',freq:1250,vib:[22,.06],dur:.9,vol:.06}` twice |\n| `reel` | noise 0.02 s click (tape start/stop); the `tape` bed is low noise while recording |\n| `siren` | sine 650→1300→650 over 3.6 s (wail, loop); `yelp`: 700↔1500 at 8 Hz for 1.2 s |\n| `radio` | noise burst 0.08 + squelch click (radio chatter in/out) |\n| `cuffs` | `{wave:'square',freq:2400,to:1800,dur:.03,vol:.12}` ×2, 60 ms apart |\n| `fence` | noise 0.22 s with vibrato (chain-link rattle on a vault) |\n| `doorRam` | `boom` preset at pitch 0.7, plus `game.shake(4)` |\n| `gunshot` | noise 0.18 s vol .45 + `boom` tail + an echo at −10 dB after 130 ms. Used exactly twice in the game (Ep3 robbery warning shot if *Go in*, and offscreen in I3 if Rook goes after Sunday) |\n| `bark` (dog) | `{wave:'saw',freq:320,to:180,dur:.12,vol:.12}` ×2 |\n| `coo` / `flap` | sine 420→380 with vibrato 0.35 s; noise bursts for wings (Pigeon's roof) |\n| `busbrake` | noise hiss 0.9 s + sine squeal 2200 Hz 0.3 s |\n| `typekey` / `typebell` | noise 0.015 s at 4 kHz; `blip` at a line end (affidavit) |\n| `stamp` | `land` preset + paper noise (judge signs) |\n| `pin` / `string` | square 900→700, 0.03 s; soft noise 0.08 s |\n| `cashflick` | noise 0.01 s, repeated for the count |\n| `ui_tick` / `ui_ok` / `ui_back` | triangle 1400 Hz 0.02 s vol .05; engine `confirm`; engine `cancel` |\n| `step_*` | engine `step` at pitch by floor tag: concrete 1.0, asphalt 0.9, alley 0.85 + grit, grass 0.7, wood (Annex) 1.1 |\n\n### 11.3 Ambience beds and voices\n- **Ambience** is built on `game.audio.ctx` from looping noise buffers and filters. Route it into the engine's sfx bus (`game.audio._sfxBus`, an internal field: check it exists, otherwise use your own gain scaled by `volume × sfxVolume × !muted`).\n  - **Street day:** low-passed traffic rumble; a bus every 60-90 s.\n  - **Street night:** traffic, plus far sirens and dog barks every 40-90 s.\n  - **Rain:** band-passed noise, with thunder from engine weather.\n  - **Annex:** HVAC hum, a phone ringing far off.\n  - **Wire room:** tape hiss, radiator clank every 20 s, clock.\n  - **Box:** 120 Hz fluorescent hum.\n  - **Chambers:** clock tick.\n- **Voices: Animalese/\"Simlish\" synth** (`Voice.speak(text, profile, { onChar, filter })`):\n  - **Syllables:** split the text into syllables (consonant cluster + vowel); punctuation is a pause (`,` 120 ms, `.?!` 260 ms). Each syllable is a 60-80 ms grain at `profile.rate` syllables/s.\n  - **Source:** an oscillator (`profile.wave`) at pitch `base × (1 + range × contour)`. The contour falls across a sentence, rises at the end of a `?`, and adds a per-syllable offset **seeded by the syllable's letters**, so the same word always sounds the same.\n  - **Filters:** two parallel band-pass formant filters (F1/F2 per vowel: a 800/1200, e 400/2300, i 300/2700, o 450/800, u 325/700, all × `formant`, Q≈9), then an envelope (attack 5 ms, release to 0 by grain end).\n  - **Consonants:** plosives (b d g k p t c q) are 12 ms noise bursts; fricatives (f s z h x j v) are 40 ms band-passed noise (2-6 kHz); nasals (m n) are a 60 ms low hum.\n  - **Breath:** noise mixed in at `profile.breath`.\n  - **Tics:** `stammer` (repeat the first syllable of 30% of words: Corey), `vibrato` (Odessa).\n  - **Sync with text:**\n    - `E.Dialog`: set `talk.voice = null`. Each update, play syllables for the letters added since `talk.shown` last frame. Pick the profile by `talk.name`. The text speed setting sets `talk.speed`.\n    - The wire transcript is driven by `Voice.speak` itself (`onChar` reveals letters).\n  - **Phone filter** (wire calls, payphone conversations): high-pass 300 Hz → low-pass 3400 Hz → a gentle `WaveShaper` → plus line hiss at −32 dB. **Radio filter** (police radio): band-pass 500-2500 Hz + squelch clicks at the start and end.\n  - **Bleeped words** (Strong language: Bleeped) get a 1 kHz sine over their syllables.\n  - **Voice volume** setting multiplies the voice bus.\n  - **Headless:** no-op.\n\n---\n\n## 12. Art direction and world building (05-world.js, 06-people.js)\n\n### 12.1 Mood by time of day (canvas lighting always; GPU lighting where available for night, `game.enableGPU({ map })`, with the same ambient set on both)\n| Preset | Ambient / tint | Lights | Weather |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `dawnRain` (cold open) | .45, blue-gray | patrol light bars (red/blue lights alternating at 2 Hz, radius 70), streetlamps fading | rain .7, wind .2 |\n| `day` | lights off (full bright), slightly desaturated palette | none | none |\n| `dusk` | .62, orange-violet | streetlamps flicker on at 17:40 | none |\n| `night` | .38, cool blue | streetlamps every 6 cells (`r.prop('streetlamp', …, { light: true, cone: true })`, color `#ffb04a`); lit windows; store signs emissive; TV-blue flicker in 1 window per block | none or rain (Ep4) |\n\n### 12.2 Wall types (App. A legend). Everything gets `cut: true` except low walls.\n| Char | What | h | Face / roof | Facade options | Colors (top/side) |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `#` | boundary rowhouses/warehouses | 56 | brick / slab | windows `{ lit: .15 }` | `#3a2a26` / `#5a3a30` |\n| `R` | brick rowhouse | 40 | brick / slab | windows `{ lit: .25 }`, door `{ chance: .35, color: '#4a2a1e' }` | `#4a3a34` / `#7a3b2e` |\n| `F` | Formstone rowhouse | 40 | material `formstone` = `'#8a8680 stones size=5'` / slab | windows `{ lit: .25 }`, door .35 | `#4a4844` / `#8a8680` |\n| `P` | painted brick | 36 | plaster / slab | windows `{ lit: .3 }`, shutters `#3a5a6a` | `#5a5048` / `#b8a27a` or `#6a7f8f` (alternate by block) |\n| `V` | vacant | 40 | brick (dark) / slab | `decorate`: plywood panels `#b08a5a` over window and door spans, spray-paint tags | `#3a2a24` / `#4a2e26` |\n| `S L E M $ K B Q` | storefronts | 32 | brick or plaster / slab | `decorate`: a lit display-window band (z 4-18, warm `#ffd890` glow texels), a sign band (z 20-28); the sign text is an `r.queue` board (§12.5) | per store |\n| `H` / `T` | church / bell tower | 64 / 88 | stone / slab | arch windows `{ chance: 1 }`, stained glass `window` props on the Ridley side | `#5a5650` / `#8a847a` |\n| `C` | Delancey Courts | 44 | brick (tan `#9a7a5a`) / slab | windows grid `{ lit: .35 }`, doors .3, balcony walkway `{ z: 22 }` | `#5a4a3a` / `#9a7a5a` |\n| `G` | garage | 24 | metal (corrugated `'#6a6a6a metal'`) / plain | roll-up door painted on the east face | `#4a4a4a` / `#6a6a6a` |\n| `k` | gas kiosk | 20 | plaster white with red band (decorate) | | `#d8d8d0` / `#e8e8e0` |\n\n### 12.3 Floors (legend values `{ floor: tag }`; `floorTex` per tag, or `floorMats`)\n| Char | Tag | Look |\n|---|---|---|\n| `.` | `walk` | concrete slabs (1-cell grid lines `#8a8a86`/`#7a7a76`, cracks); stoops (shapes) along rowhouse fronts |\n| `=` | `road` | asphalt `#2e2e32` with speckle; Ridley's dashed yellow center line; crosswalk stripes at intersections; manholes; puddles when raining (darker glossy patches with a GPU glow texel picking up lamp color) |\n| `-` | `alley` | cracked asphalt `#3a3836`, weeds in cracks, litter sprites |\n| `,` | `lot` | dirt + weeds (`E.tex.dirt` + grass props) |\n| `:` | `court` | courtyard pavers |\n| `b` | `ball` | court asphalt with painted lines |\n| `p` | `play` | rubber play surface (faded red) |\n| `v` | `vacant` | gutted floorboards, debris |\n| `g` | `garage` | oil-stained concrete |\n| `f` | `fence` | blocked floor cell; draw chain-link shapes on its edges (vaultable by a jump: §5.6) |\n| `x` | `edge` | blocked; sawhorse barricades (map exits) |\n\n### 12.4 People and palettes\n- **Cast looks:** §8.2. Skin tones span a realistic range (`#3a2418 #4a2e20 #5a3a28 #6b4630 #8a5a3c #c8946a #e0b89a #f0c8a8`). Baltimore's West Side is mostly Black, so the cast and crowds reflect that, drawn with dignity. No caricature.\n- **2004 clothes:** oversized white tees, throwback jerseys, puffy coats, hoodies, fitted caps, do-rags, Timberlands, Air Force 1s; church clothes on Odessa's friends; work uniforms; cops in windbreakers and khakis or blazers.\n- **Civilians:** 6 palette families (warm, cool, earth, sport, church, work). Seeded per NPC.\n- **Addicts:** thinner (`hunch .3`), mismatched layers. Shown as people, not monsters.\n\n### 12.5 Shapes to write (E.SHAPES data, docs/ASSETS.md format; check each with `node engine/tools/asset-sheet.mjs mine.js#id`)\n- **Vehicles** (also moving, drawn with `facing` each frame):\n  - `sedan`, `chevy` (Dana's beige Lumina)\n  - `van` (white Ford Econoline, county tags)\n  - `hearse` (black, long)\n  - `boxtruck` (white, red **HARSTAD AUTO PARTS** band: the text is a queued sign)\n  - `patrol` (white/blue with a light-bar box; the lights themselves are game lights)\n  - `montecarlo` (Rook's), `deadbuick` (flat tires), `burnedcar`\n- **Street:**\n  - `payphone` (pole, hood, handset)\n  - `busshelter`; `bench` (core)\n  - `trashbag`, `dumpster`; plus the engine props `trashcan`, `hydrant`, `firedrum`, `streetlamp`, `awning`, `sign`\n  - `stoop` (3 marble steps), `pole` (utility pole with a crossbar)\n  - `sawhorse`, `chainlink` (a 16-unit segment with posts and diamond mesh: a custom `E.PATTERNS.mesh`)\n  - `hoop` (basketball, chain net), `swings`, `gaspump`, `stroller`, `bike`, `coop` (pigeon coop), `mattress`\n- **Interiors:**\n  - `corkboard` (draws live Board state: `r.queue`), `desk` + `officechair` (cut `kenney-furniture:desk-corner`, `chair-desk` with `node engine/tools/asset-set.mjs`, or write them)\n  - `filecab`, `reel2reel` (reels drawn turning in `r.queue`), `crt`, `radiator`, `coffeemaker`, `watercooler`\n  - `table`/`chair`/`bookcase` (core), `judgedesk`, `sheetbody` (a covered body for the cold open)\n- **Signs** are `r.queue` boards: a dark panel plus `E.font.text`, lit by an emissive flag for neon (\"OPEN\", \"CHECKS CASHED\", \"WINGS · FRIES · SUBS\", \"SUDS CITY\", \"RIDLEY WIRELESS & PAGER\", \"MAMA B'S SOUL FOOD\", \"FADES & GRADES\"), plus a barber pole (stripes animated by time).\n\n### 12.6 World details that sell it\n- **Phone wires** (the motif): utility poles every 8 cells along alleys and the avenue. Between pole tops (z 70), draw 8-segment sagging catenaries with `px.line` in `r.queue` (sorted above roofs). **A pair of sneakers hangs on the wire over Gaither & Ridley.** Pigeons sit on the wire near Odessa's roof and scatter (flap) when someone runs below.\n- **Fake roofs** for walk-in interiors (the garage): an `r.queue` polygon with `footprint` that fades to 15% when Dana is inside or within 24 units of a door. The 1412 vacant has no roof (burned): draw charred beams.\n- **Vacants and decay:** plywood, a \"V\" spray mark, a mattress in the lot, the fire drum (flame prop, `light: true`) at night with two men warming their hands.\n- **Life:** a bus pulls up at P3 every 90 s (a bus shape drives the Ridley lane and stops 4 s); kids shoot hoops in daytime; Odessa sweeps her stoop at dawn.\n- **Felton's memorial** stays on his stoop through Ep5: candles, flowers, a photo. It gets smaller each episode.\n\n### 12.7 Title screen\n- **Scene:** the live iso diorama of the corner at night in rain (CornerSim with AI, no player), camera slowly turning (one 90° step every 20 s).\n- **Logo:** \"WIRETAP\" in `E.font.title` (scale 4, colors `['#fff6dc','#ffcf7a','#e08a2a']`, depth 3, depthColor `#3a1a0a`). A telephone wire runs behind the logo with sneakers hanging from it. Tagline \"Somebody's always listening.\"\n- **Menu:** `E.Menu` (canvas; keys, d-pad, stick, hover, click). `E.versionLabel()` tiny at the bottom right.\n- **Keep clear:** the top-right corner area.\n\n---\n\n## 13. About/Credits screen and the exit interview\n- **`credits.json` is the single source** of the About pages and of `exit-interview.json`. The build copies its `exitInterview` object verbatim into `../exit-interview.json` and verifies it parses.\n- **About & Credits** (title menu → DOM screen; L1/R1 pages; large type; at most about 10 short lines per page; stick scrolls long answers):\n  1. **Credits:**\n     - WIRETAP; \"An original game inspired by *The Wire* (HBO, 2002-2008). Not affiliated with HBO or the show's creators.\"\n     - Design and code: the model(s) that built it (truthfully: if the builder isn't claude-opus-5-5 at max effort, list both, e.g. \"Planned by Anthropic claude-opus-5-5 (max); built by <id>\").\n     - Engine: my-3D2dge v0.85.1 by Michael Crosato (MIT). Multiplayer: AI Hub Session Protocol v1, client 1.4.0.\n     - Any CC0 asset entries used (Kenney/KayKit via the engine's store), each with its source line.\n  2. **Source Information:** every field of TASK.md's list, same text as `exitInterview.sourceInformation`.\n  3. **Testing Feedback:** the 4 questions with answers.\n  4. **Engine Feedback:** the 6 questions with answers.\n  5. **Prompt Feedback:** the 4 questions with answers.\n- **Write \"unknown\" for anything you can't confirm.** Fill in real answers at the end of the build: no placeholders ship.\n- **Exit interview shape** (exactly TASK.md's). Suggested values to start from; correct any that turn out untrue:\n```json\n{\n  \"sourceInformation\": {\n    \"date\": \"2026-11-03 10:53\",\n    \"source\": \"The Wire (2002-2008)\",\n    \"genre\": \"Stealth investigation / crime drama with a corner-management sim and an asymmetric versus mode\",\n    \"perspective\": \"Isometric 2.5D (pixel-art 3D skeletons on a tile world); brawler-view interiors; HTML case-file screens\",\n    \"tech\": \"my-3D2dge v0.85.1 full engine (canvas 2D, optional WebGPU lighting); AI Hub session client 1.4.0; vanilla JavaScript; Web Audio\",\n    \"artDirection\": \"Engine-native retro-modern pixel art (PS1-era 2D look) pushed toward grit: sodium streetlight, rain, Formstone rowhouses, boarded vacants\",\n    \"animation\": \"Engine-native procedural Humanoid rigs (E.MOVES, poses, E.ACTIONS paired actions) plus custom joint post-processed poses; tweens and coroutine scripts\",\n    \"audio\": \"Code-written chip-synth music (engine music tracks, layered), synthesized effects and ambience, Web Audio formant gibberish voices with a telephone filter\",\n    \"online\": \"AI Hub Session Protocol v1, shared-world versus for 1-4 players (host-authoritative); local split-screen versus; no other network\",\n    \"testing\": \"<fill in: what you actually ran>\",\n    \"research\": \"my-3D2dge handoff docs (API.md, AI_GUIDE.md, ASSETS.md, kits) and the AI Hub protocol README; knowledge of the series from memory; no other web research\",\n    \"environment\": \"Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\",\n    \"model\": \"Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort max\",\n    \"usage\": \"unknown\"\n  },\n  \"testingFeedback\": [\"…\", \"…\", \"…\", \"…\"],\n  \"engineFeedback\": [\"…\", \"…\", \"…\", \"…\", \"…\", \"…\"],\n  \"promptFeedback\": [\"…\", \"…\", \"…\", \"…\"],\n  \"aiHub\": {\n    \"name\": \"WIRETAP\",\n    \"tagline\": \"Somebody's always listening.\",\n    \"description\": \"Work both sides of a West Baltimore corner in 2004: build a wiretap case one photo, page and phone call at a time, then run the corner the case is built on. Includes a 1-4 player cops-vs-corner versus mode.\",\n    \"type\": \"Game\",\n    \"genre\": \"Stealth\",\n    \"source\": \"The Wire (2002-2008)\",\n    \"series\": \"\",\n    \"players\": \"1–4\",\n    \"controls\": \"Stick/WASD move · L2/RMB watch · R2/LMB photo · ✕/E interact · △/Q partner · Create/Tab notebook\",\n    \"tags\": [\"story\", \"versus\", \"pixel art\", \"isometric\", \"crime\", \"detective\"]\n  }\n}\n```\n- **The build's final chat reply** must also contain Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback (TASK.md).\n\n---\n\n## 14. Build order and milestones\nBuild systems before content and one complete episode before breadth. **Each milestone ends with its tests green and a bundle that runs.**\n\n| M | Goal | Done when |\n|---|---|---|\n| **M0** Setup | Dev folder, engine and hub client fetched, `build.mjs`, `index.html`, `tests/headless.mjs` skeleton, blank title scene | The bundle opens with no errors; `node engine/tools/check.mjs <bundle>` passes; headless boot test passes |\n| **M1** Framework | Scenes skeleton; Controller classes; KEYS preset; settings (glyphs, stick inversion, difficulty, text speed, language, voices); canvas and DOM glyph rendering with device switching; DOM UI kit (focus nav, hover focus, legend); hover patch for E.Shell; save system; touch-only notice; About screen (rendering `credits.json`); **Voice synth prototype** (speak a line with 3 profiles, phone filter); music player with the 7 songs | Fake-gamepad test shows ✕ prompts and Xbox after switching; inversion test flips movement; the touch-only profile shows the notice; voice speaks in sync with a test dialog |\n| **M2** World | Neighborhood TileMap (App. A) with wall types, facades, floors, stoops, poles and wires, props, lights, weather, time presets; Annex map; camera rotate/zoom/peek; Dana moves (walk/run/crouch/blend); civilians with routines; FlowField cache | Screenshots of day/night/rain in 3 rotations look right (thumbnail test, check.mjs look notes acted on); 25 civilians walk 5 min without getting stuck (headless) |\n| **M3** Corner and eyes | CornerSim (all roles, sales, shutdown, ledger); perception/made; Watch, reads, photos and polaroids; HUD; interactables, cover, eavesdrop, barks | Headless: ledger invariants hold over 10 min; a careless bot gets made within 30 s; a careful bot reads 2 roles and gets 4 faces |\n| **M4** Episode 1 vertical slice | Director and mission runner; E.Story + Dialog with voices; Annex stations; Board; notebook; Pockets' shoe game; cold open; I1 as Tee (order wheel, code card, payphone keypad, count) | Ep1 playable start to finish with a pad and with keyboard+mouse; autosave/continue works; deep links `#ep1.*` reach every beat |\n| **M5** Episode 2 | Chase (escape graph, vault, tackle, cuff, ditch, search); box; cipher; affidavit and necessity; chambers; I2 | Headless chase bot catches Corey; box thresholds and lawyer rule; affidavit scoring and perjury detection; Ep2 playable |\n| **M6** Episode 3 | Wire room (scheduler, playback, minimize/spot-check, log, voice ID, pages, fast-forward, legal); van stakeout with van heat; dilemma; ops sweep; wall-off; code flip; Easy's scene (I3) | Wire session tests (legal increments, logging windows, ID); Ep3 playable on all branches |\n| **M7** Episode 4 | Tail (routes, acts, distance band, hand-off), trash stealth, kitchen talk, burners, session 3, I4 | Tail bot completes `teeDry`; Ep4 playable |\n| **M8** Episode 5 + endings | Raid, rescue, press conference, money tail with moving cone, long lens, the morning after, I5, montage rules, credits, Shut Down, episode select presets | The branch-matrix test (§16) produces a valid montage for every combination; story mode is complete |\n| **M9** Versus | VersusSim rules, roles, actions, scoring, bots, local split screen, results; then `HubTransport`, host loop, snapshots, interpolation, leave/time-up/end/server | A local bot match ends with a valid outcome; **hub harness passes** all four runs (§16) |\n| **M10** Attract and title | Attract reel (9 vignettes), idle detection, touch-only attract; title diorama; episode select; versus setup; full settings | Idle 10 s → attract; any input → title; all vignettes run 3 loops without errors |\n| **M11** Polish and ship | Balance pass (difficulty table), juice (particles, shake, stings), audio mix, writing pass against App. G, viewport/WebKit checks, final About content, bundle, exit interview | §17 checklist all ticked |\n\n**Content budgets** (to keep scope honest): at most ~90 dialogue lines per episode excluding wire calls; wire calls as in App. D; montage cards as in App. G. Write tight. The show's people say less than they mean.\n\n---\n\n## 15. Risks and how to de-risk them\n| # | Risk | Why it's risky | De-risk |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | **Scope** | Many systems and five episodes | Shared systems (one map, one CornerSim, one perception, one photo system everywhere); data-driven content; Ep1 slice by M4 proves the pipeline; content budgets; milestone gates |\n| 2 | **AI Hub shared-world passing the harness** (latency 150 / jitter 50 / loss 5, host leave, server) | Netcode bugs show up late | `LocalTransport` and a `LoopbackTransport` that simulates latency/loss in-process for headless tests; client-authoritative own movement (the arena example's pattern); message size asserts; run the real harness at the *start* of M9 with a minimal round (two dots moving, finish at 30 s), then grow |\n| 3 | **Wire room fun and readability** | Lots of text plus a clock | Few calls per session, short lines, 8 s rule shown as a visible ring, Rookie hints; deep link `#ep3.wire1` for fast iteration; thumbnail test |\n| 4 | **Voice synth** (quality, sync, CPU) | Custom Web Audio | Prototype in M1; fixed lookahead scheduling (`ctx.currentTime + 0.05`); fallback: the engine's `text` blip with per-profile pitch if formants misbehave in a browser |\n| 5 | **NPC simulation stability** | Stuck agents, flow-field cost, sorting | FlowField cache by POI; stuck rule; draw background civilians `every: 2`; invariant tests |\n| 6 | **Perception tuning** | Made too easily, or never | The target table in §5.2; the `?dev=1` overlay shows every suspicion value; careless/careful bot tests |\n| 7 | **10-foot UI and glyph switching** | Dense screens creep in | §4.5 rules; thumbnail test; fake-gamepad/mouse device-switch tests |\n| 8 | **Branch combinatorics** | Flags interacting | Few flags; endings by a rule table; episode presets; a branch-matrix headless test that runs every choice combination with action parts auto-resolved (`debug.autoResolve`) |\n| 9 | **Engine pitfalls** (heights, `cut`, sorting big shapes, iso facades, lighting cost) | New engine for most builders | Follow API.md's rules; `footprint` sorting for canopies and roofs; act on every `check.mjs` look note; keep the engine unmodified |\n| 10 | **Single-file bundling** | `</script>` in strings, the order of the hub client | The build checks; tests run against the bundle, not only the dev page |\n| 11 | **Gamepad wrapper side effects** | It overrides a browser API | `try/catch`, pass-through when both toggles are off, Playwright fake-pad test |\n| 12 | **Tone and sensitivity** | Gritty material about real communities | App. G writing guide: no slurs, everyone human, violence mostly offscreen with consequences, no glamor; a final writing pass |\n\n---\n\n## 16. Testing plan (lightweight and token-efficient)\n**Principles:**\n- Test rules headless (fast, exact, no screenshots).\n- Look at a *few* screenshots per milestone.\n- Run the hub harness only for versus.\n- Never paste big logs into context: print one PASS/FAIL line per test plus the first error.\n\n**Tools** (on this machine):\n- Node, Playwright 1.63 with Chromium/WebKit/Firefox.\n- `node engine/tools/check.mjs <page>#<deeplink>`: errors, a screenshot, look notes, `game.debug.snapshot()`.\n- `viewport-matrix <url>` (keep runs small: `--only` / `--devices`; don't run several at once). Real iOS Safari isn't available; WebKit with iPhone profiles is the closest check.\n- `python3 -m http.server` to serve the bundle and the harness side by side.\n\n**Hooks** (60-debug.js):\n- `game.debug.snapshot()` → `{ scene, ep, beat, meters, flags, dana:[x,y], objective, versus:{ev, cn, tl, sides} }`.\n- `game.debug.jump(beatId)`, `game.debug.autoResolve(on)` (missions and screens complete themselves with default good choices), `game.debug.bot(name)`.\n- Deep links: `#title`, `#attract`, `#about`, `#ep<N>.<beat>` (e.g. `#ep3.wire1`), `#versus.bots`, `#versus.local`.\n- `?dev=1` overlay: cells under the mouse, POIs, routes, suspicion numbers, agent states, F9 toggles it.\n\n**`tests/headless.mjs`** loads `engine/my-3d2dge.js` and the bundled game script into a Node `vm` context with the stand-ins from `engine/kits/test.mjs` (`window`, `addEventListener`, `location`), then runs:\n\n| Test | Asserts |\n|---|---|\n| boot | Boot steps finish; `validateData()` reports 0 problems; `game.errors.length === 0` |\n| cipher | CW/CCW are permutations and inverses; App. C's 5 pages decode to App. C's numbers; the flip page decodes with the other turn |\n| photo scoring | Fixture cases: back turned = no ★Face; 230 units = blurry; act window = ★Act; burned = 0 |\n| perception | Careless bot (stare at a lookout from 60) made in ≤ 6 s; careful bot (walk past) never noticed; blending at 100 for 30 s never made |\n| corner ledger | 10 min of sim: vial and cash conservation hold; shutdown freezes sales; re-up triggers below 30 |\n| chase | Bot pursuer with good routing catches the runner within 60 s; the ditch happens; the kid takes it after 45 s if it's not searched |\n| tail | A careful bot completes `teeDry`; a bot that stops on every `lookBack` gets made |\n| box | Thresholds unlock B1-B3; Fear ≥ 80 → lawyer; the Lean → Offer combo; flip only at B3 with Fear ≤ 60 |\n| paper | PC sums per line; a false necessity tick is always asked and denies |\n| wire | Non-pertinent past the window adds Legal 4/s; a minimized pertinent line is lost; spot-check timing; LOG windows; voice ID links the number |\n| meters | Brass 0 → shutdown scene; Heat thresholds flip the code and add lookouts |\n| branch matrix | With `autoResolve`, every combination of dilemma × sweep × wallOff × lossOn × canary × path × I5 reaches the montage with 9-11 valid cards |\n| save/load | Save at `ep3.van`, new game instance on the same storage, CONTINUE → same beat and STATE |\n| versus | A bots-only local match ends with a valid outcome; host rules (burn, tap, jump-out) apply; snapshot JSON < 1,100 bytes at the 45-entity worst case; `LoopbackTransport` at 150 ms ±50 and 5% loss still converges |\n| attract | 10.1 s idle on the title → `attract`; one `input.press` → `title`; 3 loops of the reel with no errors |\n\n**`tests/browser.mjs`** (Playwright, one browser at a time):\n1. **Gamepad:** an init script defines a fake standard gamepad (`navigator.getGamepads` returns a DualSense-like id with buttons and axes). Assert the HUD prompt reads ✕; switch Settings → Xbox → it reads A; enable `stickInvX`, push axis0 = +1 → Dana moves left (−x).\n2. **Mouse:** hover a main-menu item → it gets focus; click → it activates; the legend shows mouse/key glyphs.\n3. **Touch-only:** an iPhone profile (WebKit) shows the notice and a Settings button; after 10 s attract runs; a tap returns.\n4. **Screens:** 8 screenshots via deep links at 1920×1080 (title, `ep1.photos`, `ep3.wire1`, Board, box, versus local split, about, montage). Look at each once; apply the thumbnail test (downscale to 480×270).\n\n**Viewport sweep** (once, at M11): `viewport-matrix http://localhost:8000/<bundle> --only phone,tablet,desktop --engines chromium,webkit -o /tmp/viewport-matrix/wiretap`. Expect: phones show the touch-only notice; desktop sizes (16:9, 21:9, 4:3) fill edge to edge with the HUD inside the safe areas; no horizontal overflow; no console errors.\n\n**AI Hub harness** (`tests/hub/hub-check.mjs`): serve `tests/hub/` with the bundle copied in. Open in Playwright and wait for `document.body.dataset.complete === 'true'`, then assert `window.__hubCheck.pass === true` for:\n1. `harness.html?game=<bundle>&players=2&auto=1`\n2. `…&players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1`\n3. `…&players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1&scenario=host-leave`\n4. `…&players=2&scenario=server&auto=1`\n\nAlso open the bundle outside a session: it must still reach the title.\n\n**When to run:** headless after every change to a system; browser screens at the end of each milestone; viewport sweep and hub harness at M9 and M11.\n\n---\n\n## 17. Definition of done (tick every line before shipping)\n- [ ] Title is **WIRETAP** (RNG-picked, §0); the bundle is `Wiretap-TheWire-claude-opus-5-5-max-20261103-105319.html` in `work/`; the dev folder holds sources, tools and tests; `exit-interview.json` sits next to the html and parses.\n- [ ] One html file runs offline: the engine and hub client inlined, no runtime network, no external fonts.\n- [ ] Genre/perspective as §2; engine-native art and animation, extended (§12); all music, effects and gibberish voices written in code (§11).\n- [ ] **Story mode:** 5 episodes, 4 interludes + finale interlude, both finale paths, Shut Down, montage with computed cards, credits, episode select, continue/autosave.\n- [ ] **Every system in §5-§7 is reachable in normal play**, with no TODOs, placeholders or stubs. Each one appears in the feature matrix (App. J.6) at least once.\n- [ ] **Versus:** local (1 human vs bots; 2 humans split screen) and AI Hub shared-world (1-4). All four harness runs pass, and the game runs outside a session.\n- [ ] **Attract:** 10 s idle on title/menus → bot-played reel; any input exits; it runs on touch-only devices.\n- [ ] **10-foot UX:** controller-first; keyboard+mouse native (hover focuses, click selects, mouse aims and clicks world objects); prompts follow the last device; PlayStation glyphs by default with an Xbox option; **stick inversion toggles** for both axes; no dense data screens; thumbnail test passes.\n- [ ] **Touch-only:** no touch controls; \"Controller or keyboard required\" with a Settings button; attract allowed.\n- [ ] Standard engine features only (no custom pause/settings/rebinding/full screen); E.Shell HUD; standard settings plus the §4.7 game settings.\n- [ ] **About/Credits** screen with Credits, Source Information, Testing, Engine and Prompt Feedback, matching `exit-interview.json`; \"unknown\" where unconfirmed.\n- [ ] Headless suite green; browser checks looked at; hub harness passes; WebKit check done.\n- [ ] Writing pass done against App. G (tone, no slurs, no quotes from the show).\n\nEOF\nwc -c /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-105319/work/PLAN.md","description":"Append audio, art, credits, milestones, risks, testing, done sections"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":21618,"cache_read_input_tokens":405367,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":21618,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e2aa65a8-ee1a-45c4-b8e6-f96cf188e23d","uuid":"f68a278b-4599-4cda-96fc-699f750f85c8","timestamp":"2026-11-03T18:40:24.877Z","request_id":"req_011CggUmn6FTwK6evGwjk3KX","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01NggFuotUhAPe1sdYxWjvZM":{"command":"cat >> /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-105319/work/PLAN.md <<'EOF'\n---\n\n## 11. Audio (03-audio.js): all written in code\n\n### 11.1 Music (engine `game.audio.music`, scores in App. H)\n| Song | Plays | Layers (start `on: false`, faded with `audio.layer(name, vol, fade)`) |\n|---|---|---|\n| `theme` (84 bpm, A minor) | title, menus, about, credits, episode cards (as a `sting` of its last 2 bars) | — |\n| `field` (92 bpm, D minor) | field missions as Dana | `tension` while any observer is at `notice`+ toward Dana; `pulse` at `search`; `alarm`+`stab` for 8 s after MADE |\n| `corner` (95 bpm, G minor) | interludes as Tee; diegetic: also from a parked car's open door during Ep1-2 nights (volume by distance) | `lead` while the count is ahead of target pace |\n| `wire` (70 bpm, E minor) | wire room, evidence cage | `pulse` while a pertinent call is live |\n| `chase` (132 bpm) | foot chase, raid reactions, the 60-s rescue | — |\n| `montage` (68 bpm) | epilogue montage, Shut Down | — |\n| `versus` (104 bpm, C minor) | versus rounds | `pressure` at Evidence ≥ 50; `clock` in the last 60 s; `cash` at Count ≥ $2,000 |\n\n- **Stings** (`audio.sting`, `{ at: 'beat' }`):\n  - `made`: square A4 F4 D4, 0.12 s each\n  - `photoGood`: triangle E5 then B5\n  - `casePoint`: triangle C5 E5 G5 arp\n  - `beatDone`: the theme's last bar\n- **Ducking:** call `audio.duck(true)` while dialogue voices play.\n- **Field realism:** music volume in field missions is 0.6× the setting, so the ambience carries the street.\n\n### 11.2 Sound effects (`audio.define(name, voice)`; engine voice format)\n| Name | Recipe |\n|---|---|\n| `shutter` | `[{wave:'noise',freq:3000,dur:.03,vol:.25},{wave:'square',freq:1800,to:900,dur:.05,vol:.08}]`, then `whirr` `{wave:'saw',freq:220,to:320,dur:.18,vol:.04}` after 40 ms |\n| `pager` | three `{wave:'square',freq:'A6',dur:.07,vol:.1}` 110 ms apart, preceded by `{wave:'square',freq:'E6',dur:.07}` |\n| `dtmf_<d>` | two sines at the DTMF row/column pair (697/770/852/941 × 1209/1336/1477 Hz), 0.12 s, vol .08 |\n| `dialtone` / `ringback` | 350+440 Hz sines (loop); 440+480 Hz, 2 s on / 4 s off |\n| `phonering` | `{wave:'square',freq:1250,vib:[22,.06],dur:.9,vol:.06}` twice |\n| `reel` | noise 0.02 s click (tape start/stop); the `tape` bed is low noise while recording |\n| `siren` | sine 650→1300→650 over 3.6 s (wail, loop); `yelp`: 700↔1500 at 8 Hz for 1.2 s |\n| `radio` | noise burst 0.08 + squelch click (radio chatter in/out) |\n| `cuffs` | `{wave:'square',freq:2400,to:1800,dur:.03,vol:.12}` ×2, 60 ms apart |\n| `fence` | noise 0.22 s with vibrato (chain-link rattle on a vault) |\n| `doorRam` | `boom` preset at pitch 0.7, plus `game.shake(4)` |\n| `gunshot` | noise 0.18 s vol .45 + `boom` tail + an echo at −10 dB after 130 ms. Used exactly twice in the game (Ep3 robbery warning shot if *Go in*, and offscreen in I3 if Rook goes after Sunday) |\n| `bark` (dog) | `{wave:'saw',freq:320,to:180,dur:.12,vol:.12}` ×2 |\n| `coo` / `flap` | sine 420→380 with vibrato 0.35 s; noise bursts for wings (Pigeon's roof) |\n| `busbrake` | noise hiss 0.9 s + sine squeal 2200 Hz 0.3 s |\n| `typekey` / `typebell` | noise 0.015 s at 4 kHz; `blip` at a line end (affidavit) |\n| `stamp` | `land` preset + paper noise (judge signs) |\n| `pin` / `string` | square 900→700, 0.03 s; soft noise 0.08 s |\n| `cashflick` | noise 0.01 s, repeated for the count |\n| `ui_tick` / `ui_ok` / `ui_back` | triangle 1400 Hz 0.02 s vol .05; engine `confirm`; engine `cancel` |\n| `step_*` | engine `step` at pitch by floor tag: concrete 1.0, asphalt 0.9, alley 0.85 + grit, grass 0.7, wood (Annex) 1.1 |\n\n### 11.3 Ambience beds and voices\n- **Ambience** is built on `game.audio.ctx` from looping noise buffers and filters. Route it into the engine's sfx bus (`game.audio._sfxBus`, an internal field: check it exists, otherwise use your own gain scaled by `volume × sfxVolume × !muted`).\n  - **Street day:** low-passed traffic rumble; a bus every 60-90 s.\n  - **Street night:** traffic, plus far sirens and dog barks every 40-90 s.\n  - **Rain:** band-passed noise, with thunder from engine weather.\n  - **Annex:** HVAC hum, a phone ringing far off.\n  - **Wire room:** tape hiss, radiator clank every 20 s, clock.\n  - **Box:** 120 Hz fluorescent hum.\n  - **Chambers:** clock tick.\n- **Voices: Animalese/\"Simlish\" synth** (`Voice.speak(text, profile, { onChar, filter })`):\n  - **Syllables:** split the text into syllables (consonant cluster + vowel); punctuation is a pause (`,` 120 ms, `.?!` 260 ms). Each syllable is a 60-80 ms grain at `profile.rate` syllables/s.\n  - **Source:** an oscillator (`profile.wave`) at pitch `base × (1 + range × contour)`. The contour falls across a sentence, rises at the end of a `?`, and adds a per-syllable offset **seeded by the syllable's letters**, so the same word always sounds the same.\n  - **Filters:** two parallel band-pass formant filters (F1/F2 per vowel: a 800/1200, e 400/2300, i 300/2700, o 450/800, u 325/700, all × `formant`, Q≈9), then an envelope (attack 5 ms, release to 0 by grain end).\n  - **Consonants:** plosives (b d g k p t c q) are 12 ms noise bursts; fricatives (f s z h x j v) are 40 ms band-passed noise (2-6 kHz); nasals (m n) are a 60 ms low hum.\n  - **Breath:** noise mixed in at `profile.breath`.\n  - **Tics:** `stammer` (repeat the first syllable of 30% of words: Corey), `vibrato` (Odessa).\n  - **Sync with text:**\n    - `E.Dialog`: set `talk.voice = null`. Each update, play syllables for the letters added since `talk.shown` last frame. Pick the profile by `talk.name`. The text speed setting sets `talk.speed`.\n    - The wire transcript is driven by `Voice.speak` itself (`onChar` reveals letters).\n  - **Phone filter** (wire calls, payphone conversations): high-pass 300 Hz → low-pass 3400 Hz → a gentle `WaveShaper` → plus line hiss at −32 dB. **Radio filter** (police radio): band-pass 500-2500 Hz + squelch clicks at the start and end.\n  - **Bleeped words** (Strong language: Bleeped) get a 1 kHz sine over their syllables.\n  - **Voice volume** setting multiplies the voice bus.\n  - **Headless:** no-op.\n\n---\n\n## 12. Art direction and world building (05-world.js, 06-people.js)\n\n### 12.1 Mood by time of day (canvas lighting always; GPU lighting where available for night, `game.enableGPU({ map })`, with the same ambient set on both)\n| Preset | Ambient / tint | Lights | Weather |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `dawnRain` (cold open) | .45, blue-gray | patrol light bars (red/blue lights alternating at 2 Hz, radius 70), streetlamps fading | rain .7, wind .2 |\n| `day` | lights off (full bright), slightly desaturated palette | none | none |\n| `dusk` | .62, orange-violet | streetlamps flicker on at 17:40 | none |\n| `night` | .38, cool blue | streetlamps every 6 cells (`r.prop('streetlamp', …, { light: true, cone: true })`, color `#ffb04a`); lit windows; store signs emissive; TV-blue flicker in 1 window per block | none or rain (Ep4) |\n\n### 12.2 Wall types (App. A legend). Everything gets `cut: true` except low walls.\n| Char | What | h | Face / roof | Facade options | Colors (top/side) |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `#` | boundary rowhouses/warehouses | 56 | brick / slab | windows `{ lit: .15 }` | `#3a2a26` / `#5a3a30` |\n| `R` | brick rowhouse | 40 | brick / slab | windows `{ lit: .25 }`, door `{ chance: .35, color: '#4a2a1e' }` | `#4a3a34` / `#7a3b2e` |\n| `F` | Formstone rowhouse | 40 | material `formstone` = `'#8a8680 stones size=5'` / slab | windows `{ lit: .25 }`, door .35 | `#4a4844` / `#8a8680` |\n| `P` | painted brick | 36 | plaster / slab | windows `{ lit: .3 }`, shutters `#3a5a6a` | `#5a5048` / `#b8a27a` or `#6a7f8f` (alternate by block) |\n| `V` | vacant | 40 | brick (dark) / slab | `decorate`: plywood panels `#b08a5a` over window and door spans, spray-paint tags | `#3a2a24` / `#4a2e26` |\n| `S L E M $ K B Q` | storefronts | 32 | brick or plaster / slab | `decorate`: a lit display-window band (z 4-18, warm `#ffd890` glow texels), a sign band (z 20-28); the sign text is an `r.queue` board (§12.5) | per store |\n| `H` / `T` | church / bell tower | 64 / 88 | stone / slab | arch windows `{ chance: 1 }`, stained glass `window` props on the Ridley side | `#5a5650` / `#8a847a` |\n| `C` | Delancey Courts | 44 | brick (tan `#9a7a5a`) / slab | windows grid `{ lit: .35 }`, doors .3, balcony walkway `{ z: 22 }` | `#5a4a3a` / `#9a7a5a` |\n| `G` | garage | 24 | metal (corrugated `'#6a6a6a metal'`) / plain | roll-up door painted on the east face | `#4a4a4a` / `#6a6a6a` |\n| `k` | gas kiosk | 20 | plaster white with red band (decorate) | | `#d8d8d0` / `#e8e8e0` |\n\n### 12.3 Floors (legend values `{ floor: tag }`; `floorTex` per tag, or `floorMats`)\n| Char | Tag | Look |\n|---|---|---|\n| `.` | `walk` | concrete slabs (1-cell grid lines `#8a8a86`/`#7a7a76`, cracks); stoops (shapes) along rowhouse fronts |\n| `=` | `road` | asphalt `#2e2e32` with speckle; Ridley's dashed yellow center line; crosswalk stripes at intersections; manholes; puddles when raining (darker glossy patches with a GPU glow texel picking up lamp color) |\n| `-` | `alley` | cracked asphalt `#3a3836`, weeds in cracks, litter sprites |\n| `,` | `lot` | dirt + weeds (`E.tex.dirt` + grass props) |\n| `:` | `court` | courtyard pavers |\n| `b` | `ball` | court asphalt with painted lines |\n| `p` | `play` | rubber play surface (faded red) |\n| `v` | `vacant` | gutted floorboards, debris |\n| `g` | `garage` | oil-stained concrete |\n| `f` | `fence` | blocked floor cell; draw chain-link shapes on its edges (vaultable by a jump: §5.6) |\n| `x` | `edge` | blocked; sawhorse barricades (map exits) |\n\n### 12.4 People and palettes\n- **Cast looks:** §8.2. Skin tones span a realistic range (`#3a2418 #4a2e20 #5a3a28 #6b4630 #8a5a3c #c8946a #e0b89a #f0c8a8`). Baltimore's West Side is mostly Black, so the cast and crowds reflect that, drawn with dignity. No caricature.\n- **2004 clothes:** oversized white tees, throwback jerseys, puffy coats, hoodies, fitted caps, do-rags, Timberlands, Air Force 1s; church clothes on Odessa's friends; work uniforms; cops in windbreakers and khakis or blazers.\n- **Civilians:** 6 palette families (warm, cool, earth, sport, church, work). Seeded per NPC.\n- **Addicts:** thinner (`hunch .3`), mismatched layers. Shown as people, not monsters.\n\n### 12.5 Shapes to write (E.SHAPES data, docs/ASSETS.md format; check each with `node engine/tools/asset-sheet.mjs mine.js#id`)\n- **Vehicles** (also moving, drawn with `facing` each frame):\n  - `sedan`, `chevy` (Dana's beige Lumina)\n  - `van` (white Ford Econoline, county tags)\n  - `hearse` (black, long)\n  - `boxtruck` (white, red **HARSTAD AUTO PARTS** band: the text is a queued sign)\n  - `patrol` (white/blue with a light-bar box; the lights themselves are game lights)\n  - `montecarlo` (Rook's), `deadbuick` (flat tires), `burnedcar`\n- **Street:**\n  - `payphone` (pole, hood, handset)\n  - `busshelter`; `bench` (core)\n  - `trashbag`, `dumpster`; plus the engine props `trashcan`, `hydrant`, `firedrum`, `streetlamp`, `awning`, `sign`\n  - `stoop` (3 marble steps), `pole` (utility pole with a crossbar)\n  - `sawhorse`, `chainlink` (a 16-unit segment with posts and diamond mesh: a custom `E.PATTERNS.mesh`)\n  - `hoop` (basketball, chain net), `swings`, `gaspump`, `stroller`, `bike`, `coop` (pigeon coop), `mattress`\n- **Interiors:**\n  - `corkboard` (draws live Board state: `r.queue`), `desk` + `officechair` (cut `kenney-furniture:desk-corner`, `chair-desk` with `node engine/tools/asset-set.mjs`, or write them)\n  - `filecab`, `reel2reel` (reels drawn turning in `r.queue`), `crt`, `radiator`, `coffeemaker`, `watercooler`\n  - `table`/`chair`/`bookcase` (core), `judgedesk`, `sheetbody` (a covered body for the cold open)\n- **Signs** are `r.queue` boards: a dark panel plus `E.font.text`, lit by an emissive flag for neon (\"OPEN\", \"CHECKS CASHED\", \"WINGS · FRIES · SUBS\", \"SUDS CITY\", \"RIDLEY WIRELESS & PAGER\", \"MAMA B'S SOUL FOOD\", \"FADES & GRADES\"), plus a barber pole (stripes animated by time).\n\n### 12.6 World details that sell it\n- **Phone wires** (the motif): utility poles every 8 cells along alleys and the avenue. Between pole tops (z 70), draw 8-segment sagging catenaries with `px.line` in `r.queue` (sorted above roofs). **A pair of sneakers hangs on the wire over Gaither & Ridley.** Pigeons sit on the wire near Odessa's roof and scatter (flap) when someone runs below.\n- **Fake roofs** for walk-in interiors (the garage): an `r.queue` polygon with `footprint` that fades to 15% when Dana is inside or within 24 units of a door. The 1412 vacant has no roof (burned): draw charred beams.\n- **Vacants and decay:** plywood, a \"V\" spray mark, a mattress in the lot, the fire drum (flame prop, `light: true`) at night with two men warming their hands.\n- **Life:** a bus pulls up at P3 every 90 s (a bus shape drives the Ridley lane and stops 4 s); kids shoot hoops in daytime; Odessa sweeps her stoop at dawn.\n- **Felton's memorial** stays on his stoop through Ep5: candles, flowers, a photo. It gets smaller each episode.\n\n### 12.7 Title screen\n- **Scene:** the live iso diorama of the corner at night in rain (CornerSim with AI, no player), camera slowly turning (one 90° step every 20 s).\n- **Logo:** \"WIRETAP\" in `E.font.title` (scale 4, colors `['#fff6dc','#ffcf7a','#e08a2a']`, depth 3, depthColor `#3a1a0a`). A telephone wire runs behind the logo with sneakers hanging from it. Tagline \"Somebody's always listening.\"\n- **Menu:** `E.Menu` (canvas; keys, d-pad, stick, hover, click). `E.versionLabel()` tiny at the bottom right.\n- **Keep clear:** the top-right corner area.\n\n---\n\n## 13. About/Credits screen and the exit interview\n- **`credits.json` is the single source** of the About pages and of `exit-interview.json`. The build copies its `exitInterview` object verbatim into `../exit-interview.json` and verifies it parses.\n- **About & Credits** (title menu → DOM screen; L1/R1 pages; large type; at most about 10 short lines per page; stick scrolls long answers):\n  1. **Credits:**\n     - WIRETAP; \"An original game inspired by *The Wire* (HBO, 2002-2008). Not affiliated with HBO or the show's creators.\"\n     - Design and code: the model(s) that built it (truthfully: if the builder isn't claude-opus-5-5 at max effort, list both, e.g. \"Planned by Anthropic claude-opus-5-5 (max); built by <id>\").\n     - Engine: my-3D2dge v0.85.1 by Michael Crosato (MIT). Multiplayer: AI Hub Session Protocol v1, client 1.4.0.\n     - Any CC0 asset entries used (Kenney/KayKit via the engine's store), each with its source line.\n  2. **Source Information:** every field of TASK.md's list, same text as `exitInterview.sourceInformation`.\n  3. **Testing Feedback:** the 4 questions with answers.\n  4. **Engine Feedback:** the 6 questions with answers.\n  5. **Prompt Feedback:** the 4 questions with answers.\n- **Write \"unknown\" for anything you can't confirm.** Fill in real answers at the end of the build: no placeholders ship.\n- **Exit interview shape** (exactly TASK.md's). Suggested values to start from; correct any that turn out untrue:\n```json\n{\n  \"sourceInformation\": {\n    \"date\": \"2026-11-03 10:53\",\n    \"source\": \"The Wire (2002-2008)\",\n    \"genre\": \"Stealth investigation / crime drama with a corner-management sim and an asymmetric versus mode\",\n    \"perspective\": \"Isometric 2.5D (pixel-art 3D skeletons on a tile world); brawler-view interiors; HTML case-file screens\",\n    \"tech\": \"my-3D2dge v0.85.1 full engine (canvas 2D, optional WebGPU lighting); AI Hub session client 1.4.0; vanilla JavaScript; Web Audio\",\n    \"artDirection\": \"Engine-native retro-modern pixel art (PS1-era 2D look) pushed toward grit: sodium streetlight, rain, Formstone rowhouses, boarded vacants\",\n    \"animation\": \"Engine-native procedural Humanoid rigs (E.MOVES, poses, E.ACTIONS paired actions) plus custom joint post-processed poses; tweens and coroutine scripts\",\n    \"audio\": \"Code-written chip-synth music (engine music tracks, layered), synthesized effects and ambience, Web Audio formant gibberish voices with a telephone filter\",\n    \"online\": \"AI Hub Session Protocol v1, shared-world versus for 1-4 players (host-authoritative); local split-screen versus; no other network\",\n    \"testing\": \"<fill in: what you actually ran>\",\n    \"research\": \"my-3D2dge handoff docs (API.md, AI_GUIDE.md, ASSETS.md, kits) and the AI Hub protocol README; knowledge of the series from memory; no other web research\",\n    \"environment\": \"Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\",\n    \"model\": \"Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort max\",\n    \"usage\": \"unknown\"\n  },\n  \"testingFeedback\": [\"…\", \"…\", \"…\", \"…\"],\n  \"engineFeedback\": [\"…\", \"…\", \"…\", \"…\", \"…\", \"…\"],\n  \"promptFeedback\": [\"…\", \"…\", \"…\", \"…\"],\n  \"aiHub\": {\n    \"name\": \"WIRETAP\",\n    \"tagline\": \"Somebody's always listening.\",\n    \"description\": \"Work both sides of a West Baltimore corner in 2004: build a wiretap case one photo, page and phone call at a time, then run the corner the case is built on. Includes a 1-4 player cops-vs-corner versus mode.\",\n    \"type\": \"Game\",\n    \"genre\": \"Stealth\",\n    \"source\": \"The Wire (2002-2008)\",\n    \"series\": \"\",\n    \"players\": \"1–4\",\n    \"controls\": \"Stick/WASD move · L2/RMB watch · R2/LMB photo · ✕/E interact · △/Q partner · Create/Tab notebook\",\n    \"tags\": [\"story\", \"versus\", \"pixel art\", \"isometric\", \"crime\", \"detective\"]\n  }\n}\n```\n- **The build's final chat reply** must also contain Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback (TASK.md).\n\n---\n\n## 14. Build order and milestones\nBuild systems before content and one complete episode before breadth. **Each milestone ends with its tests green and a bundle that runs.**\n\n| M | Goal | Done when |\n|---|---|---|\n| **M0** Setup | Dev folder, engine and hub client fetched, `build.mjs`, `index.html`, `tests/headless.mjs` skeleton, blank title scene | The bundle opens with no errors; `node engine/tools/check.mjs <bundle>` passes; headless boot test passes |\n| **M1** Framework | Scenes skeleton; Controller classes; KEYS preset; settings (glyphs, stick inversion, difficulty, text speed, language, voices); canvas and DOM glyph rendering with device switching; DOM UI kit (focus nav, hover focus, legend); hover patch for E.Shell; save system; touch-only notice; About screen (rendering `credits.json`); **Voice synth prototype** (speak a line with 3 profiles, phone filter); music player with the 7 songs | Fake-gamepad test shows ✕ prompts and Xbox after switching; inversion test flips movement; the touch-only profile shows the notice; voice speaks in sync with a test dialog |\n| **M2** World | Neighborhood TileMap (App. A) with wall types, facades, floors, stoops, poles and wires, props, lights, weather, time presets; Annex map; camera rotate/zoom/peek; Dana moves (walk/run/crouch/blend); civilians with routines; FlowField cache | Screenshots of day/night/rain in 3 rotations look right (thumbnail test, check.mjs look notes acted on); 25 civilians walk 5 min without getting stuck (headless) |\n| **M3** Corner and eyes | CornerSim (all roles, sales, shutdown, ledger); perception/made; Watch, reads, photos and polaroids; HUD; interactables, cover, eavesdrop, barks | Headless: ledger invariants hold over 10 min; a careless bot gets made within 30 s; a careful bot reads 2 roles and gets 4 faces |\n| **M4** Episode 1 vertical slice | Director and mission runner; E.Story + Dialog with voices; Annex stations; Board; notebook; Pockets' shoe game; cold open; I1 as Tee (order wheel, code card, payphone keypad, count) | Ep1 playable start to finish with a pad and with keyboard+mouse; autosave/continue works; deep links `#ep1.*` reach every beat |\n| **M5** Episode 2 | Chase (escape graph, vault, tackle, cuff, ditch, search); box; cipher; affidavit and necessity; chambers; I2 | Headless chase bot catches Corey; box thresholds and lawyer rule; affidavit scoring and perjury detection; Ep2 playable |\n| **M6** Episode 3 | Wire room (scheduler, playback, minimize/spot-check, log, voice ID, pages, fast-forward, legal); van stakeout with van heat; dilemma; ops sweep; wall-off; code flip; Easy's scene (I3) | Wire session tests (legal increments, logging windows, ID); Ep3 playable on all branches |\n| **M7** Episode 4 | Tail (routes, acts, distance band, hand-off), trash stealth, kitchen talk, burners, session 3, I4 | Tail bot completes `teeDry`; Ep4 playable |\n| **M8** Episode 5 + endings | Raid, rescue, press conference, money tail with moving cone, long lens, the morning after, I5, montage rules, credits, Shut Down, episode select presets | The branch-matrix test (§16) produces a valid montage for every combination; story mode is complete |\n| **M9** Versus | VersusSim rules, roles, actions, scoring, bots, local split screen, results; then `HubTransport`, host loop, snapshots, interpolation, leave/time-up/end/server | A local bot match ends with a valid outcome; **hub harness passes** all four runs (§16) |\n| **M10** Attract and title | Attract reel (9 vignettes), idle detection, touch-only attract; title diorama; episode select; versus setup; full settings | Idle 10 s → attract; any input → title; all vignettes run 3 loops without errors |\n| **M11** Polish and ship | Balance pass (difficulty table), juice (particles, shake, stings), audio mix, writing pass against App. G, viewport/WebKit checks, final About content, bundle, exit interview | §17 checklist all ticked |\n\n**Content budgets** (to keep scope honest): at most ~90 dialogue lines per episode excluding wire calls; wire calls as in App. D; montage cards as in App. G. Write tight. The show's people say less than they mean.\n\n---\n\n## 15. Risks and how to de-risk them\n| # | Risk | Why it's risky | De-risk |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | **Scope** | Many systems and five episodes | Shared systems (one map, one CornerSim, one perception, one photo system everywhere); data-driven content; Ep1 slice by M4 proves the pipeline; content budgets; milestone gates |\n| 2 | **AI Hub shared-world passing the harness** (latency 150 / jitter 50 / loss 5, host leave, server) | Netcode bugs show up late | `LocalTransport` and a `LoopbackTransport` that simulates latency/loss in-process for headless tests; client-authoritative own movement (the arena example's pattern); message size asserts; run the real harness at the *start* of M9 with a minimal round (two dots moving, finish at 30 s), then grow |\n| 3 | **Wire room fun and readability** | Lots of text plus a clock | Few calls per session, short lines, 8 s rule shown as a visible ring, Rookie hints; deep link `#ep3.wire1` for fast iteration; thumbnail test |\n| 4 | **Voice synth** (quality, sync, CPU) | Custom Web Audio | Prototype in M1; fixed lookahead scheduling (`ctx.currentTime + 0.05`); fallback: the engine's `text` blip with per-profile pitch if formants misbehave in a browser |\n| 5 | **NPC simulation stability** | Stuck agents, flow-field cost, sorting | FlowField cache by POI; stuck rule; draw background civilians `every: 2`; invariant tests |\n| 6 | **Perception tuning** | Made too easily, or never | The target table in §5.2; the `?dev=1` overlay shows every suspicion value; careless/careful bot tests |\n| 7 | **10-foot UI and glyph switching** | Dense screens creep in | §4.5 rules; thumbnail test; fake-gamepad/mouse device-switch tests |\n| 8 | **Branch combinatorics** | Flags interacting | Few flags; endings by a rule table; episode presets; a branch-matrix headless test that runs every choice combination with action parts auto-resolved (`debug.autoResolve`) |\n| 9 | **Engine pitfalls** (heights, `cut`, sorting big shapes, iso facades, lighting cost) | New engine for most builders | Follow API.md's rules; `footprint` sorting for canopies and roofs; act on every `check.mjs` look note; keep the engine unmodified |\n| 10 | **Single-file bundling** | `</script>` in strings, the order of the hub client | The build checks; tests run against the bundle, not only the dev page |\n| 11 | **Gamepad wrapper side effects** | It overrides a browser API | `try/catch`, pass-through when both toggles are off, Playwright fake-pad test |\n| 12 | **Tone and sensitivity** | Gritty material about real communities | App. G writing guide: no slurs, everyone human, violence mostly offscreen with consequences, no glamor; a final writing pass |\n\n---\n\n## 16. Testing plan (lightweight and token-efficient)\n**Principles:**\n- Test rules headless (fast, exact, no screenshots).\n- Look at a *few* screenshots per milestone.\n- Run the hub harness only for versus.\n- Never paste big logs into context: print one PASS/FAIL line per test plus the first error.\n\n**Tools** (on this machine):\n- Node, Playwright 1.63 with Chromium/WebKit/Firefox.\n- `node engine/tools/check.mjs <page>#<deeplink>`: errors, a screenshot, look notes, `game.debug.snapshot()`.\n- `viewport-matrix <url>` (keep runs small: `--only` / `--devices`; don't run several at once). Real iOS Safari isn't available; WebKit with iPhone profiles is the closest check.\n- `python3 -m http.server` to serve the bundle and the harness side by side.\n\n**Hooks** (60-debug.js):\n- `game.debug.snapshot()` → `{ scene, ep, beat, meters, flags, dana:[x,y], objective, versus:{ev, cn, tl, sides} }`.\n- `game.debug.jump(beatId)`, `game.debug.autoResolve(on)` (missions and screens complete themselves with default good choices), `game.debug.bot(name)`.\n- Deep links: `#title`, `#attract`, `#about`, `#ep<N>.<beat>` (e.g. `#ep3.wire1`), `#versus.bots`, `#versus.local`.\n- `?dev=1` overlay: cells under the mouse, POIs, routes, suspicion numbers, agent states, F9 toggles it.\n\n**`tests/headless.mjs`** loads `engine/my-3d2dge.js` and the bundled game script into a Node `vm` context with the stand-ins from `engine/kits/test.mjs` (`window`, `addEventListener`, `location`), then runs:\n\n| Test | Asserts |\n|---|---|\n| boot | Boot steps finish; `validateData()` reports 0 problems; `game.errors.length === 0` |\n| cipher | CW/CCW are permutations and inverses; App. C's 5 pages decode to App. C's numbers; the flip page decodes with the other turn |\n| photo scoring | Fixture cases: back turned = no ★Face; 230 units = blurry; act window = ★Act; burned = 0 |\n| perception | Careless bot (stare at a lookout from 60) made in ≤ 6 s; careful bot (walk past) never noticed; blending at 100 for 30 s never made |\n| corner ledger | 10 min of sim: vial and cash conservation hold; shutdown freezes sales; re-up triggers below 30 |\n| chase | Bot pursuer with good routing catches the runner within 60 s; the ditch happens; the kid takes it after 45 s if it's not searched |\n| tail | A careful bot completes `teeDry`; a bot that stops on every `lookBack` gets made |\n| box | Thresholds unlock B1-B3; Fear ≥ 80 → lawyer; the Lean → Offer combo; flip only at B3 with Fear ≤ 60 |\n| paper | PC sums per line; a false necessity tick is always asked and denies |\n| wire | Non-pertinent past the window adds Legal 4/s; a minimized pertinent line is lost; spot-check timing; LOG windows; voice ID links the number |\n| meters | Brass 0 → shutdown scene; Heat thresholds flip the code and add lookouts |\n| branch matrix | With `autoResolve`, every combination of dilemma × sweep × wallOff × lossOn × canary × path × I5 reaches the montage with 9-11 valid cards |\n| save/load | Save at `ep3.van`, new game instance on the same storage, CONTINUE → same beat and STATE |\n| versus | A bots-only local match ends with a valid outcome; host rules (burn, tap, jump-out) apply; snapshot JSON < 1,100 bytes at the 45-entity worst case; `LoopbackTransport` at 150 ms ±50 and 5% loss still converges |\n| attract | 10.1 s idle on the title → `attract`; one `input.press` → `title`; 3 loops of the reel with no errors |\n\n**`tests/browser.mjs`** (Playwright, one browser at a time):\n1. **Gamepad:** an init script defines a fake standard gamepad (`navigator.getGamepads` returns a DualSense-like id with buttons and axes). Assert the HUD prompt reads ✕; switch Settings → Xbox → it reads A; enable `stickInvX`, push axis0 = +1 → Dana moves left (−x).\n2. **Mouse:** hover a main-menu item → it gets focus; click → it activates; the legend shows mouse/key glyphs.\n3. **Touch-only:** an iPhone profile (WebKit) shows the notice and a Settings button; after 10 s attract runs; a tap returns.\n4. **Screens:** 8 screenshots via deep links at 1920×1080 (title, `ep1.photos`, `ep3.wire1`, Board, box, versus local split, about, montage). Look at each once; apply the thumbnail test (downscale to 480×270).\n\n**Viewport sweep** (once, at M11): `viewport-matrix http://localhost:8000/<bundle> --only phone,tablet,desktop --engines chromium,webkit -o /tmp/viewport-matrix/wiretap`. Expect: phones show the touch-only notice; desktop sizes (16:9, 21:9, 4:3) fill edge to edge with the HUD inside the safe areas; no horizontal overflow; no console errors.\n\n**AI Hub harness** (`tests/hub/hub-check.mjs`): serve `tests/hub/` with the bundle copied in. Open in Playwright and wait for `document.body.dataset.complete === 'true'`, then assert `window.__hubCheck.pass === true` for:\n1. `harness.html?game=<bundle>&players=2&auto=1`\n2. `…&players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1`\n3. `…&players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1&scenario=host-leave`\n4. `…&players=2&scenario=server&auto=1`\n\nAlso open the bundle outside a session: it must still reach the title.\n\n**When to run:** headless after every change to a system; browser screens at the end of each milestone; viewport sweep and hub harness at M9 and M11.\n\n---\n\n## 17. Definition of done (tick every line before shipping)\n- [ ] Title is **WIRETAP** (RNG-picked, §0); the bundle is `Wiretap-TheWire-claude-opus-5-5-max-20261103-105319.html` in `work/`; the dev folder holds sources, tools and tests; `exit-interview.json` sits next to the html and parses.\n- [ ] One html file runs offline: the engine and hub client inlined, no runtime network, no external fonts.\n- [ ] Genre/perspective as §2; engine-native art and animation, extended (§12); all music, effects and gibberish voices written in code (§11).\n- [ ] **Story mode:** 5 episodes, 4 interludes + finale interlude, both finale paths, Shut Down, montage with computed cards, credits, episode select, continue/autosave.\n- [ ] **Every system in §5-§7 is reachable in normal play**, with no TODOs, placeholders or stubs. Each one appears in the feature matrix (App. J.6) at least once.\n- [ ] **Versus:** local (1 human vs bots; 2 humans split screen) and AI Hub shared-world (1-4). All four harness runs pass, and the game runs outside a session.\n- [ ] **Attract:** 10 s idle on title/menus → bot-played reel; any input exits; it runs on touch-only devices.\n- [ ] **10-foot UX:** controller-first; keyboard+mouse native (hover focuses, click selects, mouse aims and clicks world objects); prompts follow the last device; PlayStation glyphs by default with an Xbox option; **stick inversion toggles** for both axes; no dense data screens; thumbnail test passes.\n- [ ] **Touch-only:** no touch controls; \"Controller or keyboard required\" with a Settings button; attract allowed.\n- [ ] Standard engine features only (no custom pause/settings/rebinding/full screen); E.Shell HUD; standard settings plus the §4.7 game settings.\n- [ ] **About/Credits** screen with Credits, Source Information, Testing, Engine and Prompt Feedback, matching `exit-interview.json`; \"unknown\" where unconfirmed.\n- [ ] Headless suite green; browser checks looked at; hub harness passes; WebKit check done.\n- [ ] Writing pass done against App. G (tone, no slurs, no quotes from the show).\n\nEOF\nwc -c /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-105319/work/PLAN.md","description":"Append audio, art, credits, milestones, risks, testing, done sections"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NggFuotUhAPe1sdYxWjvZM","type":"tool_result","content":"123107 /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-105319/work/PLAN.md\n[This command modified 1 file you've previously read: PLAN.md. Call Read before editing.]","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e2aa65a8-ee1a-45c4-b8e6-f96cf188e23d","uuid":"5514a370-cf08-46db-8181-2c3da6a75ea2","timestamp":"2026-11-03T18:40:24.995Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"123107 /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-105319/work/PLAN.md","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"staleReadFileStateHint":"[This command modified 1 file you've previously read: PLAN.md. Call Read before editing.]","bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-105319/work/PLAN.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":896,"oldLines":3,"newStart":896,"newLines":325,"lines":[" "," - **Implementation:** each entry is `{ id, seconds, setup(), tick(dt), caption }`. `setup()` loads a mission/scene with `attract: true`: no saves, no tutorials, no autosave, quieter music, no HUD prompts. The attract scene owns the clock and calls `game.go` for the next entry with a short dissolve."," ","+---","+","+## 11. Audio (03-audio.js): all written in code","+","+### 11.1 Music (engine `game.audio.music`, scores in App. H)","+| Song | Plays | Layers (start `on: false`, faded with `audio.layer(name, vol, fade)`) |","+|---|---|---|","+| `theme` (84 bpm, A minor) | title, menus, about, credits, episode cards (as a `sting` of its last 2 bars) | — |","+| `field` (92 bpm, D minor) | field missions as Dana | `tension` while any observer is at `notice`+ toward Dana; `pulse` at `search`; `alarm`+`stab` for 8 s after MADE |","+| `corner` (95 bpm, G minor) | interludes as Tee; diegetic: also from a parked car's open door during Ep1-2 nights (volume by distance) | `lead` while the count is ahead of target pace |","+| `wire` (70 bpm, E minor) | wire room, evidence cage | `pulse` while a pertinent call is live |","+| `chase` (132 bpm) | foot chase, raid reactions, the 60-s rescue | — |","+| `montage` (68 bpm) | epilogue montage, Shut Down | — |","+| `versus` (104 bpm, C minor) | versus rounds | `pressure` at Evidence ≥ 50; `clock` in the last 60 s; `cash` at Count ≥ $2,000 |","+","+- **Stings** (`audio.sting`, `{ at: 'beat' }`):","+  - `made`: square A4 F4 D4, 0.12 s each","+  - `photoGood`: triangle E5 then B5","+  - `casePoint`: triangle C5 E5 G5 arp","+  - `beatDone`: the theme's last bar","+- **Ducking:** call `audio.duck(true)` while dialogue voices play.","+- **Field realism:** music volume in field missions is 0.6× the setting, so the ambience carries the street.","+","+### 11.2 Sound effects (`audio.define(name, voice)`; engine voice format)","+| Name | Recipe |","+|---|---|","+| `shutter` | `[{wave:'noise',freq:3000,dur:.03,vol:.25},{wave:'square',freq:1800,to:900,dur:.05,vol:.08}]`, then `whirr` `{wave:'saw',freq:220,to:320,dur:.18,vol:.04}` after 40 ms |","+| `pager` | three `{wave:'square',freq:'A6',dur:.07,vol:.1}` 110 ms apart, preceded by `{wave:'square',freq:'E6',dur:.07}` |","+| `dtmf_<d>` | two sines at the DTMF row/column pair (697/770/852/941 × 1209/1336/1477 Hz), 0.12 s, vol .08 |","+| `dialtone` / `ringback` | 350+440 Hz sines (loop); 440+480 Hz, 2 s on / 4 s off |","+| `phonering` | `{wave:'square',freq:1250,vib:[22,.06],dur:.9,vol:.06}` twice |","+| `reel` | noise 0.02 s click (tape start/stop); the `tape` bed is low noise while recording |","+| `siren` | sine 650→1300→650 over 3.6 s (wail, loop); `yelp`: 700↔1500 at 8 Hz for 1.2 s |","+| `radio` | noise burst 0.08 + squelch click (radio chatter in/out) |","+| `cuffs` | `{wave:'square',freq:2400,to:1800,dur:.03,vol:.12}` ×2, 60 ms apart |","+| `fence` | noise 0.22 s with vibrato (chain-link rattle on a vault) |","+| `doorRam` | `boom` preset at pitch 0.7, plus `game.shake(4)` |","+| `gunshot` | noise 0.18 s vol .45 + `boom` tail + an echo at −10 dB after 130 ms. Used exactly twice in the game (Ep3 robbery warning shot if *Go in*, and offscreen in I3 if Rook goes after Sunday) |","+| `bark` (dog) | `{wave:'saw',freq:320,to:180,dur:.12,vol:.12}` ×2 |","+| `coo` / `flap` | sine 420→380 with vibrato 0.35 s; noise bursts for wings (Pigeon's roof) |","+| `busbrake` | noise hiss 0.9 s + sine squeal 2200 Hz 0.3 s |","+| `typekey` / `typebell` | noise 0.015 s at 4 kHz; `blip` at a line end (affidavit) |","+| `stamp` | `land` preset + paper noise (judge signs) |","+| `pin` / `string` | square 900→700, 0.03 s; soft noise 0.08 s |","+| `cashflick` | noise 0.01 s, repeated for the count |","+| `ui_tick` / `ui_ok` / `ui_back` | triangle 1400 Hz 0.02 s vol .05; engine `confirm`; engine `cancel` |","+| `step_*` | engine `step` at pitch by floor tag: concrete 1.0, asphalt 0.9, alley 0.85 + grit, grass 0.7, wood (Annex) 1.1 |","+","+### 11.3 Ambience beds and voices","+- **Ambience** is built on `game.audio.ctx` from looping noise buffers and filters. Route it into the engine's sfx bus (`game.audio._sfxBus`, an internal field: check it exists, otherwise use your own gain scaled by `volume × sfxVolume × !muted`).","+  - **Street day:** low-passed traffic rumble; a bus every 60-90 s.","+  - **Street night:** traffic, plus far sirens and dog barks every 40-90 s.","+  - **Rain:** band-passed noise, with thunder from engine weather.","+  - **Annex:** HVAC hum, a phone ringing far off.","+  - **Wire room:** tape hiss, radiator clank every 20 s, clock.","+  - **Box:** 120 Hz fluorescent hum.","+  - **Chambers:** clock tick.","+- **Voices: Animalese/\"Simlish\" synth** (`Voice.speak(text, profile, { onChar, filter })`):","+  - **Syllables:** split the text into syllables (consonant cluster + vowel); punctuation is a pause (`,` 120 ms, `.?!` 260 ms). Each syllable is a 60-80 ms grain at `profile.rate` syllables/s.","+  - **Source:** an oscillator (`profile.wave`) at pitch `base × (1 + range × contour)`. The contour falls across a sentence, rises at the end of a `?`, and adds a per-syllable offset **seeded by the syllable's letters**, so the same word always sounds the same.","+  - **Filters:** two parallel band-pass formant filters (F1/F2 per vowel: a 800/1200, e 400/2300, i 300/2700, o 450/800, u 325/700, all × `formant`, Q≈9), then an envelope (attack 5 ms, release to 0 by grain end).","+  - **Consonants:** plosives (b d g k p t c q) are 12 ms noise bursts; fricatives (f s z h x j v) are 40 ms band-passed noise (2-6 kHz); nasals (m n) are a 60 ms low hum.","+  - **Breath:** noise mixed in at `profile.breath`.","+  - **Tics:** `stammer` (repeat the first syllable of 30% of words: Corey), `vibrato` (Odessa).","+  - **Sync with text:**","+    - `E.Dialog`: set `talk.voice = null`. Each update, play syllables for the letters added since `talk.shown` last frame. Pick the profile by `talk.name`. The text speed setting sets `talk.speed`.","+    - The wire transcript is driven by `Voice.speak` itself (`onChar` reveals letters).","+  - **Phone filter** (wire calls, payphone conversations): high-pass 300 Hz → low-pass 3400 Hz → a gentle `WaveShaper` → plus line hiss at −32 dB. **Radio filter** (police radio): band-pass 500-2500 Hz + squelch clicks at the start and end.","+  - **Bleeped words** (Strong language: Bleeped) get a 1 kHz sine over their syllables.","+  - **Voice volume** setting multiplies the voice bus.","+  - **Headless:** no-op.","+","+---","+","+## 12. Art direction and world building (05-world.js, 06-people.js)","+","+### 12.1 Mood by time of day (canvas lighting always; GPU lighting where available for night, `game.enableGPU({ map })`, with the same ambient set on both)","+| Preset | Ambient / tint | Lights | Weather |","+|---|---|---|---|","+| `dawnRain` (cold open) | .45, blue-gray | patrol light bars (red/blue lights alternating at 2 Hz, radius 70), streetlamps fading | rain .7, wind .2 |","+| `day` | lights off (full bright), slightly desaturated palette | none | none |","+| `dusk` | .62, orange-violet | streetlamps flicker on at 17:40 | none |","+| `night` | .38, cool blue | streetlamps every 6 cells (`r.prop('streetlamp', …, { light: true, cone: true })`, color `#ffb04a`); lit windows; store signs emissive; TV-blue flicker in 1 window per block | none or rain (Ep4) |","+","+### 12.2 Wall types (App. A legend). Everything gets `cut: true` except low walls.","+| Char | What | h | Face / roof | Facade options | Colors (top/side) |","+|---|---|---|---|---|---|","+| `#` | boundary rowhouses/warehouses | 56 | brick / slab | windows `{ lit: .15 }` | `#3a2a26` / `#5a3a30` |","+| `R` | brick rowhouse | 40 | brick / slab | windows `{ lit: .25 }`, door `{ chance: .35, color: '#4a2a1e' }` | `#4a3a34` / `#7a3b2e` |","+| `F` | Formstone rowhouse | 40 | material `formstone` = `'#8a8680 stones size=5'` / slab | windows `{ lit: .25 }`, door .35 | `#4a4844` / `#8a8680` |","+| `P` | painted brick | 36 | plaster / slab | windows `{ lit: .3 }`, shutters `#3a5a6a` | `#5a5048` / `#b8a27a` or `#6a7f8f` (alternate by block) |","+| `V` | vacant | 40 | brick (dark) / slab | `decorate`: plywood panels `#b08a5a` over window and door spans, spray-paint tags | `#3a2a24` / `#4a2e26` |","+| `S L E M $ K B Q` | storefronts | 32 | brick or plaster / slab | `decorate`: a lit display-window band (z 4-18, warm `#ffd890` glow texels), a sign band (z 20-28); the sign text is an `r.queue` board (§12.5) | per store |","+| `H` / `T` | church / bell tower | 64 / 88 | stone / slab | arch windows `{ chance: 1 }`, stained glass `window` props on the Ridley side | `#5a5650` / `#8a847a` |","+| `C` | Delancey Courts | 44 | brick (tan `#9a7a5a`) / slab | windows grid `{ lit: .35 }`, doors .3, balcony walkway `{ z: 22 }` | `#5a4a3a` / `#9a7a5a` |","+| `G` | garage | 24 | metal (corrugated `'#6a6a6a metal'`) / plain | roll-up door painted on the east face | `#4a4a4a` / `#6a6a6a` |","+| `k` | gas kiosk | 20 | plaster white with red band (decorate) | | `#d8d8d0` / `#e8e8e0` |","+","+### 12.3 Floors (legend values `{ floor: tag }`; `floorTex` per tag, or `floorMats`)","+| Char | Tag | Look |","+|---|---|---|","+| `.` | `walk` | concrete slabs (1-cell grid lines `#8a8a86`/`#7a7a76`, cracks); stoops (shapes) along rowhouse fronts |","+| `=` | `road` | asphalt `#2e2e32` with speckle; Ridley's dashed yellow center line; crosswalk stripes at intersections; manholes; puddles when raining (darker glossy patches with a GPU glow texel picking up lamp color) |","+| `-` | `alley` | cracked asphalt `#3a3836`, weeds in cracks, litter sprites |","+| `,` | `lot` | dirt + weeds (`E.tex.dirt` + grass props) |","+| `:` | `court` | courtyard pavers |","+| `b` | `ball` | court asphalt with painted lines |","+| `p` | `play` | rubber play surface (faded red) |","+| `v` | `vacant` | gutted floorboards, debris |","+| `g` | `garage` | oil-stained concrete |","+| `f` | `fence` | blocked floor cell; draw chain-link shapes on its edges (vaultable by a jump: §5.6) |","+| `x` | `edge` | blocked; sawhorse barricades (map exits) |","+","+### 12.4 People and palettes","+- **Cast looks:** §8.2. Skin tones span a realistic range (`#3a2418 #4a2e20 #5a3a28 #6b4630 #8a5a3c #c8946a #e0b89a #f0c8a8`). Baltimore's West Side is mostly Black, so the cast and crowds reflect that, drawn with dignity. No caricature.","+- **2004 clothes:** oversized white tees, throwback jerseys, puffy coats, hoodies, fitted caps, do-rags, Timberlands, Air Force 1s; church clothes on Odessa's friends; work uniforms; cops in windbreakers and khakis or blazers.","+- **Civilians:** 6 palette families (warm, cool, earth, sport, church, work). Seeded per NPC.","+- **Addicts:** thinner (`hunch .3`), mismatched layers. Shown as people, not monsters.","+","+### 12.5 Shapes to write (E.SHAPES data, docs/ASSETS.md format; check each with `node engine/tools/asset-sheet.mjs mine.js#id`)","+- **Vehicles** (also moving, drawn with `facing` each frame):","+  - `sedan`, `chevy` (Dana's beige Lumina)","+  - `van` (white Ford Econoline, county tags)","+  - `hearse` (black, long)","+  - `boxtruck` (white, red **HARSTAD AUTO PARTS** band: the text is a queued sign)","+  - `patrol` (white/blue with a light-bar box; the lights themselves are game lights)","+  - `montecarlo` (Rook's), `deadbuick` (flat tires), `burnedcar`","+- **Street:**","+  - `payphone` (pole, hood, handset)","+  - `busshelter`; `bench` (core)","+  - `trashbag`, `dumpster`; plus the engine props `trashcan`, `hydrant`, `firedrum`, `streetlamp`, `awning`, `sign`","+  - `stoop` (3 marble steps), `pole` (utility pole with a crossbar)","+  - `sawhorse`, `chainlink` (a 16-unit segment with posts and diamond mesh: a custom `E.PATTERNS.mesh`)","+  - `hoop` (basketball, chain net), `swings`, `gaspump`, `stroller`, `bike`, `coop` (pigeon coop), `mattress`","+- **Interiors:**","+  - `corkboard` (draws live Board state: `r.queue`), `desk` + `officechair` (cut `kenney-furniture:desk-corner`, `chair-desk` with `node engine/tools/asset-set.mjs`, or write them)","+  - `filecab`, `reel2reel` (reels drawn turning in `r.queue`), `crt`, `radiator`, `coffeemaker`, `watercooler`","+  - `table`/`chair`/`bookcase` (core), `judgedesk`, `sheetbody` (a covered body for the cold open)","+- **Signs** are `r.queue` boards: a dark panel plus `E.font.text`, lit by an emissive flag for neon (\"OPEN\", \"CHECKS CASHED\", \"WINGS · FRIES · SUBS\", \"SUDS CITY\", \"RIDLEY WIRELESS & PAGER\", \"MAMA B'S SOUL FOOD\", \"FADES & GRADES\"), plus a barber pole (stripes animated by time).","+","+### 12.6 World details that sell it","+- **Phone wires** (the motif): utility poles every 8 cells along alleys and the avenue. Between pole tops (z 70), draw 8-segment sagging catenaries with `px.line` in `r.queue` (sorted above roofs). **A pair of sneakers hangs on the wire over Gaither & Ridley.** Pigeons sit on the wire near Odessa's roof and scatter (flap) when someone runs below.","+- **Fake roofs** for walk-in interiors (the garage): an `r.queue` polygon with `footprint` that fades to 15% when Dana is inside or within 24 units of a door. The 1412 vacant has no roof (burned): draw charred beams.","+- **Vacants and decay:** plywood, a \"V\" spray mark, a mattress in the lot, the fire drum (flame prop, `light: true`) at night with two men warming their hands.","+- **Life:** a bus pulls up at P3 every 90 s (a bus shape drives the Ridley lane and stops 4 s); kids shoot hoops in daytime; Odessa sweeps her stoop at dawn.","+- **Felton's memorial** stays on his stoop through Ep5: candles, flowers, a photo. It gets smaller each episode.","+","+### 12.7 Title screen","+- **Scene:** the live iso diorama of the corner at night in rain (CornerSim with AI, no player), camera slowly turning (one 90° step every 20 s).","+- **Logo:** \"WIRETAP\" in `E.font.title` (scale 4, colors `['#fff6dc','#ffcf7a','#e08a2a']`, depth 3, depthColor `#3a1a0a`). A telephone wire runs behind the logo with sneakers hanging from it. Tagline \"Somebody's always listening.\"","+- **Menu:** `E.Menu` (canvas; keys, d-pad, stick, hover, click). `E.versionLabel()` tiny at the bottom right.","+- **Keep clear:** the top-right corner area.","+","+---","+","+## 13. About/Credits screen and the exit interview","+- **`credits.json` is the single source** of the About pages and of `exit-interview.json`. The build copies its `exitInterview` object verbatim into `../exit-interview.json` and verifies it parses.","+- **About & Credits** (title menu → DOM screen; L1/R1 pages; large type; at most about 10 short lines per page; stick scrolls long answers):","+  1. **Credits:**","+     - WIRETAP; \"An original game inspired by *The Wire* (HBO, 2002-2008). Not affiliated with HBO or the show's creators.\"","+     - Design and code: the model(s) that built it (truthfully: if the builder isn't claude-opus-5-5 at max effort, list both, e.g. \"Planned by Anthropic claude-opus-5-5 (max); built by <id>\").","+     - Engine: my-3D2dge v0.85.1 by Michael Crosato (MIT). Multiplayer: AI Hub Session Protocol v1, client 1.4.0.","+     - Any CC0 asset entries used (Kenney/KayKit via the engine's store), each with its source line.","+  2. **Source Information:** every field of TASK.md's list, same text as `exitInterview.sourceInformation`.","+  3. **Testing Feedback:** the 4 questions with answers.","+  4. **Engine Feedback:** the 6 questions with answers.","+  5. **Prompt Feedback:** the 4 questions with answers.","+- **Write \"unknown\" for anything you can't confirm.** Fill in real answers at the end of the build: no placeholders ship.","+- **Exit interview shape** (exactly TASK.md's). Suggested values to start from; correct any that turn out untrue:","+```json","+{","+  \"sourceInformation\": {","+    \"date\": \"2026-11-03 10:53\",","+    \"source\": \"The Wire (2002-2008)\",","+    \"genre\": \"Stealth investigation / crime drama with a corner-management sim and an asymmetric versus mode\",","+    \"perspective\": \"Isometric 2.5D (pixel-art 3D skeletons on a tile world); brawler-view interiors; HTML case-file screens\",","+    \"tech\": \"my-3D2dge v0.85.1 full engine (canvas 2D, optional WebGPU lighting); AI Hub session client 1.4.0; vanilla JavaScript; Web Audio\",","+    \"artDirection\": \"Engine-native retro-modern pixel art (PS1-era 2D look) pushed toward grit: sodium streetlight, rain, Formstone rowhouses, boarded vacants\",","+    \"animation\": \"Engine-native procedural Humanoid rigs (E.MOVES, poses, E.ACTIONS paired actions) plus custom joint post-processed poses; tweens and coroutine scripts\",","+    \"audio\": \"Code-written chip-synth music (engine music tracks, layered), synthesized effects and ambience, Web Audio formant gibberish voices with a telephone filter\",","+    \"online\": \"AI Hub Session Protocol v1, shared-world versus for 1-4 players (host-authoritative); local split-screen versus; no other network\",","+    \"testing\": \"<fill in: what you actually ran>\",","+    \"research\": \"my-3D2dge handoff docs (API.md, AI_GUIDE.md, ASSETS.md, kits) and the AI Hub protocol README; knowledge of the series from memory; no other web research\",","+    \"environment\": \"Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\",","+    \"model\": \"Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort max\",","+    \"usage\": \"unknown\"","+  },","+  \"testingFeedback\": [\"…\", \"…\", \"…\", \"…\"],","+  \"engineFeedback\": [\"…\", \"…\", \"…\", \"…\", \"…\", \"…\"],","+  \"promptFeedback\": [\"…\", \"…\", \"…\", \"…\"],","+  \"aiHub\": {","+    \"name\": \"WIRETAP\",","+    \"tagline\": \"Somebody's always listening.\",","+    \"description\": \"Work both sides of a West Baltimore corner in 2004: build a wiretap case one photo, page and phone call at a time, then run the corner the case is built on. Includes a 1-4 player cops-vs-corner versus mode.\",","+    \"type\": \"Game\",","+    \"genre\": \"Stealth\",","+    \"source\": \"The Wire (2002-2008)\",","+    \"series\": \"\",","+    \"players\": \"1–4\",","+    \"controls\": \"Stick/WASD move · L2/RMB watch · R2/LMB photo · ✕/E interact · △/Q partner · Create/Tab notebook\",","+    \"tags\": [\"story\", \"versus\", \"pixel art\", \"isometric\", \"crime\", \"detective\"]","+  }","+}","+```","+- **The build's final chat reply** must also contain Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback (TASK.md).","+","+---","+","+## 14. Build order and milestones","+Build systems before content and one complete episode before breadth. **Each milestone ends with its tests green and a bundle that runs.**","+","+| M | Goal | Done when |","+|---|---|---|","+| **M0** Setup | Dev folder, engine and hub client fetched, `build.mjs`, `index.html`, `tests/headless.mjs` skeleton, blank title scene | The bundle opens with no errors; `node engine/tools/check.mjs <bundle>` passes; headless boot test passes |","+| **M1** Framework | Scenes skeleton; Controller classes; KEYS preset; settings (glyphs, stick inversion, difficulty, text speed, language, voices); canvas and DOM glyph rendering with device switching; DOM UI kit (focus nav, hover focus, legend); hover patch for E.Shell; save system; touch-only notice; About screen (rendering `credits.json`); **Voice synth prototype** (speak a line with 3 profiles, phone filter); music player with the 7 songs | Fake-gamepad test shows ✕ prompts and Xbox after switching; inversion test flips movement; the touch-only profile shows the notice; voice speaks in sync with a test dialog |","+| **M2** World | Neighborhood TileMap (App. A) with wall types, facades, floors, stoops, poles and wires, props, lights, weather, time presets; Annex map; camera rotate/zoom/peek; Dana moves (walk/run/crouch/blend); civilians with routines; FlowField cache | Screenshots of day/night/rain in 3 rotations look right (thumbnail test, check.mjs look notes acted on); 25 civilians walk 5 min without getting stuck (headless) |","+| **M3** Corner and eyes | CornerSim (all roles, sales, shutdown, ledger); perception/made; Watch, reads, photos and polaroids; HUD; interactables, cover, eavesdrop, barks | Headless: ledger invariants hold over 10 min; a careless bot gets made within 30 s; a careful bot reads 2 roles and gets 4 faces |","+| **M4** Episode 1 vertical slice | Director and mission runner; E.Story + Dialog with voices; Annex stations; Board; notebook; Pockets' shoe game; cold open; I1 as Tee (order wheel, code card, payphone keypad, count) | Ep1 playable start to finish with a pad and with keyboard+mouse; autosave/continue works; deep links `#ep1.*` reach every beat |","+| **M5** Episode 2 | Chase (escape graph, vault, tackle, cuff, ditch, search); box; cipher; affidavit and necessity; chambers; I2 | Headless chase bot catches Corey; box thresholds and lawyer rule; affidavit scoring and perjury detection; Ep2 playable |","+| **M6** Episode 3 | Wire room (scheduler, playback, minimize/spot-check, log, voice ID, pages, fast-forward, legal); van stakeout with van heat; dilemma; ops sweep; wall-off; code flip; Easy's scene (I3) | Wire session tests (legal increments, logging windows, ID); Ep3 playable on all branches |","+| **M7** Episode 4 | Tail (routes, acts, distance band, hand-off), trash stealth, kitchen talk, burners, session 3, I4 | Tail bot completes `teeDry`; Ep4 playable |","+| **M8** Episode 5 + endings | Raid, rescue, press conference, money tail with moving cone, long lens, the morning after, I5, montage rules, credits, Shut Down, episode select presets | The branch-matrix test (§16) produces a valid montage for every combination; story mode is complete |","+| **M9** Versus | VersusSim rules, roles, actions, scoring, bots, local split screen, results; then `HubTransport`, host loop, snapshots, interpolation, leave/time-up/end/server | A local bot match ends with a valid outcome; **hub harness passes** all four runs (§16) |","+| **M10** Attract and title | Attract reel (9 vignettes), idle detection, touch-only attract; title diorama; episode select; versus setup; full settings | Idle 10 s → attract; any input → title; all vignettes run 3 loops without errors |","+| **M11** Polish and ship | Balance pass (difficulty table), juice (particles, shake, stings), audio mix, writing pass against App. G, viewport/WebKit checks, final About content, bundle, exit interview | §17 checklist all ticked |","+","+**Content budgets** (to keep scope honest): at most ~90 dialogue lines per episode excluding wire calls; wire calls as in App. D; montage cards as in App. G. Write tight. The show's people say less than they mean.","+","+---","+","+## 15. Risks and how to de-risk them","+| # | Risk | Why it's risky | De-risk |","+|---|---|---|---|","+| 1 | **Scope** | Many systems and five episodes | Shared systems (one map, one CornerSim, one perception, one photo system everywhere); data-driven content; Ep1 slice by M4 proves the pipeline; content budgets; milestone gates |","+| 2 | **AI Hub shared-world passing the harness** (latency 150 / jitter 50 / loss 5, host leave, server) | Netcode bugs show up late | `LocalTransport` and a `LoopbackTransport` that simulates latency/loss in-process for headless tests; client-authoritative own movement (the arena example's pattern); message size asserts; run the real harness at the *start* of M9 with a minimal round (two dots moving, finish at 30 s), then grow |","+| 3 | **Wire room fun and readability** | Lots of text plus a clock | Few calls per session, short lines, 8 s rule shown as a visible ring, Rookie hints; deep link `#ep3.wire1` for fast iteration; thumbnail test |","+| 4 | **Voice synth** (quality, sync, CPU) | Custom Web Audio | Prototype in M1; fixed lookahead scheduling (`ctx.currentTime + 0.05`); fallback: the engine's `text` blip with per-profile pitch if formants misbehave in a browser |","+| 5 | **NPC simulation stability** | Stuck agents, flow-field cost, sorting | FlowField cache by POI; stuck rule; draw background civilians `every: 2`; invariant tests |","+| 6 | **Perception tuning** | Made too easily, or never | The target table in §5.2; the `?dev=1` overlay shows every suspicion value; careless/careful bot tests |","+| 7 | **10-foot UI and glyph switching** | Dense screens creep in | §4.5 rules; thumbnail test; fake-gamepad/mouse device-switch tests |","+| 8 | **Branch combinatorics** | Flags interacting | Few flags; endings by a rule table; episode presets; a branch-matrix headless test that runs every choice combination with action parts auto-resolved (`debug.autoResolve`) |","+| 9 | **Engine pitfalls** (heights, `cut`, sorting big shapes, iso facades, lighting cost) | New engine for most builders | Follow API.md's rules; `footprint` sorting for canopies and roofs; act on every `check.mjs` look note; keep the engine unmodified |","+| 10 | **Single-file bundling** | `</script>` in strings, the order of the hub client | The build checks; tests run against the bundle, not only the dev page |","+| 11 | **Gamepad wrapper side effects** | It overrides a browser API | `try/catch`, pass-through when both toggles are off, Playwright fake-pad test |","+| 12 | **Tone and sensitivity** | Gritty material about real communities | App. G writing guide: no slurs, everyone human, violence mostly offscreen with consequences, no glamor; a final writing pass |","+","+---","+","+## 16. Testing plan (lightweight and token-efficient)","+**Principles:**","+- Test rules headless (fast, exact, no screenshots).","+- Look at a *few* screenshots per milestone.","+- Run the hub harness only for versus.","+- Never paste big logs into context: print one PASS/FAIL line per test plus the first error.","+","+**Tools** (on this machine):","+- Node, Playwright 1.63 with Chromium/WebKit/Firefox.","+- `node engine/tools/check.mjs <page>#<deeplink>`: errors, a screenshot, look notes, `game.debug.snapshot()`.","+- `viewport-matrix <url>` (keep runs small: `--only` / `--devices`; don't run several at once). Real iOS Safari isn't available; WebKit with iPhone profiles is the closest check.","+- `python3 -m http.server` to serve the bundle and the harness side by side.","+","+**Hooks** (60-debug.js):","+- `game.debug.snapshot()` → `{ scene, ep, beat, meters, flags, dana:[x,y], objective, versus:{ev, cn, tl, sides} }`.","+- `game.debug.jump(beatId)`, `game.debug.autoResolve(on)` (missions and screens complete themselves with default good choices), `game.debug.bot(name)`.","+- Deep links: `#title`, `#attract`, `#about`, `#ep<N>.<beat>` (e.g. `#ep3.wire1`), `#versus.bots`, `#versus.local`.","+- `?dev=1` overlay: cells under the mouse, POIs, routes, suspicion numbers, agent states, F9 toggles it.","+","+**`tests/headless.mjs`** loads `engine/my-3d2dge.js` and the bundled game script into a Node `vm` context with the stand-ins from `engine/kits/test.mjs` (`window`, `addEventListener`, `location`), then runs:","+","+| Test | Asserts |","+|---|---|","+| boot | Boot steps finish; `validateData()` reports 0 problems; `game.errors.length === 0` |","+| cipher | CW/CCW are permutations and inverses; App. C's 5 pages decode to App. C's numbers; the flip page decodes with the other turn |","+| photo scoring | Fixture cases: back turned = no ★Face; 230 units = blurry; act window = ★Act; burned = 0 |","+| perception | Careless bot (stare at a lookout from 60) made in ≤ 6 s; careful bot (walk past) never noticed; blending at 100 for 30 s never made |","+| corner ledger | 10 min of sim: vial and cash conservation hold; shutdown freezes sales; re-up triggers below 30 |","+| chase | Bot pursuer with good routing catches the runner within 60 s; the ditch happens; the kid takes it after 45 s if it's not searched |","+| tail | A careful bot completes `teeDry`; a bot that stops on every `lookBack` gets made |","+| box | Thresholds unlock B1-B3; Fear ≥ 80 → lawyer; the Lean → Offer combo; flip only at B3 with Fear ≤ 60 |","+| paper | PC sums per line; a false necessity tick is always asked and denies |","+| wire | Non-pertinent past the window adds Legal 4/s; a minimized pertinent line is lost; spot-check timing; LOG windows; voice ID links the number |","+| meters | Brass 0 → shutdown scene; Heat thresholds flip the code and add lookouts |","+| branch matrix | With `autoResolve`, every combination of dilemma × sweep × wallOff × lossOn × canary × path × I5 reaches the montage with 9-11 valid cards |","+| save/load | Save at `ep3.van`, new game instance on the same storage, CONTINUE → same beat and STATE |","+| versus | A bots-only local match ends with a valid outcome; host rules (burn, tap, jump-out) apply; snapshot JSON < 1,100 bytes at the 45-entity worst case; `LoopbackTransport` at 150 ms ±50 and 5% loss still converges |","+| attract | 10.1 s idle on the title → `attract`; one `input.press` → `title`; 3 loops of the reel with no errors |","+","+**`tests/browser.mjs`** (Playwright, one browser at a time):","+1. **Gamepad:** an init script defines a fake standard gamepad (`navigator.getGamepads` returns a DualSense-like id with buttons and axes). Assert the HUD prompt reads ✕; switch Settings → Xbox → it reads A; enable `stickInvX`, push axis0 = +1 → Dana moves left (−x).","+2. **Mouse:** hover a main-menu item → it gets focus; click → it activates; the legend shows mouse/key glyphs.","+3. **Touch-only:** an iPhone profile (WebKit) shows the notice and a Settings button; after 10 s attract runs; a tap returns.","+4. **Screens:** 8 screenshots via deep links at 1920×1080 (title, `ep1.photos`, `ep3.wire1`, Board, box, versus local split, about, montage). Look at each once; apply the thumbnail test (downscale to 480×270).","+","+**Viewport sweep** (once, at M11): `viewport-matrix http://localhost:8000/<bundle> --only phone,tablet,desktop --engines chromium,webkit -o /tmp/viewport-matrix/wiretap`. Expect: phones show the touch-only notice; desktop sizes (16:9, 21:9, 4:3) fill edge to edge with the HUD inside the safe areas; no horizontal overflow; no console errors.","+","+**AI Hub harness** (`tests/hub/hub-check.mjs`): serve `tests/hub/` with the bundle copied in. Open in Playwright and wait for `document.body.dataset.complete === 'true'`, then assert `window.__hubCheck.pass === true` for:","+1. `harness.html?game=<bundle>&players=2&auto=1`","+2. `…&players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1`","+3. `…&players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1&scenario=host-leave`","+4. `…&players=2&scenario=server&auto=1`","+","+Also open the bundle outside a session: it must still reach the title.","+","+**When to run:** headless after every change to a system; browser screens at the end of each milestone; viewport sweep and hub harness at M9 and M11.","+","+---","+","+## 17. Definition of done (tick every line before shipping)","+- [ ] Title is **WIRETAP** (RNG-picked, §0); the bundle is `Wiretap-TheWire-claude-opus-5-5-max-20261103-105319.html` in `work/`; the dev folder holds sources, tools and tests; `exit-interview.json` sits next to the html and parses.","+- [ ] One html file runs offline: the engine and hub client inlined, no runtime network, no external fonts.","+- [ ] Genre/perspective as §2; engine-native art and animation, extended (§12); all music, effects and gibberish voices written in code (§11).","+- [ ] **Story mode:** 5 episodes, 4 interludes + finale interlude, both finale paths, Shut Down, montage with computed cards, credits, episode select, continue/autosave.","+- [ ] **Every system in §5-§7 is reachable in normal play**, with no TODOs, placeholders or stubs. Each one appears in the feature matrix (App. J.6) at least once.","+- [ ] **Versus:** local (1 human vs bots; 2 humans split screen) and AI Hub shared-world (1-4). All four harness runs pass, and the game runs outside a session.","+- [ ] **Attract:** 10 s idle on title/menus → bot-played reel; any input exits; it runs on touch-only devices.","+- [ ] **10-foot UX:** controller-first; keyboard+mouse native (hover focuses, click selects, mouse aims and clicks world objects); prompts follow the last device; PlayStation glyphs by default with an Xbox option; **stick inversion toggles** for both axes; no dense data screens; thumbnail test passes.","+- [ ] **Touch-only:** no touch controls; \"Controller or keyboard required\" with a Settings button; attract allowed.","+- [ ] Standard engine features only (no custom pause/settings/rebinding/full screen); E.Shell HUD; standard settings plus the §4.7 game settings.","+- [ ] **About/Credits** screen with Credits, Source Information, Testing, Engine and Prompt Feedback, matching `exit-interview.json`; \"unknown\" where unconfirmed.","+- [ ] Headless suite green; browser checks looked at; hub harness passes; WebKit check done.","+- [ ] Writing pass done against App. G (tone, no slurs, no quotes from the show).","+"]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-105319/work/PLAN.md"]}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01NggFuotUhAPe1sdYxWjvZM","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
