he game? / TAVON: They ain't got no bullpen. None. / TEE: They got a bullpen. Bullpen just tired. / ★TEE: Tell your man the thing go down at the place where Dre messed up his ankle. Four o'clock. / TAVON: Where Dre… oh. Yeah. / TEE: Don't \"yeah\" me. Be there. | Re-up riddle (map pick), time 16:00; teaches spot-check |","+| S1-3 | 17:10 | pager | page `555-0743 11 00` | P | — | Decode → P3, \"package ready\" (page evidence) |","+| S1-4 | 17:25 | P3 (else P2) | Dale → Tee | P | DALE: Usual? / TEE: Usual. But your count been light, my man. / DALE: Count is the count. I don't open the boxes. / ★TEE: Somebody opening them. / ★DALE: Four o'clock. Don't make me wait, I got a route. | Courier voice (ID later), \"route\" → delivery truck |","+| S1-5 | 18:00 | P2 | Ms. Arnetta (citizen) → cab company | N | \"I need a cab at Ridley and Gaither, the laundromat… No, I am not waiting forty minutes…\" | — |","+| S1-6 | 18:30 | P1 | Rook → Keisha | N | ROOK: I said I'ma bring it. / KEISHA: You said that Friday. He need shoes, Ricky. His toes out the front. / ROOK: I got him. Tonight. | Rook is a father (used in his ending) |","+| S1-7 | 19:05 | P1 | Tee → Lil Moe | P | If Dana was made before: ★TEE: That lady on the bench Tuesday, leather coat? / MOE: She was reading the paper. / TEE: Nobody reads the paper on Ridley. Otherwise: ★TEE: Knockers came through twice. Nothing in the pockets, nothing on the corner. | Shows they know Dana's face (Heat note) or crew discipline (+4) |","+| S1-8 | 19:40 | P3/P2 | Rev. Mayfield → church office | N | \"Sister Pauline, about the folding chairs for Sunday…\" | — |","+| S1-9 | 20:30 | P2 | Tavon → Dink | P | TAVON: How we looking. / ★DINK: Light. Like nine hundred light. / TAVON: Nine hundred? / DINK: Testers was weak. Overtime ain't moving like last week. / TAVON: Don't tell Tee. I'll tell Tee. | Money flow evidence |","+| S1-10 | 21:15 | pager | page `555-0769 33 07` | P | — | Decode → P1, \"the count\" |","+","+**Session 2 (Ep3 night, 20:00-01:00, after the van and the ops choice):**","+| id | Time | Line | Speakers | Type | Lines (★ key) | Unlocks |","+|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|","+| S2-1 | 20:10 | P2 (P1 if not swept) | Tee → Rook | P | TEE: Man took it right off the boy. Walked up like he was asking directions. / ROOK: In a hearse? A *hearse*? / ★TEE: Hit me at the laundry later. Not this phone. / ROOK: It's Sunday. Gotta be. / ★TEE: Don't say names on the phone. | Sunday named (+4); sets up the flip page |","+| S2-2 | 20:45 | P3/P2 | Rook → \"Smokey\" | P | ★ROOK: I need a hammer. Tonight. / SMOKEY: What kind of hammer? / ★ROOK: The kind that finishes a job. / SMOKEY: Come by the shop at eleven. Cash. | **Threat to life → decision:** let it ride / wall-off stop |","+| S2-3 | 21:20 | P2 | Odessa → the laundromat payphone | N | ODESSA: Hello? Is this the laundromat phone? Is my grandson out there? Junior Hollis. Little red hoodie. / MAN: Ain't nobody here, ma'am. | — |","+| S2-4 | 21:50 | pager | Heat ≥ 50: **flip page** `555-0329 22 07` (CCW); else `555-0781 22 07` | P | — | Known-plaintext puzzle (§6.3) |","+| S2-5 | 22:30 | P1/P2 | Lonnie → Tee | P | LONNIE: He wants to see you. / TEE: Tonight? / ★LONNIE: You know where. Mama B's. The back. / TEE: I'm coming. / LONNIE: And Terrence. Come by yourself. | THE MONEY tier: Boss ?, Mama B's |","+| S2-6 | 23:10 | P2 | two teenage girls (citizens) | N | Arguing about a boy named Marcus and a borrowed jacket | — |","+| S2-7 | 23:50 | P3/P2 | Tavon → unknown | P | TAVON: Tee say we gotta be easy for a minute. No more phones on Ridley after Friday. / UNKNOWN: Then what we using? / ★TAVON: He gonna get us something. Throwaways. | Foreshadows burners (+4) |","+| S2-8 | 00:30 | P1/P2 | drunk citizen → his ex | N | Sad, funny, about a dog he misses more than her | — |","+","+**Session 3 (Ep4, burners B1-B5, 22:00-01:00):**","+| id | Time | Line | Speakers | Type | Lines (★ key) | Unlocks |","+|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|","+| S3-1 | 22:05 | B1↔B2 | Lonnie → 