{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CggVYJ9jwBLUKxyRgk5qi","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Music data verified in Node (32 tracks, every bar 16 steps). Writing the last appendices: writing guide and key scenes, ending cards, music, voice profiles, data schemas and the feature matrix."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1233,"cache_read_input_tokens":479508,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1233,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e2aa65a8-ee1a-45c4-b8e6-f96cf188e23d","uuid":"d540e604-b3ec-4f24-8d16-3dfeb7d4b006","timestamp":"2026-11-03T18:47:40.565Z","request_id":"req_011CggVYHdypcY8rBPvmMs7v"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CggVYJ9jwBLUKxyRgk5qi","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01NKjxeA6mbbgvovTLq5TByM","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"{\ncat <<'EOF'\n## Appendix G: Writing guide, key scenes, endings\n**Tone:**\n- Understated and specific. People talk around things and say less than they mean.\n- Humor is dry and dark.\n- Cops and crew both have bosses, quotas and rent.\n- Profanity exists but isn't every line.\n- No exposition dumps. The player learns by watching.\n\n**Do:**\n- Concrete details: the number 22 bus, the Orioles' bullpen, court dates, overtime, a son who needs shoes.\n- Institutional logic: stats, clearance, OT, the count, the re-up, the 24-hour report.\n\n**Don't:**\n- No slurs, ever, in any setting.\n- No quoting the show (not its catchphrases or famous lines).\n- No glamorized violence.\n- No caricatured dialect. Write it lightly: \"ain't\", \"y'all\", dropped g's now and then, \"yo\" or \"na'mean\" at most once a scene.\n\n**Vocabulary** (characters use it; UI and narration stay plain): re-up, package, testers, hoppers, the count, knockers / jump-out boys, 5-0, throwaway, the box, red ball (a high-profile case), OT, stat sheet, clearance rate, Central Booking, the Western, downtown, ASA, \"up on the wire\", minimize, pertinent, PC, CI, dry cleaning (counter-surveillance), walled-off stop.\n\n**Bleep list** (Strong language: Bleeped → \"—\" plus a voice bleep): shit, fuck/fucking, motherfucker, bitch, ass, damn.\n\n**Epigraphs:** §8.3-8.7 (all original lines spoken by characters in that episode).\n\n**Cold open (1.1):**\n- DUKES: Detective. Neighbor found him at five, going out for the paper. Nobody heard nothing.\n- DANA: Nobody heard a man get beat on his own steps.\n- DUKES: That's what nobody said.\n- LOU *(kneeling by the sheet)*: Cornelius Felton. Thirty-one years driving the number 22. Retired in March.\n- DANA: He called the corner in. Three times since August. Name and address every time.\n- LOU: Then somebody read his name out loud to the wrong person.\n- DANA: You're Homicide. This is yours.\n- LOU: It's mine till Friday. Then it's a file. You know the street?\n- DANA: Grew up three blocks off it.\n- *(at Odessa's stoop)* DANA: Morning, Miss Odessa.\n- ODESSA: Dana Lynn. Your mama know you're out here this early?\n- **Choice:** *\"Did you see anything last night?\"* / *\"I remember your choir, Miss Odessa.\"* The respectful second choice sets `odessaRespect` (+15 Trust in the kitchen) and she adds: \"Then you remember I don't say things twice.\"\n- ODESSA: I saw the TV and the inside of my eyelids. I got a grandbaby to raise, Dana Lynn.\n- *(the camera drifts up to Pigeon on the roof, feeding his birds)*\n- LOU: This ain't a whodunit, Dana. It's a who-cares.\n\n**The detail assembles (1.3):**\n- NAVARRE: The Sun put Mr. Felton on page one. So now the Deputy Commissioner cares. Six weeks. One corner. Arrests.\n- LOU: Arrests. Not a case.\n- NAVARRE: He said arrests. I heard case. We'll see who's right. Detective Szabo, Homicide.\n- LOU: Formerly. I said something true at a retirement party.\n- NAVARRE: Detective Pettiford, pawn unit.\n- HAL: Thirteen years. Nobody complained, because nobody knew I was there.\n- NAVARRE: Officer Ocasio, on loan from Southwest.\n- REN: I brought my own camera. The department's has a crack in the lens.\n- NAVARRE: Detective Whitlock, Western narcotics. She knows Ridley.\n- DANA: Ridley knows me. That might be the problem.\n- NAVARRE: The Major wants bodies by Friday. I want to know who pays for that corner. We'll try to give him both.\n\n**Pockets' shoes (1.4).** After each description, the player picks the matching photo. Photos show full bodies, shoes included (§5.3).\n- POCKETS: Pockets don't do faces, Detective. Faces get you a funeral. Shoes, though. Shoes don't talk back. Twenty for the shoes. Pockets don't do credit.\n- Wheat Timbs, laces tucked, not a scuff on 'em. That's a man who thinks he's a businessman. Terrence. Tee.\n- Black Air Force, red check, size thirteen. Ricky Batts. Rook. Don't let him see you looking.\n- Nikes with the duct tape on the left toe. Corey. He holds for 'em in the vacant. Nervous boy. Nervous boys live longer.\n- Little sneakers that light up when he runs. Junior. Miss Odessa's grandbaby. They call him Pigeon on account of the birds. He's fourteen. *(beat)* Fourteen.\n- And Dre ain't with 'em no more. Broke his ankle jumping the fence at the old Arundel station, running from y'all. They still meet out there. Ain't nobody fixed that fence.\n\n**Easy's back room (I3):**\n- EASY: Sit down, Terrence.\n- TEE: I'd rather stand.\n- EASY: I didn't ask what you'd rather. *(Tee sits.)* You lost my package to a man who drives a hearse.\n- TEE: Sunday hit the boy right after the drop. Nobody could've—\n- EASY: Somebody knew where the drop was. Somebody always knows. That's the cost of doing business outside.\n- EASY: You know why they call me Easy? Because I never make anything hard that doesn't have to be. Make it back, Terrence. By the count.\n- LONNIE: And the phones.\n- EASY: The phones. Lonnie says you like the payphones.\n- TEE: Payphones don't have names on 'em.\n- EASY: Everything has a name on it. Stop using them.\n- *(Tee leaves)* EASY *(to Lonnie)*: He's smart. Smart gets you so far.\n\n**The van dilemma (3.4):**\n- REN: He's got a gun on that kid. We have to do something.\n- LOU *(radio)*: We do something, the wire's dead by tonight, and that kid's still a corner kid tomorrow.\n- **Go in:**\n  - DANA: Police. Put it down.\n  - SUNDAY: Detective. Ain't Sunday, so it's business. But I don't do police. *(sets the bag on the hood)* Police do me. *(drives off in the hearse)*\n\n**The finale choice (5.2):**\n- PRUITT: Friday. A table. Dope, guns, cash. The Deputy's bringing Channel 11.\n- NAVARRE: Hit the re-up Friday, we get Mabry and a package. Wait for Thursday's count, we might get the man who owns the package.\n- PRUITT: \"Might\" doesn't fit on a stat sheet, Lieutenant.\n- LOU: Neither does a soul-food restaurant with a check-cashing license. But it should.\n\n**Montage cards** (11-13 shown; rules evaluated top to bottom, first match wins per person):\n| Who | Condition | Card |\n|---|---|---|\n| Corner (always first) | — | \"The corner at Gaither & Ridley: open for business by Monday.\" |\n| Tee | A + weight + Case high | \"Terrence Mabry: pleaded to twelve years. Never said Easy's name.\" |\n| | A + weight | \"Terrence Mabry: pleaded to six years. Out in four. Never said Easy's name.\" |\n| | A + talk | \"Terrence Mabry: agreed to testify. Moved to a prison in Pennsylvania under another name.\" |\n| | B + stay | \"Terrence Mabry: indicted with Darnell Booker eighteen months later.\" |\n| | B + run | \"Terrence Mabry: last seen boarding a Greyhound to Charlotte.\" |\n| | Shut Down | \"Terrence Mabry: runs three corners now.\" |\n| Easy | B + Case high | \"Darnell Booker: arrested at Mama B's on a Thursday. The count was light.\" |\n| | B | \"Darnell Booker: indicted. The case is still in discovery.\" |\n| | A | \"Darnell Booker: opened a second check-cashing store on Cathedral Row.\" |\n| | Shut Down | \"Darnell Booker: sponsored the church's back-to-school drive.\" |\n| Pigeon | `lossOn = pigeon` + `rookFree` + A | \"Nobody has seen Junior Hollis since October. His grandmother still feeds the birds.\" |\n| | `lossOn = pigeon` | \"Junior Hollis: back on the roof. The birds are gone.\" |\n| | `pigeonTrust ≥ 70` or (B and the runner wasn't Pigeon) | \"Junior Hollis: started ninth grade at a school in the county. Still keeps one bird.\" |\n| | otherwise | \"Junior Hollis: running for Tavon now. Fourteen.\" |\n| Corey | CI, not exposed | \"Corey Lyle: moved to an aunt's in Richmond. Calls Detective Whitlock on her birthday.\" |\n| | CI, exposed, rescued | \"Corey Lyle: relocated by the State's Attorney. Testified for two days.\" |\n| | CI, exposed, not rescued | \"Corey Lyle: found in a vacant on Harlow Street. No witnesses.\" |\n| | not CI | \"Corey Lyle: serving five years for possession with intent.\" |\n| Rook *(shown if `wallOff` or `rookFree`; otherwise the Sunday card)* | `wallOff` | \"Ricky Batts: eight years on a gun charge from a taillight stop.\" |\n| | `rookFree` | \"Ricky Batts: shot in December over a parking space. His son got the shoes.\" |\n| Sunday *(shown when Rook's card isn't)* | stay | \"Royal Odom: still drives the hearse. Still doesn't work Sundays.\" |\n| | call | \"Royal Odom: robbed a Hurricane stash in November. Nobody called it in.\" |\n| | go in | \"Royal Odom: sent Detective Whitlock a card at Christmas. No return address.\" |\n| Pruitt (always) | — | \"Maj. Leland Pruitt: promoted to Colonel, Administrative Bureau.\" |\n| Dana | A / B / Shut Down | \"Dana Whitlock: back in Western narcotics. Drives past the corner every day.\" / \"…assigned to the State's Attorney's money task force.\" / \"…back in uniform on the midnight shift.\" Add \"Her mother moved to the county in November.\" if `momSafe` |\n| Lou | not Shut Down / Shut Down | \"Lou Szabo: back in Homicide. Fourteen open cases on the board.\" / \"Lou Szabo: retired. Took up fishing. Hates fishing.\" |\n| Navarre | A / else | \"Gil Navarre: promoted to captain.\" / \"Gil Navarre: passed over for captain.\" |\n| Hal (always) | — | \"Hal Pettiford: kept the wire room. Nobody told him to leave.\" |\n| Teaser (always last) | — | \"Glenn Harstad: guest of honor at State Senator Marian Ocheltree's harbor fundraiser.\" → **TO BE CONTINUED** |\n\n## Appendix H: Music scores (engine `audio.music` format; all checked: every bar is 16 steps, notes are valid, the JS parses)\n```js\nEOF\ncat /tmp/wireplan-scripts/songs.js\ncat <<'EOF'\n```\n- **Use:** `game.audio.music(SONGS.field, { sync: true })`. Layers are tracks with `on: false`; turn them up with `game.audio.layer('tension', 1, .6)` and down with `layer('tension', 0, 2)`.\n- **Gospel loop** for Odessa's kitchen: write 4 bars in C major (I-IV-I-V), sine, vol .05.\n- **Jingles:** §11.1.\n\n## Appendix I: Voice profiles (Animalese synth, §11.3)\n| id | base Hz | range | syll/s | wave | formant | breath | tics |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| dana | 205 | .22 | 13 | triangle | 1.05 | .10 | — |\n| lou | 118 | .18 | 10.5 | sawtooth | .90 | .25 | gravel (+noise) |\n| hal | 142 | .15 | 9.5 | sine | .95 | .12 | — |\n| ren | 255 | .30 | 15 | square | 1.12 | .08 | — |\n| navarre | 135 | .16 | 12 | triangle | .97 | .08 | — |\n| pruitt | 112 | .25 | 12.5 | square | .90 | .10 | loud (gain 1.2) |\n| ostrowski | 108 | .20 | 11 | square | .88 | .10 | — |\n| vance | 220 | .20 | 14 | triangle | 1.08 | .06 | — |\n| halloway | 98 | .14 | 9 | sawtooth | .88 | .20 | — |\n| easy | 108 | .10 | 9 | sine | .90 | .18 | soft (gain .8) |\n| lonnie | 125 | .18 | 11 | sawtooth | .92 | .20 | — |\n| tee | 158 | .20 | 13.5 | triangle | 1.00 | .10 | — |\n| rook | 102 | .30 | 12 | sawtooth | .87 | .30 | — |\n| corey | 188 | .35 | 15.5 | square | 1.05 | .12 | stammer .3 |\n| pigeon | 330 | .30 | 15 | square | 1.20 | .05 | — |\n| moe | 350 | .30 | 16 | square | 1.22 | .05 | — |\n| dink / tavon | 200 / 175 | .25 | 14 | triangle | 1.05 / 1.0 | .08 | — |\n| pockets | 172 | .40 | 16 | sawtooth | 1.00 | .35 | — |\n| odessa | 238 | .18 | 10 | sine | 1.08 | .15 | vibrato .03 |\n| sunday | 128 | .12 | 10 | triangle | .93 | .15 | — |\n| dale | 132 | .15 | 11 | square | .95 | .10 | — |\n| civilians | seeded: men 100-170, women 190-280, kids 300-360 | .15-.35 | 10-15 | any | .9-1.2 | .05-.3 | — |\n\n**Voiceprint glyph** (voice ID, §6.6): 16 bars. Bar *i* height = `round(8 × (0.5 + 0.5 × sin(base/37 × (i+1) + formant × 3 + wave index)))`, colored by `range`. Deterministic, distinct per profile, shown in the LIVE panel during a call and in the ID strip.\n\n## Appendix J: Data schemas and the feature matrix\n**J.1 STATE** (the only thing saved):\n```js\n{ v: 1, ep: 1, beat: 'e1.cold', played: 0, tips: {},\n  meters: { brass: 60, heat: 10, legal: 0, case: 0, fund: 200 },\n  flags: { odessaRespect: false, pocketsMet: false, coreyCI: false, wireUp: false, reupSpot: null, dilemma: null, sweep: false,\n           wallOff: false, rookFree: true, lossOn: null, pigeonTrust: 0, promise: false, canary: false, coreyExposed: false,\n           coreyRescued: false, momSafe: false, path: null, i5: null, danaKnown: false, teeShort: false, rookDrew: false },\n  photos: [{ id, subject, t, place, stars, tags, turn, light, ep }],\n  evidence: [{ id, kind: 'photo'|'obs'|'stmt'|'page'|'int'|'seizure'|'plate'|'serials', ref, pts, text }],\n  facts: ['face:tee', 'obs:corey:stash', 'num:P1:tee', …],\n  numbers: { P1: { n: '555-0187', known: true, tapped: false, dead: false, user: 'tee' }, … },\n  board: { pins: { lieutenant: 'tee', … }, links: [['tee','P1'], …] },\n  wire: { lines: { P1: 'up' }, logs: [{ call, line, t }], ids: { UM1: 'tee' }, voiceprints: ['tee','rook', …] },\n  cipher: { dir: 'cw', solved: { cw: false, ccw: false } },\n  crew: { discipline: 1, goodwill: 0, count: 0, stash: 'v1412', phones: 'payphones', knows: ['dana'] },\n  stats: { photos: 0, made: 0, minimized: 0, violations: 0, chases: 0, tails: 0, retries: 0 } }\n```\n**J.2 Mission** (`def('missions', id, {...})`):\n```js\n{ id: 'photos1', time: 'day', clock: [15, 0, 17, 30], weather: null, music: 'field', player: 'dana', start: [24, 29], partner: null,\n  cast: [{ person: 'tee', role: 'lieutenant', at: 'post' }, { person: 'pigeon', role: 'lookout', at: [35, 36, 40] }, …],\n  civilians: 25, corner: { open: true, rate: .12 }, interactables: ['pocketsAlley', 'busBench', 'marketSoda', 'chevy'],\n  objectives: [{ id: 'faces', text: 'Photograph the crew', need: 'facesAll(tee,rook,corey,pigeon)' }, { id: 'reads', need: 'reads>=2' },\n               { id: 'pockets', need: 'flag:pocketsMet' }, { id: 'act', optional: true, need: 'photoTag:act' }],\n  events: [{ at: '16:10', every: '0:12', do: 'teeCallsP1' }], done: 'all(faces,reads,pockets) && at(chevy)', fail: null, checkpoints: [] }\n```\n**J.3 Beat** (`EPISODES[n].beats[]`): `{ id: 'e2.box', kind: 'card'|'annex'|'field'|'wire'|'box'|'chambers'|'paper'|'cipher'|'corner'|'ops'|'scene'|'montage', ref, stations?, story?, if?, next? }`.\n\n**J.4 Person** (`def('people', id, {...})`): `{ name, alias, role, rig: { build, size, outfit, hair, hat, hood, sleeves, hunch, colors }, voice, shoes: 'text for Pockets', portrait: { zoom, turn } }`.\n\n**J.5 Call** (`def('calls', id, {...})`): `{ session: 's1', t: '16:40', line: 'P1', from: 'tee', to: 'tavon', type: 'N'|'P'|'T', turnAt?, lines: [['tee','You see the game?'], …], keys: [3], unlock: ['fact:reupRiddle'], if?: 'flag:danaKnown' }`.\nRoutes: `{ id, waypoints: [[x,y], …], acts: { 3: ['window', 3] }, checkpoints: [4, 9] }`. Escape graphs: `{ nodes: { A: [30,33], … }, edges: [['A','B','run'], …], exits: ['X1','X2'] }`. Interactables: `{ id, at, r, verb, when, act }`. Montage cards: `{ who, if, text }`.\n\n**J.6 Feature matrix** (every feature, where it's taught → where it comes back):\n| Feature | Taught | Comes back |\n|---|---|---|\n| Move/run/crouch/blend/cover, heat and made | Ep1 cold open + 1.4 | every field beat, versus |\n| Watch, read roles, photos, polaroids, shoes | 1.4 | 2.3, 3.4 (long lens), 5.3B, versus |\n| Eavesdrop, barks, informant | 1.4 | 3.3 (Pockets fallback) |\n| Annex hub, car scenes, notebook, Board | 1.3, 1.5 | every episode |\n| Tee: order wheel, code card, payphone keypad, the count, counter-surveillance | I1 | I2-I4, versus (Corner) |\n| Payphone numbers | 2.3 | affidavit, wire |\n| Chase: sprint, vault, tackle, cuff, ditch, search | 2.3 | 5.3A rescue sprint, attract |\n| Box (4 approaches, evidence, combo, flip, lawyer) | 2.4 | 3.6 (Rook), 4.5 (kitchen variant) |\n| Cipher (turn the pad), known-plaintext flip | 2.5 | 3.3/3.6 live pages |\n| Affidavit + necessity honesty + judge | 2.6-2.7 | 4.6 (amendment) |\n| Wire: minimize, spot-check, log, voice ID, pages, fast-forward, legal | 3.2-3.3 | 3.6, 4.7 |\n| Van stakeout, van heat, plate photo | 3.4 | — |\n| Moral choices (dilemma, threat to life, mother, canary, loss) | 3.4 | 3.6, 4.7, I3, I4 |\n| Ops choices and Brass/Heat/Legal/Case meters | 1.3 | every episode, endings |\n| Tail with partner hand-off | 4.3 | 5.3B (moving cone) |\n| Stealth search (trash) | 4.4 | — |\n| Raid (plan, breach, flush, search) | 5.3A | — |\n| Endings, montage, credits, episode select | 5.6 | — |\n| Versus (hidden identity, call-outs, burn, tap, jump-out, bots, split screen, hub) | versus | attract |\n| Attract reel, touch-only notice, settings (glyphs, inversion) | title | everywhere |\nEOF\n} >> PLAN.md && wc -c PLAN.md && grep -c \"\" PLAN.md","description":"Append writing guide, endings, music, voices, schemas, matrix"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1233,"cache_read_input_tokens":479508,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1233,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e2aa65a8-ee1a-45c4-b8e6-f96cf188e23d","uuid":"59649b39-acda-435c-9dba-459113feee4c","timestamp":"2026-11-03T18:48:41.518Z","request_id":"req_011CggVYHdypcY8rBPvmMs7v","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01NKjxeA6mbbgvovTLq5TByM":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-105319/work && {\ncat <<'EOF'\n## Appendix G: Writing guide, key scenes, endings\n**Tone:**\n- Understated and specific. People talk around things and say less than they mean.\n- Humor is dry and dark.\n- Cops and crew both have bosses, quotas and rent.\n- Profanity exists but isn't every line.\n- No exposition dumps. The player learns by watching.\n\n**Do:**\n- Concrete details: the number 22 bus, the Orioles' bullpen, court dates, overtime, a son who needs shoes.\n- Institutional logic: stats, clearance, OT, the count, the re-up, the 24-hour report.\n\n**Don't:**\n- No slurs, ever, in any setting.\n- No quoting the show (not its catchphrases or famous lines).\n- No glamorized violence.\n- No caricatured dialect. Write it lightly: \"ain't\", \"y'all\", dropped g's now and then, \"yo\" or \"na'mean\" at most once a scene.\n\n**Vocabulary** (characters use it; UI and narration stay plain): re-up, package, testers, hoppers, the count, knockers / jump-out boys, 5-0, throwaway, the box, red ball (a high-profile case), OT, stat sheet, clearance rate, Central Booking, the Western, downtown, ASA, \"up on the wire\", minimize, pertinent, PC, CI, dry cleaning (counter-surveillance), walled-off stop.\n\n**Bleep list** (Strong language: Bleeped → \"—\" plus a voice bleep): shit, fuck/fucking, motherfucker, bitch, ass, damn.\n\n**Epigraphs:** §8.3-8.7 (all original lines spoken by characters in that episode).\n\n**Cold open (1.1):**\n- DUKES: Detective. Neighbor found him at five, going out for the paper. Nobody heard nothing.\n- DANA: Nobody heard a man get beat on his own steps.\n- DUKES: That's what nobody said.\n- LOU *(kneeling by the sheet)*: Cornelius Felton. Thirty-one years driving the number 22. Retired in March.\n- DANA: He called the corner in. Three times since August. Name and address every time.\n- LOU: Then somebody read his name out loud to the wrong person.\n- DANA: You're Homicide. This is yours.\n- LOU: It's mine till Friday. Then it's a file. You know the street?\n- DANA: Grew up three blocks off it.\n- *(at Odessa's stoop)* DANA: Morning, Miss Odessa.\n- ODESSA: Dana Lynn. Your mama know you're out here this early?\n- **Choice:** *\"Did you see anything last night?\"* / *\"I remember your choir, Miss Odessa.\"* The respectful second choice sets `odessaRespect` (+15 Trust in the kitchen) and she adds: \"Then you remember I don't say things twice.\"\n- ODESSA: I saw the TV and the inside of my eyelids. I got a grandbaby to raise, Dana Lynn.\n- *(the camera drifts up to Pigeon on the roof, feeding his birds)*\n- LOU: This ain't a whodunit, Dana. It's a who-cares.\n\n**The detail assembles (1.3):**\n- NAVARRE: The Sun put Mr. Felton on page one. So now the Deputy Commissioner cares. Six weeks. One corner. Arrests.\n- LOU: Arrests. Not a case.\n- NAVARRE: He said arrests. I heard case. We'll see who's right. Detective Szabo, Homicide.\n- LOU: Formerly. I said something true at a retirement party.\n- NAVARRE: Detective Pettiford, pawn unit.\n- HAL: Thirteen years. Nobody complained, because nobody knew I was there.\n- NAVARRE: Officer Ocasio, on loan from Southwest.\n- REN: I brought my own camera. The department's has a crack in the lens.\n- NAVARRE: Detective Whitlock, Western narcotics. She knows Ridley.\n- DANA: Ridley knows me. That might be the problem.\n- NAVARRE: The Major wants bodies by Friday. I want to know who pays for that corner. We'll try to give him both.\n\n**Pockets' shoes (1.4).** After each description, the player picks the matching photo. Photos show full bodies, shoes included (§5.3).\n- POCKETS: Pockets don't do faces, Detective. Faces get you a funeral. Shoes, though. Shoes don't talk back. Twenty for the shoes. Pockets don't do credit.\n- Wheat Timbs, laces tucked, not a scuff on 'em. That's a man who thinks he's a businessman. Terrence. Tee.\n- Black Air Force, red check, size thirteen. Ricky Batts. Rook. Don't let him see you looking.\n- Nikes with the duct tape on the left toe. Corey. He holds for 'em in the vacant. Nervous boy. Nervous boys live longer.\n- Little sneakers that light up when he runs. Junior. Miss Odessa's grandbaby. They call him Pigeon on account of the birds. He's fourteen. *(beat)* Fourteen.\n- And Dre ain't with 'em no more. Broke his ankle jumping the fence at the old Arundel station, running from y'all. They still meet out there. Ain't nobody fixed that fence.\n\n**Easy's back room (I3):**\n- EASY: Sit down, Terrence.\n- TEE: I'd rather stand.\n- EASY: I didn't ask what you'd rather. *(Tee sits.)* You lost my package to a man who drives a hearse.\n- TEE: Sunday hit the boy right after the drop. Nobody could've—\n- EASY: Somebody knew where the drop was. Somebody always knows. That's the cost of doing business outside.\n- EASY: You know why they call me Easy? Because I never make anything hard that doesn't have to be. Make it back, Terrence. By the count.\n- LONNIE: And the phones.\n- EASY: The phones. Lonnie says you like the payphones.\n- TEE: Payphones don't have names on 'em.\n- EASY: Everything has a name on it. Stop using them.\n- *(Tee leaves)* EASY *(to Lonnie)*: He's smart. Smart gets you so far.\n\n**The van dilemma (3.4):**\n- REN: He's got a gun on that kid. We have to do something.\n- LOU *(radio)*: We do something, the wire's dead by tonight, and that kid's still a corner kid tomorrow.\n- **Go in:**\n  - DANA: Police. Put it down.\n  - SUNDAY: Detective. Ain't Sunday, so it's business. But I don't do police. *(sets the bag on the hood)* Police do me. *(drives off in the hearse)*\n\n**The finale choice (5.2):**\n- PRUITT: Friday. A table. Dope, guns, cash. The Deputy's bringing Channel 11.\n- NAVARRE: Hit the re-up Friday, we get Mabry and a package. Wait for Thursday's count, we might get the man who owns the package.\n- PRUITT: \"Might\" doesn't fit on a stat sheet, Lieutenant.\n- LOU: Neither does a soul-food restaurant with a check-cashing license. But it should.\n\n**Montage cards** (11-13 shown; rules evaluated top to bottom, first match wins per person):\n| Who | Condition | Card |\n|---|---|---|\n| Corner (always first) | — | \"The corner at Gaither & Ridley: open for business by Monday.\" |\n| Tee | A + weight + Case high | \"Terrence Mabry: pleaded to twelve years. Never said Easy's name.\" |\n| | A + weight | \"Terrence Mabry: pleaded to six years. Out in four. Never said Easy's name.\" |\n| | A + talk | \"Terrence Mabry: agreed to testify. Moved to a prison in Pennsylvania under another name.\" |\n| | B + stay | \"Terrence Mabry: indicted with Darnell Booker eighteen months later.\" |\n| | B + run | \"Terrence Mabry: last seen boarding a Greyhound to Charlotte.\" |\n| | Shut Down | \"Terrence Mabry: runs three corners now.\" |\n| Easy | B + Case high | \"Darnell Booker: arrested at Mama B's on a Thursday. The count was light.\" |\n| | B | \"Darnell Booker: indicted. The case is still in discovery.\" |\n| | A | \"Darnell Booker: opened a second check-cashing store on Cathedral Row.\" |\n| | Shut Down | \"Darnell Booker: sponsored the church's back-to-school drive.\" |\n| Pigeon | `lossOn = pigeon` + `rookFree` + A | \"Nobody has seen Junior Hollis since October. His grandmother still feeds the birds.\" |\n| | `lossOn = pigeon` | \"Junior Hollis: back on the roof. The birds are gone.\" |\n| | `pigeonTrust ≥ 70` or (B and the runner wasn't Pigeon) | \"Junior Hollis: started ninth grade at a school in the county. Still keeps one bird.\" |\n| | otherwise | \"Junior Hollis: running for Tavon now. Fourteen.\" |\n| Corey | CI, not exposed | \"Corey Lyle: moved to an aunt's in Richmond. Calls Detective Whitlock on her birthday.\" |\n| | CI, exposed, rescued | \"Corey Lyle: relocated by the State's Attorney. Testified for two days.\" |\n| | CI, exposed, not rescued | \"Corey Lyle: found in a vacant on Harlow Street. No witnesses.\" |\n| | not CI | \"Corey Lyle: serving five years for possession with intent.\" |\n| Rook *(shown if `wallOff` or `rookFree`; otherwise the Sunday card)* | `wallOff` | \"Ricky Batts: eight years on a gun charge from a taillight stop.\" |\n| | `rookFree` | \"Ricky Batts: shot in December over a parking space. His son got the shoes.\" |\n| Sunday *(shown when Rook's card isn't)* | stay | \"Royal Odom: still drives the hearse. Still doesn't work Sundays.\" |\n| | call | \"Royal Odom: robbed a Hurricane stash in November. Nobody called it in.\" |\n| | go in | \"Royal Odom: sent Detective Whitlock a card at Christmas. No return address.\" |\n| Pruitt (always) | — | \"Maj. Leland Pruitt: promoted to Colonel, Administrative Bureau.\" |\n| Dana | A / B / Shut Down | \"Dana Whitlock: back in Western narcotics. Drives past the corner every day.\" / \"…assigned to the State's Attorney's money task force.\" / \"…back in uniform on the midnight shift.\" Add \"Her mother moved to the county in November.\" if `momSafe` |\n| Lou | not Shut Down / Shut Down | \"Lou Szabo: back in Homicide. Fourteen open cases on the board.\" / \"Lou Szabo: retired. Took up fishing. Hates fishing.\" |\n| Navarre | A / else | \"Gil Navarre: promoted to captain.\" / \"Gil Navarre: passed over for captain.\" |\n| Hal (always) | — | \"Hal Pettiford: kept the wire room. Nobody told him to leave.\" |\n| Teaser (always last) | — | \"Glenn Harstad: guest of honor at State Senator Marian Ocheltree's harbor fundraiser.\" → **TO BE CONTINUED** |\n\n## Appendix H: Music scores (engine `audio.music` format; all checked: every bar is 16 steps, notes are valid, the JS parses)\n```js\nEOF\ncat /tmp/wireplan-scripts/songs.js\ncat <<'EOF'\n```\n- **Use:** `game.audio.music(SONGS.field, { sync: true })`. Layers are tracks with `on: false`; turn them up with `game.audio.layer('tension', 1, .6)` and down with `layer('tension', 0, 2)`.\n- **Gospel loop** for Odessa's kitchen: write 4 bars in C major (I-IV-I-V), sine, vol .05.\n- **Jingles:** §11.1.\n\n## Appendix I: Voice profiles (Animalese synth, §11.3)\n| id | base Hz | range | syll/s | wave | formant | breath | tics |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| dana | 205 | .22 | 13 | triangle | 1.05 | .10 | — |\n| lou | 118 | .18 | 10.5 | sawtooth | .90 | .25 | gravel (+noise) |\n| hal | 142 | .15 | 9.5 | sine | .95 | .12 | — |\n| ren | 255 | .30 | 15 | square | 1.12 | .08 | — |\n| navarre | 135 | .16 | 12 | triangle | .97 | .08 | — |\n| pruitt | 112 | .25 | 12.5 | square | .90 | .10 | loud (gain 1.2) |\n| ostrowski | 108 | .20 | 11 | square | .88 | .10 | — |\n| vance | 220 | .20 | 14 | triangle | 1.08 | .06 | — |\n| halloway | 98 | .14 | 9 | sawtooth | .88 | .20 | — |\n| easy | 108 | .10 | 9 | sine | .90 | .18 | soft (gain .8) |\n| lonnie | 125 | .18 | 11 | sawtooth | .92 | .20 | — |\n| tee | 158 | .20 | 13.5 | triangle | 1.00 | .10 | — |\n| rook | 102 | .30 | 12 | sawtooth | .87 | .30 | — |\n| corey | 188 | .35 | 15.5 | square | 1.05 | .12 | stammer .3 |\n| pigeon | 330 | .30 | 15 | square | 1.20 | .05 | — |\n| moe | 350 | .30 | 16 | square | 1.22 | .05 | — |\n| dink / tavon | 200 / 175 | .25 | 14 | triangle | 1.05 / 1.0 | .08 | — |\n| pockets | 172 | .40 | 16 | sawtooth | 1.00 | .35 | — |\n| odessa | 238 | .18 | 10 | sine | 1.08 | .15 | vibrato .03 |\n| sunday | 128 | .12 | 10 | triangle | .93 | .15 | — |\n| dale | 132 | .15 | 11 | square | .95 | .10 | — |\n| civilians | seeded: men 100-170, women 190-280, kids 300-360 | .15-.35 | 10-15 | any | .9-1.2 | .05-.3 | — |\n\n**Voiceprint glyph** (voice ID, §6.6): 16 bars. Bar *i* height = `round(8 × (0.5 + 0.5 × sin(base/37 × (i+1) + formant × 3 + wave index)))`, colored by `range`. Deterministic, distinct per profile, shown in the LIVE panel during a call and in the ID strip.\n\n## Appendix J: Data schemas and the feature matrix\n**J.1 STATE** (the only thing saved):\n```js\n{ v: 1, ep: 1, beat: 'e1.cold', played: 0, tips: {},\n  meters: { brass: 60, heat: 10, legal: 0, case: 0, fund: 200 },\n  flags: { odessaRespect: false, pocketsMet: false, coreyCI: false, wireUp: false, reupSpot: null, dilemma: null, sweep: false,\n           wallOff: false, rookFree: true, lossOn: null, pigeonTrust: 0, promise: false, canary: false, coreyExposed: false,\n           coreyRescued: false, momSafe: false, path: null, i5: null, danaKnown: false, teeShort: false, rookDrew: false },\n  photos: [{ id, subject, t, place, stars, tags, turn, light, ep }],\n  evidence: [{ id, kind: 'photo'|'obs'|'stmt'|'page'|'int'|'seizure'|'plate'|'serials', ref, pts, text }],\n  facts: ['face:tee', 'obs:corey:stash', 'num:P1:tee', …],\n  numbers: { P1: { n: '555-0187', known: true, tapped: false, dead: false, user: 'tee' }, … },\n  board: { pins: { lieutenant: 'tee', … }, links: [['tee','P1'], …] },\n  wire: { lines: { P1: 'up' }, logs: [{ call, line, t }], ids: { UM1: 'tee' }, voiceprints: ['tee','rook', …] },\n  cipher: { dir: 'cw', solved: { cw: false, ccw: false } },\n  crew: { discipline: 1, goodwill: 0, count: 0, stash: 'v1412', phones: 'payphones', knows: ['dana'] },\n  stats: { photos: 0, made: 0, minimized: 0, violations: 0, chases: 0, tails: 0, retries: 0 } }\n```\n**J.2 Mission** (`def('missions', id, {...})`):\n```js\n{ id: 'photos1', time: 'day', clock: [15, 0, 17, 30], weather: null, music: 'field', player: 'dana', start: [24, 29], partner: null,\n  cast: [{ person: 'tee', role: 'lieutenant', at: 'post' }, { person: 'pigeon', role: 'lookout', at: [35, 36, 40] }, …],\n  civilians: 25, corner: { open: true, rate: .12 }, interactables: ['pocketsAlley', 'busBench', 'marketSoda', 'chevy'],\n  objectives: [{ id: 'faces', text: 'Photograph the crew', need: 'facesAll(tee,rook,corey,pigeon)' }, { id: 'reads', need: 'reads>=2' },\n               { id: 'pockets', need: 'flag:pocketsMet' }, { id: 'act', optional: true, need: 'photoTag:act' }],\n  events: [{ at: '16:10', every: '0:12', do: 'teeCallsP1' }], done: 'all(faces,reads,pockets) && at(chevy)', fail: null, checkpoints: [] }\n```\n**J.3 Beat** (`EPISODES[n].beats[]`): `{ id: 'e2.box', kind: 'card'|'annex'|'field'|'wire'|'box'|'chambers'|'paper'|'cipher'|'corner'|'ops'|'scene'|'montage', ref, stations?, story?, if?, next? }`.\n\n**J.4 Person** (`def('people', id, {...})`): `{ name, alias, role, rig: { build, size, outfit, hair, hat, hood, sleeves, hunch, colors }, voice, shoes: 'text for Pockets', portrait: { zoom, turn } }`.\n\n**J.5 Call** (`def('calls', id, {...})`): `{ session: 's1', t: '16:40', line: 'P1', from: 'tee', to: 'tavon', type: 'N'|'P'|'T', turnAt?, lines: [['tee','You see the game?'], …], keys: [3], unlock: ['fact:reupRiddle'], if?: 'flag:danaKnown' }`.\nRoutes: `{ id, waypoints: [[x,y], …], acts: { 3: ['window', 3] }, checkpoints: [4, 9] }`. Escape graphs: `{ nodes: { A: [30,33], … }, edges: [['A','B','run'], …], exits: ['X1','X2'] }`. Interactables: `{ id, at, r, verb, when, act }`. Montage cards: `{ who, if, text }`.\n\n**J.6 Feature matrix** (every feature, where it's taught → where it comes back):\n| Feature | Taught | Comes back |\n|---|---|---|\n| Move/run/crouch/blend/cover, heat and made | Ep1 cold open + 1.4 | every field beat, versus |\n| Watch, read roles, photos, polaroids, shoes | 1.4 | 2.3, 3.4 (long lens), 5.3B, versus |\n| Eavesdrop, barks, informant | 1.4 | 3.3 (Pockets fallback) |\n| Annex hub, car scenes, notebook, Board | 1.3, 1.5 | every episode |\n| Tee: order wheel, code card, payphone keypad, the count, counter-surveillance | I1 | I2-I4, versus (Corner) |\n| Payphone numbers | 2.3 | affidavit, wire |\n| Chase: sprint, vault, tackle, cuff, ditch, search | 2.3 | 5.3A rescue sprint, attract |\n| Box (4 approaches, evidence, combo, flip, lawyer) | 2.4 | 3.6 (Rook), 4.5 (kitchen variant) |\n| Cipher (turn the pad), known-plaintext flip | 2.5 | 3.3/3.6 live pages |\n| Affidavit + necessity honesty + judge | 2.6-2.7 | 4.6 (amendment) |\n| Wire: minimize, spot-check, log, voice ID, pages, fast-forward, legal | 3.2-3.3 | 3.6, 4.7 |\n| Van stakeout, van heat, plate photo | 3.4 | — |\n| Moral choices (dilemma, threat to life, mother, canary, loss) | 3.4 | 3.6, 4.7, I3, I4 |\n| Ops choices and Brass/Heat/Legal/Case meters | 1.3 | every episode, endings |\n| Tail with partner hand-off | 4.3 | 5.3B (moving cone) |\n| Stealth search (trash) | 4.4 | — |\n| Raid (plan, breach, flush, search) | 5.3A | — |\n| Endings, montage, credits, episode select | 5.6 | — |\n| Versus (hidden identity, call-outs, burn, tap, jump-out, bots, split screen, hub) | versus | attract |\n| Attract reel, touch-only notice, settings (glyphs, inversion) | title | everywhere |\nEOF\n} >> PLAN.md && wc -c PLAN.md && grep -c \"\" PLAN.md","description":"Append writing guide, endings, music, voices, schemas, matrix"}},"wire_ingest_context":{"toolu_01NKjxeA6mbbgvovTLq5TByM":{"cwd":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-105319/work"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NKjxeA6mbbgvovTLq5TByM","type":"tool_result","content":"172774 PLAN.md\n1790","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e2aa65a8-ee1a-45c4-b8e6-f96cf188e23d","uuid":"25499952-b351-4564-98a7-98166b039816","timestamp":"2026-11-03T18:48:41.646Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"172774 PLAN.md\n1790","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-105319/work/PLAN.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":1524,"oldLines":3,"newStart":1524,"newLines":267,"lines":[" - \"I read every log. If I find a grandmother's phone call in your transcripts, I'll pull this wire myself.\""," - Signing: \"You're up. Thirty days.\" (stamp)"," ","+## Appendix G: Writing guide, key scenes, endings","+**Tone:**","+- Understated and specific. People talk around things and say less than they mean.","+- Humor is dry and dark.","+- Cops and crew both have bosses, quotas and rent.","+- Profanity exists but isn't every line.","+- No exposition dumps. The player learns by watching.","+","+**Do:**","+- Concrete details: the number 22 bus, the Orioles' bullpen, court dates, overtime, a son who needs shoes.","+- Institutional logic: stats, clearance, OT, the count, the re-up, the 24-hour report.","+","+**Don't:**","+- No slurs, ever, in any setting.","+- No quoting the show (not its catchphrases or famous lines).","+- No glamorized violence.","+- No caricatured dialect. Write it lightly: \"ain't\", \"y'all\", dropped g's now and then, \"yo\" or \"na'mean\" at most once a scene.","+","+**Vocabulary** (characters use it; UI and narration stay plain): re-up, package, testers, hoppers, the count, knockers / jump-out boys, 5-0, throwaway, the box, red ball (a high-profile case), OT, stat sheet, clearance rate, Central Booking, the Western, downtown, ASA, \"up on the wire\", minimize, pertinent, PC, CI, dry cleaning (counter-surveillance), walled-off stop.","+","+**Bleep list** (Strong language: Bleeped → \"—\" plus a voice bleep): shit, fuck/fucking, motherfucker, bitch, ass, damn.","+","+**Epigraphs:** §8.3-8.7 (all original lines spoken by characters in that episode).","+","+**Cold open (1.1):**","+- DUKES: Detective. Neighbor found him at five, going out for the paper. Nobody heard nothing.","+- DANA: Nobody heard a man get beat on his own steps.","+- DUKES: That's what nobody said.","+- LOU *(kneeling by the sheet)*: Cornelius Felton. Thirty-one years driving the number 22. Retired in March.","+- DANA: He called the corner in. Three times since August. Name and address every time.","+- LOU: Then somebody read his name out loud to the wrong person.","+- DANA: You're Homicide. This is yours.","+- LOU: It's mine till Friday. Then it's a file. You know the street?","+- DANA: Grew up three blocks off it.","+- *(at Odessa's stoop)* DANA: Morning, Miss Odessa.","+- ODESSA: Dana Lynn. Your mama know you're out here this early?","+- **Choice:** *\"Did you see anything last night?\"* / *\"I remember your choir, Miss Odessa.\"* The respectful second choice sets `odessaRespect` (+15 Trust in the kitchen) and she adds: \"Then you remember I don't say things twice.\"","+- ODESSA: I saw the TV and the inside of my eyelids. I got a grandbaby to raise, Dana Lynn.","+- *(the camera drifts up to Pigeon on the roof, feeding his birds)*","+- LOU: This ain't a whodunit, Dana. It's a who-cares.","+","+**The detail assembles (1.3):**","+- NAVARRE: The Sun put Mr. Felton on page one. So now the Deputy Commissioner cares. Six weeks. One corner. Arrests.","+- LOU: Arrests. Not a case.","+- NAVARRE: He said arrests. I heard case. We'll see who's right. Detective Szabo, Homicide.","+- LOU: Formerly. I said something true at a retirement party.","+- NAVARRE: Detective Pettiford, pawn unit.","+- HAL: Thirteen years. Nobody complained, because nobody knew I was there.","+- NAVARRE: Officer Ocasio, on loan from Southwest.","+- REN: I brought my own camera. The department's has a crack in the lens.","+- NAVARRE: Detective Whitlock, Western narcotics. She knows Ridley.","+- DANA: Ridley knows me. That might be the problem.","+- NAVARRE: The Major wants bodies by Friday. I want to know who pays for that corner. We'll try to give him both.","+","+**Pockets' shoes (1.4).** After each description, the player picks the matching photo. Photos show full bodies, shoes included (§5.3).","+- POCKETS: Pockets don't do faces, Detective. Faces get you a funeral. Shoes, though. Shoes don't talk back. Twenty for the shoes. Pockets don't do credit.","+- Wheat Timbs, laces tucked, not a scuff on 'em. That's a man who thinks he's a businessman. Terrence. Tee.","+- Black Air Force, red check, size thirteen. Ricky Batts. Rook. Don't let him see you looking.","+- Nikes with the duct tape on the left toe. Corey. He holds for 'em in the vacant. Nervous boy. Nervous boys live longer.","+- Little sneakers that light up when he runs. Junior. Miss Odessa's grandbaby. They call him Pigeon on account of the birds. He's fourteen. *(beat)* Fourteen.","+- And Dre ain't with 'em no more. Broke his ankle jumping the fence at the old Arundel station, running from y'all. They still meet out there. Ain't nobody fixed that fence.","+","+**Easy's back room (I3):**","+- EASY: Sit down, Terrence.","+- TEE: I'd rather stand.","+- EASY: I didn't ask what you'd rather. *(Tee sits.)* You lost my package to a man who drives a hearse.","+- TEE: Sunday hit the boy right after the drop. Nobody could've—","+- EASY: Somebody knew where the drop was. Somebody always knows. That's the cost of doing business outside.","+- EASY: You know why they call me Easy? Because I never make anything hard that doesn't have to be. Make it back, Terrence. By the count.","+- LONNIE: And the phones.","+- EASY: The phones. Lonnie says you like the payphones.","+- TEE: Payphones don't have names on 'em.","+- EASY: Everything has a name on it. Stop using them.","+- *(Tee leaves)* EASY *(to Lonnie)*: He's smart. Smart gets you so far.","+","+**The van dilemma (3.4):**","+- REN: He's got a gun on that kid. We have to do something.","+- LOU *(radio)*: We do something, the wire's dead by tonight, and that kid's still a corner kid tomorrow.","+- **Go in:**","+  - DANA: Police. Put it down.","+  - SUNDAY: Detective. Ain't Sunday, so it's business. But I don't do police. *(sets the bag on the hood)* Police do me. *(drives off in the hearse)*","+","+**The finale choice (5.2):**","+- PRUITT: Friday. A table. Dope, guns, cash. The Deputy's bringing Channel 11.","+- NAVARRE: Hit the re-up Friday, we get Mabry and a package. Wait for Thursday's count, we might get the man who owns the package.","+- PRUITT: \"Might\" doesn't fit on a stat sheet, Lieutenant.","+- LOU: Neither does a soul-food restaurant with a check-cashing license. But it should.","+","+**Montage cards** (11-13 shown; rules evaluated top to bottom, first match wins per person):","+| Who | Condition | Card |","+|---|---|---|","+| Corner (always first) | — | \"The corner at Gaither & Ridley: open for business by Monday.\" |","+| Tee | A + weight + Case high | \"Terrence Mabry: pleaded to twelve years. Never said Easy's name.\" |","+| | A + weight | \"Terrence Mabry: pleaded to six years. Out in four. Never said Easy's name.\" |","+| | A + talk | \"Terrence Mabry: agreed to testify. Moved to a prison in Pennsylvania under another name.\" |","+| | B + stay | \"Terrence Mabry: indicted with Darnell Booker eighteen months later.\" |","+| | B + run | \"Terrence Mabry: last seen boarding a Greyhound to Charlotte.\" |","+| | Shut Down | \"Terrence Mabry: runs three corners now.\" |","+| Easy | B + Case high | \"Darnell Booker: arrested at Mama B's on a Thursday. The count was light.\" |","+| | B | \"Darnell Booker: indicted. The case is still in discovery.\" |","+| | A | \"Darnell Booker: opened a second check-cashing store on Cathedral Row.\" |","+| | Shut Down | \"Darnell Booker: sponsored the church's back-to-school drive.\" |","+| Pigeon | `lossOn = pigeon` + `rookFree` + A | \"Nobody has seen Junior Hollis since October. His grandmother still feeds the birds.\" |","+| | `lossOn = pigeon` | \"Junior Hollis: back on the roof. The birds are gone.\" |","+| | `pigeonTrust ≥ 70` or (B and the runner wasn't Pigeon) | \"Junior Hollis: started ninth grade at a school in the county. Still keeps one bird.\" |","+| | otherwise | \"Junior Hollis: running for Tavon now. Fourteen.\" |","+| Corey | CI, not exposed | \"Corey Lyle: moved to an aunt's in Richmond. Calls Detective Whitlock on her birthday.\" |","+| | CI, exposed, rescued | \"Corey Lyle: relocated by the State's Attorney. Testified for two days.\" |","+| | CI, exposed, not rescued | \"Corey Lyle: found in a vacant on Harlow Street. No witnesses.\" |","+| | not CI | \"Corey Lyle: serving five years for possession with intent.\" |","+| Rook *(shown if `wallOff` or `rookFree`; otherwise the Sunday card)* | `wallOff` | \"Ricky Batts: eight years on a gun charge from a taillight stop.\" |","+| | `rookFree` | \"Ricky Batts: shot in December over a parking space. His son got the shoes.\" |","+| Sunday *(shown when Rook's card isn't)* | stay | \"Royal Odom: still drives the hearse. Still doesn't work Sundays.\" |","+| | call | \"Royal Odom: robbed a Hurricane stash in November. Nobody called it in.\" |","+| | go in | \"Royal Odom: sent Detective Whitlock a card at Christmas. No return address.\" |","+| Pruitt (always) | — | \"Maj. Leland Pruitt: promoted to Colonel, Administrative Bureau.\" |","+| Dana | A / B / Shut Down | \"Dana Whitlock: back in Western narcotics. Drives past the corner every day.\" / \"…assigned to the State's Attorney's money task force.\" / \"…back in uniform on the midnight shift.\" Add \"Her mother moved to the county in November.\" if `momSafe` |","+| Lou | not Shut Down / Shut Down | \"Lou Szabo: back in Homicide. Fourteen open cases on the board.\" / \"Lou Szabo: retired. Took up fishing. Hates fishing.\" |","+| Navarre | A / else | \"Gil Navarre: promoted to captain.\" / \"Gil Navarre: passed over for captain.\" |","+| Hal (always) | — | \"Hal Pettiford: kept the wire room. Nobody told him to leave.\" |","+| Teaser (always last) | — | \"Glenn Harstad: guest of honor at State Senator Marian Ocheltree's harbor fundraiser.\" → **TO BE CONTINUED** |","+","+## Appendix H: Music scores (engine `audio.music` format; all checked: every bar is 16 steps, notes are valid, the JS parses)","+```js","+const H = '- - - - - - - - - - - - - - -';        // 15 holds: the note before it lasts the whole bar","+const BAR = '- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -';    // a whole bar of holds: the note carries on","+const SONGS = {","+  theme: { bpm: 84, steps: 4, tracks: [","+    { name: 'drums', wave: 'drums', vol: 0.2, notes: 'k . h . s . h k . h k . s . h . | k . h . s . h k . k h . s . o .' },","+    { name: 'bass', wave: 'triangle', vol: 0.3, notes: 'A2 . . . . . A2 . C3 . . . E3 . D3 . | A2 . . . . . A2 . G2 . . . E2 . G2 . | D3 . . . . . D3 . F3 . . . A3 . G3 . | D3 . . . . . D3 . C3 . . . A2 . C3 . | F2 . . . . . F2 . A2 . . . C3 . A2 . | E2 . . . . . E2 . G#2 . . . B2 . D3 . | A2 . . . . . A2 . C3 . . . E3 . C3 . | E2 . . . G#2 . . . B2 . . . D3 . B2 .' },","+    { name: 'padA', wave: 'sine', vol: 0.07, notes: `C4 ${H} | ${BAR} | F4 ${H} | ${BAR} | A4 ${H} | G#4 ${H} | C4 ${H} | G#4 ${H}` },","+    { name: 'padB', wave: 'sine', vol: 0.06, notes: `G4 ${H} | ${BAR} | C5 ${H} | ${BAR} | E4 ${H} | D5 ${H} | G4 ${H} | D5 ${H}` },","+    { name: 'lead', wave: 'pulse12', vol: 0.06, notes: '. . . . E5 . . G5 . . A5 - - . . . | C6 . A5 . G5 . E5 - - - - . . . . . | . . . . D5 . . F5 . . A5 - - . . . | G5 . F5 . D5 . C5 - - - - . . . . . | . . A4 . C5 . . D5 . D#5 . E5 - - . . | G#4 - - - . . B4 . . D5 . . . . . . | . . . . E5 . . G5 . A5 . C6 . A5 . . | B5 - - - G#5 - - - E5 - - - . . . .' },","+  ] },","+  field: { bpm: 92, steps: 4, tracks: [","+    { name: 'hats', wave: 'drums', vol: 0.05, notes: 'h . . h . . h . h . . h . . h .' },","+    { name: 'bass', wave: 'triangle', vol: 0.26, notes: 'D2 . . . . . . . D2 . . . . . F2 . | C2 . . . . . . . C2 . . . . . E2 . | A#1 . . . . . . . A#1 . . . . . D2 . | A1 . . . . . . . A1 . . . C#2 . E2 .' },","+    { name: 'keys', wave: 'sine', vol: 0.05, notes: '. . . . F4 . . . . . . . A4 . . . | . . . . E4 . . . . . . . G4 . . . | . . . . D4 . . . . . . . F4 . . . | . . . . C#4 . . . . . . . E4 . . .' },","+    { name: 'tension', wave: 'saw', vol: 0.04, on: false, notes: `D4 ${H} | C4 ${H} | A#3 ${H} | A3 ${H}` },","+    { name: 'pulse', wave: 'drums', vol: 0.1, on: false, notes: 'k . . . . . k . k . . . . . . .' },","+    { name: 'alarm', wave: 'drums', vol: 0.14, on: false, notes: 'k . k . s . . k k . . k s . k .' },","+    { name: 'stab', wave: 'square', vol: 0.05, on: false, notes: 'D5 . . D5 . . F5 . E5 . . C5 . . A4 .' },","+  ] },","+  corner: { bpm: 95, steps: 4, tracks: [","+    { name: 'drums', wave: 'drums', vol: 0.22, notes: 'k . . k s . . . k . k . s . . h | k . . k s . . k . . k . s . h h' },","+    { name: 'bass', wave: 'triangle', vol: 0.32, notes: 'G2 . . G2 . . A#2 . C3 . . . A#2 . G2 . | G2 . . G2 . . A#2 . D3 . . . C3 . A#2 . | D#2 . . D#2 . . G2 . A#2 . . . G2 . D#2 . | D2 . . D2 . . F#2 . A2 . . . D3 . C3 .' },","+    { name: 'keys', wave: 'pulse12', vol: 0.06, notes: 'G4 . A#4 . D5 . . . . . . . C5 . A#4 . | . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . | D#4 . G4 . A#4 . . . . . . . A4 . G4 . | F#4 - - - . . . . . . . . . . . .' },","+    { name: 'lead', wave: 'square', vol: 0.04, on: false, notes: 'D5 . . . D5 . C5 . A#4 . . . G4 . . . | . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .' },","+  ] },","+  wire: { bpm: 70, steps: 4, tracks: [","+    { name: 'tick', wave: 'drums', vol: 0.04, notes: 't . . . t . . . t . . . t . . .' },","+    { name: 'pad', wave: 'sine', vol: 0.06, notes: `E3 ${H} | ${BAR} | C3 ${H} | D3 ${H}` },","+    { name: 'bell', wave: 'triangle', vol: 0.04, notes: '. . . . . . . . B4 . . . . . . . | . . . . . . . . . . . . G4 . . . | . . . . . . . . E5 . . . . . . . | . . . . . . . . F#4 . . . . . . .' },","+    { name: 'pulse', wave: 'drums', vol: 0.08, on: false, notes: 'k . . . . . . . k . . . . . . .' },","+  ] },","+  chase: { bpm: 132, steps: 4, tracks: [","+    { name: 'drums', wave: 'drums', vol: 0.22, notes: 'k . h k s . h . k k h . s . h h' },","+    { name: 'bass', wave: 'saw', vol: 0.12, notes: 'E2 E2 . E2 G2 . E2 . A2 . G2 . E2 . D2 . | E2 E2 . E2 G2 . E2 . B2 . A2 . G2 . F#2 .' },","+    { name: 'stab', wave: 'square', vol: 0.05, notes: 'E4 . . . . . E4 . G4 . . . F#4 . . . | E4 . . . . . E4 . B4 . . . A4 . G4 .' },","+  ] },","+  montage: { bpm: 68, steps: 4, tracks: [","+    { name: 'drums', wave: 'drums', vol: 0.08, notes: 'k . . . . . . . s . . . . . h .' },","+    { name: 'bass', wave: 'triangle', vol: 0.26, notes: `A2 ${H} | F2 ${H} | C3 ${H} | G2 ${H}` },","+    { name: 'chords', wave: 'sine', vol: 0.06, notes: 'A3 . C4 . E4 . C4 . A3 . C4 . E4 . C4 . | F3 . A3 . C4 . A3 . F3 . A3 . C4 . A3 . | C4 . E4 . G4 . E4 . C4 . E4 . G4 . E4 . | G3 . B3 . D4 . B3 . G3 . B3 . D4 . B3 .' },","+    { name: 'lead', wave: 'triangle', vol: 0.07, notes: 'E5 - - - . . D5 . C5 - - - . . . . | . . . . A4 . C5 . D5 - - - . . . . | E5 - - - . . G5 . E5 - - - D5 . C5 . | D5 - - - - - - - . . . . . . . . | E5 - - - . . D5 . C5 - - - . . A4 . | C5 - - - . . D5 . E5 - - - . . . . | G5 - - - E5 - - - D5 - - - C5 - - - | B4 - - - - - - - - - - - . . . .' },","+  ] },","+  versus: { bpm: 104, steps: 4, tracks: [","+    { name: 'drums', wave: 'drums', vol: 0.2, notes: 'k . . . s . . k . k . . s . . .' },","+    { name: 'bass', wave: 'triangle', vol: 0.3, notes: 'C2 . . C2 . . D#2 . F2 . . . D#2 . C2 . | G#1 . . G#1 . . C2 . D#2 . . . D2 . A#1 .' },","+    { name: 'pressure', wave: 'saw', vol: 0.04, on: false, notes: `C4 ${H} | G#3 ${H}` },","+    { name: 'clock', wave: 'drums', vol: 0.06, on: false, notes: 'h h h h h h h h h h h h h h h h' },","+    { name: 'cash', wave: 'pulse12', vol: 0.05, on: false, notes: 'G4 . . G4 . . A#4 . C5 . . . A#4 . G4 . | D#4 . . D#4 . . F4 . G4 . . . F4 . D#4 .' },","+  ] },","+};","+```","+- **Use:** `game.audio.music(SONGS.field, { sync: true })`. Layers are tracks with `on: false`; turn them up with `game.audio.layer('tension', 1, .6)` and down with `layer('tension', 0, 2)`.","+- **Gospel loop** for Odessa's kitchen: write 4 bars in C major (I-IV-I-V), sine, vol .05.","+- **Jingles:** §11.1.","+","+## Appendix I: Voice profiles (Animalese synth, §11.3)","+| id | base Hz | range | syll/s | wave | formant | breath | tics |","+|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|","+| dana | 205 | .22 | 13 | triangle | 1.05 | .10 | — |","+| lou | 118 | .18 | 10.5 | sawtooth | .90 | .25 | gravel (+noise) |","+| hal | 142 | .15 | 9.5 | sine | .95 | .12 | — |","+| ren | 255 | .30 | 15 | square | 1.12 | .08 | — |","+| navarre | 135 | .16 | 12 | triangle | .97 | .08 | — |","+| pruitt | 112 | .25 | 12.5 | square | .90 | .10 | loud (gain 1.2) |","+| ostrowski | 108 | .20 | 11 | square | .88 | .10 | — |","+| vance | 220 | .20 | 14 | triangle | 1.08 | .06 | — |","+| halloway | 98 | .14 | 9 | sawtooth | .88 | .20 | — |","+| easy | 108 | .10 | 9 | sine | .90 | .18 | soft (gain .8) |","+| lonnie | 125 | .18 | 11 | sawtooth | .92 | .20 | — |","+| tee | 158 | .20 | 13.5 | triangle | 1.00 | .10 | — |","+| rook | 102 | .30 | 12 | sawtooth | .87 | .30 | — |","+| corey | 188 | .35 | 15.5 | square | 1.05 | .12 | stammer .3 |","+| pigeon | 330 | .30 | 15 | square | 1.20 | .05 | — |","+| moe | 350 | .30 | 16 | square | 1.22 | .05 | — |","+| dink / tavon | 200 / 175 | .25 | 14 | triangle | 1.05 / 1.0 | .08 | — |","+| pockets | 172 | .40 | 16 | sawtooth | 1.00 | .35 | — |","+| odessa | 238 | .18 | 10 | sine | 1.08 | .15 | vibrato .03 |","+| sunday | 128 | .12 | 10 | triangle | .93 | .15 | — |","+| dale | 132 | .15 | 11 | square | .95 | .10 | — |","+| civilians | seeded: men 100-170, women 190-280, kids 300-360 | .15-.35 | 10-15 | any | .9-1.2 | .05-.3 | — |","+","+**Voiceprint glyph** (voice ID, §6.6): 16 bars. Bar *i* height = `round(8 × (0.5 + 0.5 × sin(base/37 × (i+1) + formant × 3 + wave index)))`, colored by `range`. Deterministic, distinct per profile, shown in the LIVE panel during a call and in the ID strip.","+","+## Appendix J: Data schemas and the feature matrix","+**J.1 STATE** (the only thing saved):","+```js","+{ v: 1, ep: 1, beat: 'e1.cold', played: 0, tips: {},","+  meters: { brass: 60, heat: 10, legal: 0, case: 0, fund: 200 },","+  flags: { odessaRespect: false, pocketsMet: false, coreyCI: false, wireUp: false, reupSpot: null, dilemma: null, sweep: false,","+           wallOff: false, rookFree: true, lossOn: null, pigeonTrust: 0, promise: false, canary: false, coreyExposed: false,","+           coreyRescued: false, momSafe: false, path: null, i5: null, danaKnown: false, teeShort: false, rookDrew: false },","+  photos: [{ id, subject, t, place, stars, tags, turn, light, ep }],","+  evidence: [{ id, kind: 'photo'|'obs'|'stmt'|'page'|'int'|'seizure'|'plate'|'serials', ref, pts, text }],","+  facts: ['face:tee', 'obs:corey:stash', 'num:P1:tee', …],","+  numbers: { P1: { n: '555-0187', known: true, tapped: false, dead: false, user: 'tee' }, … },","+  board: { pins: { lieutenant: 'tee', … }, links: [['tee','P1'], …] },","+  wire: { lines: { P1: 'up' }, logs: [{ call, line, t }], ids: { UM1: 'tee' }, voiceprints: ['tee','rook', …] },","+  cipher: { dir: 'cw', solved: { cw: false, ccw: false } },","+  crew: { discipline: 1, goodwill: 0, count: 0, stash: 'v1412', phones: 'payphones', knows: ['dana'] },","+  stats: { photos: 0, made: 0, minimized: 0, violations: 0, chases: 0, tails: 0, retries: 0 } }","+```","+**J.2 Mission** (`def('missions', id, {...})`):","+```js","+{ id: 'photos1', time: 'day', clock: [15, 0, 17, 30], weather: null, music: 'field', player: 'dana', start: [24, 29], partner: null,","+  cast: [{ person: 'tee', role: 'lieutenant', at: 'post' }, { person: 'pigeon', role: 'lookout', at: [35, 36, 40] }, …],","+  civilians: 25, corner: { open: true, rate: .12 }, interactables: ['pocketsAlley', 'busBench', 'marketSoda', 'chevy'],","+  objectives: [{ id: 'faces', text: 'Photograph the crew', need: 'facesAll(tee,rook,corey,pigeon)' }, { id: 'reads', need: 'reads>=2' },","+               { id: 'pockets', need: 'flag:pocketsMet' }, { id: 'act', optional: true, need: 'photoTag:act' }],","+  events: [{ at: '16:10', every: '0:12', do: 'teeCallsP1' }], done: 'all(faces,reads,pockets) && at(chevy)', fail: null, checkpoints: [] }","+```","+**J.3 Beat** (`EPISODES[n].beats[]`): `{ id: 'e2.box', kind: 'card'|'annex'|'field'|'wire'|'box'|'chambers'|'paper'|'cipher'|'corner'|'ops'|'scene'|'montage', ref, stations?, story?, if?, next? }`.","+","+**J.4 Person** (`def('people', id, {...})`): `{ name, alias, role, rig: { build, size, outfit, hair, hat, hood, sleeves, hunch, colors }, voice, shoes: 'text for Pockets', portrait: { zoom, turn } }`.","+","+**J.5 Call** (`def('calls', id, {...})`): `{ session: 's1', t: '16:40', line: 'P1', from: 'tee', to: 'tavon', type: 'N'|'P'|'T', turnAt?, lines: [['tee','You see the game?'], …], keys: [3], unlock: ['fact:reupRiddle'], if?: 'flag:danaKnown' }`.","+Routes: `{ id, waypoints: [[x,y], …], acts: { 3: ['window', 3] }, checkpoints: [4, 9] }`. Escape graphs: `{ nodes: { A: [30,33], … }, edges: [['A','B','run'], …], exits: ['X1','X2'] }`. Interactables: `{ id, at, r, verb, when, act }`. Montage cards: `{ who, if, text }`.","+","+**J.6 Feature matrix** (every feature, where it's taught → where it comes back):","+| Feature | Taught | Comes back |","+|---|---|---|","+| Move/run/crouch/blend/cover, heat and made | Ep1 cold open + 1.4 | every field beat, versus |","+| Watch, read roles, photos, polaroids, shoes | 1.4 | 2.3, 3.4 (long lens), 5.3B, versus |","+| Eavesdrop, barks, informant | 1.4 | 3.3 (Pockets fallback) |","+| Annex hub, car scenes, notebook, Board | 1.3, 1.5 | every episode |","+| Tee: order wheel, code card, payphone keypad, the count, counter-surveillance | I1 | I2-I4, versus (Corner) |","+| Payphone numbers | 2.3 | affidavit, wire |","+| Chase: sprint, vault, tackle, cuff, ditch, search | 2.3 | 5.3A rescue sprint, attract |","+| Box (4 approaches, evidence, combo, flip, lawyer) | 2.4 | 3.6 (Rook), 4.5 (kitchen variant) |","+| Cipher (turn the pad), known-plaintext flip | 2.5 | 3.3/3.6 live pages |","+| Affidavit + necessity honesty + judge | 2.6-2.7 | 4.6 (amendment) |","+| Wire: minimize, spot-check, log, voice ID, pages, fast-forward, legal | 3.2-3.3 | 3.6, 4.7 |","+| Van stakeout, van heat, plate photo | 3.4 | — |","+| Moral choices (dilemma, threat to life, mother, canary, loss) | 3.4 | 3.6, 4.7, I3, I4 |","+| Ops choices and Brass/Heat/Legal/Case meters | 1.3 | every episode, endings |","+| Tail with partner hand-off | 4.3 | 5.3B (moving cone) |","+| Stealth search (trash) | 4.4 | — |","+| Raid (plan, breach, flush, search) | 5.3A | — |","+| Endings, montage, credits, episode select | 5.6 | — |","+| Versus (hidden identity, call-outs, burn, tap, jump-out, bots, split screen, hub) | versus | attract |","+| Attract reel, touch-only notice, settings (glyphs, inversion) | title | everywhere |"]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-105319/work/PLAN.md"]}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01NKjxeA6mbbgvovTLq5TByM","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
