{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CggVgjPWVWDBjsDpQpMuA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Eight gaps turned up in the sweep, including missing `tests/hub` creation, unset manual saves and clock speed, and the `hubWait` scene absent from the table. I'm applying all of these fixes as exact, checked replacements now.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2193,"cache_read_input_tokens":492144,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2193,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e2aa65a8-ee1a-45c4-b8e6-f96cf188e23d","uuid":"bc554fde-d167-40e1-8764-f6fc89f9e8db","timestamp":"2026-11-03T18:50:06.743Z","request_id":"req_011CggVgiwELBj7g3BNoKTge","narration_block_indexes":[0],"thinking_duration_ms":1,"thinking_display":"updates"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CggVgjPWVWDBjsDpQpMuA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01EUDj8dzKKRTkhZbRFy4PVs","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cp PLAN.md /tmp/wireplan-scripts/PLAN.backup.md && python3 - <<'EOF'\np = 'PLAN.md'; s = open(p).read()\ndef rep(old, new):\n    global s\n    n = s.count(old)\n    assert n == 1, f'expected 1 match, found {n}: {old[:70]!r}'\n    s = s.replace(old, new)\n# (a) create tests/hub before downloading the harness\nrep(\"mkdir -p $DEV/engine $DEV/vendor && cp -r\", \"mkdir -p $DEV/engine $DEV/vendor $DEV/tests/hub && cp -r\")\n# (b) manual saves at the Annex\nrep(\"settings: GAME_SETTINGS, controls: CONTROL_NAMES, quit: 'title', saves: false } });\",\n    \"settings: GAME_SETTINGS, controls: CONTROL_NAMES, quit: 'title', saves: true } });   // Save/Load in the pause menu; saves.canSave only in the Annex\")\nrep(\"- **Saves:** `game.saves` slots (3 + autosave). Autosave at every beat start.\",\n    \"- **Saves:** `game.saves` slots (3 + autosave). `saves.write = () => ({ data: STATE, place: 'Ep 2 · Paper', level: 'Episode 2' })`, `saves.read = s => restoreState(s.data)`. Autosave at every beat start. Manual Save/Load sits in the pause menu (`menu.saves: true`), and `saves.canSave` is true only in the Annex: your desk is the save point, so a save never lands mid-mission.\")\n# (c) mission clock\nrep(\"`field` loads a **mission** (data, App. J) and gets from it the time of day, weather, cast spawns and behaviors, objectives, events, checkpoints, music and rules. One scene runs every neighborhood mission.\",\n    \"`field` loads a **mission** (data, App. J) and gets from it the time of day, weather, cast spawns and behaviors, objectives, events, checkpoints, music and rules. One scene runs every neighborhood mission.\\n\\n**Mission clock:** an `E.Clock` running at 30 game minutes per real minute from the mission's start time. Lighting interpolates between the time presets (§12.1) and scheduled events fire on it. It stops at the mission's end time. There are **no time limits** unless a mission says so (the tail's timers, the chase, the 60-s rescue, the raid's 30 s).\")\n# (d) ops choices with explicit consequences\nrep(\"| 1 | *Ask for the van (Ren)* vs *Ask for overtime (more wire hours later)* |\",\n    \"| 1 | *Ask for the van*: the Ep3 stakeout uses Ren's van (normal van heat) · vs · *Ask for overtime*: the stakeout uses Dana's Chevy (heat ×1.5), but each Ep3 wire session gets one extra hour with one extra pertinent call (S1-OT: Tavon confirms the count spot, +4; S2-OT: Dink complains Tee is \\\"scared of phones now\\\", +4) |\")\nrep(\"| 2 | *Use Pockets* vs *Pay for a second informant* (Fund −$100) |\",\n    \"| 2 | *Use Pockets* (free; his statement only counts with a direct item) · vs · *Pay Miss Pat*, the Gaither Market cashier (Fund −$100): a citizen witness whose statement is worth **2** PC points on P1 by itself |\")\nrep(\"| 4 | *Burner subpoenas: rush (Legal +10, faster)* vs *by the book (Brass −5)* |\",\n    \"| 4 | *Rush the burner subpoenas* (Legal +10, Brass +5: the Major likes speed) · vs · *By the book* (Brass −5). Same calls either way: the choice is Legal against Brass |\")\n# (e) the code flip always happens after the robbery\nrep(\"- **Code flip (Ep3):** at Heat ≥ 50 after the robbery, Tee switches to counter-clockwise (the inverse).\",\n    \"- **Code flip (Ep3):** after the robbery Tee **always** switches to counter-clockwise (the inverse), so every playthrough meets the puzzle.\")\nrep(\"| S2-4 | 21:50 | pager | Heat ≥ 50: **flip page** `555-0329 22 07` (CCW); else `555-0781 22 07` | P | — | Known-plaintext puzzle (§6.3) |\",\n    \"| S2-4 | 21:50 | pager | **flip page** `555-0329 22 07` (CCW) | P | — | Known-plaintext puzzle (§6.3) |\")\nrep(\"- **The flip page (Ep3 S2, when Heat ≥ 50):** `555-0329 22 07`.\",\n    \"- **The flip page (Ep3 S2, every playthrough):** `555-0329 22 07`.\")\nrep(\"Lonnie: \\\"He wants to see you. Mama B's.\\\" → THE MONEY tier gets \\\"Boss ?\\\" and Mama B's. **Code flip** if Heat ≥ 50 |\",\n    \"Lonnie: \\\"He wants to see you. Mama B's.\\\" → THE MONEY tier gets \\\"Boss ?\\\" and Mama B's. **Code flip** (known-plaintext page) |\")\nrep(\"≥30: a 3rd lookout and customer screening. ≥50: code flip and payphone rotation.\",\n    \"≥30: a 3rd lookout and customer screening. ≥50: payphone rotation (a tapped line goes dead one session early; the scheduler moves its calls).\")\n# (f) hubWait scene\nrep(\"| `shutdown` | none | no | Detail shut down (game over) → retry from autosave or montage |\",\n    \"| `shutdown` | none | no | Detail shut down (game over) → retry from autosave or montage |\\n| `hubWait` | none | no | AI Hub only: \\\"Connecting…\\\" while `AIHub.connect` resolves (no prompts, no menus) |\")\n# (h) consistent episode presets\nrep(\"  - Ep2: 4 faces with names; Heat 20, Brass 55.\\n  - Ep3: wire up on P1, P2 and the pager clone; `coreyCI` false; Brass 50.\\n  - Ep4: dilemma \\\"stay\\\", sweep false, `wallOff` true, Heat 45.\\n  - Ep5: burners known, `pigeonTrust` 75, Brass 45.\",\n    \"  - Ep2: 4 faces with names; Heat 20, Brass 50.\\n  - Ep3: wire up on P1, P2 and the pager clone; `coreyCI` false; Heat 25, Brass 60.\\n  - Ep4: dilemma \\\"stay\\\", sweep false, `wallOff` true; Heat 45, Brass 55.\\n  - Ep5: burners known, `pigeonTrust` 75; Heat 40, Brass 45.\")\n# (g) UI look / theme subsection after the title screen subsection\nrep(\"- **Keep clear:** the top-right corner area.\\n\",\n    \"- **Keep clear:** the top-right corner area.\\n\\n\"\n    \"### 12.8 UI look (ui.css and the E.Shell theme)\\n\"\n    \"- **E.Shell theme:** `THEME = { ink: '#f2ead8', paper: '#141210', accent: '#ffb347', muted: '#9a9080', danger: '#ff5a4a', line: '#3a342c', font: 'system-ui, -apple-system, \\\"Segoe UI\\\", Roboto, sans-serif', titleFont: '\\\"Arial Narrow\\\", \\\"Roboto Condensed\\\", \\\"Helvetica Neue\\\", Arial, sans-serif' }`\\n\"\n    \"- **Case-file panels** (Board, notebook, affidavit, evidence): manila `#e9dcb5` with ink `#2b2418`; typewriter text in `\\\"Courier New\\\", Courier, ui-monospace, monospace`; headings condensed uppercase with letter-spacing .04em; red string `#b3261e`; pushpins as CSS circles; polaroids `#f4f1ea` with a soft shadow and ±2° tilt; corkboard `#a8794a` with a subtle noise background (CSS gradients, no images).\\n\"\n    \"- **Wire-room panels:** near-black `#0b0f0c`, phosphor green text `#8fe388`, amber `#ffb347` for actions, a faint scanline overlay (CSS `repeating-linear-gradient`), tape counters in tabular numerals.\\n\"\n    \"- **Focus and legends:** §4.5. Glyph chips: §4.3.\\n\")\nopen(p, 'w').write(s)\nprint('all replacements applied')\nEOF\nwc -c PLAN.md","description":"Apply consistency fixes to PLAN.md with exact-match replacements"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2193,"cache_read_input_tokens":492144,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2193,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e2aa65a8-ee1a-45c4-b8e6-f96cf188e23d","uuid":"b09d6dee-69a2-4e50-bd3e-b46056f7b71a","timestamp":"2026-11-03T18:50:30.201Z","request_id":"req_011CggVgiwELBj7g3BNoKTge","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01EUDj8dzKKRTkhZbRFy4PVs":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-105319/work && cp PLAN.md /tmp/wireplan-scripts/PLAN.backup.md && python3 - <<'EOF'\np = 'PLAN.md'; s = open(p).read()\ndef rep(old, new):\n    global s\n    n = s.count(old)\n    assert n == 1, f'expected 1 match, found {n}: {old[:70]!r}'\n    s = s.replace(old, new)\n# (a) create tests/hub before downloading the harness\nrep(\