{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EUDj8dzKKRTkhZbRFy4PVs","type":"tool_result","content":"all replacements applied\n175220 PLAN.md\n[This command modified 1 file you've previously read: PLAN.md. Call Read before editing.]","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e2aa65a8-ee1a-45c4-b8e6-f96cf188e23d","uuid":"56bd4309-db15-4c9a-88de-2b007ffd0efc","timestamp":"2026-11-03T18:50:30.360Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"all replacements applied\n175220 PLAN.md","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"staleReadFileStateHint":"[This command modified 1 file you've previously read: PLAN.md. Call Read before editing.]","bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-105319/work/PLAN.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":91,"oldLines":7,"newStart":91,"newLines":7,"lines":[" DEV=Wiretap-TheWire-claude-opus-5-5-max-20261103-105319"," git clone --depth 1 --filter=blob:none --sparse https://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge.git /tmp/wt-engine"," git -C /tmp/wt-engine sparse-checkout set dist/handoff","-mkdir -p $DEV/engine $DEV/vendor && cp -r /tmp/wt-engine/dist/handoff/* $DEV/engine/","+mkdir -p $DEV/engine $DEV/vendor $DEV/tests/hub && cp -r /tmp/wt-engine/dist/handoff/* $DEV/engine/"," curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/session.js -o $DEV/vendor/aihub-session.js"," for f in harness.html bridge.js round.js; do curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/$f -o $DEV/tests/hub/$f; done"," ```"]},{"oldStart":181,"oldLines":6,"newStart":181,"newLines":7,"lines":[" | `about` | DOM | no | About & Credits pages (§13) |"," | `versusSetup`, `versus`, `versusResults` | iso, split | versus yes (local only) | §9 |"," | `shutdown` | none | no | Detail shut down (game over) → retry from autosave or montage |","+| `hubWait` | none | no | AI Hub only: \"Connecting…\" while `AIHub.connect` resolves (no prompts, no menus) |"," "," The Board, notebook, cipher, affidavit editor, ops choice and evidence viewer are **UI screens** opened over `annex`/`field`/`wire`, not scenes."," "]},{"oldStart":188,"oldLines":7,"newStart":189,"newLines":7,"lines":[" ```js"," const game = new E.Game({ canvas: 'screen', res: 'ps1', expand: true, view: 'iso', views: ['iso'], input: KEYS, id: 'wiretap',","   menu: { items: [['Restart this part', () => Director.restartBeat()], ['Episode select', () => Director.toEpisodes()]],","-          settings: GAME_SETTINGS, controls: CONTROL_NAMES, quit: 'title', saves: false } });","+          settings: GAME_SETTINGS, controls: CONTROL_NAMES, quit: 'title', saves: true } });   // Save/Load in the pause menu; saves.canSave only in the Annex"," E.style.propSize = 1.35;                       // props match size-1.25 heroes"," installGamepadInversion(game);                  // before the first tick (§4.4)"," const ui = new E.Shell(game, { theme: THEME }); // HUD, toasts, standard pause/settings/controls"]},{"oldStart":322,"oldLines":6,"newStart":323,"newLines":8,"lines":[" ### 5.1 Field scene and interactions"," `field` loads a **mission** (data, App. J) and gets from it the time of day, weather, cast spawns and behaviors, objectives, events, checkpoints, music and rules. One scene runs every neighborhood mission."," ","+**Mission clock:** an `E.Clock` running at 30 game minutes per real minute from the mission's start time. Lighting interpolates between the time presets (§12.1) and scheduled events fire on it. It stops at the mission's end time. There are **no time limits** unless a mission says so (the tail's timers, the chase, the 60-s rescue, the raid's 30 s).","+"," **Interactables** are registered per mission. Each has `{ id, at: {x,y}, r: 18, verb: 'Talk'|'Read number'|'Search'|'Sit'|'Buy a soda'|'Vault'|..., when(ctx), act(ctx) }`."," - The nearest valid one within its radius drives the HUD prompt."," - The mouse hovering one (screen-pick through `{ pick: obj }` on `r.actor`/`r.shape`, then `r.pick(sx, sy)`) highlights it with a 1-px outline."]},{"oldStart":494,"oldLines":7,"newStart":497,"newLines":7,"lines":[" - **The crew's code:** \"turn the pad\". Each digit is replaced by the digit that sits in its place after the keypad is turned a quarter-turn clockwise (`1→7 2→4 3→1 4→8 5→5 6→2 7→9 8→6 9→3 0→0`)."," - **Format:** pages are `<encoded callback> <crew code> <sender id>`. Crew codes are sent in the clear (vocabulary from Corey and intercepts): `11` package ready · `22` call me at the usual phone · `33` the count · `44` need product · `55` all clear · `77` police around · `99` stop everything. Sender ids: Tee 07, Rook 13, Pigeon 14, Corey 21, Easy's people 00."," - **Decoder UI:** a big 3×4 keypad on the left and the encoded digits on the right. L1/R1 (or click the arrows) **turn the keypad** 90° at a time, and the decoded digits update live by position. When the decoded number matches a number Dana knows (notebook Phones), it locks with \"MATCH: Suds City payphone\" and becomes evidence `page:<n>` (Case +3). △ toggles a hint: Corey's line \"It's the phone... you turn it.\"","-- **Code flip (Ep3):** at Heat ≥ 50 after the robbery, Tee switches to counter-clockwise (the inverse). Old decodes stop matching (\"NO MATCH ×3\"). It's a **known-plaintext** puzzle: a page arrives right after Tee is overheard saying \"call me at the laundry\". The player turns the pad the other way until it matches P2. Hal: \"They didn't change the lock. They just turned the key the other way.\"","+- **Code flip (Ep3):** after the robbery Tee **always** switches to counter-clockwise (the inverse), so every playthrough meets the puzzle. Old decodes stop matching (\"NO MATCH ×3\"). It's a **known-plaintext** puzzle: a page arrives right after Tee is overheard saying \"call me at the laundry\". The player turns the pad the other way until it matches P2. Hal: \"They didn't change the lock. They just turned the key the other way.\""," "," ### 6.4 The box: interrogation (17-box.js; App. E)"," - **Scene:** `brawler` view of a small room: table, two chairs, one-way glass, a buzzing fluorescent light (flicker light plus a 120 Hz hum). The suspect sits (sit pose). Dana and Lou stand or sit."]},{"oldStart":554,"oldLines":7,"newStart":557,"newLines":7,"lines":[" | Meter | Range / start | Up | Down | Effects |"," |---|---|---|---|---|"," | **Brass** (Major's patience) | 0-100 / 60 | Arrests and seizures: Corey +10, Rook gun stop +15, sweep +25, raid +40; Sunday package +10 | Each episode start without new stats −10; affidavit denied −10; perjury −15; wire pulled −20; tail retries −5; corner gone dark −15 | **0 → the detail is shut down** (game over → retry the beat from its autosave, or take the Shut Down ending). Below 30 in Ep5 locks Path B |","-| **Heat** (crew wariness) | 0-100 / 10 | Made +15; van burned +10; Corey arrest +10; seizure +15; sweep +20; wall-off stop +5; confronting Sunday +30; Tee's interlude choices ±10 | −5 per episode; good discipline as Tee is the reverse (higher Heat means a tighter crew) | ≥30: a 3rd lookout and customer screening. ≥50: code flip and payphone rotation. ≥70: more `lookBack`s in tails (+50%). ≥90: corner goes dark for a day (Brass −15) |","+| **Heat** (crew wariness) | 0-100 / 10 | Made +15; van burned +10; Corey arrest +10; seizure +15; sweep +20; wall-off stop +5; confronting Sunday +30; Tee's interlude choices ±10 | −5 per episode; good discipline as Tee is the reverse (higher Heat means a tighter crew) | ≥30: a 3rd lookout and customer screening. ≥50: payphone rotation (a tapped line goes dead one session early; the scheduler moves its calls). ≥70: more `lookBack`s in tails (+50%). ≥90: corner goes dark for a day (Brass −15) |"," | **Legal** | 0-100 / 0 | Minimization violations; perjury +30; an illegal search (searching a person without cause in a field beat) +15 | −10 per episode | 100 → the wire is pulled; it also lowers the conviction lines in the endings |"," | **Case** | 0+ / 0 | Faces +2, reads +1, ACT +5, statements +2, pages +3, intercepts +4, voice IDs +2, plate +5, seizure +5, Easy ACT +20 | never | Bands at the end: low < 60, mid 60-119, high ≥ 120 → sentences in the montage |"," "]},{"oldStart":562,"oldLines":10,"newStart":565,"newLines":10,"lines":[" "," | Ep | Choice |"," |---|---|","-| 1 | *Ask for the van (Ren)* vs *Ask for overtime (more wire hours later)* |","-| 2 | *Use Pockets* vs *Pay for a second informant* (Fund −$100) |","+| 1 | *Ask for the van*: the Ep3 stakeout uses Ren's van (normal van heat) · vs · *Ask for overtime*: the stakeout uses Dana's Chevy (heat ×1.5), but each Ep3 wire session gets one extra hour with one extra pertinent call (S1-OT: Tavon confirms the count spot, +4; S2-OT: Dink complains Tee is \"scared of phones now\", +4) |","+| 2 | *Use Pockets* (free; his statement only counts with a direct item) · vs · *Pay Miss Pat*, the Gaither Market cashier (Fund −$100): a citizen witness whose statement is worth **2** PC points on P1 by itself |"," | 3 | **Give the Major bodies (sweep)** vs **Hold the line** |","-| 4 | *Burner subpoenas: rush (Legal +10, faster)* vs *by the book (Brass −5)* |","+| 4 | *Rush the burner subpoenas* (Legal +10, Brass +5: the Major likes speed) · vs · *By the book* (Brass −5). Same calls either way: the choice is Legal against Brass |"," | 5 | **Dope on the table** vs **Follow the money** |"," "," ---"]},{"oldStart":725,"oldLines":7,"newStart":728,"newLines":7,"lines":[" | 3.3 | **Session 1** | wire, 16:00-23:00 | Calls S1-1…S1-10 (App. D). The re-up riddle: \"the place where Dre messed up his ankle\" → pick the place on the notebook map (Arundel Gas). If Pockets' line was missed, Hal suggests finding Pockets (a 1-minute field beat at the bus stop) | `reupSpot` |"," | 3.4 | **The van** | field, 15:30-16:30, next day | Ren drives. Choose a spot (V1 Harlow curb, V2 Ridley east, V3 lot gap); van heat (§5.2); long lens (48 shots). Photograph the **Harstad box truck** (logo + plate), **Dale** (★Act re-up handoff with Tavon) and Pigeon circling on a bike. Then **Sunday's hearse**: he robs Tavon of the package at gunpoint, quick, no shots (act `robbery`, photographable). **Dilemma:** *Stay on the eye* (Sunday on the Board; violence follows) / *Call it in anonymously* (patrol rolls up, Sunday escapes, Heat +20) / *Go in yourself* (stand-off dialogue; Sunday leaves the package: \"I don't do police, Detective. Police do me.\" Van burned, Heat +30, Brass +10) | `dilemma` |"," | 3.5 | **The Major** | Annex | Pruitt in person. **Ops choice 3:** *Give him bodies* (sweep: Brass +25, Heat +20, P1 line goes dead) vs *Hold the line* (Brass −20). Board: THE PACKAGE tier (plate → Harstad Auto Parts; 555-0174 matches) | `sweep` |","-| 3.6 | **Session 2** | wire, 20:00-01:00 | Calls S2-1…S2-8. Rook asks for \"a hammer\" → **threat to life:** *Let it ride* vs *Wall-off stop* (a patrol car stops Rook's Monte Carlo for a broken taillight, finds the gun, arrests him: Brass +15, Heat +5; Rook in the box, 3 lines: \"Lawyer.\"). Lonnie: \"He wants to see you. Mama B's.\" → THE MONEY tier gets \"Boss ?\" and Mama B's. **Code flip** if Heat ≥ 50 | `wallOff`, `rookFree` |","+| 3.6 | **Session 2** | wire, 20:00-01:00 | Calls S2-1…S2-8. Rook asks for \"a hammer\" → **threat to life:** *Let it ride* vs *Wall-off stop* (a patrol car stops Rook's Monte Carlo for a broken taillight, finds the gun, arrests him: Brass +15, Heat +5; Rook in the box, 3 lines: \"Lawyer.\"). Lonnie: \"He wants to see you. Mama B's.\" → THE MONEY tier gets \"Boss ?\" and Mama B's. **Code flip** (known-plaintext page) | `wallOff`, `rookFree` |"," | 3.7 | **Interlude I3** | Tee | Easy's scene at Mama B's; who takes the loss | `lossOn` |"," "," ### 8.6 Episode 4: DRY CLEANING (~15 min)"]},{"oldStart":777,"oldLines":13,"newStart":780,"newLines":13,"lines":[" - **How a card is shown:** a live vignette (camera on a POI, characters posed, letterboxed 2.35:1), caption at the bottom, 6 s each, crossfade, the `montage` song (App. H)."," "," ### 8.9 Episode select and saves","-- **Saves:** `game.saves` slots (3 + autosave). Autosave at every beat start.","+- **Saves:** `game.saves` slots (3 + autosave). `saves.write = () => ({ data: STATE, place: 'Ep 2 · Paper', level: 'Episode 2' })`, `saves.read = s => restoreState(s.data)`. Autosave at every beat start. Manual Save/Load sits in the pause menu (`menu.saves: true`), and `saves.canSave` is true only in the Annex: your desk is the save point, so a save never lands mid-mission."," - **Title menu:** CONTINUE (latest), NEW CASE, EPISODES (unlocked), THE GAME, SETTINGS, ABOUT & CREDITS."," - **Episode select** starts an episode from a **canonical state** (STATE presets in data):","-  - Ep2: 4 faces with names; Heat 20, Brass 55.","-  - Ep3: wire up on P1, P2 and the pager clone; `coreyCI` false; Brass 50.","-  - Ep4: dilemma \"stay\", sweep false, `wallOff` true, Heat 45.","-  - Ep5: burners known, `pigeonTrust` 75, Brass 45.","+  - Ep2: 4 faces with names; Heat 20, Brass 50.","+  - Ep3: wire up on P1, P2 and the pager clone; `coreyCI` false; Heat 25, Brass 60.","+  - Ep4: dilemma \"stay\", sweep false, `wallOff` true; Heat 45, Brass 55.","+  - Ep5: burners known, `pigeonTrust` 75; Heat 40, Brass 45."," - **Restarting:** the pause menu offers *Restart this part* (the beat's autosave) and *Episode select*."," "," ---"]},{"oldStart":1049,"oldLines":6,"newStart":1052,"newLines":12,"lines":[" - **Menu:** `E.Menu` (canvas; keys, d-pad, stick, hover, click). `E.versionLabel()` tiny at the bottom right."," - **Keep clear:** the top-right corner area."," ","+### 12.8 UI look (ui.css and the E.Shell theme)","+- **E.Shell theme:** `THEME = { ink: '#f2ead8', paper: '#141210', accent: '#ffb347', muted: '#9a9080', danger: '#ff5a4a', line: '#3a342c', font: 'system-ui, -apple-system, \"Segoe UI\", Roboto, sans-serif', titleFont: '\"Arial Narrow\", \"Roboto Condensed\", \"Helvetica Neue\", Arial, sans-serif' }`","+- **Case-file panels** (Board, notebook, affidavit, evidence): manila `#e9dcb5` with ink `#2b2418`; typewriter text in `\"Courier New\", Courier, ui-monospace, monospace`; headings condensed uppercase with letter-spacing .04em; red string `#b3261e`; pushpins as CSS circles; polaroids `#f4f1ea` with a soft shadow and ±2° tilt; corkboard `#a8794a` with a subtle noise background (CSS gradients, no images).","+- **Wire-room panels:** near-black `#0b0f0c`, phosphor green text `#8fe388`, amber `#ffb347` for actions, a faint scanline overlay (CSS `repeating-linear-gradient`), tape counters in tabular numerals.","+- **Focus and legends:** §4.5. Glyph chips: §4.3.","+"," ---"," "," ## 13. About/Credits screen and the exit interview"]},{"oldStart":1412,"oldLines":7,"newStart":1421,"newLines":7,"lines":[" | 5 | `555-0798 44 07` | 555-0174 | Tee: need product → **unknown number** until Ep3 links it to Harstad |"," "," - **Live pages in Ep3 Session 1:** `555-0743 11 00`, `555-0769 33 07`.","-- **The flip page (Ep3 S2, when Heat ≥ 50):** `555-0329 22 07`. It only matches P2 when the keypad is turned the *other* way. The setup: S2-1's line \"hit me at the laundry\" comes right before it.","+- **The flip page (Ep3 S2, every playthrough):** `555-0329 22 07`. It only matches P2 when the keypad is turned the *other* way. The setup: S2-1's line \"hit me at the laundry\" comes right before it."," "," **Burners (Ep4 subpoena):**"," | Phone | Number | User |"]},{"oldStart":1449,"oldLines":7,"newStart":1458,"newLines":7,"lines":[" | S2-1 | 20:10 | P2 (P1 if not swept) | Tee → Rook | P | TEE: Man took it right off the boy. Walked up like he was asking directions. / ROOK: In a hearse? A *hearse*? / ★TEE: Hit me at the laundry later. Not this phone. / ROOK: It's Sunday. Gotta be. / ★TEE: Don't say names on the phone. | Sunday named (+4); sets up the flip page |"," | S2-2 | 20:45 | P3/P2 | Rook → \"Smokey\" | P | ★ROOK: I need a hammer. Tonight. / SMOKEY: What kind of hammer? / ★ROOK: The kind that finishes a job. / SMOKEY: Come by the shop at eleven. Cash. | **Threat to life → decision:** let it ride / wall-off stop |"," | S2-3 | 21:20 | P2 | Odessa → the laundromat payphone | N | ODESSA: Hello? Is this the laundromat phone? Is my grandson out there? Junior Hollis. Little red hoodie. / MAN: Ain't nobody here, ma'am. | — |","-| S2-4 | 21:50 | pager | Heat ≥ 50: **flip page** `555-0329 22 07` (CCW); else `555-0781 22 07` | P | — | Known-plaintext puzzle (§6.3) |","+| S2-4 | 21:50 | pager | **flip page** `555-0329 22 07` (CCW) | P | — | Known-plaintext puzzle (§6.3) |"," | S2-5 | 22:30 | P1/P2 | Lonnie → Tee | P | LONNIE: He wants to see you. / TEE: Tonight? / ★LONNIE: You know where. Mama B's. The back. / TEE: I'm coming. / LONNIE: And Terrence. Come by yourself. | THE MONEY tier: Boss ?, Mama B's |"," | S2-6 | 23:10 | P2 | two teenage girls (citizens) | N | Arguing about a boy named Marcus and a borrowed jacket | — |"," | S2-7 | 23:50 | P3/P2 | Tavon → unknown | P | TAVON: Tee say we gotta be easy for a minute. No more phones on Ridley after Friday. / UNKNOWN: Then what we using? / ★TAVON: He gonna get us something. Throwaways. | Foreshadows burners (+4) |"]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-105319/work/PLAN.md"]}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01EUDj8dzKKRTkhZbRFy4PVs","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
