{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Krm85fEVn71C4QRbqKUXdi","type":"tool_result","content":"150\t4. `<body>`: boot splash markup (run the engine in Node `vm` at build time and insert `My3D2dge.bootSplash('WIRETAP')`), then `<canvas id=\"screen\"></canvas><div id=\"ui\"></div>`\n151\t5. `<script>` engine `</script>`, then `<script>` game: `(() => { 'use strict'; const CREDITS = <credits.json>; …src files in order… })();`\n152\t\n153\tThe build must:\n154\t- fail if any inlined JS contains `</script` (escape it as `<\\/script`)\n155\t- re-parse `credits.json`\n156\t- write `../exit-interview.json` from `credits.json` (§13) and `JSON.parse` it back to verify\n157\t- print the bundle size (expect about 1.6-1.9 MB)\n158\t\n159\t### 3.4 Architecture rules (non-negotiable; they make attract, bots, network and tests possible)\n160\t1. **Controllers, not input.** Gameplay never reads `game.input` directly. Every controllable character has a `ctl`: `HumanController(input)`, `BotController`, `RemoteController` (network) or a scripted one. A controller exposes `move()`, `aim()`, `down(a)`, `pressed(a)` and `released(a)`. Scenes build the `E.Mover` intent `{ move, sprint, crouch, jumpPressed }` from `ctl`.\n161\t2. **Systems are model + view.** Every system keeps pure state and rules (headless-testable). Drawing (canvas) and DOM views read the state. The UI kit and `E.Shell` are headless-safe: no DOM means no view and the same model.\n162\t3. **Content is data.** People, missions, beats, dialogue nodes, calls, routes, evidence, board slots, ending cards and credits live in `30-data-*.js` objects with documented schemas (App. J). A boot step `validateData()` checks cross-references (missing ids, unknown people, bad cells) and reports them through `game.fail`. That is the \"infrastructure for designer tools\" the task asks for.\n163\t4. **Registries + event bus.** `def(kind, id, spec)` / `get(kind, id)`. `bus.on('photo' | 'made' | 'evidence' | 'beat' | 'sale' | 'callLogged' | …)`. Meters, toasts, achievements-style stats and the debug overlay listen. Systems never call each other's UI.\n164\t5. **Seeded randomness.** Use `E.rng(seed)` streams per system (`rng.world`, `rng.sim`, `rng.cosmetic`), never `Math.random`, in anything that affects play. Versus host streams come from `AIHub.seed` / `AIHub.rng(label)`.\n165\t6. **World units and dt.** Engine rules: 1 tile = 16 units, z up, fixed step 1/120 s, draw only through engine primitives on the game buffer.\n166\t7. **One save state.** `STATE` (App. J) is the only thing `game.saves` writes. Systems rebuild themselves from it.\n167\t\n168\t### 3.5 Scenes\n169\t| Scene | View | Pausable | Purpose |\n170\t|---|---|---|---|\n171\t| `title` | iso (live diorama) | no | Logo, main menu, idle timer → attract, touch-only notice |\n172\t| `attract` | varies | no | Demo reel (§10) |\n173\t| `card` | none | no | Episode title + epigraph (black, white text) |\n174\t| `annex` | iso interior | yes | Hub between missions: stations (§6.0) |\n175\t| `field` | iso | yes | All neighborhood missions (photos, tail, chase, van, trash, raid, money tail, cold open, corner interludes as Tee) |\n176\t| `wire` | brawler interior + DOM | yes | Wire room shifts (§6.6) |\n177\t| `box` | brawler interior + DOM | yes | Interrogation / kitchen talk (§6.4) |\n178\t| `chambers` | brawler interior + DOM | yes | Affidavit review with the judge (§6.5) |\n179\t| `montage` | iso/brawler stills | no | Epilogue cards (§8.8) |\n180\t| `credits` | none | no | Credits roll after the finale |\n181\t| `about` | DOM | no | About & Credits pages (§13) |\n182\t| `versusSetup`, `versus`, `versusResults` | iso, split | versus yes (local only) | §9 |\n183\t| `shutdown` | none | no | Detail shut down (game over) → retry from autosave or montage |\n184\t| `hubWait` | none | no | AI Hub only: \"Connecting…\" while `AIHub.connect` resolves (no prompts, no menus) |\n185\t\n186\tThe Board, notebook, cipher, affidavit editor, ops choice and evidence viewer are **UI screens** opened over `annex`/`field`/`wire`, not scenes.\n187\t\n188\t### 3.6 Engine setup (99-start.js)\n189\t```js\n190\tconst game = new E.Game({ canvas: 'screen', res: 'ps1', expand: true, view: 'iso', views: ['iso'], input: KEYS, id: 'wiretap',\n191\t  menu: { items: [['Restart this part', () => Director.restartBeat()], ['Episode select', () => Director.toEpisodes()]],\n192\t          settings: GAME_SETTINGS, controls: CONTROL_NAMES, quit: 'title', saves: true } });   // Save/Load in the pause menu; saves.canSave only in the Annex\n193\tE.style.propSize = 1.35;                       // props match size-1.25 heroes\n194\tinstallGamepadInversion(game);                  // before the first tick (§4.4)\n195\tconst ui = new E.Shell(game, { theme: THEME }); // HUD, toasts, standard pause/settings/controls\n196\tgame.start({ scenes, scene: 'title', boot: { title: 'WIRETAP', version: '1.0', steps: BOOT_STEPS, messages: BOOT_LINES } });\n197\t```\n198\t- **Boot steps:** \"Laying Ridley Avenue\" (map, FlowField cache), \"Hanging the phone lines\" (wires, shapes), \"Waking the block\" (roster/rigs), \"Checking the paperwork\" (`validateData`), \"Charging the pagers\" (audio defs).\n199\t- **Boot lines** (the engine's flavor messages): \"Pouring the coffee\", \"Juking the stats\", \"Filling out the 24-hour report\", \"Finding a parking space on Ridley\".\n200\t- **In an AI Hub session** (`AIHub.active`), 99-start skips the title: `menu.quit = false`, `autoPause: false`, and goes straight into the versus round (§9.6).\n201\t\n202\t---\n203\t\n204\t## 4. Controls and 10-foot UX\n205\t\n206\t### 4.1 Input preset `KEYS` (custom; include moves and the menu keys verbatim, since custom presets don't inherit them)\n207\t```js\n208\tconst KEYS = {\n209\t  up: ['KeyW','ArrowUp','Pad12'], down: ['KeyS','ArrowDown','Pad13'], left: ['KeyA','ArrowLeft','Pad14'], right: ['KeyD','ArrowRight','Pad15'],\n210\t  start: ['Enter','NumpadEnter','Pad9'], pause: ['Escape','KeyP','Pad9'],\n211\t  confirm: ['Enter','NumpadEnter','Space','KeyJ','KeyZ','Pad0'], cancel: ['Escape','Backspace','KeyX','KeyK','Pad1'],\n212\t  interact: ['KeyE','Pad0'], crouch: ['KeyC','ControlLeft','Pad1'], blend: ['KeyF','Pad2'], partner: ['KeyQ','Pad3'],\n213\t  notebook: ['Tab','KeyN','Pad8'], map: ['KeyM'],\n214\t  watch: ['Mouse2','Pad6'], photo: ['Mouse0','Pad7'], sprint: ['ShiftLeft','ShiftRight','Pad10'],\n215\t  rotL: ['BracketLeft','Pad4'], rotR: ['BracketRight','Pad5'], camReset: ['KeyR','Pad11'],\n216\t  tabPrev: ['KeyQ','Pad4'], tabNext: ['KeyE','Pad5'], uiAlt: ['Digit2','KeyT','Pad2'], uiInfo: ['Digit3','KeyI','Pad3'], uiFast: ['ShiftLeft','Pad7']\n217\t};\n218\t```\n219\tOn the Controls screen, hide `tabPrev`, `tabNext`, `uiAlt`, `uiInfo` and `uiFast` with `menu.controls: { tabPrev: false, … }`, and name the rest (`interact: 'Interact / vault / tackle'`, `blend: 'Act natural (hold)'`, `partner: 'Partner / crew orders'`, `watch: 'Watch (aim camera)'`, `photo: 'Take photo'`). Pad8 (Create) opens the notebook **on release, and only if Options (Pad9) wasn't pressed during the hold**, because Create+Options belongs to the AI Hub. While Pad8 is held in a session, call `input.suppress('pause')`. Don't use the touchpad button (Pad17): the engine has no label for it and not every browser reports it.\n220\t\n221\t### 4.2 Context maps (DualSense / keyboard + mouse)\n222\t| Context | DualSense | Keyboard + mouse |\n223\t|---|---|---|\n224\t| Move / sneak | L-stick (analog: walk) · ○ crouch toggle | WASD/arrows · C or Ctrl |\n225\t| Run | L3 toggles run · (chase/tail: run becomes sprint, with stamina) | hold Shift |\n226\t| Act natural (blend) | hold □ | hold F |\n227\t| Interact / vault / tackle / cuff | ✕ (context) | E · or left-click the highlighted thing in the world (walks there if far) |\n228\t| Watch (aim camera) | hold L2, aim with R-stick | hold right mouse, aim with the mouse |\n229\t| Photo | R2 while watching | left click while watching |\n230\t| Look ahead | R-stick (when not watching): camera peeks up to 64 px | move mouse toward a screen edge (edge peek, optional setting) |\n231\t| Rotate view / reset | L1 / R1 · R3 | [ / ] · R |\n232\t| Zoom | (engine) via Settings · D-pad ↑/↓ is movement, not zoom | wheel, - / = |\n233\t| Partner (hand off the eye, commands) / crew orders as Tee | △ (Tee: hold △ for the order wheel) | Q (Tee: hold Q, wheel follows the mouse) |\n234\t| Notebook / map | Create | Tab (or N) / M |\n235\t| Pause | Options | Esc / P |\n236\t| UI screens | D-pad/L-stick move focus · ✕ select · ○ back · □ alt · △ info · L1/R1 tabs · R2 hold fast | arrows/WASD · Enter/Space · Esc/Backspace · 2 / T · 3 / I · Q / E · Shift · **hover focuses, click selects, wheel scrolls** |\n237\t| Dialogue choices | ✕ on highlighted · face-button shortcuts when the choice shows a glyph (△ □ ○ ✕ diamond in the box, §6.4) | arrows + Enter, number keys 1-4, hover + click |\n238\t\n239\tSettings add **Run: Hold / Toggle** and **Watch: Hold / Toggle**.\n240\t\n241\t### 4.3 Prompts and glyphs\n242\t- **Source of truth:** `game.input.label(action)` (the player's bindings, `lastDevice`, `glyphs`). It returns, for example, `'✕' '○' '□' '△' 'L1' 'R2' 'Create' 'Options' 'L3' 'R3'` (PlayStation), `'A' 'B' 'X' 'Y' 'LB' 'RT' 'View' 'Menu' 'LS' 'RS'` (Xbox), and `'E' 'Shift' 'Tab' 'Space' 'Left click' 'Right click'` (keyboard/mouse).\n243\t- **Canvas glyphs** (`Glyph.draw(g, label, x, y)` in 02-input.js), 9×9 pixel art:\n244\t  - PlayStation: disc with symbol. ✕ `#7aa7ff` · ○ `#ff6b6b` · □ `#f08fd8` · △ `#45d6a0`.\n245\t  - Xbox: disc with letter. A `#5dc24a` · B `#e8483c` · X `#3d8ef0` · Y `#f2c230`.\n246\t  - Shoulders and triggers: a rounded pill with text (`L1`, `R2`, `LB`, `RT`). Create/Options/View/Menu: a small pill.\n247\t  - Keys: a keycap box with `E.font` text. Mouse: a 7×11 mouse sprite with the pressed button lit.\n248\t- **DOM glyphs** (`<span class=\"g g-ps-cross\">✕</span>`, `<kbd>E</kbd>`, `<span class=\"g g-mouse-l\"></span>`) use the same colors in CSS. Style E.Shell's key chips (`.esh-k`, `.esh-pr`, `.esh-keys`) with an override stylesheet so its prompts show the same colored glyphs. Don't hide the `esh-` CSS. Map label text to classes.\n249\t- **Follow the last device.** Every frame, compare `input.lastDevice` (plus `padStyle()` and the glyph setting) with last frame's. On change, re-render DOM legends and prompts. Add hysteresis: ignore mouse moves under 6 px so a nudged mouse doesn't flip a pad player's prompts.\n250\t- **Defaults:** PlayStation glyphs. Settings → *Button symbols: PlayStation / Xbox*. Override the standard `glyphs` setting by defining it again in `GAME_SETTINGS` with `{ key: 'glyphs', group: 'Game', label: 'Button symbols', options: [['playstation','PlayStation  ✕ ○ □ △'],['xbox','Xbox  A B X Y']], value: 'playstation', apply: (g, v) => g.players.forEach(p => p.glyphs = v) }`. Verify it now appears on the Settings screen. If redefining a standard key misbehaves, use a new key `padSymbols` that also calls `game.settings.set('glyphs', v)`.\n251\t\n252\t### 4.4 Gamepad axis inversion (the ~10% inverted-input issue)\n253\tSettings (group *Game*): **Invert stick left/right** (`stickInvX`) and **Invert stick up/down** (`stickInvY`). Don't reuse the key `invertY`: the engine already has that one, and it only inverts the aim stick. They flip both sticks' axes for every pad and every consumer (gameplay, engine menus, E.Shell, versus) through one wrapper installed before the first `input.tick`:\n254\t```js\n255\tfunction installGamepadInversion(game) {\n256\t  const real = navigator.getGamepads ? navigator.getGamepads.bind(navigator) : () => [];\n257\t  const wrap = p => { if (!p) return p; const ix = game.settings.stickInvX, iy = game.settings.stickInvY; if (!ix && !iy) return p;\n258\t    const a = Array.from(p.axes); if (ix) { a[0] = -a[0]; if (a.length > 2) a[2] = -a[2]; } if (iy) { a[1] = -a[1]; if (a.length > 3) a[3] = -a[3]; }\n259\t    return { id: p.id, index: p.index, connected: p.connected, mapping: p.mapping, timestamp: p.timestamp, buttons: p.buttons, axes: a,\n260\t             vibrationActuator: p.vibrationActuator, hapticActuators: p.hapticActuators }; };\n261\t  try { Object.defineProperty(navigator, 'getGamepads', { configurable: true, value: () => Array.from(real() || []).map(wrap) }); } catch (e) { game.fail('gamepad inversion', e); }\n262\t}\n263\t```\n264\tHelp text: \"Flips the sticks for controllers that report them backwards.\" Test it with a fake gamepad (§16).\n265\t\n266\t### 4.5 10-foot UI rules\n267\t- **Type.** HTML body `font-size: clamp(18px, 2.6vh, 34px)` (about 28 px at 1080p), headings 1.6-2.4×. Canvas text uses the engine's 5×7 font at `res 'ps1'` (about 28 px glyphs at 1080p) for dialogue and barks. Never below that.\n268\t- **Density.** At most 6 focusable items in a list, at most 8 cards in a grid page, no tables of data, one primary action per screen. Long content pages with L1/R1.\n269\t- **Thumbnail test.** Scale a 1920×1080 screenshot to 480×270. If any essential text is unreadable there, it's too small or dense.\n270\t- **Safe area.** 5% margins on all screen-anchored UI (TV overscan). Keep the top-right 110×60 CSS px clear for the engine's corner buttons (`game.cornerArea()`).\n271\t- **Focus.** 4 px amber `#ffb347` outline, 1.04 scale and a soft tick sound. Spatial navigation: nearest focusable in the pressed direction, by rect centers with an angle penalty. **Hover focuses** (pointerover) and click activates.\n272\t- **Hover patch.** Add one global handler so hover moves focus in the engine's own E.Shell screens too: `document.addEventListener('pointerover', e => { if (e.pointerType !== 'mouse') return; const b = e.target.closest && e.target.closest('.esh-sh button, .esh-sh [tabindex], .esh-sh select, .esh-sh input'); if (b) b.focus({ preventScroll: true }); });` E.Shell navigates by `document.activeElement`, so this keeps them in sync.\n273\t- **Legend.** Every screen has a footer legend built from actions (`UI.legend([['confirm','Select'],['cancel','Back'],['tabNext','Next page']])`) that re-renders on device change.\n274\t- **Same game on every device.** Keyboard+mouse and pad use the same screens and layouts. Only prompts differ. No desktop-only layout.\n275\t- **Color is never the only signal.** Suspicion uses icons (`·` `?` `!`) plus meters. Pertinent/non-pertinent uses icons plus text.\n276\t\n277\t### 4.6 HUD (E.Shell `ui.hud` each step; field scenes)\n278\t- `objective: { step: 'EP1 · 2/4', title, text, at, from: dana }`. It shows distance and above/below. Use `meters: .0625` (16 units = 1 m).\n279\t- `status`: `Unnoticed` / `Noticed` / `Watched` / `MADE` / `Blending` / `In the van` / `Winded`, with a color *and* a word.\n280\t- `bars`: **Heat** (max suspicion toward the player 0..1, label \"Eyes on you\"), **Stamina** (chase/tail), **Distance** (tail, §5.5).\n281\t- `counts`: `[['Film', 27], ['Fund', '$180']]`.\n282\t- `prompt: { act: 'interact', label: 'Talk', hint: 'Pockets' }` for the nearest/hovered interactable (§5.1).\n283\t- `minimap: { map, at: dana, markers }` (objective, known payphones, last-seen target).\n284\t- `ui.toast(title, text)` for photos (\"Terrence 'Tee' Mabry ★★☆ ACT\"), numbers, evidence and meter changes. `ui.tutorial(title, text)` for first-time tips (once each, stored in STATE.tips).\n285\t- Over each watcher's head in the world: `·` (calm, only with the assist on), `?` (noticed, amber), `!` (made, red), with a 12-px suspicion bar. Same as the stealth kit's overlay.\n286\t\n287\t### 4.7 Settings (game group; the engine adds Display/Sound/Comfort/Controls)\n288\t| Key | Label | Values (default first) |\n289\t|---|---|---|\n290\t| `glyphs` | Button symbols | PlayStation, Xbox |\n291\t| `stickInvX` / `stickInvY` | Invert stick left/right · up/down | off |\n292\t| `difficulty` | Case difficulty | Detective, Rookie, Murder Police |\n293\t| `runMode` / `watchMode` | Run · Watch | Hold, Toggle |\n294\t| `textSpeed` | Text speed | Normal (45 cps), Slow (28), Fast (80), Instant |\n295\t| `voices` | Voice volume | slider .8 (multiplies the voice bus) |\n296\t| `language` | Strong language | Uncensored, Bleeped (replaces a small word list with `—`) |\n297\t| `hints` | Investigation hints | on: highlights key wire lines on Rookie, Szabo hints after 2 failed tries |\n298\t| `cones` | Show sight cones | on (assist; `r.sightCone` for watchers when you're near) |\n299\t| `edgePeek` | Mouse edge peek | on |"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01XnCMPJrdKsvgzZ1BF12Jst","agent_id":"af67e84b720105c7c","session_id":"e2aa65a8-ee1a-45c4-b8e6-f96cf188e23d","uuid":"e63f388f-2c2e-43b1-bc27-d0697b9e15bd","timestamp":"2026-11-03T18:51:11.397Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Krm85fEVn71C4QRbqKUXdi","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review game plan for gaps"}
