{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KtbaF3oVVpM1dJeqEcendF","type":"tool_result","content":"300\t\n301\tDifficulty multiplies suspicion rise (Rookie .7 · Detective 1 · Murder Police 1.35), the minimization window (10 s · 8 s · 6 s), Brass decay (.7 · 1 · 1.3) and tail tolerance (lost after 16 s · 12 s · 9 s).\n302\t\n303\t### 4.8 Touch-only devices\n304\t- **Detection** at boot and on every input: `touchOnly = matchMedia('(pointer: coarse)').matches && !matchMedia('(any-pointer: fine)').matches && navigator.maxTouchPoints > 0`, and no gamepad connected, and no keydown seen yet.\n305\t- **What shows:** the title shows a centered panel, \"**Controller or keyboard required**\" (subtext: \"Connect a controller or keyboard to play. The demo will run in the meantime.\"), and a large **Settings** button. Tap it → `game.menu('settings')`.\n306\t- **No touch controls anywhere:** never pass `touch:` in scenes, set `game.input.touchEnabled = false`, and `game.settings.set('touch', 'off')` on touch-only devices.\n307\t- **Attract still runs:** after 10 s it starts, and a tap returns to the panel.\n308\t- **Recovery:** `gamepadconnected` or any `keydown` hides the panel and shows the normal menu.\n309\t\n310\t---\n311\t\n312\t## 5. Core systems\n313\t\n314\t### 5.0 Shared numbers\n315\t| Thing | Value |\n316\t|---|---|\n317\t| Tile | 16 units; map 72×56 cells = 1152×896 units |\n318\t| Dana walk / run / sprint / crouch | 52 / 85 / 125 / 32 u/s. Intent magnitude ×0.62 = walk; `sprint` held = run; in `pursuit` (chase) run becomes sprint |\n319\t| Stamina (pursuit and tail sprinting only) | 100; drains 14/s sprinting; regenerates 10/s otherwise; at 0 \"Winded\" for 2 s (jog 60, breathing sfx) |\n320\t| Humanoid sizes | adults `size 1.25, build 'heroic'`; teens 1.1; kids 13-14 1.0; Rook `build 'bulky'` |\n321\t| Field camera | `camera: { zoom: [.8, 2], start: 1.2, tall: 1.4 }`, `game.follow(dana, { z: 16, lead: 18 })`, `cam.bounds = v => map.bounds(v)`, rotation in 90° steps with a 0.35 s tween |\n322\t\n323\t### 5.1 Field scene and interactions\n324\t`field` loads a **mission** (data, App. J) and gets from it the time of day, weather, cast spawns and behaviors, objectives, events, checkpoints, music and rules. One scene runs every neighborhood mission.\n325\t\n326\t**Mission clock:** an `E.Clock` running at 30 game minutes per real minute from the mission's start time. Lighting interpolates between the time presets (§12.1) and scheduled events fire on it. It stops at the mission's end time. There are **no time limits** unless a mission says so (the tail's timers, the chase, the 60-s rescue, the raid's 30 s).\n327\t\n328\t**Interactables** are registered per mission. Each has `{ id, at: {x,y}, r: 18, verb: 'Talk'|'Read number'|'Search'|'Sit'|'Buy a soda'|'Vault'|..., when(ctx), act(ctx) }`.\n329\t- The nearest valid one within its radius drives the HUD prompt.\n330\t- The mouse hovering one (screen-pick through `{ pick: obj }` on `r.actor`/`r.shape`, then `r.pick(sx, sy)`) highlights it with a 1-px outline.\n331\t- Left click on a hovered interactable: in range → act; out of range → Dana walks to it along the cached FlowField and then acts. Any movement input cancels the walk.\n332\t\n333\t**Cover activities** (§5.2 behavior factor \"cover\"):\n334\t- sit at the bus stop\n335\t- sit on a stoop where allowed (Odessa's, after her scene)\n336\t- buy a soda at Gaither Market (Dana goes inside for 6 s: hidden, and suspicion decays at 3× the normal rate)\n337\t- lean at a wall (any wall cell edge)\n338\t- wait in a car (Dana's unmarked Chevy on Ridley, or the van)\n339\t\n340\t**Eavesdrop.** Barks (speech bubbles over NPCs, §7.5) are readable within 48 units *and* while the speaker's suspicion of you is below \"notice\". Otherwise they show as \"…\". Key barks carry intel and add an observation log.\n341\t\n342\t### 5.2 Perception: getting \"made\" (08-perception.js)\n343\t- **Observers:** every crew member flagged `watcher`, plus the target in a tail.\n344\t- **Watched:** every police character (Dana, the partner, AI plainclothes; in versus, detective players).\n345\t- One `E.Suspicion` per (observer, police) pair, updated each step:\n346\t```js\n347\tconst seen = E.sees(o, p, { map, range: o.range ?? 150, fov: o.fov ?? 1.7 });\n348\tlet b = 1;                                                   // behavior factor\n349\tif (p.watching && aimedAt(p, o, 0.17)) b = 2.2;              // staring through the camera at this observer (±10°)\n350\telse if (p.still > 2 && !p.cover) b = 1.6;                   // loitering in plain view\n351\tif (p.sprinting) b = Math.max(b, 1.4); if (p.crouching) b = Math.max(b, 1.3);\n352\tif (p.cover) b *= 0.6; if (p.blending) b *= 0.35; if (p.inCar) b *= 0.3;\n353\tif (o.knows && o.knows.has(p.id)) b *= 1.5;                  // a face they've made before\n354\tconst light = map.lit(p) ? 1.1 : (night ? 0.7 : 1);          // under a lamp vs dark\n355\to.minds[p.id].update(dt, { ...seen, exposure: seen.exposure * b * light * DIFF.rise }, p);\n356\t```\n357\t- **Tuning targets.** Tune `E.Suspicion` options until these hold on Detective; record the constants in one table:\n358\t  - Staring at a lookout from 60 units: made in about 4 s.\n359\t  - Walking past at 60 units without watching: never noticed.\n360\t  - Standing still, uncovered, 100 units away: noticed about 3 s, made about 9 s.\n361\t  - Blending at 100 units: never made.\n362\t  - Watching a non-watcher (e.g., the money man) from 120 units while a watcher only sees you from the side: made in about 15 s.\n363\t- **States:** `calm` → `notice` (`?`, the observer turns to look, the tout stops calling for 2 s) → `search` (`??`, whistles, nudges the next crew member, who also starts watching you) → `alert` = **MADE**.\n364\t- **Made consequences:**\n365\t  - The corner shuts down (§7.2) for 60 s (bark \"Five-oh!\" plus a two-tone whistle).\n366\t  - Heat +15.\n367\t  - That observer and everyone within 120 units add Dana to `knows`.\n368\t  - `p.burnedUntil = now + 60`: Dana's photos score 0 stars while burned and the HUD shows \"MADE: walk it off\".\n369\t  - Leaving every observer's sight for 20 s and getting 2 blocks away resets the local state.\n370\t  - In story missions, being made never fails the mission. It costs time and Heat, and some events (Tee's payphone call) skip a cycle. Exceptions: tail and trash (§5.5, §5.7).\n371\t- **Van heat:** each van parking spot has `heat` that rises 1 per 12 s while any watcher is within 160 units. When a crew member passes within 40 units and the van has been parked more than 90 s, add 25. At 100 the van is burned (bark \"That van been there two days\", Heat +10, and the mission asks you to relocate: choose one of the other spots).\n372\t\n373\t### 5.3 Watch mode, reading roles and photos (10-camera.js)\n374\t- **Enter.** Hold `watch`: zoom tween ×1.6 (0.25 s), a reticle at screen center, and the camera keeps the reticle in the central 60% (pans up to 7 tiles from Dana). The R-stick moves the reticle at 220 px/s (mouse: the reticle *is* the pointer). Dana's rig plays the camera-raise pose. Movement slows to 20.\n375\t- **Target.** The nearest NPC whose screen anchor (chest, `r.w(x,y,z+22)`) lies within 10 px of the reticle. Show its name if known, else \"Unknown\", plus a focus ring that tightens over 0.4 s while the reticle moves under 30 px/s.\n376\t- **Read.** Holding the reticle on a person performing a role behavior fills a read meter over 3 s. When full: an observation log (`obs:<person>:<role>`), the role tag shows on the person's card (\"LOOKOUT\", \"RUNNER\", \"STASH\", \"MONEY\", \"MUSCLE\", \"LIEUTENANT\") and Case +1. Reading a watcher who can see you is risky (b = 2.2).\n377\t- **Photo.** Press `photo`. Shutter sound (synthesized click-whirr), no flash (covert), a 2-frame white border flicker on the HUD. Film −1 (30 shots per mission; Ep3 van: 48). Score:\n378\t  - **★ Face:** the target is within 220 units, `map.sight(dana, npc)` is clear, and |angle between the NPC's facing and the NPC→Dana direction| ≤ 75°.\n379\t  - **★ Focus:** the focus ring completed.\n380\t  - **★ Act:** the NPC is in an evidentiary act right now (`sale-money`, `sale-product`, `reup-handoff`, `payphone`, `stash-access`, `count-handoff`, `robbery`), each exposing a 1.5-2.5 s `actWindow`.\n381\t  - 0 stars = \"Blurry\", which is kept but useless. Burned Dana always gets 0.\n382\t  - **First ★ Face of a person** identifies the face (Case +2). **★ Act** adds evidence (Case +5) tagged with place and time (`act:sale-money@corner 16:42`).\n383\t- **Photo object:** `{ id, subject, t, place, stars, tags, turn, light, ep }`. Rendering: `rig.drawPortrait(g, x, y, 64, { zoom: .95, turn, bg })` onto an offscreen canvas, where `turn` is the subject's facing relative to Dana's line of sight. **The photo shows them from your angle:** the back of a head if they faced away. Add a background tone by time of day, 6% grain noise, and an orange LCD date stamp `10 14 '04 16:42`. In the DOM it's a polaroid with a slight random tilt. Thumbnails are cached as dataURLs (not saved; re-render from data on load).\n384\t- **Plates and signs.** Vehicles and storefronts can carry a photo `tag` (Harstad truck → `plate:HARSTAD`). Photographing them with ★Focus yields evidence.\n385\t\n386\t### 5.4 Agents and routines (07-agents.js)\n387\t- **Agent** = `E.Mover` (or `E.Body` for crowds) + `E.Humanoid` + `brain` + `ctl` (BotController) + `say()` barks.\n388\t- **Movement:** a `FlowField` cache keyed by destination POI id (precompute about 30 POIs at boot; compute others lazily and keep them). Agents read `flow.next(x, y)` and steer.\n389\t- **Stuck rule:** less than 4 units of progress in 3 s → nudge sideways, then teleport to the nearest walkable cell out of the camera's view.\n390\t- **Routines** (data): a list of `{ go: poi, do: activity, for: [min,max] }` with activities `idle`, `lean`, `sit`, `smoke`, `phone`, `chat`, `dice`, `ball`, `wash-car`, `sweep`, `wait-bus`, `shop`, `pray` (church steps), `pigeons` (Pigeon on the roof).\n391\t- **Civilian generator:** ~25 at a time in day missions, ~12 at night. Seeded outfits from palettes (§12.4), age/sex varying size and voice. They spawn and despawn at map-edge sidewalks out of view.\n392\t- **Custom poses** (06-people.js). Post-process `rig.J` after `rig.update`, as the guide's Emberdeep notes describe. Use `E.ik3` for arms:\n393\t  - **sit:** hips to z+10, thighs forward\n394\t  - **lean:** torso tilted 8° toward the wall, one foot flat on it\n395\t  - **phone:** right hand at the head\n396\t  - **camera:** both hands at the face, elbows out\n397\t  - **smoke:** hand to mouth every 4 s, with an ember particle\n398\t  - **count money:** hands forward, thumb flick\n399\t  - **cuffed:** hands behind the back\n400\t  - **hands up**\n401\t  - **dice:** crouch, plus the `throw` move\n402\t  - **sweep:** a broom held from the hand joints\n403\t\n404\t  If a pose fights the rig, the repo's mocap clips (Mesh2Motion \"sitting\", \"talking\") are allowed through `tools/anim-set.mjs` + `Mocap.drive` (AI_GUIDE, *Where to find more*). Prefer the procedural poses.\n405\t\n406\t### 5.5 Tail (11-tail.js)\n407\t- **Route data:** `waypoints` (cells) and `acts` at waypoint indices, App. J. The target walks at 46 u/s (Dana's walk is 52). The target is an observer with `fov 1.5`, `range 170`.\n408\t- **Counter-surveillance acts:**\n409\t  - `lookBack` (2.5 s): turns 180°, fov 2.2.\n410\t  - `doubleBack`: walks back 48 units, then resumes.\n411\t  - `window` (3 s): stops at a storefront and watches the reflection, i.e. a backward cone at 0.6 strength.\n412\t  - `cutThrough`: through the 1412 vacant or the Courts breezeway at a jog (70).\n413\t  - `phoneStop` (4 s): at a payphone.\n414\t  - `wait` (n s): leans on a wall.\n415\t- **Distance band** (HUD bar with zones):\n416\t  - under 48: too close; suspicion ×1.8 whenever you're in his view\n417\t  - 64-160: good\n418\t  - 160-220: amber\n419\t  - over 220 or no line of sight: the **Losing him** timer runs (difficulty 12 s), and at 0 he's lost.\n420\t- **Mirroring rule:** while he's in `lookBack`/`window`/`wait` and Dana is visible, Dana standing still within 3 s of his stop counts as loitering (b = 1.8). Teach it: \"When he stops, keep walking or take cover. Don't stop when he stops.\"\n421\t- **Partner hand-off** (△/Q):\n422\t  - Szabo (AI) shadows on a parallel street: he picks the candidate point 120-200 units from the target, outside its cone, preferring the opposite side of a block.\n423\t  - Available when Szabo is within 200 of the target, his own suspicion < 0.3, and the 20 s cooldown is over.\n424\t  - Press: control switches to the other detective (camera tween 0.6 s), and the previous one becomes AI and peels off. Each detective has separate suspicion pairs (a different face).\n425\t- **Fail:** lost or made → \"Retry from the last checkpoint\" (one every 3 waypoints) with Brass −5 per retry, or Heat +10 if made. The tail always completes eventually.\n426\t- **Success:** reach the route's end and fulfil its objective (photo or observation).\n427\t\n428\t### 5.6 Foot chase (12-chase.js)\n429\t- **Escape graph** (data): nodes on cells with edges typed `run`, `vault` (a fence cell: 0.5 s for the runner, 0.7 s for Dana), `cut` (vacant or breezeway) and `gate`."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01XnCMPJrdKsvgzZ1BF12Jst","agent_id":"af67e84b720105c7c","session_id":"e2aa65a8-ee1a-45c4-b8e6-f96cf188e23d","uuid":"1127e33c-20c1-49d2-8447-f599bbec4923","timestamp":"2026-11-03T18:51:27.812Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01KtbaF3oVVpM1dJeqEcendF","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review game plan for gaps"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UbW2CH5utk26TBJai6KcNS","type":"tool_result","content":"ok\n349:if (p.watching && aimedAt(p, o, 0.17)) b = 2.2;              // staring through the camera at this observer (±10°)\n354:const light = isLit(p) ? 1.1 : (night ? 0.7 : 1);             // game helper: within 40 units of a lit lamp/light this frame","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e2aa65a8-ee1a-45c4-b8e6-f96cf188e23d","uuid":"2e76fdaf-e395-4b8a-9f19-276773108093","timestamp":"2026-11-03T18:51:27.939Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"ok\n349:if (p.watching && aimedAt(p, o, 0.17)) b = 2.2;              // staring through the camera at this observer (±10°)\n354:const light = isLit(p) ? 1.1 : (night ? 0.7 : 1);             // game helper: within 40 units of a lit lamp/light this frame","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-105319/agent.out","hunks":[{"oldStart":2197,"oldLines":3,"newStart":2197,"newLines":6,"lines":[" {\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-opus-5-5\",\"id\":\"msg_011CggVp8QoXU5L57QtvXB5Y\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"thinking\",\"thinking\":\"I checked every engine call in the plan against the API index; all exist except `map.lit(p)`, which I'm replacing with a defined helper and making the HUD meters-per-unit option explicit.\\n\\n\",\"signature\":\"\"}],\"container\":null,\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":2,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":2445,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":502374,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":2445,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":0},\"output_tokens\":3,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"global\",\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"input_transformations\":[],\"diagnostics\":null,\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"e2aa65a8-ee1a-45c4-b8e6-f96cf188e23d\",\"uuid\":\"b7f7e525-2365-4642-a997-c5fc088b2d33\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-03T18:51:24.473Z\",\"request_id\":\"req_011CggVp7YDurRdZMqDKZvFr\",\"narration_block_indexes\":[0],\"thinking_duration_ms\":1,\"thinking_display\":\"updates\"}"," {\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-opus-5-5\",\"id\":\"msg_011CggVqSua7vtDc4LjXf4Bg\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"thinking\",\"thinking\":\"\",\"signature\":\"\"}],\"container\":null,\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":2,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":7916,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":32796,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":7916,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":0},\"output_tokens\":3,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"global\",\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"input_transformations\":[],\"diagnostics\":null,\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01XnCMPJrdKsvgzZ1BF12Jst\",\"agent_id\":\"af67e84b720105c7c\",\"session_id\":\"e2aa65a8-ee1a-45c4-b8e6-f96cf188e23d\",\"uuid\":\"723f3430-0272-46d3-b031-e4f3ce1dae42\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-03T18:51:26.978Z\",\"request_id\":\"req_011CggVqSVGxtd3zyRcsqyHH\",\"subagent_type\":\"general-purpose\",\"task_description\":\"Review game plan for gaps\"}"," {\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-opus-5-5\",\"id\":\"msg_011CggVp8QoXU5L57QtvXB5Y\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"toolu_01UbW2CH5utk26TBJai6KcNS\",\"name\":\"Bash\",\"input\":{\"command\":\"python3 - <<'EOF'\\np = 'PLAN.md'; s = open(p).read()\\ndef rep(old, new):\\n    global s\\n    n = s.count(old); assert n == 1, f'{n} matches for {old[:60]!r}'\\n    s = s.replace(old, new)\\nrep(\\\"const light = map.lit(p) ? 1.1 : (night ? 0.7 : 1);          // under a lamp vs dark\\\",\\n    \\\"const light = isLit(p) ? 1.1 : (night ? 0.7 : 1);             // game helper: within 40 units of a lit lamp/light this frame\\\")\\nrep(\\\"const ui = new E.Shell(game, { theme: THEME }); // HUD, toasts, standard pause/settings/controls\\\",\\n    \\\"const ui = new E.Shell(game, { theme: THEME, meters: .0625 });   // HUD, toasts, standard pause/settings/controls; 16 units = 1 m\\\")\\nrep(\\\"It shows distance and above/below. Use `meters: .0625` (16 units = 1 m).\\\",\\n    \\\"It shows distance and above/below (the Shell was built with `meters: .0625`, so 16 units = 1 m).\\\")\\nopen(p, 'w').write(s); print('ok')\\nEOF\\ngrep -n \\\"isLit\\\\|aimedAt\\\" PLAN.md | head -5\",\"description\":\"Replace the non-engine map.lit call and clarify Shell meters\"},\"caller\":{\"type\":\"direct\"}}],\"container\":null,\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":2,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":2445,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":502374,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":2445,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":0},\"output_tokens\":3,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"global\",\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"input_transformations\":[],\"diagnostics\":null,\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"e2aa65a8-ee1a-45c4-b8e6-f96cf188e23d\",\"uuid\":\"1f1205be-b430-41ac-9f57-6789d6e3fa86\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-03T18:51:27.767Z\",\"request_id\":\"req_011CggVp7YDurRdZMqDKZvFr\",\"wire_tool_inputs\":{\"toolu_01UbW2CH5utk26TBJai6KcNS\":{\"command\":\"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-105319/work && python3 - <<'EOF'\\np = 'PLAN.md'; s = open(p).read()\\ndef rep(old, new):\\n    global s\\n    n = s.count(old); assert n == 1, f'{n} matches for {old[:60]!r}'\\n    s = s.replace(old, new)\\nrep(\\\"const light = map.lit(p) ? 1.1 : (night ? 0.7 : 1);          // under a lamp vs dark\\\",\\n    \\\"const light = isLit(p) ? 1.1 : (night ? 0.7 : 1);             // game helper: within 40 units of a lit lamp/light this frame\\\")\\nrep(\\\"const ui = new E.Shell(game, { theme: THEME }); // HUD, toasts, standard pause/settings/controls\\\",\\n    \\\"const ui = new E.Shell(game, { theme: THEME, meters: .0625 });   // HUD, toasts, standard pause/settings/controls; 16 units = 1 m\\\")\\nrep(\\\"It shows distance and above/below. Use `meters: .0625` (16 units = 1 m).\\\",\\n    \\\"It shows distance and above/below (the Shell was built with `meters: .0625`, so 16 units = 1 m).\\\")\\nopen(p, 'w').write(s); print('ok')\\nEOF\\ngrep -n \\\"isLit\\\\|aimedAt\\\" PLAN.md | head -5\",\"description\":\"Replace the non-engine map.lit call and clarify Shell meters\"}},\"wire_ingest_context\":{\"toolu_01UbW2CH5utk26TBJai6KcNS\":{\"cwd\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-105319/work\"}}}","+{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-opus-5-5\",\"id\":\"msg_011CggVqSua7vtDc4LjXf4Bg\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"toolu_01KtbaF3oVVpM1dJeqEcendF\",\"name\":\"Read\",\"input\":{\"file_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-105319/work/PLAN.md\",\"offset\":300,\"limit\":130},\"caller\":{\"type\":\"direct\"}}],\"container\":null,\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":2,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":7916,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":32796,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":7916,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":0},\"output_tokens\":3,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"global\",\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"input_transformations\":[],\"diagnostics\":null,\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01XnCMPJrdKsvgzZ1BF12Jst\",\"agent_id\":\"af67e84b720105c7c\",\"session_id\":\"e2aa65a8-ee1a-45c4-b8e6-f96cf188e23d\",\"uuid\":\"e5469a3c-44af-4abd-bf96-c5eef5fc1301\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-03T18:51:27.808Z\",\"request_id\":\"req_011CggVqSVGxtd3zyRcsqyHH\",\"subagent_type\":\"general-purpose\",\"task_description\":\"Review game plan for gaps\"}","+{\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"task_progress\",\"task_id\":\"af67e84b720105c7c\",\"run_id\":\"0mw11mrym-a34b9b94\",\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01XnCMPJrdKsvgzZ1BF12Jst\",\"description\":\"Reading PLAN.md\",\"subagent_type\":\"general-purpose\",\"usage\":{\"total_tokens\":42486,\"tool_uses\":7,\"duration_ms\":34485},\"last_tool_name\":\"Read\",\"uuid\":\"6d2f1362-7b84-4f79-ae40-2feb58e0a0dc\",\"session_id\":\"e2aa65a8-ee1a-45c4-b8e6-f96cf188e23d\"}","+{\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01KtbaF3oVVpM1dJeqEcendF\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"300\\t\\n301\\tDifficulty multiplies suspicion rise (Rookie .7 · Detective 1 · Murder Police 1.35), the minimization window (10 s · 8 s · 6 s), Brass decay (.7 · 1 · 1.3) and tail tolerance (lost after 16 s · 12 s · 9 s).\\n302\\t\\n303\\t### 4.8 Touch-only devices\\n304\\t- **Detection** at boot and on every input: `touchOnly = matchMedia('(pointer: coarse)').matches && !matchMedia('(any-pointer: fine)').matches && navigator.maxTouchPoints > 0`, and no gamepad connected, and no keydown seen yet.\\n305\\t- **What shows:** the title shows a centered panel, \\\"**Controller or keyboard required**\\\" (subtext: \\\"Connect a controller or keyboard to play. The demo will run in the meantime.\\\"), and a large **Settings** button. Tap it → `game.menu('settings')`.\\n306\\t- **No touch controls anywhere:** never pass `touch:` in scenes, set `game.input.touchEnabled = false`, and `game.settings.set('touch', 'off')` on touch-only devices.\\n307\\t- **Attract still runs:** after 10 s it starts, and a tap returns to the panel.\\n308\\t- **Recovery:** `gamepadconnected` or any `keydown` hides the panel and shows the normal menu.\\n309\\t\\n310\\t---\\n311\\t\\n312\\t## 5. Core systems\\n313\\t\\n314\\t### 5.0 Shared numbers\\n315\\t| Thing | Value |\\n316\\t|---|---|\\n317\\t| Tile | 16 units; map 72×56 cells = 1152×896 units |\\n318\\t| Dana walk / run / sprint / crouch | 52 / 85 / 125 / 32 u/s. Intent magnitude ×0.62 = walk; `sprint` held = run; in `pursuit` (chase) run becomes sprint |\\n319\\t| Stamina (pursuit and tail sprinting only) | 100; drains 14/s sprinting; regenerates 10/s otherwise; at 0 \\\"Winded\\\" for 2 s (jog 60, breathing sfx) |\\n320\\t| Humanoid sizes | adults `size 1.25, build 'heroic'`; teens 1.1; kids 13-14 1.0; Rook `build 'bulky'` |\\n321\\t| Field camera | `camera: { zoom: [.8, 2], start: 1.2, tall: 1.4 }`, `game.follow(dana, { z: 16, lead: 18 })`, `cam.bounds = v => map.bounds(v)`, rotation in 90° steps with a 0.35 s tween |\\n322\\t\\n323\\t### 5.1 Field scene and interactions\\n324\\t`field` loads a **mission** (data, App. J) and gets from it the time of day, weather, cast spawns and behaviors, objectives, events, checkpoints, music and rules. One scene runs every neighborhood mission.\\n325\\t\\n326\\t**Mission clock:** an `E.Clock` running at 30 game minutes per real minute from the mission's start time. Lighting interpolates between the time presets (§12.1) and scheduled events fire on it. It stops at the mission's end time. There are **no time limits** unless a mission says so (the tail's timers, the chase, the 60-s rescue, the raid's 30 s).\\n327\\t\\n328\\t**Interactables** are registered per mission. Each has `{ id, at: {x,y}, r: 18, verb: 'Talk'|'Read number'|'Search'|'Sit'|'Buy a soda'|'Vault'|..., when(ctx), act(ctx) }`.\\n329\\t- The nearest valid one within its radius drives the HUD prompt.\\n330\\t- The mouse hovering one (screen-pick through `{ pick: obj }` on `r.actor`/`r.shape`, then `r.pick(sx, sy)`) highlights it with a 1-px outline.\\n331\\t- Left click on a hovered interactable: in range → act; out of range → Dana walks to it along the cached FlowField and then acts. Any movement input cancels the walk.\\n332\\t\\n333\\t**Cover activities** (§5.2 behavior factor \\\"cover\\\"):\\n334\\t- sit at the bus stop\\n335\\t- sit on a stoop where allowed (Odessa's, after her scene)\\n336\\t- buy a soda at Gaither Market (Dana goes inside for 6 s: hidden, and suspicion decays at 3× the normal rate)\\n337\\t- lean at a wall (any wall cell edge)\\n338\\t- wait in a car (Dana's unmarked Chevy on Ridley, or the van)\\n339\\t\\n340\\t**Eavesdrop.** Barks (speech bubbles over NPCs, §7.5) are readable within 48 units *and* while the speaker's suspicion of you is below \\\"notice\\\". Otherwise they show as \\\"…\\\". Key barks carry intel and add an observation log.\\n341\\t\\n342\\t### 5.2 Perception: getting \\\"made\\\" (08-perception.js)\\n343\\t- **Observers:** every crew member flagged `watcher`, plus the target in a tail.\\n344\\t- **Watched:** every police character (Dana, the partner, AI plainclothes; in versus, detective players).\\n345\\t- One `E.Suspicion` per (observer, police) pair, updated each step:\\n346\\t```js\\n347\\tconst seen = E.sees(o, p, { map, range: o.range ?? 150, fov: o.fov ?? 1.7 });\\n348\\tlet b = 1;                                                   // behavior factor\\n349\\tif (p.watching && aimedAt(p, o, 0.17)) b = 2.2;              // staring through the camera at this observer (±10°)\\n350\\telse if (p.still > 2 && !p.cover) b = 1.6;                   // loitering in plain view\\n351\\tif (p.sprinting) b = Math.max(b, 1.4); if (p.crouching) b = Math.max(b, 1.3);\\n352\\tif (p.cover) b *= 0.6; if (p.blending) b *= 0.35; if (p.inCar) b *= 0.3;\\n353\\tif (o.knows && o.knows.has(p.id)) b *= 1.5;                  // a face they've made before\\n354\\tconst light = map.lit(p) ? 1.1 : (night ? 0.7 : 1);          // under a lamp vs dark\\n355\\to.minds[p.id].update(dt, { ...seen, exposure: seen.exposure * b * light * DIFF.rise }, p);\\n356\\t```\\n357\\t- **Tuning targets.** Tune `E.Suspicion` options until these hold on Detective; record the constants in one table:\\n358\\t  - Staring at a lookout from 60 units: made in about 4 s.\\n359\\t  - Walking past at 60 units without watching: never noticed.\\n360\\t  - Standing still, uncovered, 100 units away: noticed about 3 s, made about 9 s.\\n361\\t  - Blending at 100 units: never made.\\n362\\t  - Watching a non-watcher (e.g., the money man) from 120 units while a watcher only sees you from the side: made in about 15 s.\\n363\\t- **States:** `calm` → `notice` (`?`, the observer turns to look, the tout stops calling for 2 s) → `search` (`??`, whistles, nudges the next crew member, who also starts watching you) → `alert` = **MADE**.\\n364\\t- **Made consequences:**\\n365\\t  - The corner shuts down (§7.2) for 60 s (bark \\\"Five-oh!\\\" plus a two-tone whistle).\\n366\\t  - Heat +15.\\n367\\t  - That observer and everyone within 120 units add Dana to `knows`.\\n368\\t  - `p.burnedUntil = now + 60`: Dana's photos score 0 stars while burned and the HUD shows \\\"MADE: walk it off\\\".\\n369\\t  - Leaving every observer's sight for 20 s and getting 2 blocks away resets the local state.\\n370\\t  - In story missions, being made never fails the mission. It costs time and Heat, and some events (Tee's payphone call) skip a cycle. Exceptions: tail and trash (§5.5, §5.7).\\n371\\t- **Van heat:** each van parking spot has `heat` that rises 1 per 12 s while any watcher is within 160 units. When a crew member passes within 40 units and the van has been parked more than 90 s, add 25. At 100 the van is burned (bark \\\"That van been there two days\\\", Heat +10, and the mission asks you to relocate: choose one of the other spots).\\n372\\t\\n373\\t### 5.3 Watch mode, reading roles and photos (10-camera.js)\\n374\\t- **Enter.** Hold `watch`: zoom tween ×1.6 (0.25 s), a reticle at screen center, and the camera keeps the reticle in the central 60% (pans up to 7 tiles from Dana). The R-stick moves the reticle at 220 px/s (mouse: the reticle *is* the pointer). Dana's rig plays the camera-raise pose. Movement slows to 20.\\n375\\t- **Target.** The nearest NPC whose screen anchor (chest, `r.w(x,y,z+22)`) lies within 10 px of the reticle. Show its name if known, else \\\"Unknown\\\", plus a focus ring that tightens over 0.4 s while the reticle moves under 30 px/s.\\n376\\t- **Read.** Holding the reticle on a person performing a role behavior fills a read meter over 3 s. When full: an observation log (`obs:<person>:<role>`), the role tag shows on the person's card (\\\"LOOKOUT\\\", \\\"RUNNER\\\", \\\"STASH\\\", \\\"MONEY\\\", \\\"MUSCLE\\\", \\\"LIEUTENANT\\\") and Case +1. Reading a watcher who can see you is risky (b = 2.2).\\n377\\t- **Photo.** Press `photo`. Shutter sound (synthesized click-whirr), no flash (covert), a 2-frame white border flicker on the HUD. Film −1 (30 shots per mission; Ep3 van: 48). Score:\\n378\\t  - **★ Face:** the target is within 220 units, `map.sight(dana, npc)` is clear, and |angle between the NPC's facing and the NPC→Dana direction| ≤ 75°.\\n379\\t  - **★ Focus:** the focus ring completed.\\n380\\t  - **★ Act:** the NPC is in an evidentiary act right now (`sale-money`, `sale-product`, `reup-handoff`, `payphone`, `stash-access`, `count-handoff`, `robbery`), each exposing a 1.5-2.5 s `actWindow`.\\n381\\t  - 0 stars = \\\"Blurry\\\", which is kept but useless. Burned Dana always gets 0.\\n382\\t  - **First ★ Face of a person** identifies the face (Case +2). **★ Act** adds evidence (Case +5) tagged with place and time (`act:sale-money@corner 16:42`).\\n383\\t- **Photo object:** `{ id, subject, t, place, stars, tags, turn, light, ep }`. Rendering: `rig.drawPortrait(g, x, y, 64, { zoom: .95, turn, bg })` onto an offscreen canvas, where `turn` is the subject's facing relative to Dana's line of sight. **The photo shows them from your angle:** the back of a head if they faced away. Add a background tone by time of day, 6% grain noise, and an orange LCD date stamp `10 14 '04 16:42`. In the DOM it's a polaroid with a slight random tilt. Thumbnails are cached as dataURLs (not saved; re-render from data on load).\\n384\\t- **Plates and signs.** Vehicles and storefronts can carry a photo `tag` (Harstad truck → `plate:HARSTAD`). Photographing them with ★Focus yields evidence.\\n385\\t\\n386\\t### 5.4 Agents and routines (07-agents.js)\\n387\\t- **Agent** = `E.Mover` (or `E.Body` for crowds) + `E.Humanoid` + `brain` + `ctl` (BotController) + `say()` barks.\\n388\\t- **Movement:** a `FlowField` cache keyed by destination POI id (precompute about 30 POIs at boot; compute others lazily and keep them). Agents read `flow.next(x, y)` and steer.\\n389\\t- **Stuck rule:** less than 4 units of progress in 3 s → nudge sideways, then teleport to the nearest walkable cell out of the camera's view.\\n390\\t- **Routines** (data): a list of `{ go: poi, do: activity, for: [min,max] }` with activities `idle`, `lean`, `sit`, `smoke`, `phone`, `chat`, `dice`, `ball`, `wash-car`, `sweep`, `wait-bus`, `shop`, `pray` (church steps), `pigeons` (Pigeon on the roof).\\n391\\t- **Civilian generator:** ~25 at a time in day missions, ~12 at night. Seeded outfits from palettes (§12.4), age/sex varying size and voice. They spawn and despawn at map-edge sidewalks out of view.\\n392\\t- **Custom poses** (06-people.js). Post-process `rig.J` after `rig.update`, as the guide's Emberdeep notes describe. Use `E.ik3` for arms:\\n393\\t  - **sit:** hips to z+10, thighs forward\\n394\\t  - **lean:** torso tilted 8° toward the wall, one foot flat on it\\n395\\t  - **phone:** right hand at the head\\n396\\t  - **camera:** both hands at the face, elbows out\\n397\\t  - **smoke:** hand to mouth every 4 s, with an ember particle\\n398\\t  - **count money:** hands forward, thumb flick\\n399\\t  - **cuffed:** hands behind the back\\n400\\t  - **hands up**\\n401\\t  - **dice:** crouch, plus the `throw` move\\n402\\t  - **sweep:** a broom held from the hand joints\\n403\\t\\n404\\t  If a pose fights the rig, the repo's mocap clips (Mesh2Motion \\\"sitting\\\", \\\"talking\\\") are allowed through `tools/anim-set.mjs` + `Mocap.drive` (AI_GUIDE, *Where to find more*). Prefer the procedural poses.\\n405\\t\\n406\\t### 5.5 Tail (11-tail.js)\\n407\\t- **Route data:** `waypoints` (cells) and `acts` at waypoint indices, App. J. The target walks at 46 u/s (Dana's walk is 52). The target is an observer with `fov 1.5`, `range 170`.\\n408\\t- **Counter-surveillance acts:**\\n409\\t  - `lookBack` (2.5 s): turns 180°, fov 2.2.\\n410\\t  - `doubleBack`: walks back 48 units, then resumes.\\n411\\t  - `window` (3 s): stops at a storefront and watches the reflection, i.e. a backward cone at 0.6 strength.\\n412\\t  - `cutThrough`: through the 1412 vacant or the Courts breezeway at a jog (70).\\n413\\t  - `phoneStop` (4 s): at a payphone.\\n414\\t  - `wait` (n s): leans on a wall.\\n415\\t- **Distance band** (HUD bar with zones):\\n416\\t  - under 48: too close; suspicion ×1.8 whenever you're in his view\\n417\\t  - 64-160: good\\n418\\t  - 160-220: amber\\n419\\t  - over 220 or no line of sight: the **Losing him** timer runs (difficulty 12 s), and at 0 he's lost.\\n420\\t- **Mirroring rule:** while he's in `lookBack`/`window`/`wait` and Dana is visible, Dana standing still within 3 s of his stop counts as loitering (b = 1.8). Teach it: \\\"When he stops, keep walking or take cover. Don't stop when he stops.\\\"\\n421\\t- **Partner hand-off** (△/Q):\\n422\\t  - Szabo (AI) shadows on a parallel street: he picks the candidate point 120-200 units from the target, outside its cone, preferring the opposite side of a block.\\n423\\t  - Available when Szabo is within 200 of the target, his own suspicion < 0.3, and the 20 s cooldown is over.\\n424\\t  - Press: control switches to the other detective (camera tween 0.6 s), and the previous one becomes AI and peels off. Each detective has separate suspicion pairs (a different face).\\n425\\t- **Fail:** lost or made → \\\"Retry from the last checkpoint\\\" (one every 3 waypoints) with Brass −5 per retry, or Heat +10 if made. The tail always completes eventually.\\n426\\t- **Success:** reach the route's end and fulfil its objective (photo or observation).\\n427\\t\\n428\\t### 5.6 Foot chase (12-chase.js)\\n429\\t- **Escape graph** (data): nodes on cells with edges typed `run`, `vault` (a fence cell: 0.5 s for the runner, 0.7 s for Dana), `cut` (vacant or breezeway) and `gate`.\"}]},\"parent_tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01XnCMPJrdKsvgzZ1BF12Jst\",\"agent_id\":\"af67e84b720105c7c\",\"session_id\":\"e2aa65a8-ee1a-45c4-b8e6-f96cf188e23d\",\"uuid\":\"1127e33c-20c1-49d2-8447-f599bbec4923\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-03T18:51:27.812Z\",\"tool_result_meta\":[{\"id\":\"toolu_01KtbaF3oVVpM1dJeqEcendF\",\"permission_decision\":{\"decision\":\"accept\",\"source\":\"config\",\"reason_type\":\"mode\"}}],\"subagent_type\":\"general-purpose\",\"task_description\":\"Review game plan for gaps\"}"]}]},{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-105319/work/PLAN.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":192,"oldLines":7,"newStart":192,"newLines":7,"lines":["           settings: GAME_SETTINGS, controls: CONTROL_NAMES, quit: 'title', saves: true } });   // Save/Load in the pause menu; saves.canSave only in the Annex"," E.style.propSize = 1.35;                       // props match size-1.25 heroes"," installGamepadInversion(game);                  // before the first tick (§4.4)","-const ui = new E.Shell(game, { theme: THEME }); // HUD, toasts, standard pause/settings/controls","+const ui = new E.Shell(game, { theme: THEME, meters: .0625 });   // HUD, toasts, standard pause/settings/controls; 16 units = 1 m"," game.start({ scenes, scene: 'title', boot: { title: 'WIRETAP', version: '1.0', steps: BOOT_STEPS, messages: BOOT_LINES } });"," ```"," - **Boot steps:** \"Laying Ridley Avenue\" (map, FlowField cache), \"Hanging the phone lines\" (wires, shapes), \"Waking the block\" (roster/rigs), \"Checking the paperwork\" (`validateData`), \"Charging the pagers\" (audio defs)."]},{"oldStart":275,"oldLines":7,"newStart":275,"newLines":7,"lines":[" - **Color is never the only signal.** Suspicion uses icons (`·` `?` `!`) plus meters. Pertinent/non-pertinent uses icons plus text."," "," ### 4.6 HUD (E.Shell `ui.hud` each step; field scenes)","-- `objective: { step: 'EP1 · 2/4', title, text, at, from: dana }`. It shows distance and above/below. Use `meters: .0625` (16 units = 1 m).","+- `objective: { step: 'EP1 · 2/4', title, text, at, from: dana }`. It shows distance and above/below (the Shell was built with `meters: .0625`, so 16 units = 1 m)."," - `status`: `Unnoticed` / `Noticed` / `Watched` / `MADE` / `Blending` / `In the van` / `Winded`, with a color *and* a word."," - `bars`: **Heat** (max suspicion toward the player 0..1, label \"Eyes on you\"), **Stamina** (chase/tail), **Distance** (tail, §5.5)."," - `counts`: `[['Film', 27], ['Fund', '$180']]`."]},{"oldStart":351,"oldLines":7,"newStart":351,"newLines":7,"lines":[" if (p.sprinting) b = Math.max(b, 1.4); if (p.crouching) b = Math.max(b, 1.3);"," if (p.cover) b *= 0.6; if (p.blending) b *= 0.35; if (p.inCar) b *= 0.3;"," if (o.knows && o.knows.has(p.id)) b *= 1.5;                  // a face they've made before","-const light = map.lit(p) ? 1.1 : (night ? 0.7 : 1);          // under a lamp vs dark","+const light = isLit(p) ? 1.1 : (night ? 0.7 : 1);             // game helper: within 40 units of a lit lamp/light this frame"," o.minds[p.id].update(dt, { ...seen, exposure: seen.exposure * b * light * DIFF.rise }, p);"," ```"," - **Tuning targets.** Tune `E.Suspicion` options until these hold on Detective; record the constants in one table:"]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-105319/agent.out","/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-105319/work/PLAN.md"]}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01UbW2CH5utk26TBJai6KcNS","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
