{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Fcukb6wpCVw9e3jmcjnmtx","type":"tool_result","content":"430\t- **Runner AI:** at each node, pick the next node maximizing `dist(pursuer, node) − 0.5·alignment + rng·20`, never the edge blocked by Szabo's car (after 15 s the partner \"takes the car around\" and blocks one alley mouth: a parked car shape plus a blocked floor cell).\n431\t- **Speeds:** runner sprints 118 for 9 s, then jogs 95 (no regen). Dana sprints 125 with stamina (§5.0).\n432\t- **Vault:** a context prompt at fence cells, when moving toward the fence and within 14 units. `✕` triggers a jump arc over the blocked `fence` floor cell. Fences are floor-tagged and blocked (App. A), so walkers stop and jumpers pass.\n433\t- **Ditch:** when Dana gets within 90 units, or after 10 s, the runner throws the package into the nearest ditch spot within 40 units: trash can, under a parked car, storm drain (lost) or vacant window. Cues: throw animation, a soft \"plink\", 6 glint particles.\n434\t- **Tackle:** within 14 units while sprinting, the prompt `✕ Tackle`. The paired action `E.ACTIONS.tackle` is written like the engine's `takedown` (lunge 0.25 s, both bodies fall). A miss means a stumble of 0.8 s. A hit means the runner is `down`. Then **hold ✕ for 1.2 s** to cuff (cuffed pose; a rumble of 0.4 for 0.2 s).\n435\t- **Search:** ditch spots within 30 units show \"Search\" (2 s each). After 45 s a kid on a bike rides in and takes the package if it's still there (no drugs charge, Heat +5). A storm drain is gone.\n436\t- **Win:** cuffed. **Lose:** the runner reaches the map-edge exit node; retry from the chase start.\n437\t\n438\t### 5.7 Stealth search (trash, Ep4) and the long lens (Ep5B)\n439\t- **Trash:** 5 trash bags behind Ridley Wireless (alley cells 39-43, 20-21), each needing a 2.5 s search with a rustle sound that `E.hears` can pick up (loud 60). Two observers patrol: the store owner's nephew smoking at the back door, and Lil Moe on his bike through the alley every 40 s. Dark alley cells drop exposure (light factor 0.7 → 0.5 when crouched). Being made here aborts the search (retry from the alley entrance, Heat +5). Find the bag with 12 phone boxes: serial numbers become evidence `serials:burners`.\n440\t- **Long lens (Ep5B):** from the roof of the vacant at cells 49-51 × 16-19, directly across the alley from Mama B's back window (about 80 units away). Dana reaches it with ✕ on the vacant's alley door at (50, 20), which fades to her on the roof at z 40 and puts the camera in Watch. Watching that window opens a framed close-up vignette: a 2D painted room. Draw Easy and Lonnie with `drawPortrait` (zoom 1.2), money stacks as `px` rects and a lamp light. Easy's face shows only during `count-handoff` (4 s windows, three times). A ★★★ photo of Easy in the act is the Path B win condition.\n441\t\n442\t### 5.8 Raid (13-raid.js, Ep5A)\n443\t1. **Plan screen** (DOM, 3 cards): *Front (roll-up door)*, *Side door*, *Both (split the team)*. This sets which AI officers stand where.\n444\t2. **Stack and breach:** Dana at the chosen door. Press `✕ Breach` (a ram animation, a heavy thud with shake 4, the door cell opens with `map.set(...)`). The garage's fake roof fades (§12.6).\n445\t3. **Reactions:** 30 s real time.\n446\t   - Lil Moe runs to the toilet corner to flush. Dana must reach him within 6 s; Szabo reaches him with 50% chance if the side door is covered.\n447\t   - Dale (the courier) bolts for the roll-up door: caught if covered, otherwise he escapes (flag).\n448\t   - Tee sits on a crate: \"Let me see the paper.\" Interact → Dana shows the warrant (dialogue).\n449\t   - Rook, if free, reaches for a pistol on the workbench. Dana must interact within 3 s (\"Hands!\"). There's no shooting: if missed, Rook drops it anyway after a tense 2 s stand-off, and the flag `rookDrew` changes later lines.\n450\t4. **Search:** 4 suspicious spots (car trunk, ceiling tile, toolbox, false wall). Two hold the stash, picked from a seed. Clue decals: plaster dust under the false wall, a ladder under the ceiling tile.\n451\t5. **Results:** the package, cash and gun are seized. The press-conference cutscene follows (§8.7).\n452\t\n453\t---\n454\t\n455\t## 6. Investigation systems\n456\t\n457\t### 6.0 The Annex (hub scene) and the car\n458\tThe detail's office is a converted records room above the city impound lot, 22×10 cells (App. B). Dana walks it in iso. **Stations** are interactables, lit only when the current beat allows them:\n459\t\n460\t| Station | What it does |\n461\t|---|---|\n462\t| **The Board** (north wall, bullpen) | Opens the Board screen (§6.1). The wall shape redraws its pinned cards and strings from STATE, so progress shows in the world too |\n463\t| **Lt. Navarre's office** (glass, east) | Briefings (story nodes), the **ops choice** of the episode (§6.7), the Major's phone calls. Shows the Brass gauge |\n464\t| **Wire room** (west door) | The wire scene (§6.6), only while a line is up |\n465\t| **Evidence cage** (south-west) | Evidence viewer: photos large, items, decoded pages; also the cipher (§6.3) when a pager is in evidence |\n466\t| **Coffee** (south-east) | Talk to whoever is on break: hints (the `hints` setting), flavor, relationship lines |\n467\t| **Hal's bench** | Hal fixing a 1962 Zenith radio: wire tips, voice-ID practice |\n468\t| **Ren's desk** | Photo prints come out here (flavor); van requests |\n469\t| **Stairs** (south exit) | Leave for the next field beat → **car scene** |\n470\t\n471\t**Car scene:** Dana and Lou in a beige Chevy Lumina, as a side view of a city-night `E.Backdrop` scrolling (parallax by time), the car body drawn as a `px` silhouette with the two of them in the windows. It runs 1-3 short topics (E.Story with choices: \"the case\", \"Lou's daughter\", \"the Orioles\", \"Felton\"). It's skippable with ○ after the first line. It replaces free driving and carries character beats the way the show's car conversations do.\n472\t\n473\t### 6.1 The Board (14-board.js)\n474\t- **Model:** `slots` by tier, `cards` (people, phones, places, vehicles, businesses) and `links` (string between cards). Each slot has `needs` (facts). Facts come from photos (★Face → `face:<id>`), reads (`obs:<id>:<role>`), informants (`name:<id>`, `stmt:<id>:<fact>`), intercepts and decoded pages (`num:<phone>:<person>`) and plates (`plate:harstad`).\n475\t- **Tiers and slots:**\n476\t  - **THE CORNER:** Lieutenant (Tee), Muscle (Rook), Stash (Corey), Money (Dink), Runner (Tavon), Lookout ×2 (Pigeon, Lil Moe).\n477\t  - **THE PACKAGE:** Courier (Dale), Supplier front (Harstad Auto Parts), Re-up spot (Arundel Gas → the garage).\n478\t  - **THE MONEY:** Boss (Easy), Driver (Lonnie), Front (Mama B's), Count (Thursday after close).\n479\t  - **PHONES** column: P1, P2, P3, pager clone, burners B1-B5.\n480\t- **Interaction** (DOM corkboard, 10-ft sized: at most 8 cards visible per tier page, L1/R1 change tier):\n481\t  - Select a card (✕/click), then a slot or another card (✕/click): pin it or tie a string. Mouse drag-and-drop works too. □ unpins. △ inspects (a polaroid big, with its facts).\n482\t  - **Validation:** a pin succeeds only if the card has the slot's needed fact. Otherwise Szabo says why not (\"Says who? Get me something that puts him on the stash.\"). Nothing is lost.\n483\t  - Correct pins and links add Case points (§6.7) and play a pin-push sound.\n484\t  - An unknown person shows as a silhouette card with \"?\". Easy's slot shows \"?\" until Ep3 (name) and Ep5 (face).\n485\t- **Board tutorial** (Ep1): pin 4 faces, assign roles, and tie Tee to P1 if you photographed his payphone call.\n486\t\n487\t### 6.2 Notebook (15-notebook.js; Create / Tab)\n488\tTabs with L1/R1, at most 6 items each:\n489\t- **Objectives:** current and optional, plain sentences.\n490\t- **Map:** the neighborhood at 1 px per 2 units, with markers (objective, payphones, known places, last-seen target) and a legend.\n491\t- **People:** cards with portrait, name/alias, role, notes.\n492\t- **Evidence:** polaroids and items.\n493\t- **Phones:** known numbers, what they are, decoded pages.\n494\t- **Case:** Case strength bar, Major's patience, estimated street heat (\"Calm / Wary / Spooked / Gone dark\"), Legal risk, episode stats.\n495\t\n496\t### 6.3 Pager cipher (16-cipher.js; App. C)\n497\t- **The crew's code:** \"turn the pad\". Each digit is replaced by the digit that sits in its place after the keypad is turned a quarter-turn clockwise (`1→7 2→4 3→1 4→8 5→5 6→2 7→9 8→6 9→3 0→0`).\n498\t- **Format:** pages are `<encoded callback> <crew code> <sender id>`. Crew codes are sent in the clear (vocabulary from Corey and intercepts): `11` package ready · `22` call me at the usual phone · `33` the count · `44` need product · `55` all clear · `77` police around · `99` stop everything. Sender ids: Tee 07, Rook 13, Pigeon 14, Corey 21, Easy's people 00.\n499\t- **Decoder UI:** a big 3×4 keypad on the left and the encoded digits on the right. L1/R1 (or click the arrows) **turn the keypad** 90° at a time, and the decoded digits update live by position. When the decoded number matches a number Dana knows (notebook Phones), it locks with \"MATCH: Suds City payphone\" and becomes evidence `page:<n>` (Case +3). △ toggles a hint: Corey's line \"It's the phone... you turn it.\"\n500\t- **Code flip (Ep3):** after the robbery Tee **always** switches to counter-clockwise (the inverse), so every playthrough meets the puzzle. Old decodes stop matching (\"NO MATCH ×3\"). It's a **known-plaintext** puzzle: a page arrives right after Tee is overheard saying \"call me at the laundry\". The player turns the pad the other way until it matches P2. Hal: \"They didn't change the lock. They just turned the key the other way.\"\n501\t\n502\t### 6.4 The box: interrogation (17-box.js; App. E)\n503\t- **Scene:** `brawler` view of a small room: table, two chairs, one-way glass, a buzzing fluorescent light (flicker light plus a 120 Hz hum). The suspect sits (sit pose). Dana and Lou stand or sit.\n504\t- **DOM side panel:** the suspect's **Resolve** (100 → 0), **Fear** (0 → 100) and a clock (\"Booking wants him at Central in 20 min\" = 12 exchanges). Each is a bar with a word, with no color-only meaning.\n505\t- **Each exchange,** choose an approach. The four sit on a face-button diamond drawn in the dialog area (glyph + verb; keys 1-4; hover/click):\n506\t  - **△ Show evidence:** opens a 6-card evidence picker. Relevant evidence = a big Resolve drop. Irrelevant = Resolve +10 (\"That's a picture of a corner, Detective.\").\n507\t  - **□ Bluff:** \"Your boy already told us…\". Succeeds only if the bluffed fact is known on the Board (Resolve −25). Otherwise Resolve +20 and Trust −1.\n508\t  - **○ Lean on him:** Resolve −12, Fear +15.\n509\t  - **✕ Offer a way out:** Fear −15, Resolve −8. Right after a Lean (Lou plays bad cop, you play good cop) it combos: an extra Resolve −20 and Trust +1.\n510\t- **Beats:** 3 info beats per suspect, unlocked at Resolve thresholds and/or specific evidence. Each adds facts to the Board.\n511\t- **Lawyer:** Fear ≥ 80 → \"I want a lawyer.\" The session ends and you keep what you have.\n512\t- **Flip:** when beat 3 is reached and Fear ≤ 60, a fourth approach appears: **\"Work for us\"**. Accept → CI flag (with consequences later).\n513\t- **Kitchen variant (Ep4, Pigeon at Miss Odessa's table):**\n514\t  - Meters: **Trust** (0 → 100) and **Fear**.\n515\t  - Approaches: △ *Be honest* (+Trust if Board facts back it), □ *Promise* (+Trust now; broken promises cost later), ○ *Push* (+Fear, risky), ✕ *Listen* (small +Trust, lets him talk; Odessa approves).\n516\t  - Goal: Trust ≥ 70 → he agrees to tell Dana when the count moves (Path B enabler). Push twice → Odessa ends it.\n517\t- **Lines:** every approach × Resolve band (high/mid/low) has 2 variants per side. That's about 40 lines per suspect, written in App. E style.\n518\t\n519\t### 6.5 Paper: affidavit and the judge (18-paper.js; App. F)\n520\t- **Affidavit screen:** a typed document (typewriter keys sound as text appears) with a section per **target line** (e.g., P1, P2, pager clone).\n521\t  - Each line takes up to 3 evidence cards from the evidence locker. **Probable-cause points:**\n522\t\n523\t    | Evidence | Points |\n524\t    |---|---|\n525\t    | ACT photo tied to that number | 2 |\n526\t    | Decoded page showing the number | 2 |\n527\t    | Intercept or observation log of a crew member using it | 1 |\n528\t    | Informant statement | 1 (counts only with a direct item) |\n529\t    | Seizure | 1 |\n530\t    | Face ID linking the user to the Board | 1 |\n531\t\n532\t  - A line needs **≥ 4 points including at least one direct item** (ACT photo or page).\n533\t- **Necessity section:** checkboxes for techniques tried: *Physical surveillance*, *Confidential informant*, *Undercover purchase*, *Search warrant*, *Grand jury subpoena*. Only what STATE says you did is true. Ticking a technique you didn't use is **perjury**: hidden until the judge asks. It's a real choice: an honest affidavit with fewer ticks is weaker but safe.\n534\t- **Chambers (judge cross-examination):** Judge Halloway (crossword in hand) asks **3 questions**, chosen from App. F's pool: the weakest lines first, then any false necessity tick (always asked if present).\n535\t  - Each question offers 3-4 answers, built from your evidence and statements. The right answers cite the right item.\n536\t  - A wrong answer strikes that line. A caught lie denies everything: Brass −15, Legal +30, and Vance is furious.\n537\t  - Signed lines go up for 30 days.\n538\t  - All lines struck → denied (Brass −10). The mission runner then offers a short field beat to get one more item (any ACT photo at a payphone), and you resubmit.\n539\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01XnCMPJrdKsvgzZ1BF12Jst","agent_id":"af67e84b720105c7c","session_id":"e2aa65a8-ee1a-45c4-b8e6-f96cf188e23d","uuid":"6756e426-bbca-4aea-9b4a-4855b50c64d9","timestamp":"2026-11-03T18:51:39.859Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Fcukb6wpCVw9e3jmcjnmtx","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review game plan for gaps"}
