{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JKsQJzVdNsRCQ5mqadh1bp","type":"tool_result","content":"539\t\n540\t### 6.6 The wire room (19-wire.js; App. D) — the signature system\n541\t- **Layout:** the room on the left 38% of the screen (canvas: Hal at the reel-to-reel, which turns while recording, a green CRT, a radiator that clanks) and three DOM panels on the right, switched with L1/R1:\n542\t  - **LIVE:** the current call. Line and number, time, speakers (`UNKNOWN MALE 1` until identified), an animated speech-energy strip, and the transcript typing in sync with the voice.\n543\t  - **LOG:** recorded pertinent calls; replay any of them.\n544\t  - **PAGER:** clone-pager pages, plus the cipher.\n545\t- **A shift** is a scheduled list of calls on a session clock (e.g., 16:00 → 23:00). One game hour passes in about 45 s; hold **R2 / Shift** to fast-forward silence ×4. About 8-10 calls per session, each 15-45 s of speech. Voices go through the phone filter (§11.3).\n546\t- **Minimization (the law).**\n547\t  - On every call you may listen for the first **8 s** (difficulty 6-10 s) to judge pertinence.\n548\t  - If it's **non-pertinent** (family, food, a citizen on a public payphone), press **□ MINIMIZE** before the window ends. Listening past it on a non-pertinent call adds **Legal +4 per second**.\n549\t  - While minimized: the audio cuts, the transcript shows \"— minimized —\" and the reels stop. You may **spot-check (□ again) for 3 s once every 10 s** to catch a call that turns pertinent, then keep listening if it did.\n550\t  - Minimizing a pertinent call loses whatever is said while minimized.\n551\t- **Logging:** press **✕ LOG** while a key line is spoken (or up to 2 s after) to log it. That becomes evidence `int:<call>:<line>` (Case +4). Key lines aren't highlighted unless `hints` is on and difficulty is Rookie. Logging a line that isn't key does nothing (\"Hal: Write that down if you want, it ain't evidence.\").\n552\t- **Voice ID:** **△ ID** opens a strip of known voiceprints: people Dana heard talk in person (dialogue and barks record them in STATE) and confirmed IDs. A voiceprint is a 16-bar glyph generated from the voice profile (App. I). Matching the current speaker's glyph links the number to the person (Case +2, Board fact) for every call from now on. A wrong pick only gets \"Listen to the vowels.\"\n553\t- **Live pages** arrive on the clone pager (a beep and a toast). Decode them in PAGER (§6.3).\n554\t- **Session result screen:** pertinent calls logged, intel unlocked, minimization record, Legal change. This feeds the Director. If **Legal ≥ 100**, the judge pulls the wire: the rest of the session is skipped, a fallback beat has Dana get the missing intel the hard way (a field observation), and Brass −20.\n555\t\n556\t### 6.7 Meters and ops choices (20-meters.js)\n557\t| Meter | Range / start | Up | Down | Effects |\n558\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n559\t| **Brass** (Major's patience) | 0-100 / 60 | Arrests and seizures: Corey +10, Rook gun stop +15, sweep +25, raid +40; Sunday package +10 | Each episode start without new stats −10; affidavit denied −10; perjury −15; wire pulled −20; tail retries −5; corner gone dark −15 | **0 → the detail is shut down** (game over → retry the beat from its autosave, or take the Shut Down ending). Below 30 in Ep5 locks Path B |\n560\t| **Heat** (crew wariness) | 0-100 / 10 | Made +15; van burned +10; Corey arrest +10; seizure +15; sweep +20; wall-off stop +5; confronting Sunday +30; Tee's interlude choices ±10 | −5 per episode; good discipline as Tee is the reverse (higher Heat means a tighter crew) | ≥30: a 3rd lookout and customer screening. ≥50: payphone rotation (a tapped line goes dead one session early; the scheduler moves its calls). ≥70: more `lookBack`s in tails (+50%). ≥90: corner goes dark for a day (Brass −15) |\n561\t| **Legal** | 0-100 / 0 | Minimization violations; perjury +30; an illegal search (searching a person without cause in a field beat) +15 | −10 per episode | 100 → the wire is pulled; it also lowers the conviction lines in the endings |\n562\t| **Case** | 0+ / 0 | Faces +2, reads +1, ACT +5, statements +2, pages +3, intercepts +4, voice IDs +2, plate +5, seizure +5, Easy ACT +20 | never | Bands at the end: low < 60, mid 60-119, high ≥ 120 → sentences in the montage |\n563\t\n564\t**Ops choice** (one per episode, Navarre's office, 2-3 cards with consequences spelled out):\n565\t\n566\t| Ep | Choice |\n567\t|---|---|\n568\t| 1 | *Ask for the van*: the Ep3 stakeout uses Ren's van (normal van heat) · vs · *Ask for overtime*: the stakeout uses Dana's Chevy (heat ×1.5), but each Ep3 wire session gets one extra hour with one extra pertinent call (S1-OT: Tavon confirms the count spot, +4; S2-OT: Dink complains Tee is \"scared of phones now\", +4) |\n569\t| 2 | *Use Pockets* (free; his statement only counts with a direct item) · vs · *Pay Miss Pat*, the Gaither Market cashier (Fund −$100): a citizen witness whose statement is worth **2** PC points on P1 by itself |\n570\t| 3 | **Give the Major bodies (sweep)** vs **Hold the line** |\n571\t| 4 | *Rush the burner subpoenas* (Legal +10, Brass +5: the Major likes speed) · vs · *By the book* (Brass −5). Same calls either way: the choice is Legal against Brass |\n572\t| 5 | **Dope on the table** vs **Follow the money** |\n573\t\n574\t---\n575\t\n576\t## 7. The corner: crew side (09-corner.js)\n577\t\n578\t### 7.1 CornerSim (one system for story, interludes, versus and attract)\n579\t**Roles** (each an Agent with a role brain):\n580\t- **lieutenant:** oversees, collects cash, uses payphones and the pager.\n581\t- **muscle:** stands near the money; deals with trouble.\n582\t- **stash:** guards the stash spot and fetches product.\n583\t- **money:** takes cash from customers.\n584\t- **runner:** carries product from stash to customer.\n585\t- **tout:** calls out the brand, steers customers.\n586\t- **lookout ×1-3:** watchers on roofs, corners and bikes.\n587\t\n588\t**Places:**\n589\t- **post** (sidewalk cells 30,31-30,34, beside the corner vacant)\n590\t- **stash** (one of the stash spots: vacant 1412 inside 27,36 · trash can by the basketball court gate 19,45 · wheel well of a dead Buick on Gaither 32,40)\n591\t- **handoff spot** (alley mouth 29,42 or the vacant's side 30,35)\n592\t- **payphones** P1/P2/P3 (App. A)\n593\t- **re-up drop** (Arundel Gas → the garage in Ep4-5)\n594\t\n595\t**A sale:**\n596\t1. A customer arrives (spawn at the map edge, walks to the tout area).\n597\t2. **Money exchange** with the money man (2 s, act `sale-money`).\n598\t3. The money man signals the runner (a hand sign).\n599\t4. The runner walks to the stash and back (or the stash keeper hands it out at the vacant door, act `stash-access`).\n600\t5. **Product handoff** at the handoff spot (1.5 s, act `sale-product`).\n601\t6. The customer leaves.\n602\t\n603\t$10 a vial, and a customer buys 1-3.\n604\t\n605\t**Rates:**\n606\t- Customer arrivals: Poisson λ = 0.12/s base (story), 0.25/s (versus); × night 1.2; × package freshness (1.2 fresh → 0.8 stale); × 0 while shut down.\n607\t- The money man walks the cash to the lieutenant every $300 (act `count-handoff`).\n608\t- Re-up needed when the stash < 30 vials (versus: < 20).\n609\t\n610\t**Shutdown** (\"5-0!\"): triggered by any lookout reaching `alert` on police, a patrol car or knockers in view, or a call (player Tee or bot).\n611\t- Touts go quiet, sales freeze, runners stash what they carry, and everyone switches to innocent idles (dice, phone, lean).\n612\t- \"All clear\" after 20 s with no police in any lookout's view (versus: after the player calls it).\n613\t- Customers waiting during a shutdown leave after 15 s.\n614\t\n615\t**Ledger** (invariant tests): `vials_start − vials_sold − vials_seized = vials_now` and `cash_taken = cash_banked + cash_on_money + cash_seized`.\n616\t\n617\t### 7.2 Police pressure (for crew-side play, versus and attract)\n618\t- **Patrol car:** a sedan shape drives a lane loop (Ridley → Gaither → Dunmore → Abbott) at 70 u/s every 60-90 s, with a light bar off. It triggers shutdowns when seen.\n619\t- **Knockers:** an unmarked car stops; 2 officers jump out and frisk the nearest crew member carrying product or cash. Seized if not stashed in time.\n620\t- **Detectives** (AI plainclothes in interludes/attract, players in versus) behave like civilians but linger and raise cameras (a visible tell: the camera-raise pose for 0.6 s before a shot).\n621\t\n622\t### 7.3 Playing Tee (interludes)\n623\t- **Controls:** same movement as Dana. **✕** talks and gives a context order (\"Wake up, Pigeon\", \"Count it again\", \"Walk with me\").\n624\t- **Hold △/Q for the order wheel** (canvas radial around Tee; stick or mouse selects; release issues):\n625\t  - *Shut it down* (5-0)\n626\t  - *Open up*\n627\t  - *Move the stash* (pick a spot)\n628\t  - *Post up* (send a lookout to a spot chosen with the reticle)\n629\t- **Watch (L2/RMB)** works for Tee too: he can study people. A suspicious read reveals undercover cops and the van, and lets you call them out.\n630\t- **Pager and code card** (Create/Tab): incoming pages, and a keypad to send pages. **The code card shows Tee's plaintext and the encoded result side by side.** An observant player can learn the cipher from the crew side. That's dramatic irony on purpose; the police side still needs evidence (Corey's statement) to use it legally.\n631\t- **Payphones:** walk up and ✕, then dial on a keypad with real DTMF tones (697/770/852/941 × 1209/1336/1477 Hz).\n632\t- **The count** at the end of the shift: an animated tally (bills flick, a running total), compared with the target, then the episode's interlude choice.\n633\t- **Shortfall:** missing the target sets `teeShort`. Easy's scenes get colder and Tee's ending changes. There's no game over.\n634\t\n635\t### 7.4 Interludes (all at night, 4-6 min, CornerSim running)\n636\t| # | After | Target | Events (scripted on the sim) | Choice at the end (flags) |\n637\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n638\t| I1 | Ep1 | $2,400 | Tutorial; Dutch is $2 short (let it slide / turn him away / let Rook handle it); a patrol drive-by (call 5-0 in time); Pigeon asleep on the roof; page the re-up with the code card; Rook and Tee talk about Felton (\"who told you his name?\" → the 911 leak thread) | Dutch: `goodwill±`, `discipline±` |"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01XnCMPJrdKsvgzZ1BF12Jst","agent_id":"af67e84b720105c7c","session_id":"e2aa65a8-ee1a-45c4-b8e6-f96cf188e23d","uuid":"0db5eafc-ce22-4c41-8599-addc92b5b108","timestamp":"2026-11-03T18:52:15.395Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01JKsQJzVdNsRCQ5mqadh1bp","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review game plan for gaps"}
