{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016sJPeGxKtXdyZiJzssSNu6","type":"tool_result","content":"639\t| I2 | Ep2 | $2,800 | Corey locked up; choose a new stash spot (3 options: near/risky, far/safe, slow/safe); re-up via a **payphone choice P1/P2/P3**. Tapped phones = more intel for Dana in Ep3; untapped P3 → Ep3 starts with Hal amending (Brass −5); knockers jump out | Corey: bail him out / let him sit / \"Rook wants to send a message\" (danger flag on Corey) |\n640\t| I3 | Ep3 | $3,600 | Easy's summons at Mama B's back room (scene: Easy, Lonnie, Tee); double shift with Pigeon promoted to runner; the van event (if burned); Sunday's hearse rolls by (panic shutdown); Rook missing if arrested | **Who takes the loss?** Tee / Corey / Pigeon (`lossOn`) |\n641\t| I4 | Ep4 | $3,000 | Burner handout at the basketball court; Tee spots Dana's car (dramatic irony); Lonnie's message about the count | **Canary trap?** Feed Corey a fake re-up time (yes/no). If yes and Corey is a CI → Corey exposed in Ep5 (a rescue objective in Path A/B) |\n642\t| I5 | Ep5 | none | Path A: Central Booking, Easy's lawyer visits. Path B: dawn on the corner | A: take the weight / talk. B: run / stay |\n643\t\n644\t### 7.5 Barks\n645\tShort speech bubbles (`E.font` on a small box over the head, 2.5 s) with Animalese voice, from a data table per role and state:\n646\t- tout: \"Overtime! Got that Overtime!\", \"Orange tops, orange tops!\"\n647\t- lookout warning: \"Five-oh!\", \"Hoppers up!\", two-tone whistle\n648\t- customers: \"Y'all open?\", \"Lemme get two.\"\n649\t- civilians: small talk, Orioles, the heat, the bus being late\n650\t\n651\tIntel barks (eavesdrop) carry facts: \"Re-up at four, the old gas station.\" / \"Pigeon, get your little ass back on that roof.\"\n652\t\n653\t---\n654\t\n655\t## 8. Story mode: The Case\n656\t\n657\t### 8.1 Setting\n658\t- **Place and time:** **Penn Row**, a fictional neighborhood in West Baltimore, **October 2004**. Pagers, payphones and the first throwaway cell phones. Use the real city, invent the streets and places:\n659\t  - **Ridley Avenue** (the main drag), **Gaither Street** (the corner at Gaither & Ridley), **Dunmore**, **Abbott** and **Harlow** Streets.\n660\t  - Shops: **Gaither Market** (corner store), **Suds City** (laundromat), **Ridley Wireless & Pager** (sells the burners), **Mama B's Soul Food** (Easy's front), **Ridley Check Cashing**, **Fades & Grades** (barbershop), **Abbott Liquors**, **Ridley Carryout**.\n661\t  - Also: **Greater Hope Baptist Church**, **the Delancey Courts** (low-rise projects), **Arundel Gas** (closed station), **the garage behind the Courts**.\n662\t- **The crew's product:** **Overtime** (orange-top vials). A rival brand, **Hurricane**, is only talked about.\n663\t- **The detail:** officially \"Special Detail 9\", which everyone calls *the detail*. Its office is **the Annex**, above the city impound lot.\n664\t- **Real things stay generic:** \"Central Booking\", \"the courthouse\", \"the Western District\". All phone numbers use the fictional `555-01xx` block.\n665\t\n666\t### 8.2 Cast (all original; App. I has voices, §12.4 has colors)\n667\t| id | Name | Who | Look (Humanoid options) |\n668\t|---|---|---|---|\n669\t| dana | **Det. Dana Whitlock**, 34 | Player. Western District narcotics, grew up three blocks off Ridley; her mother Gloria still lives there. Patient, watchful, dry; takes it personally | heroic 1.25, hair short, coat (brown leather), cream sweater, jeans |\n670\t| lou | **Det. Louis \"Lou\" Szabo**, 52 | Partner. Exiled from Homicide for embarrassing a deputy commissioner. Smokes, Orioles, his father's sayings; very good in the box | heroic 1.25, bald, tan trench, hunch .15 |\n671\t| hal | **Det. Harold \"Hal\" Pettiford**, 61 | Thirteen years in the pawn unit, Army Signal Corps. Fixes tube radios at his desk; runs the wire room with infinite patience | heroic 1.2, gray hair, brown cardigan, hunch .2 |\n672\t| ren | **Officer Renata \"Ren\" Ocasio**, 26 | On loan from Southwest patrol. Digital camera, laptop, drives the van; talks fast | heroic 1.15, ponytail, navy hoodie |\n673\t| navarre | **Lt. Gilbert \"Gil\" Navarre**, 45 | Runs the detail. Careful careerist with a conscience; an old rumor follows him | heroic 1.25, shirt and burgundy tie |\n674\t| pruitt | **Maj. Leland Pruitt**, 55 | District commander. Lives for the stat sheet | bulky 1.3, navy uniform coat, gold trim, cap |\n675\t| ostrowski | **Deputy Commissioner Raymond Ostrowski** | The politics (speakerphone, press conference) | bulky 1.3, dark suit |\n676\t| vance | **ASA Corinne Vance**, 38 | Prosecutor who shepherds the affidavit; sharp, impatient | heroic 1.2, long hair pulled back, charcoal suit |\n677\t| halloway | **Judge Abner Halloway**, 68 | Signs or refuses the wire. Crosswords, bow tie, reads every log | heroic 1.2, white hair, black robe, hunch .25 |\n678\t| easy | **Darnell \"Easy\" Booker**, 39 | The boss. Never on the corner, never on a phone. Owns Mama B's and the check-cashing store. Soft-spoken, frightening | heroic 1.3, black leather coat |\n679\t| lonnie | **Lonnie Fitch**, 45 | Easy's driver and voice on the phone | bulky 1.25, gray cap |\n680\t| tee | **Terrence \"Tee\" Mabry**, 24 | Lieutenant; the second playable character. Reads business books; the counter-surveillance brain | heroic 1.25, black fitted cap, white tee, jeans, **wheat Timberlands** |\n681\t| rook | **Ricky \"Rook\" Batts**, 27 | Muscle; volatile | bulky 1.35, black do-rag, black hoodie, **black Air Force 1s, red swoosh** |\n682\t| corey | **Corey \"Stash\" Lyle**, 19 | Stash keeper; nervous, stammers; flip candidate | heroic 1.15, gray hood up, **duct-taped Nikes**, hunch .25 |\n683\t| pigeon | **Junior \"Pigeon\" Hollis**, 14 | Roof lookout; keeps pigeons on his grandmother's roof; comics. The heart of the story | heroic 1.0, red hoodie, **light-up sneakers** (blink while he runs) |\n684\t| moe | **Maurice \"Lil Moe\" Dorsey**, 13 | Bike lookout | heroic 1.0, green cap, yellow tee, bike |\n685\t| dink | **Darius \"Dink\" Pratt**, 16 | Money man | heroic 1.1, blue jersey |\n686\t| tavon | **Tavon Gibbs**, 17 | Runner/tout | heroic 1.15, black puffy coat, red band |\n687\t| pockets | **Wesley \"Pockets\" Gaines**, 47 | Informant and addict. Sells loosies and batteries from a baby stroller. Never looks at faces, knows everyone by their **shoes** | heroic 1.15, army jacket, old red cap, hunch .3, stroller shape |\n688\t| odessa | **Miss Odessa Tillman**, 70 | Pigeon's grandmother, church usher, sits on her stoop; calls Dana \"Dana Lynn\" | heroic 1.1, gray hair, plum housedress, hunch .2 |\n689\t| sunday | **Royal \"Sunday\" Odom**, 52 | Stick-up man with a code: never on Sunday, never a citizen, never a child. Drives an old **hearse** | heroic 1.25, flat cap, fishing vest |\n690\t| dale | **Dale Kucharski**, 50s | Courier; drives the **Harstad Auto Parts** box truck | bulky 1.25, red company cap, work shirt |\n691\t| harstad | **Glenn Harstad**, 57 | The connect (Dundalk). Montage teaser only | heroic 1.25, navy blazer |\n692\t| felton | **Cornelius Felton**, 66 | Retired MTA bus driver who called in the corner. Murdered in the cold open (seen only under a sheet; a photo on his stoop memorial) | |\n693\t| others | Officers Dukes and Kowalczyk (patrol), knockers, civilians, \"Dutch\" (a customer), Gloria Whitlock (phone only), State Senator Marian Ocheltree (montage) | | |\n694\t\n695\t### 8.3 Episode 1: EYES ON (~15 min)\n696\tEpigraph: *\"Everybody on that corner is working. Question is, who's signing the checks.\"* (Lou Szabo)\n697\t\n698\t| # | Beat | Where | What happens / mechanics | Exit, flags |\n699\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n700\t| 1.1 | **Cold open** | field, 05:40, rain | Police tape at 1407 Gaither, two patrol cars with light bars (red/blue lights), Felton under a sheet on his stoop, candles and flowers. Dana walks in (move tutorial). Talk to Officer Dukes, then Lou (Homicide primary), then Miss Odessa across the street. She won't talk (\"I got a grandbaby to raise.\"), and the camera drifts up to Pigeon on her roof with his birds, watching. Optional: read the cards on the stoop | Lou: \"This ain't a whodunit, Dana. It's a who-cares.\" |\n701\t| 1.2 | Card | | WIRETAP logo sting, then \"Episode 1: Eyes On\" and the epigraph | |\n702\t| 1.3 | **Briefing** | Annex | Navarre assembles the detail (introductions in App. G). The Sun ran Felton's photo; the Deputy Commissioner wants \"six weeks, one corner, arrests\". Brass gauge appears. Stations: Board (empty: tutorial arrow), Evidence cage (take the camera: 30 shots; Fund $200), Coffee (Lou). Ops choice 1 | Car scene |\n703\t| 1.4 | **Eyes on** | field, 15:00-17:30, overcast | **Required:** ★Face photos of Tee, Rook, Corey and Pigeon; read 2 roles; meet Pockets in the alley behind Gaither Market (pay $20, show photos, match shoes to names: App. G). **Optional:** an ★Act photo of a sale; Tee's call at P1 (16:10, then every 12 game minutes). Pockets also drops \"Dre broke his ankle jumping the fence at the old Arundel station\". It's needed in Ep3 and logged in the notebook. Tutorials as each first happens: Watch, Photo, Blend, Cover, Heat, Made, Eavesdrop | Back to the Chevy |\n704\t| 1.5 | **Board** | Annex | Board tutorial: pin faces, assign roles, tie Tee to P1 if photographed. Pruitt calls Navarre (speaker): \"I've got a dead taxpayer on page one and a detail with no arrests.\" | Autosave |\n705\t| 1.6 | **Interlude I1** | field, night, as Tee | §7.4 | flags |\n706\t\n707\t### 8.4 Episode 2: PAPER (~15 min)\n708\tEpigraph: *\"A judge doesn't care what you know. He cares what you can write down.\"* (ASA Corinne Vance)\n709\t\n710\t| # | Beat | Where | What happens / mechanics | Exit, flags |\n711\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n712\t| 2.1 | Card | | | |\n713\t| 2.2 | Briefing | Annex | Vance explains what a wire needs (numbers, probable cause, necessity). Hal: \"They don't carry cell phones. Payphones and pagers.\" Ops choice 2 | Car scene |\n714\t| 2.3 | **Payphones** | field, 11:00-13:00, day | Read the number plates on P1, P2 and P3 (interact; reading in a watcher's view counts as loitering). ★Act payphone photos (Tee at P1, Tavon at P2 on schedules). Then Navarre on the radio: the knockers are rolling on the corner to grab the stash kid with the pager. **Corey bolts → CHASE** (tutorial: sprint, vault, tackle, cuff), ditch and search | Corey in custody (+ package if found) |\n715\t| 2.4 | **The box** | box | Corey (App. E): B1 who he works for (Tee), B2 the code hint (\"you turn it\"), B3 the stash (1412 vacant, behind the radiator). Flip offer | `coreyCI`, facts |\n716\t| 2.5 | **Cipher** | Evidence cage | Decode Corey's pager memory (5 pages, App. C). Matches P1/P2/P3; 555-0174 stays unknown (later Harstad) | evidence |\n717\t| 2.6 | **Affidavit** | Annex | Lines for P1, P2 and the pager clone (+P3 if supported). Necessity honesty | |\n718\t| 2.7 | **Chambers** | chambers | Halloway, 3 questions (App. F). Signed: \"You're up. Thirty days. Minimize, Detective. I read the logs.\" Denied: an extra field beat (one more ★Act payphone photo), then resubmit | `wireUp` |"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01XnCMPJrdKsvgzZ1BF12Jst","agent_id":"af67e84b720105c7c","session_id":"e2aa65a8-ee1a-45c4-b8e6-f96cf188e23d","uuid":"ec4b0009-0831-4a4b-8c33-b4995171849b","timestamp":"2026-11-03T18:52:44.672Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_016sJPeGxKtXdyZiJzssSNu6","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review game plan for gaps"}
