{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QSZkmaunSLYYVkt8aDRHrL","type":"tool_result","content":"719\t| 2.8 | **Interlude I2** | Tee | Includes the payphone choice that shapes Ep3 | flags |\n720\t\n721\t### 8.5 Episode 3: UP (~18 min)\n722\tEpigraph: *\"You don't listen to a phone. You listen to a man getting comfortable.\"* (Hal Pettiford)\n723\t\n724\t| # | Beat | Where | What happens / mechanics | Exit, flags |\n725\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n726\t| 3.1 | Card | | | |\n727\t| 3.2 | **We're up** | Annex | Hal's wire tutorial (minimize, spot-check, log, ID, pages, fast-forward) | |\n728\t| 3.3 | **Session 1** | wire, 16:00-23:00 | Calls S1-1…S1-10 (App. D). The re-up riddle: \"the place where Dre messed up his ankle\" → pick the place on the notebook map (Arundel Gas). If Pockets' line was missed, Hal suggests finding Pockets (a 1-minute field beat at the bus stop) | `reupSpot` |\n729\t| 3.4 | **The van** | field, 15:30-16:30, next day | Ren drives. Choose a spot (V1 Harlow curb, V2 Ridley east, V3 lot gap); van heat (§5.2); long lens (48 shots). Photograph the **Harstad box truck** (logo + plate), **Dale** (★Act re-up handoff with Tavon) and Pigeon circling on a bike. Then **Sunday's hearse**: he robs Tavon of the package at gunpoint, quick, no shots (act `robbery`, photographable). **Dilemma:** *Stay on the eye* (Sunday on the Board; violence follows) / *Call it in anonymously* (patrol rolls up, Sunday escapes, Heat +20) / *Go in yourself* (stand-off dialogue; Sunday leaves the package: \"I don't do police, Detective. Police do me.\" Van burned, Heat +30, Brass +10) | `dilemma` |\n730\t| 3.5 | **The Major** | Annex | Pruitt in person. **Ops choice 3:** *Give him bodies* (sweep: Brass +25, Heat +20, P1 line goes dead) vs *Hold the line* (Brass −20). Board: THE PACKAGE tier (plate → Harstad Auto Parts; 555-0174 matches) | `sweep` |\n731\t| 3.6 | **Session 2** | wire, 20:00-01:00 | Calls S2-1…S2-8. Rook asks for \"a hammer\" → **threat to life:** *Let it ride* vs *Wall-off stop* (a patrol car stops Rook's Monte Carlo for a broken taillight, finds the gun, arrests him: Brass +15, Heat +5; Rook in the box, 3 lines: \"Lawyer.\"). Lonnie: \"He wants to see you. Mama B's.\" → THE MONEY tier gets \"Boss ?\" and Mama B's. **Code flip** (known-plaintext page) | `wallOff`, `rookFree` |\n732\t| 3.7 | **Interlude I3** | Tee | Easy's scene at Mama B's; who takes the loss | `lossOn` |\n733\t\n734\t### 8.6 Episode 4: DRY CLEANING (~15 min)\n735\tEpigraph: *\"Smart ain't never being seen. Smart is being boring when they look.\"* (Terrence Mabry)\n736\t\n737\t| # | Beat | Where | What happens / mechanics | Exit, flags |\n738\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n739\t| 4.1 | Card | | | |\n740\t| 4.2 | Quiet lines | Annex | The payphones went dead: \"Throwaways.\" Hal explains burners: bought for cash, used a week, thrown in the harbor. Plan: tail Tee to the handout, get the packaging, subpoena the carrier. Ops choice 4. Gloria calls: \"Somebody was asking about you at the market.\" | Car scene |\n741\t| 4.3 | **The tail** | field, 20:00, rain | Tee's dry-cleaning route (App. J `teeDry`) with Lou hand-offs (§5.5). Ends at the basketball court: Tee hands phones to the crew (read = observation `burners`) | checkpoint |\n742\t| 4.4 | **Trash** | field, 21:30, rain | The alley behind Ridley Wireless (§5.7): find the bag with 12 phone boxes | `serials` |\n743\t| 4.5 | **Kitchen** | Odessa's kitchen (box scene variant, warm light) | Pigeon at the table, Odessa at the stove (§6.4 kitchen) | `pigeonTrust` |\n744\t| 4.6 | Numbers | Annex | The subpoena returns B1-B5. Halloway amends by phone (\"Same rules, Detective.\"). Pin burners to people | |\n745\t| 4.7 | **Session 3** | wire, 6 calls (App. D) | The count is Thursdays at Mama B's after close; Friday's truck goes to \"the garage behind the Courts\". Tee mentions Dana's mother → choice: *call your mother* (`momSafe`: she goes to her sister's in the county) / *stay on the wire* | |\n746\t| 4.8 | **Interlude I4** | Tee | The canary trap | `canary` |\n747\t\n748\t### 8.7 Episode 5: THE COUNT (~15-20 min)\n749\tEpigraph: *\"Every week the money gets counted. Every week somebody comes up short.\"* (Darnell \"Easy\" Booker)\n750\t\n751\t| # | Beat | Where | What happens / mechanics |\n752\t|---|---|---|---|\n753\t| 5.1 | Card | | |\n754\t| 5.2 | **Two ways** | Annex | Pruitt, with Ostrowski on speakerphone: \"Friday. Dope on the table, cameras rolling.\" Navarre lays out both paths. **Ops choice 5:** **A, Dope on the table** (raid the garage, Friday 21:00) or **B, Follow the money** (Thursday's count at Mama B's). B needs Brass ≥ 30 and either (`coreyCI` and Corey not exposed) or `pigeonTrust` ≥ 70; otherwise its card says why it's locked |\n755\t| 5.3A | **Raid** | field, Friday 21:00 | §5.8. If the canary trap exposed Corey, first a **60-second rescue:** Rook holds Corey in the 1412 vacant (sprint there; Rook flees from police; there's no fight). Late means Corey disappears |\n756\t| 5.4A | **Press conference** | outside the garage | A table with dope, guns and cash. Pruitt and Ostrowski at the mic, camera flashes, the detail at the back. Ostrowski: \"a major blow to the drug trade in West Baltimore.\" Lou: \"Major blow. They'll be open by Monday.\" |\n757\t| 5.3B | **The count** | field, Thursday 22:30 | Tail the count runner (Pigeon if he trusts Dana and tells her the route: easier; otherwise Tavon) to Mama B's back door. Lonnie's car circles (a moving headlight cone = an observer). Then the vacant roof and the long lens (§5.7): ★★★ Easy in the act |\n758\t| 5.4B | **The morning after** | Annex | Navarre: the detail is disbanded anyway (\"The Deputy wanted a podium, not a case file.\"). Vance takes the file to a grand jury: \"Eighteen months, Detective. If you're lucky.\" |\n759\t| 5.5 | **Interlude I5** | Tee | A: Central Booking; Easy's lawyer: \"Easy says your mother's rent is paid through spring.\" Take the weight / talk. B: dawn on the corner. Run / stay |\n760\t| 5.6 | **Montage → credits** | | §8.8. Then the credits roll (names, plus \"Inspired by The Wire (2002-2008)\") → title. All episodes unlock in Episode select |\n761\t\n762\t**Shut Down** at any point (Brass 0) → the `shutdown` scene: Navarre packing boxes: \"Detail 9 is disbanded, effective Monday.\" Choose *Retry from the last autosave* or *See how it ends* (the Shut Down montage).\n763\t\n764\t### 8.8 Endings and montage\n765\t- **Three paths:** A (raid), B (money) or Shut Down. Each montage is 11-13 cards, picked by rules over the flags (App. G's card table).\n766\t- **Fixed cards** (the game goes on):\n767\t  - \"The corner at Gaither & Ridley: open for business by Monday.\"\n768\t  - \"Maj. Leland Pruitt: promoted to Colonel.\"\n769\t  - \"Hal Pettiford: kept the wire room. Nobody told him to leave.\"\n770\t- **Variable cards:**\n771\t  - Tee: by I5 choice and Case band\n772\t  - Easy: by path\n773\t  - Pigeon (3 fates): by `lossOn`, `pigeonTrust`, Path B runner and `rookFree`\n774\t  - Corey (3 fates): `coreyCI`, `canary`, rescue\n775\t  - Rook: `wallOff`, `rookDrew`\n776\t  - Sunday: `dilemma`\n777\t  - Dana: by path\n778\t  - Lou, Ren, Navarre\n779\t- **The teaser** always runs last: \"Glenn Harstad: guest of honor at State Senator Marian Ocheltree's harbor fundraiser.\" Then **TO BE CONTINUED**.\n780\t- **How a card is shown:** a live vignette (camera on a POI, characters posed, letterboxed 2.35:1), caption at the bottom, 6 s each, crossfade, the `montage` song (App. H).\n781\t\n782\t### 8.9 Episode select and saves\n783\t- **Saves:** `game.saves` slots (3 + autosave). `saves.write = () => ({ data: STATE, place: 'Ep 2 · Paper', level: 'Episode 2' })`, `saves.read = s => restoreState(s.data)`. Autosave at every beat start. Manual Save/Load sits in the pause menu (`menu.saves: true`), and `saves.canSave` is true only in the Annex: your desk is the save point, so a save never lands mid-mission.\n784\t- **Title menu:** CONTINUE (latest), NEW CASE, EPISODES (unlocked), THE GAME, SETTINGS, ABOUT & CREDITS.\n785\t- **Episode select** starts an episode from a **canonical state** (STATE presets in data):\n786\t  - Ep2: 4 faces with names; Heat 20, Brass 50.\n787\t  - Ep3: wire up on P1, P2 and the pager clone; `coreyCI` false; Heat 25, Brass 60.\n788\t  - Ep4: dilemma \"stay\", sweep false, `wallOff` true; Heat 45, Brass 55.\n789\t  - Ep5: burners known, `pigeonTrust` 75; Heat 40, Brass 45.\n790\t- **Restarting:** the pause menu offers *Restart this part* (the beat's autosave) and *Episode select*.\n791\t\n792\t---\n793\t\n794\t## 9. Versus mode and online play: THE GAME (50-versus.js, 51-net.js)\n795\t\n796\t### 9.1 The round\n797\t- **Sides:** *The Corner* (crew) vs *The Detail* (police) on the **versus zone** of the same map (cells 18-50 × 16-44: Ridley between Abbott and Harlow, Gaither, the two alleys, the Courts lane). Barricades and police tape block the zone's edge (blocked floor cells, sawhorse shapes). AI civilians walk through; detectives look like civilians.\n798\t- **Length:** 5:00 (local setup: 3, 5 or 8 min)."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01XnCMPJrdKsvgzZ1BF12Jst","agent_id":"af67e84b720105c7c","session_id":"e2aa65a8-ee1a-45c4-b8e6-f96cf188e23d","uuid":"52c6578a-6fb8-497d-a28b-e69e11874e9e","timestamp":"2026-11-03T18:53:02.832Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01QSZkmaunSLYYVkt8aDRHrL","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review game plan for gaps"}
