{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WXPJoXAD4sToJPjgB8Q8yV","type":"tool_result","content":"799\t- **Outcome:**\n800\t  - **Detail win:** Evidence reaches **100** (immediate).\n801\t  - **Corner win:** at time-up, Count ≥ **$3,000** and Evidence < 100.\n802\t  - **Draw:** neither (\"The game goes on\").\n803\t- **Seats:** side of seat *i* = `(i + round) % 2 === 0 ? 'corner' : 'detail'`, so players alternate sides between rounds. With 1 player: Detail vs bot Corner. With 3: two on one side.\n804\t  - Corner players take the **Lieutenant** first, then the **Runner**. Detail players are **Detectives** (up to 2).\n805\t  - Bots fill every empty crew role (always) and empty detective slots (to at least 1 detective).\n806\t\n807\t| Corner actions | Detail actions |\n808\t|---|---|\n809\t| **Lieutenant:** watch people (L2/RMB); **call out** a person (△/Q while watching). A detective → **burned** 25 s (their photos score 0, they're outlined red for the Corner, and AI lookouts track them). A civilian → −$200 and customers avoid the corner for 10 s; cooldown 15 s. **Shut it down / open up** (□/F). Move the stash (✕ at the stash, pick a spot). **Re-up** at a payphone (✕, 2 s) when the stash < 20 → a car drops the package in 20 s, which the Runner must fetch | **Photos** (L2 + R2 / RMB + LMB): first ★Face of each crew member +4; ★Act +12 (max 2 per crew member). Photo of the **stash** in use +25 (+15 again after it moves). **Tap a payphone** (✕, 4 s, unseen) → each Corner re-up call from it +10. **Jump-out** (△/Q while watching, once per round): patrol frisks the target 8 s later. Carrying → seizure +20 and the Corner loses what was carried; clean → −10 |\n810\t| **Runner:** pick up product at the stash (✕), hand off to a waiting customer (✕), ditch (○) if a cop closes in (lost product) | **Blend** (□/F) and cover activities work as in story. AI lookouts build suspicion on detectives (§5.2); full = auto-burn |\n811\t\n812\t- **Bots:**\n813\t  - **Corner bot:** the CornerSim role brains, plus a lieutenant brain. It shuts down when any lookout reaches `search`. It calls out the person with the highest *observed* suspicion score once that passes 0.8 (from behaviors it can see: lingering, camera raises, following the runner). It re-ups at the payphone it hasn't seen tampered with. It moves the stash after a stash photo it noticed.\n814\t  - **Detective bot:** picks vantage points (data list of 12), photographs the next sale it sees, moves when its heat passes 0.5, sometimes tails the runner, and taps a payphone when no crew is within 120 units.\n815\t  - Bots may cheat a little on perception (they read exact act windows). They're for filling seats, not balance.\n816\t- **Personal score:** Detail = the evidence they earned. Corner = the count they handled ÷ 10 + correct call-outs × 20.\n817\t- **Results screen:** outcome, then per player: photos, burns, call-outs, count. Awards (*Eyes On*: most ★Act; *Made You*: first correct call-out; *Clean Hands*: Corner player never seized; *Paper Trail*: most tap points).\n818\t\n819\t### 9.2 Local play (\"on its own\")\n820\t- **Setup screen** (DOM): P1 side, *P2: press ✕ on a second controller or Enter on the keyboard's right half* (`game.allowJoin({ max: 2 })`), round length, Start.\n821\t- **1 human:** vs bots.\n822\t- **2 humans:** split screen with `game.splitScreen(2, { follow: [c1, c2], layout: 'auto' })`. Each viewport draws its own HUD on the canvas inside `r.viewport` (E.Shell's HUD is single-screen, so versus uses a canvas HUD). Then `scene.hud(r)` draws the timer and the shared Count/Evidence bar at the top.\n823\t- **Caveat:** hidden identity can be peeked at on one screen. Accept it locally; online it's truly hidden.\n824\t- **Same code path:** local play runs the same `VersusSim` through `LocalTransport` (this copy is the host; all players are local).\n825\t\n826\t### 9.3 AI Hub: shared-world (AI Hub Session Protocol v1, client 1.4.0)\n827\t**Tags** (in `<head>`, after the client script):\n828\t```html\n829\t<meta name=\"hub:session\" content=\"1\">\n830\t<meta name=\"hub:session-players\" content=\"1-4\">\n831\t<meta name=\"hub:session-mode\" content=\"shared-world\">\n832\t<meta name=\"hub:session-minutes\" content=\"6\">\n833\t<meta name=\"hub:session-goal\" content=\"Cops: build a 100-point case. Corner: make $3,000 unseen.\">\n834\t<meta name=\"hub:session-howto\" content=\"Move: stick/WASD · Watch: L2/RMB · Photo: R2/LMB · Act: ✕/E · Call out: △/Q\">\n835\t```\n836\t**Flow** (99-start.js):\n837\t```js\n838\tif (window.AIHub && AIHub.active) {                      // straight into the round: no title, attract or menus\n839\t  game.start({ scenes, scene: 'hubWait', boot });        // 'Connecting…' (no prompts)\n840\t  const info = await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'shared-world', seats: [1, 4] });   // the hub's own card (no card: true)\n841\t  if (!info) game.go('title');                           // no hub after all: the normal game\n842\t  else { await Versus.buildRound(info); AIHub.ready(); } // roster from AIHub.rng('roster'); sides from seats + info.round\n843\t}\n844\tAIHub.on('start', () => Versus.countdown());             // overlay: role card + 3-2-1 until AIHub.time() >= 0\n845\t```\n846\t- **Host authority** (`info.isHost`): the host copy runs `VersusSim`: NPCs, crew AI, bots, rules, scoring, the timer (from `AIHub.time()`).\n847\t- **Every copy moves its own character locally** (no input lag) and reports it. The host trusts positions inside a speed check.\n848\t- **Other copies render snapshots** with 150 ms interpolation.\n849\t- **Messages:**\n850\t  - Host → all, unreliable, 10 Hz: `{t:'s', at, tl, ev, cn, ph, p:[[id,x,y,f,st,fl],…], n:[[nid,x,y,f,st],…]}`.\n851\t    - x, y are integers (world units); f is facing quantized 0-63; st is an animation code (0 idle, 1 walk, 2 run, 3 crouch, 4 watch, 5 act, 6 down, 7 sit, 8 phone, 9 bike); fl is flags (burned, carrying, shut).\n852\t    - **Keep each message under 1,100 bytes.** If the NPC list makes it bigger, send NPCs in two alternating halves (5 Hz each).\n853\t  - Host → all, reliable, on events: `{t:'e', k:'photo'|'burn'|'callout'|'tap'|'jump'|'seize'|'stash'|'reup'|'shut'|'open'|'sale', …}` (sounds, toasts, particles).\n854\t  - Client → host, unreliable, 10 Hz: `{t:'me', at, x, y, f, st, w, ax, ay}` (w = watching; ax, ay = the aimed world point).\n855\t  - Client → host, reliable: `{t:'act', k:'photo', target, q, at}` · `{k:'callout', target}` · `{k:'tap', phone}` · `{k:'jump', target}` · `{k:'shut'|'open'|'stash'|'reup'|'pickup'|'handoff'|'ditch', …}`.\n856\t  - Budget: host 10 snapshots + under 5 events per second (< 20/s); clients 10 + a few.\n857\t- **Validation on the host:**\n858\t  - Positions are clamped to `maxSpeed × elapsed × 1.5` and to walkable cells.\n859\t  - A photo claim needs: the target exists, is within 240 units of the claimer, and `map.sight` is clear on the host. If ★Act is claimed, the host's 1-second act history must show an act within 600 ms.\n860\t  - Call-outs are checked against the true identity.\n861\t- **Events:**\n862\t  - `leave` → that player's character becomes a bot on the same side; the round goes on.\n863\t  - The host leaving voids the round (the hub sends `end` `host-left`) → show \"Round cancelled\".\n864\t  - `time-up` → the host finishes at once with the timer-end outcome.\n865\t  - `end` → stop input (controllers to null), stop music and effects, show our results under the hub's. After `end`, send nothing.\n866\t- **Server** (`AIHub.server`): the host has no local player. It runs the sim and shows a spectator camera (`cam.frame` over all players). No audio, no input.\n867\t- **Finish** (host only, once):\n868\t  - `standings`: winners `[[winning side ids],[losing side ids]]`; draw `[[all ids]]`. Only hub player ids, never bots.\n869\t  - `scores`: personal scores.\n870\t  - `stats`: `{id:{Photos, Burns, Count}}`.\n871\t  - `awards`.\n872\t- **Session rules:**\n873\t  - No other network use.\n874\t  - No `alert`/`confirm`/`prompt`, no new windows.\n875\t  - Pause doesn't stop the host: the versus scene is `pausable: false` in a session. Options opens a non-pausing overlay with Settings/Controls (`game.menu('settings')`) while the character's input is suppressed.\n876\t  - `menu.quit: false` and no restart items.\n877\t  - While Create (Pad8) is held, ignore Options.\n878\t- **Randomness:** the host never uses `Math.random` for the sim. Shared rolls come from `AIHub.rng(label)`, and the roster from `AIHub.rng('roster')`, so every copy builds identical NPC rigs."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01XnCMPJrdKsvgzZ1BF12Jst","agent_id":"af67e84b720105c7c","session_id":"e2aa65a8-ee1a-45c4-b8e6-f96cf188e23d","uuid":"342c9fb6-383d-4769-ba83-f2bdf7cb2d6e","timestamp":"2026-11-03T18:53:26.850Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01WXPJoXAD4sToJPjgB8Q8yV","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review game plan for gaps"}
