{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01D5frFCqfhupYQJURLmBqhC","type":"tool_result","content":"879\t\n880\t---\n881\t\n882\t## 10. Attract mode (52-attract.js)\n883\t- **Trigger:** 10 s with no input (keys, mouse buttons, mouse moves over 6 px, wheel, touches, gamepad buttons, or axes past 0.3) on **title, main menu, episode select or versus setup**. Settings, About and Controls don't count (a player may be reading).\n884\t- **Exit:** any input → back to the title, and the idle timer resets. On touch-only devices, a tap → the notice panel.\n885\t- **The reel:** a looping playlist of vignettes, each a real system running with bot controllers. Bots may cheat: no suspicion, unlimited film, teleports, scripted perfect actions.\n886\t  - **Overlay:** letterbox bars, a **DEMO** badge, a small WIRETAP logo, a caption, and a blinking \"Press any button\" built from the current device's glyph.\n887\t\n888\t| # | s | Vignette | Bot does |\n889\t|---|---|---|---|\n890\t| 1 | 12 | **THE CORNER**: night, rain, CornerSim full; the camera turns 90° twice | Nothing: customers, touts, lookouts |\n891\t| 2 | 10 | **EYES ON**: Dana on the bus-stop bench | Enter Watch, aim at the next sale, snap ★★★, polaroid slides in |\n892\t| 3 | 10 | **THE TAIL**: Tee's route | Dana tails; Tee looks back; Dana takes cover in a doorway; hand-off to Lou |\n893\t| 4 | 9 | **THE CHASE**: Corey bolts | Sprint, vault the court fence, tackle, cuff |\n894\t| 5 | 10 | **THE WIRE**: wire room | Grandma call → MINIMIZE; pertinent call → LOG; a page decodes with a keypad turn |\n895\t| 6 | 7 | **THE BOARD**: corkboard | Cards fly onto slots; red string ties Tee to P1 |\n896\t| 7 | 8 | **THE BOX**: Corey | Lean → Offer a way out → beat unlocked |\n897\t| 8 | 10 | **THE GAME**: versus, split screen, bots | A call-out burns a detective; a stash photo |\n898\t| 9 | 8 | **THE COUNT**: Tee's tally | Bills flick, the total ticks up, then the title card |\n899\t\n900\t- **Implementation:** each entry is `{ id, seconds, setup(), tick(dt), caption }`. `setup()` loads a mission/scene with `attract: true`: no saves, no tutorials, no autosave, quieter music, no HUD prompts. The attract scene owns the clock and calls `game.go` for the next entry with a short dissolve.\n901\t\n902\t---\n903\t\n904\t## 11. Audio (03-audio.js): all written in code\n905\t\n906\t### 11.1 Music (engine `game.audio.music`, scores in App. H)\n907\t| Song | Plays | Layers (start `on: false`, faded with `audio.layer(name, vol, fade)`) |\n908\t|---|---|---|\n909\t| `theme` (84 bpm, A minor) | title, menus, about, credits, episode cards (as a `sting` of its last 2 bars) | — |\n910\t| `field` (92 bpm, D minor) | field missions as Dana | `tension` while any observer is at `notice`+ toward Dana; `pulse` at `search`; `alarm`+`stab` for 8 s after MADE |\n911\t| `corner` (95 bpm, G minor) | interludes as Tee; diegetic: also from a parked car's open door during Ep1-2 nights (volume by distance) | `lead` while the count is ahead of target pace |\n912\t| `wire` (70 bpm, E minor) | wire room, evidence cage | `pulse` while a pertinent call is live |\n913\t| `chase` (132 bpm) | foot chase, raid reactions, the 60-s rescue | — |\n914\t| `montage` (68 bpm) | epilogue montage, Shut Down | — |\n915\t| `versus` (104 bpm, C minor) | versus rounds | `pressure` at Evidence ≥ 50; `clock` in the last 60 s; `cash` at Count ≥ $2,000 |\n916\t\n917\t- **Stings** (`audio.sting`, `{ at: 'beat' }`):\n918\t  - `made`: square A4 F4 D4, 0.12 s each\n919\t  - `photoGood`: triangle E5 then B5\n920\t  - `casePoint`: triangle C5 E5 G5 arp\n921\t  - `beatDone`: the theme's last bar\n922\t- **Ducking:** call `audio.duck(true)` while dialogue voices play.\n923\t- **Field realism:** music volume in field missions is 0.6× the setting, so the ambience carries the street.\n924\t\n925\t### 11.2 Sound effects (`audio.define(name, voice)`; engine voice format)\n926\t| Name | Recipe |\n927\t|---|---|\n928\t| `shutter` | `[{wave:'noise',freq:3000,dur:.03,vol:.25},{wave:'square',freq:1800,to:900,dur:.05,vol:.08}]`, then `whirr` `{wave:'saw',freq:220,to:320,dur:.18,vol:.04}` after 40 ms |\n929\t| `pager` | three `{wave:'square',freq:'A6',dur:.07,vol:.1}` 110 ms apart, preceded by `{wave:'square',freq:'E6',dur:.07}` |\n930\t| `dtmf_<d>` | two sines at the DTMF row/column pair (697/770/852/941 × 1209/1336/1477 Hz), 0.12 s, vol .08 |\n931\t| `dialtone` / `ringback` | 350+440 Hz sines (loop); 440+480 Hz, 2 s on / 4 s off |\n932\t| `phonering` | `{wave:'square',freq:1250,vib:[22,.06],dur:.9,vol:.06}` twice |\n933\t| `reel` | noise 0.02 s click (tape start/stop); the `tape` bed is low noise while recording |\n934\t| `siren` | sine 650→1300→650 over 3.6 s (wail, loop); `yelp`: 700↔1500 at 8 Hz for 1.2 s |\n935\t| `radio` | noise burst 0.08 + squelch click (radio chatter in/out) |\n936\t| `cuffs` | `{wave:'square',freq:2400,to:1800,dur:.03,vol:.12}` ×2, 60 ms apart |\n937\t| `fence` | noise 0.22 s with vibrato (chain-link rattle on a vault) |\n938\t| `doorRam` | `boom` preset at pitch 0.7, plus `game.shake(4)` |\n939\t| `gunshot` | noise 0.18 s vol .45 + `boom` tail + an echo at −10 dB after 130 ms. Used exactly twice in the game (Ep3 robbery warning shot if *Go in*, and offscreen in I3 if Rook goes after Sunday) |\n940\t| `bark` (dog) | `{wave:'saw',freq:320,to:180,dur:.12,vol:.12}` ×2 |\n941\t| `coo` / `flap` | sine 420→380 with vibrato 0.35 s; noise bursts for wings (Pigeon's roof) |\n942\t| `busbrake` | noise hiss 0.9 s + sine squeal 2200 Hz 0.3 s |\n943\t| `typekey` / `typebell` | noise 0.015 s at 4 kHz; `blip` at a line end (affidavit) |\n944\t| `stamp` | `land` preset + paper noise (judge signs) |\n945\t| `pin` / `string` | square 900→700, 0.03 s; soft noise 0.08 s |\n946\t| `cashflick` | noise 0.01 s, repeated for the count |\n947\t| `ui_tick` / `ui_ok` / `ui_back` | triangle 1400 Hz 0.02 s vol .05; engine `confirm`; engine `cancel` |\n948\t| `step_*` | engine `step` at pitch by floor tag: concrete 1.0, asphalt 0.9, alley 0.85 + grit, grass 0.7, wood (Annex) 1.1 |\n949\t\n950\t### 11.3 Ambience beds and voices\n951\t- **Ambience** is built on `game.audio.ctx` from looping noise buffers and filters. Route it into the engine's sfx bus (`game.audio._sfxBus`, an internal field: check it exists, otherwise use your own gain scaled by `volume × sfxVolume × !muted`).\n952\t  - **Street day:** low-passed traffic rumble; a bus every 60-90 s.\n953\t  - **Street night:** traffic, plus far sirens and dog barks every 40-90 s.\n954\t  - **Rain:** band-passed noise, with thunder from engine weather.\n955\t  - **Annex:** HVAC hum, a phone ringing far off.\n956\t  - **Wire room:** tape hiss, radiator clank every 20 s, clock.\n957\t  - **Box:** 120 Hz fluorescent hum.\n958\t  - **Chambers:** clock tick.\n959\t- **Voices: Animalese/\"Simlish\" synth** (`Voice.speak(text, profile, { onChar, filter })`):\n960\t  - **Syllables:** split the text into syllables (consonant cluster + vowel); punctuation is a pause (`,` 120 ms, `.?!` 260 ms). Each syllable is a 60-80 ms grain at `profile.rate` syllables/s.\n961\t  - **Source:** an oscillator (`profile.wave`) at pitch `base × (1 + range × contour)`. The contour falls across a sentence, rises at the end of a `?`, and adds a per-syllable offset **seeded by the syllable's letters**, so the same word always sounds the same.\n962\t  - **Filters:** two parallel band-pass formant filters (F1/F2 per vowel: a 800/1200, e 400/2300, i 300/2700, o 450/800, u 325/700, all × `formant`, Q≈9), then an envelope (attack 5 ms, release to 0 by grain end).\n963\t  - **Consonants:** plosives (b d g k p t c q) are 12 ms noise bursts; fricatives (f s z h x j v) are 40 ms band-passed noise (2-6 kHz); nasals (m n) are a 60 ms low hum.\n964\t  - **Breath:** noise mixed in at `profile.breath`.\n965\t  - **Tics:** `stammer` (repeat the first syllable of 30% of words: Corey), `vibrato` (Odessa).\n966\t  - **Sync with text:**\n967\t    - `E.Dialog`: set `talk.voice = null`. Each update, play syllables for the letters added since `talk.shown` last frame. Pick the profile by `talk.name`. The text speed setting sets `talk.speed`.\n968\t    - The wire transcript is driven by `Voice.speak` itself (`onChar` reveals letters)."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01XnCMPJrdKsvgzZ1BF12Jst","agent_id":"af67e84b720105c7c","session_id":"e2aa65a8-ee1a-45c4-b8e6-f96cf188e23d","uuid":"812fac5d-c116-490b-adcf-65914ed0565a","timestamp":"2026-11-03T18:54:32.163Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01D5frFCqfhupYQJURLmBqhC","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review game plan for gaps"}
