{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VT5FQLNj7oQcoexdm7B1qi","type":"tool_result","content":"969\t  - **Phone filter** (wire calls, payphone conversations): high-pass 300 Hz → low-pass 3400 Hz → a gentle `WaveShaper` → plus line hiss at −32 dB. **Radio filter** (police radio): band-pass 500-2500 Hz + squelch clicks at the start and end.\n970\t  - **Bleeped words** (Strong language: Bleeped) get a 1 kHz sine over their syllables.\n971\t  - **Voice volume** setting multiplies the voice bus.\n972\t  - **Headless:** no-op.\n973\t\n974\t---\n975\t\n976\t## 12. Art direction and world building (05-world.js, 06-people.js)\n977\t\n978\t### 12.1 Mood by time of day (canvas lighting always; GPU lighting where available for night, `game.enableGPU({ map })`, with the same ambient set on both)\n979\t| Preset | Ambient / tint | Lights | Weather |\n980\t|---|---|---|---|\n981\t| `dawnRain` (cold open) | .45, blue-gray | patrol light bars (red/blue lights alternating at 2 Hz, radius 70), streetlamps fading | rain .7, wind .2 |\n982\t| `day` | lights off (full bright), slightly desaturated palette | none | none |\n983\t| `dusk` | .62, orange-violet | streetlamps flicker on at 17:40 | none |\n984\t| `night` | .38, cool blue | streetlamps every 6 cells (`r.prop('streetlamp', …, { light: true, cone: true })`, color `#ffb04a`); lit windows; store signs emissive; TV-blue flicker in 1 window per block | none or rain (Ep4) |\n985\t\n986\t### 12.2 Wall types (App. A legend). Everything gets `cut: true` except low walls.\n987\t| Char | What | h | Face / roof | Facade options | Colors (top/side) |\n988\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n989\t| `#` | boundary rowhouses/warehouses | 56 | brick / slab | windows `{ lit: .15 }` | `#3a2a26` / `#5a3a30` |\n990\t| `R` | brick rowhouse | 40 | brick / slab | windows `{ lit: .25 }`, door `{ chance: .35, color: '#4a2a1e' }` | `#4a3a34` / `#7a3b2e` |\n991\t| `F` | Formstone rowhouse | 40 | material `formstone` = `'#8a8680 stones size=5'` / slab | windows `{ lit: .25 }`, door .35 | `#4a4844` / `#8a8680` |\n992\t| `P` | painted brick | 36 | plaster / slab | windows `{ lit: .3 }`, shutters `#3a5a6a` | `#5a5048` / `#b8a27a` or `#6a7f8f` (alternate by block) |\n993\t| `V` | vacant | 40 | brick (dark) / slab | `decorate`: plywood panels `#b08a5a` over window and door spans, spray-paint tags | `#3a2a24` / `#4a2e26` |\n994\t| `S L E M $ K B Q` | storefronts | 32 | brick or plaster / slab | `decorate`: a lit display-window band (z 4-18, warm `#ffd890` glow texels), a sign band (z 20-28); the sign text is an `r.queue` board (§12.5) | per store |\n995\t| `H` / `T` | church / bell tower | 64 / 88 | stone / slab | arch windows `{ chance: 1 }`, stained glass `window` props on the Ridley side | `#5a5650` / `#8a847a` |\n996\t| `C` | Delancey Courts | 44 | brick (tan `#9a7a5a`) / slab | windows grid `{ lit: .35 }`, doors .3, balcony walkway `{ z: 22 }` | `#5a4a3a` / `#9a7a5a` |\n997\t| `G` | garage | 24 | metal (corrugated `'#6a6a6a metal'`) / plain | roll-up door painted on the east face | `#4a4a4a` / `#6a6a6a` |\n998\t| `k` | gas kiosk | 20 | plaster white with red band (decorate) | | `#d8d8d0` / `#e8e8e0` |\n999\t\n1000\t### 12.3 Floors (legend values `{ floor: tag }`; `floorTex` per tag, or `floorMats`)\n1001\t| Char | Tag | Look |\n1002\t|---|---|---|\n1003\t| `.` | `walk` | concrete slabs (1-cell grid lines `#8a8a86`/`#7a7a76`, cracks); stoops (shapes) along rowhouse fronts |\n1004\t| `=` | `road` | asphalt `#2e2e32` with speckle; Ridley's dashed yellow center line; crosswalk stripes at intersections; manholes; puddles when raining (darker glossy patches with a GPU glow texel picking up lamp color) |\n1005\t| `-` | `alley` | cracked asphalt `#3a3836`, weeds in cracks, litter sprites |\n1006\t| `,` | `lot` | dirt + weeds (`E.tex.dirt` + grass props) |\n1007\t| `:` | `court` | courtyard pavers |\n1008\t| `b` | `ball` | court asphalt with painted lines |\n1009\t| `p` | `play` | rubber play surface (faded red) |\n1010\t| `v` | `vacant` | gutted floorboards, debris |\n1011\t| `g` | `garage` | oil-stained concrete |\n1012\t| `f` | `fence` | blocked floor cell; draw chain-link shapes on its edges (vaultable by a jump: §5.6) |\n1013\t| `x` | `edge` | blocked; sawhorse barricades (map exits) |\n1014\t\n1015\t### 12.4 People and palettes\n1016\t- **Cast looks:** §8.2. Skin tones span a realistic range (`#3a2418 #4a2e20 #5a3a28 #6b4630 #8a5a3c #c8946a #e0b89a #f0c8a8`). Baltimore's West Side is mostly Black, so the cast and crowds reflect that, drawn with dignity. No caricature.\n1017\t- **2004 clothes:** oversized white tees, throwback jerseys, puffy coats, hoodies, fitted caps, do-rags, Timberlands, Air Force 1s; church clothes on Odessa's friends; work uniforms; cops in windbreakers and khakis or blazers.\n1018\t- **Civilians:** 6 palette families (warm, cool, earth, sport, church, work). Seeded per NPC.\n1019\t- **Addicts:** thinner (`hunch .3`), mismatched layers. Shown as people, not monsters.\n1020\t\n1021\t### 12.5 Shapes to write (E.SHAPES data, docs/ASSETS.md format; check each with `node engine/tools/asset-sheet.mjs mine.js#id`)\n1022\t- **Vehicles** (also moving, drawn with `facing` each frame):\n1023\t  - `sedan`, `chevy` (Dana's beige Lumina)\n1024\t  - `van` (white Ford Econoline, county tags)\n1025\t  - `hearse` (black, long)\n1026\t  - `boxtruck` (white, red **HARSTAD AUTO PARTS** band: the text is a queued sign)\n1027\t  - `patrol` (white/blue with a light-bar box; the lights themselves are game lights)\n1028\t  - `montecarlo` (Rook's), `deadbuick` (flat tires), `burnedcar`\n1029\t- **Street:**\n1030\t  - `payphone` (pole, hood, handset)\n1031\t  - `busshelter`; `bench` (core)\n1032\t  - `trashbag`, `dumpster`; plus the engine props `trashcan`, `hydrant`, `firedrum`, `streetlamp`, `awning`, `sign`\n1033\t  - `stoop` (3 marble steps), `pole` (utility pole with a crossbar)\n1034\t  - `sawhorse`, `chainlink` (a 16-unit segment with posts and diamond mesh: a custom `E.PATTERNS.mesh`)\n1035\t  - `hoop` (basketball, chain net), `swings`, `gaspump`, `stroller`, `bike`, `coop` (pigeon coop), `mattress`\n1036\t- **Interiors:**\n1037\t  - `corkboard` (draws live Board state: `r.queue`), `desk` + `officechair` (cut `kenney-furniture:desk-corner`, `chair-desk` with `node engine/tools/asset-set.mjs`, or write them)\n1038\t  - `filecab`, `reel2reel` (reels drawn turning in `r.queue`), `crt`, `radiator`, `coffeemaker`, `watercooler`\n1039\t  - `table`/`chair`/`bookcase` (core), `judgedesk`, `sheetbody` (a covered body for the cold open)\n1040\t- **Signs** are `r.queue` boards: a dark panel plus `E.font.text`, lit by an emissive flag for neon (\"OPEN\", \"CHECKS CASHED\", \"WINGS · FRIES · SUBS\", \"SUDS CITY\", \"RIDLEY WIRELESS & PAGER\", \"MAMA B'S SOUL FOOD\", \"FADES & GRADES\"), plus a barber pole (stripes animated by time).\n1041\t\n1042\t### 12.6 World details that sell it\n1043\t- **Phone wires** (the motif): utility poles every 8 cells along alleys and the avenue. Between pole tops (z 70), draw 8-segment sagging catenaries with `px.line` in `r.queue` (sorted above roofs). **A pair of sneakers hangs on the wire over Gaither & Ridley.** Pigeons sit on the wire near Odessa's roof and scatter (flap) when someone runs below.\n1044\t- **Fake roofs** for walk-in interiors (the garage): an `r.queue` polygon with `footprint` that fades to 15% when Dana is inside or within 24 units of a door. The 1412 vacant has no roof (burned): draw charred beams.\n1045\t- **Vacants and decay:** plywood, a \"V\" spray mark, a mattress in the lot, the fire drum (flame prop, `light: true`) at night with two men warming their hands.\n1046\t- **Life:** a bus pulls up at P3 every 90 s (a bus shape drives the Ridley lane and stops 4 s); kids shoot hoops in daytime; Odessa sweeps her stoop at dawn.\n1047\t- **Felton's memorial** stays on his stoop through Ep5: candles, flowers, a photo. It gets smaller each episode.\n1048\t\n1049\t### 12.7 Title screen\n1050\t- **Scene:** the live iso diorama of the corner at night in rain (CornerSim with AI, no player), camera slowly turning (one 90° step every 20 s).\n1051\t- **Logo:** \"WIRETAP\" in `E.font.title` (scale 4, colors `['#fff6dc','#ffcf7a','#e08a2a']`, depth 3, depthColor `#3a1a0a`). A telephone wire runs behind the logo with sneakers hanging from it. Tagline \"Somebody's always listening.\"\n1052\t- **Menu:** `E.Menu` (canvas; keys, d-pad, stick, hover, click). `E.versionLabel()` tiny at the bottom right.\n1053\t- **Keep clear:** the top-right corner area.\n1054\t\n1055\t### 12.8 UI look (ui.css and the E.Shell theme)\n1056\t- **E.Shell theme:** `THEME = { ink: '#f2ead8', paper: '#141210', accent: '#ffb347', muted: '#9a9080', danger: '#ff5a4a', line: '#3a342c', font: 'system-ui, -apple-system, \"Segoe UI\", Roboto, sans-serif', titleFont: '\"Arial Narrow\", \"Roboto Condensed\", \"Helvetica Neue\", Arial, sans-serif' }`\n1057\t- **Case-file panels** (Board, notebook, affidavit, evidence): manila `#e9dcb5` with ink `#2b2418`; typewriter text in `\"Courier New\", Courier, ui-monospace, monospace`; headings condensed uppercase with letter-spacing .04em; red string `#b3261e`; pushpins as CSS circles; polaroids `#f4f1ea` with a soft shadow and ±2° tilt; corkboard `#a8794a` with a subtle noise background (CSS gradients, no images).\n1058\t- **Wire-room panels:** near-black `#0b0f0c`, phosphor green text `#8fe388`, amber `#ffb347` for actions, a faint scanline overlay (CSS `repeating-linear-gradient`), tape counters in tabular numerals."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01XnCMPJrdKsvgzZ1BF12Jst","agent_id":"af67e84b720105c7c","session_id":"e2aa65a8-ee1a-45c4-b8e6-f96cf188e23d","uuid":"7a67a9c2-0dba-4eab-8c55-113d6feaefd6","timestamp":"2026-11-03T18:54:46.544Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01VT5FQLNj7oQcoexdm7B1qi","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review game plan for gaps"}
