{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01784nxXZ5rgbUDisfCWqVJf","type":"tool_result","content":"1059\t- **Focus and legends:** §4.5. Glyph chips: §4.3.\n1060\t\n1061\t---\n1062\t\n1063\t## 13. About/Credits screen and the exit interview\n1064\t- **`credits.json` is the single source** of the About pages and of `exit-interview.json`. The build copies its `exitInterview` object verbatim into `../exit-interview.json` and verifies it parses.\n1065\t- **About & Credits** (title menu → DOM screen; L1/R1 pages; large type; at most about 10 short lines per page; stick scrolls long answers):\n1066\t  1. **Credits:**\n1067\t     - WIRETAP; \"An original game inspired by *The Wire* (HBO, 2002-2008). Not affiliated with HBO or the show's creators.\"\n1068\t     - Design and code: the model(s) that built it (truthfully: if the builder isn't claude-opus-5-5 at max effort, list both, e.g. \"Planned by Anthropic claude-opus-5-5 (max); built by <id>\").\n1069\t     - Engine: my-3D2dge v0.85.1 by Michael Crosato (MIT). Multiplayer: AI Hub Session Protocol v1, client 1.4.0.\n1070\t     - Any CC0 asset entries used (Kenney/KayKit via the engine's store), each with its source line.\n1071\t  2. **Source Information:** every field of TASK.md's list, same text as `exitInterview.sourceInformation`.\n1072\t  3. **Testing Feedback:** the 4 questions with answers.\n1073\t  4. **Engine Feedback:** the 6 questions with answers.\n1074\t  5. **Prompt Feedback:** the 4 questions with answers.\n1075\t- **Write \"unknown\" for anything you can't confirm.** Fill in real answers at the end of the build: no placeholders ship.\n1076\t- **Exit interview shape** (exactly TASK.md's). Suggested values to start from; correct any that turn out untrue:\n1077\t```json\n1078\t{\n1079\t  \"sourceInformation\": {\n1080\t    \"date\": \"2026-11-03 10:53\",\n1081\t    \"source\": \"The Wire (2002-2008)\",\n1082\t    \"genre\": \"Stealth investigation / crime drama with a corner-management sim and an asymmetric versus mode\",\n1083\t    \"perspective\": \"Isometric 2.5D (pixel-art 3D skeletons on a tile world); brawler-view interiors; HTML case-file screens\",\n1084\t    \"tech\": \"my-3D2dge v0.85.1 full engine (canvas 2D, optional WebGPU lighting); AI Hub session client 1.4.0; vanilla JavaScript; Web Audio\",\n1085\t    \"artDirection\": \"Engine-native retro-modern pixel art (PS1-era 2D look) pushed toward grit: sodium streetlight, rain, Formstone rowhouses, boarded vacants\",\n1086\t    \"animation\": \"Engine-native procedural Humanoid rigs (E.MOVES, poses, E.ACTIONS paired actions) plus custom joint post-processed poses; tweens and coroutine scripts\",\n1087\t    \"audio\": \"Code-written chip-synth music (engine music tracks, layered), synthesized effects and ambience, Web Audio formant gibberish voices with a telephone filter\",\n1088\t    \"online\": \"AI Hub Session Protocol v1, shared-world versus for 1-4 players (host-authoritative); local split-screen versus; no other network\",\n1089\t    \"testing\": \"<fill in: what you actually ran>\",\n1090\t    \"research\": \"my-3D2dge handoff docs (API.md, AI_GUIDE.md, ASSETS.md, kits) and the AI Hub protocol README; knowledge of the series from memory; no other web research\",\n1091\t    \"environment\": \"Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\",\n1092\t    \"model\": \"Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort max\",\n1093\t    \"usage\": \"unknown\"\n1094\t  },\n1095\t  \"testingFeedback\": [\"…\", \"…\", \"…\", \"…\"],\n1096\t  \"engineFeedback\": [\"…\", \"…\", \"…\", \"…\", \"…\", \"…\"],\n1097\t  \"promptFeedback\": [\"…\", \"…\", \"…\", \"…\"],\n1098\t  \"aiHub\": {\n1099\t    \"name\": \"WIRETAP\",\n1100\t    \"tagline\": \"Somebody's always listening.\",\n1101\t    \"description\": \"Work both sides of a West Baltimore corner in 2004: build a wiretap case one photo, page and phone call at a time, then run the corner the case is built on. Includes a 1-4 player cops-vs-corner versus mode.\",\n1102\t    \"type\": \"Game\",\n1103\t    \"genre\": \"Stealth\",\n1104\t    \"source\": \"The Wire (2002-2008)\",\n1105\t    \"series\": \"\",\n1106\t    \"players\": \"1–4\",\n1107\t    \"controls\": \"Stick/WASD move · L2/RMB watch · R2/LMB photo · ✕/E interact · △/Q partner · Create/Tab notebook\",\n1108\t    \"tags\": [\"story\", \"versus\", \"pixel art\", \"isometric\", \"crime\", \"detective\"]\n1109\t  }\n1110\t}\n1111\t```\n1112\t- **The build's final chat reply** must also contain Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback (TASK.md).\n1113\t\n1114\t---\n1115\t\n1116\t## 14. Build order and milestones\n1117\tBuild systems before content and one complete episode before breadth. **Each milestone ends with its tests green and a bundle that runs.**\n1118\t\n1119\t| M | Goal | Done when |\n1120\t|---|---|---|\n1121\t| **M0** Setup | Dev folder, engine and hub client fetched, `build.mjs`, `index.html`, `tests/headless.mjs` skeleton, blank title scene | The bundle opens with no errors; `node engine/tools/check.mjs <bundle>` passes; headless boot test passes |\n1122\t| **M1** Framework | Scenes skeleton; Controller classes; KEYS preset; settings (glyphs, stick inversion, difficulty, text speed, language, voices); canvas and DOM glyph rendering with device switching; DOM UI kit (focus nav, hover focus, legend); hover patch for E.Shell; save system; touch-only notice; About screen (rendering `credits.json`); **Voice synth prototype** (speak a line with 3 profiles, phone filter); music player with the 7 songs | Fake-gamepad test shows ✕ prompts and Xbox after switching; inversion test flips movement; the touch-only profile shows the notice; voice speaks in sync with a test dialog |\n1123\t| **M2** World | Neighborhood TileMap (App. A) with wall types, facades, floors, stoops, poles and wires, props, lights, weather, time presets; Annex map; camera rotate/zoom/peek; Dana moves (walk/run/crouch/blend); civilians with routines; FlowField cache | Screenshots of day/night/rain in 3 rotations look right (thumbnail test, check.mjs look notes acted on); 25 civilians walk 5 min without getting stuck (headless) |\n1124\t| **M3** Corner and eyes | CornerSim (all roles, sales, shutdown, ledger); perception/made; Watch, reads, photos and polaroids; HUD; interactables, cover, eavesdrop, barks | Headless: ledger invariants hold over 10 min; a careless bot gets made within 30 s; a careful bot reads 2 roles and gets 4 faces |\n1125\t| **M4** Episode 1 vertical slice | Director and mission runner; E.Story + Dialog with voices; Annex stations; Board; notebook; Pockets' shoe game; cold open; I1 as Tee (order wheel, code card, payphone keypad, count) | Ep1 playable start to finish with a pad and with keyboard+mouse; autosave/continue works; deep links `#ep1.*` reach every beat |\n1126\t| **M5** Episode 2 | Chase (escape graph, vault, tackle, cuff, ditch, search); box; cipher; affidavit and necessity; chambers; I2 | Headless chase bot catches Corey; box thresholds and lawyer rule; affidavit scoring and perjury detection; Ep2 playable |\n1127\t| **M6** Episode 3 | Wire room (scheduler, playback, minimize/spot-check, log, voice ID, pages, fast-forward, legal); van stakeout with van heat; dilemma; ops sweep; wall-off; code flip; Easy's scene (I3) | Wire session tests (legal increments, logging windows, ID); Ep3 playable on all branches |\n1128\t| **M7** Episode 4 | Tail (routes, acts, distance band, hand-off), trash stealth, kitchen talk, burners, session 3, I4 | Tail bot completes `teeDry`; Ep4 playable |\n1129\t| **M8** Episode 5 + endings | Raid, rescue, press conference, money tail with moving cone, long lens, the morning after, I5, montage rules, credits, Shut Down, episode select presets | The branch-matrix test (§16) produces a valid montage for every combination; story mode is complete |\n1130\t| **M9** Versus | VersusSim rules, roles, actions, scoring, bots, local split screen, results; then `HubTransport`, host loop, snapshots, interpolation, leave/time-up/end/server | A local bot match ends with a valid outcome; **hub harness passes** all four runs (§16) |\n1131\t| **M10** Attract and title | Attract reel (9 vignettes), idle detection, touch-only attract; title diorama; episode select; versus setup; full settings | Idle 10 s → attract; any input → title; all vignettes run 3 loops without errors |\n1132\t| **M11** Polish and ship | Balance pass (difficulty table), juice (particles, shake, stings), audio mix, writing pass against App. G, viewport/WebKit checks, final About content, bundle, exit interview | §17 checklist all ticked |\n1133\t\n1134\t**Content budgets** (to keep scope honest): at most ~90 dialogue lines per episode excluding wire calls; wire calls as in App. D; montage cards as in App. G. Write tight. The show's people say less than they mean.\n1135\t\n1136\t---\n1137\t\n1138\t## 15. Risks and how to de-risk them\n1139\t| # | Risk | Why it's risky | De-risk |\n1140\t|---|---|---|---|\n1141\t| 1 | **Scope** | Many systems and five episodes | Shared systems (one map, one CornerSim, one perception, one photo system everywhere); data-driven content; Ep1 slice by M4 proves the pipeline; content budgets; milestone gates |\n1142\t| 2 | **AI Hub shared-world passing the harness** (latency 150 / jitter 50 / loss 5, host leave, server) | Netcode bugs show up late | `LocalTransport` and a `LoopbackTransport` that simulates latency/loss in-process for headless tests; client-authoritative own movement (the arena example's pattern); message size asserts; run the real harness at the *start* of M9 with a minimal round (two dots moving, finish at 30 s), then grow |\n1143\t| 3 | **Wire room fun and readability** | Lots of text plus a clock | Few calls per session, short lines, 8 s rule shown as a visible ring, Rookie hints; deep link `#ep3.wire1` for fast iteration; thumbnail test |\n1144\t| 4 | **Voice synth** (quality, sync, CPU) | Custom Web Audio | Prototype in M1; fixed lookahead scheduling (`ctx.currentTime + 0.05`); fallback: the engine's `text` blip with per-profile pitch if formants misbehave in a browser |\n1145\t| 5 | **NPC simulation stability** | Stuck agents, flow-field cost, sorting | FlowField cache by POI; stuck rule; draw background civilians `every: 2`; invariant tests |\n1146\t| 6 | **Perception tuning** | Made too easily, or never | The target table in §5.2; the `?dev=1` overlay shows every suspicion value; careless/careful bot tests |\n1147\t| 7 | **10-foot UI and glyph switching** | Dense screens creep in | §4.5 rules; thumbnail test; fake-gamepad/mouse device-switch tests |\n1148\t| 8 | **Branch combinatorics** | Flags interacting | Few flags; endings by a rule table; episode presets; a branch-matrix headless test that runs every choice combination with action parts auto-resolved (`debug.autoResolve`) |"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01XnCMPJrdKsvgzZ1BF12Jst","agent_id":"af67e84b720105c7c","session_id":"e2aa65a8-ee1a-45c4-b8e6-f96cf188e23d","uuid":"9cab9b1a-d3c6-4798-b8d9-559b8517664f","timestamp":"2026-11-03T18:54:53.527Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01784nxXZ5rgbUDisfCWqVJf","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review game plan for gaps"}
