{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011aiPzw99eUJUbZzBvYa8gZ","type":"tool_result","content":"1149\t| 9 | **Engine pitfalls** (heights, `cut`, sorting big shapes, iso facades, lighting cost) | New engine for most builders | Follow API.md's rules; `footprint` sorting for canopies and roofs; act on every `check.mjs` look note; keep the engine unmodified |\n1150\t| 10 | **Single-file bundling** | `</script>` in strings, the order of the hub client | The build checks; tests run against the bundle, not only the dev page |\n1151\t| 11 | **Gamepad wrapper side effects** | It overrides a browser API | `try/catch`, pass-through when both toggles are off, Playwright fake-pad test |\n1152\t| 12 | **Tone and sensitivity** | Gritty material about real communities | App. G writing guide: no slurs, everyone human, violence mostly offscreen with consequences, no glamor; a final writing pass |\n1153\t\n1154\t---\n1155\t\n1156\t## 16. Testing plan (lightweight and token-efficient)\n1157\t**Principles:**\n1158\t- Test rules headless (fast, exact, no screenshots).\n1159\t- Look at a *few* screenshots per milestone.\n1160\t- Run the hub harness only for versus.\n1161\t- Never paste big logs into context: print one PASS/FAIL line per test plus the first error.\n1162\t\n1163\t**Tools** (on this machine):\n1164\t- Node, Playwright 1.63 with Chromium/WebKit/Firefox.\n1165\t- `node engine/tools/check.mjs <page>#<deeplink>`: errors, a screenshot, look notes, `game.debug.snapshot()`.\n1166\t- `viewport-matrix <url>` (keep runs small: `--only` / `--devices`; don't run several at once). Real iOS Safari isn't available; WebKit with iPhone profiles is the closest check.\n1167\t- `python3 -m http.server` to serve the bundle and the harness side by side.\n1168\t\n1169\t**Hooks** (60-debug.js):\n1170\t- `game.debug.snapshot()` → `{ scene, ep, beat, meters, flags, dana:[x,y], objective, versus:{ev, cn, tl, sides} }`.\n1171\t- `game.debug.jump(beatId)`, `game.debug.autoResolve(on)` (missions and screens complete themselves with default good choices), `game.debug.bot(name)`.\n1172\t- Deep links: `#title`, `#attract`, `#about`, `#ep<N>.<beat>` (e.g. `#ep3.wire1`), `#versus.bots`, `#versus.local`.\n1173\t- `?dev=1` overlay: cells under the mouse, POIs, routes, suspicion numbers, agent states, F9 toggles it.\n1174\t\n1175\t**`tests/headless.mjs`** loads `engine/my-3d2dge.js` and the bundled game script into a Node `vm` context with the stand-ins from `engine/kits/test.mjs` (`window`, `addEventListener`, `location`), then runs:\n1176\t\n1177\t| Test | Asserts |\n1178\t|---|---|\n1179\t| boot | Boot steps finish; `validateData()` reports 0 problems; `game.errors.length === 0` |\n1180\t| cipher | CW/CCW are permutations and inverses; App. C's 5 pages decode to App. C's numbers; the flip page decodes with the other turn |\n1181\t| photo scoring | Fixture cases: back turned = no ★Face; 230 units = blurry; act window = ★Act; burned = 0 |\n1182\t| perception | Careless bot (stare at a lookout from 60) made in ≤ 6 s; careful bot (walk past) never noticed; blending at 100 for 30 s never made |\n1183\t| corner ledger | 10 min of sim: vial and cash conservation hold; shutdown freezes sales; re-up triggers below 30 |\n1184\t| chase | Bot pursuer with good routing catches the runner within 60 s; the ditch happens; the kid takes it after 45 s if it's not searched |\n1185\t| tail | A careful bot completes `teeDry`; a bot that stops on every `lookBack` gets made |\n1186\t| box | Thresholds unlock B1-B3; Fear ≥ 80 → lawyer; the Lean → Offer combo; flip only at B3 with Fear ≤ 60 |\n1187\t| paper | PC sums per line; a false necessity tick is always asked and denies |\n1188\t| wire | Non-pertinent past the window adds Legal 4/s; a minimized pertinent line is lost; spot-check timing; LOG windows; voice ID links the number |\n1189\t| meters | Brass 0 → shutdown scene; Heat thresholds flip the code and add lookouts |\n1190\t| branch matrix | With `autoResolve`, every combination of dilemma × sweep × wallOff × lossOn × canary × path × I5 reaches the montage with 11-13 valid cards |\n1191\t| save/load | Save at `ep3.van`, new game instance on the same storage, CONTINUE → same beat and STATE |\n1192\t| versus | A bots-only local match ends with a valid outcome; host rules (burn, tap, jump-out) apply; snapshot JSON < 1,100 bytes at the 45-entity worst case; `LoopbackTransport` at 150 ms ±50 and 5% loss still converges |\n1193\t| attract | 10.1 s idle on the title → `attract`; one `input.press` → `title`; 3 loops of the reel with no errors |\n1194\t\n1195\t**`tests/browser.mjs`** (Playwright, one browser at a time):\n1196\t1. **Gamepad:** an init script defines a fake standard gamepad (`navigator.getGamepads` returns a DualSense-like id with buttons and axes). Assert the HUD prompt reads ✕; switch Settings → Xbox → it reads A; enable `stickInvX`, push axis0 = +1 → Dana moves left (−x).\n1197\t2. **Mouse:** hover a main-menu item → it gets focus; click → it activates; the legend shows mouse/key glyphs.\n1198\t3. **Touch-only:** an iPhone profile (WebKit) shows the notice and a Settings button; after 10 s attract runs; a tap returns.\n1199\t4. **Screens:** 8 screenshots via deep links at 1920×1080 (title, `ep1.photos`, `ep3.wire1`, Board, box, versus local split, about, montage). Look at each once; apply the thumbnail test (downscale to 480×270).\n1200\t\n1201\t**Viewport sweep** (once, at M11): `viewport-matrix http://localhost:8000/<bundle> --only phone,tablet,desktop --engines chromium,webkit -o /tmp/viewport-matrix/wiretap`. Expect: phones show the touch-only notice; desktop sizes (16:9, 21:9, 4:3) fill edge to edge with the HUD inside the safe areas; no horizontal overflow; no console errors.\n1202\t\n1203\t**AI Hub harness** (`tests/hub/hub-check.mjs`): serve `tests/hub/` with the bundle copied in. Open in Playwright and wait for `document.body.dataset.complete === 'true'`, then assert `window.__hubCheck.pass === true` for:\n1204\t1. `harness.html?game=<bundle>&players=2&auto=1`\n1205\t2. `…&players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1`\n1206\t3. `…&players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1&scenario=host-leave`\n1207\t4. `…&players=2&scenario=server&auto=1`\n1208\t\n1209\tAlso open the bundle outside a session: it must still reach the title.\n1210\t\n1211\t**When to run:** headless after every change to a system; browser screens at the end of each milestone; viewport sweep and hub harness at M9 and M11.\n1212\t\n1213\t---\n1214\t\n1215\t## 17. Definition of done (tick every line before shipping)\n1216\t- [ ] Title is **WIRETAP** (RNG-picked, §0); the bundle is `Wiretap-TheWire-claude-opus-5-5-max-20261103-105319.html` in `work/`; the dev folder holds sources, tools and tests; `exit-interview.json` sits next to the html and parses.\n1217\t- [ ] One html file runs offline: the engine and hub client inlined, no runtime network, no external fonts.\n1218\t- [ ] Genre/perspective as §2; engine-native art and animation, extended (§12); all music, effects and gibberish voices written in code (§11).\n1219\t- [ ] **Story mode:** 5 episodes, 4 interludes + finale interlude, both finale paths, Shut Down, montage with computed cards, credits, episode select, continue/autosave.\n1220\t- [ ] **Every system in §5-§7 is reachable in normal play**, with no TODOs, placeholders or stubs. Each one appears in the feature matrix (App. J.6) at least once.\n1221\t- [ ] **Versus:** local (1 human vs bots; 2 humans split screen) and AI Hub shared-world (1-4). All four harness runs pass, and the game runs outside a session.\n1222\t- [ ] **Attract:** 10 s idle on title/menus → bot-played reel; any input exits; it runs on touch-only devices.\n1223\t- [ ] **10-foot UX:** controller-first; keyboard+mouse native (hover focuses, click selects, mouse aims and clicks world objects); prompts follow the last device; PlayStation glyphs by default with an Xbox option; **stick inversion toggles** for both axes; no dense data screens; thumbnail test passes.\n1224\t- [ ] **Touch-only:** no touch controls; \"Controller or keyboard required\" with a Settings button; attract allowed.\n1225\t- [ ] Standard engine features only (no custom pause/settings/rebinding/full screen); E.Shell HUD; standard settings plus the §4.7 game settings.\n1226\t- [ ] **About/Credits** screen with Credits, Source Information, Testing, Engine and Prompt Feedback, matching `exit-interview.json`; \"unknown\" where unconfirmed.\n1227\t- [ ] Headless suite green; browser checks looked at; hub harness passes; WebKit check done.\n1228\t- [ ] Writing pass done against App. G (tone, no slurs, no quotes from the show).\n1229\t\n1230\t---\n1231\t\n1232\t# Appendices\n1233\t\n1234\t## Appendix A: Penn Row neighborhood map (72 × 56 cells; 1 cell = 16 units; x east, y south)\n1235\tGenerated and checked by script: 56 rows of 72 characters, every listed POI on a walkable cell. Paste `ROWS` into `30-data-world.js` as-is. Wall heights and looks: §12.2. Floors: §12.3.\n1236\t\n1237\t```js\n1238\tconst ROWS = [   // x: 000000000011111111112222222222333333333344444444445555555555666666666677"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01XnCMPJrdKsvgzZ1BF12Jst","agent_id":"af67e84b720105c7c","session_id":"e2aa65a8-ee1a-45c4-b8e6-f96cf188e23d","uuid":"b5fa6f8c-7047-4c90-a1ec-9898c0a75cc2","timestamp":"2026-11-03T18:55:08.371Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_011aiPzw99eUJUbZzBvYa8gZ","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review game plan for gaps"}
