{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016BsDzBDcVuTbVCcr72h7tJ","type":"tool_result","content":"1426\t**Burners (Ep4 subpoena):**\n1427\t| Phone | Number | User |\n1428\t|---|---|---|\n1429\t| B1 | 555-0102 | Tee |\n1430\t| B2 | 555-0115 | Lonnie |\n1431\t| B3 | 555-0136 | Rook, or Tavon if Rook is locked up |\n1432\t| B4 | 555-0158 | Dale |\n1433\t| B5 | 555-0190 | Pigeon |\n1434\t\n1435\t## Appendix D: Wire calls\n1436\t- **Type:** **N** = non-pertinent (minimize within the window). **P** = pertinent. **T@k** = turns pertinent at line k (a spot-check catches it). **★** = key line (log it).\n1437\t- **Speakers** show as `UNKNOWN MALE n` until voice-ID'd.\n1438\t- **Lines:** if a call's line is down (swept or untapped), the scheduler moves it to the nearest live line, or drops it if none.\n1439\t- **Length:** each call is its lines plus 1.5-3 s of dial and hang-up sounds. Write any extra filler in the same voice.\n1440\t\n1441\t**Session 1 (Ep3, 16:00-23:00):**\n1442\t| id | Time | Line | Speakers | Type | Lines (★ key) | Unlocks |\n1443\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n1444\t| S1-1 | 16:05 | P2 | Pigeon → Odessa | N | PIGEON: Hey Grandma. I'm at the library. / ODESSA: Library closes at five on Tuesdays, Junior. / PIGEON: It's the study room. They got a study room now. / ODESSA: Mm-hm. You eat? / PIGEON: I ate. I'll be home by the streetlights. / ODESSA: You be home *before* them. | Teaches minimizing. Over the window: Hal: \"That's a boy and his grandmother, Detective.\" |\n1445\t| S1-2 | 16:40 | P1 | Tee → Tavon | T@4 | TEE: You see the game? / TAVON: They ain't got no bullpen. None. / TEE: They got a bullpen. Bullpen just tired. / ★TEE: Tell your man the thing go down at the place where Dre messed up his ankle. Four o'clock. / TAVON: Where Dre… oh. Yeah. / TEE: Don't \"yeah\" me. Be there. | Re-up riddle (map pick), time 16:00; teaches spot-check |\n1446\t| S1-3 | 17:10 | pager | page `555-0743 11 00` | P | — | Decode → P3, \"package ready\" (page evidence) |\n1447\t| S1-4 | 17:25 | P3 (else P2) | Dale → Tee | P | DALE: Usual? / TEE: Usual. But your count been light, my man. / DALE: Count is the count. I don't open the boxes. / ★TEE: Somebody opening them. / ★DALE: Four o'clock. Don't make me wait, I got a route. | Courier voice (ID later), \"route\" → delivery truck |\n1448\t| S1-5 | 18:00 | P2 | Ms. Arnetta (citizen) → cab company | N | \"I need a cab at Ridley and Gaither, the laundromat… No, I am not waiting forty minutes…\" | — |\n1449\t| S1-6 | 18:30 | P1 | Rook → Keisha | N | ROOK: I said I'ma bring it. / KEISHA: You said that Friday. He need shoes, Ricky. His toes out the front. / ROOK: I got him. Tonight. | Rook is a father (used in his ending) |\n1450\t| S1-7 | 19:05 | P1 | Tee → Lil Moe | P | If Dana was made before: ★TEE: That lady on the bench Tuesday, leather coat? / MOE: She was reading the paper. / TEE: Nobody reads the paper on Ridley. Otherwise: ★TEE: Knockers came through twice. Nothing in the pockets, nothing on the corner. | Shows they know Dana's face (Heat note) or crew discipline (+4) |\n1451\t| S1-8 | 19:40 | P3/P2 | Rev. Mayfield → church office | N | \"Sister Pauline, about the folding chairs for Sunday…\" | — |\n1452\t| S1-9 | 20:30 | P2 | Tavon → Dink | P | TAVON: How we looking. / ★DINK: Light. Like nine hundred light. / TAVON: Nine hundred? / DINK: Testers was weak. Overtime ain't moving like last week. / TAVON: Don't tell Tee. I'll tell Tee. | Money flow evidence |\n1453\t| S1-10 | 21:15 | pager | page `555-0769 33 07` | P | — | Decode → P1, \"the count\" |\n1454\t\n1455\t**Session 2 (Ep3 night, 20:00-01:00, after the van and the ops choice):**\n1456\t| id | Time | Line | Speakers | Type | Lines (★ key) | Unlocks |\n1457\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n1458\t| S2-1 | 20:10 | P2 (P1 if not swept) | Tee → Rook | P | TEE: Man took it right off the boy. Walked up like he was asking directions. / ROOK: In a hearse? A *hearse*? / ★TEE: Hit me at the laundry later. Not this phone. / ROOK: It's Sunday. Gotta be. / ★TEE: Don't say names on the phone. | Sunday named (+4); sets up the flip page |\n1459\t| S2-2 | 20:45 | P3/P2 | Rook → \"Smokey\" | P | ★ROOK: I need a hammer. Tonight. / SMOKEY: What kind of hammer? / ★ROOK: The kind that finishes a job. / SMOKEY: Come by the shop at eleven. Cash. | **Threat to life → decision:** let it ride / wall-off stop |\n1460\t| S2-3 | 21:20 | P2 | Odessa → the laundromat payphone | N | ODESSA: Hello? Is this the laundromat phone? Is my grandson out there? Junior Hollis. Little red hoodie. / MAN: Ain't nobody here, ma'am. | — |\n1461\t| S2-4 | 21:50 | pager | **flip page** `555-0329 22 07` (CCW) | P | — | Known-plaintext puzzle (§6.3) |\n1462\t| S2-5 | 22:30 | P1/P2 | Lonnie → Tee | P | LONNIE: He wants to see you. / TEE: Tonight? / ★LONNIE: You know where. Mama B's. The back. / TEE: I'm coming. / LONNIE: And Terrence. Come by yourself. | THE MONEY tier: Boss ?, Mama B's |\n1463\t| S2-6 | 23:10 | P2 | two teenage girls (citizens) | N | Arguing about a boy named Marcus and a borrowed jacket | — |\n1464\t| S2-7 | 23:50 | P3/P2 | Tavon → unknown | P | TAVON: Tee say we gotta be easy for a minute. No more phones on Ridley after Friday. / UNKNOWN: Then what we using? / ★TAVON: He gonna get us something. Throwaways. | Foreshadows burners (+4) |\n1465\t| S2-8 | 00:30 | P1/P2 | drunk citizen → his ex | N | Sad, funny, about a dog he misses more than her | — |\n1466\t\n1467\t**Session 3 (Ep4, burners B1-B5, 22:00-01:00):**\n1468\t| id | Time | Line | Speakers | Type | Lines (★ key) | Unlocks |\n1469\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n1470\t| S3-1 | 22:05 | B1↔B2 | Lonnie → Tee | P | ★LONNIE: Thursday. After close. Same as always. / TEE: Same as always. / LONNIE: He says bring it counted this time. Counted twice. | The count: Thursdays at Mama B's |\n1471\t| S3-2 | 22:30 | B3 | Rook (or Tavon) → girlfriend | N | Small talk about a cousin's cookout | — |\n1472\t| S3-3 | 23:00 | B1↔B4 | Tee → Dale | P | DALE: Friday, the truck, nine o'clock. / ★TEE: Not the gas station. The new place. / DALE: Which new place? / ★TEE: The garage behind the Courts. Pull in off Harlow. | Raid target and time |\n1473\t| S3-4 | 23:25 | B5 | Pigeon → Odessa | N | PIGEON: Grandma? I'm okay. I'm at Tavon's… Past the window (the temptation): PIGEON: I don't wanna do this no more. / ODESSA: Then come home, baby. | Nothing. Listening past the window costs Legal, and if Dana mentions it in the kitchen, Trust −40 (\"You was listening to me?\") |\n1474\t| S3-5 | 23:50 | B1↔B2 | Tee → Lonnie | P | ★TEE: That detective. Whitlock. She grew up on Ridley. Her mother still stays over by the church. / LONNIE: He ain't gonna like you saying that on a phone. Or at all. | Dana's choice: call her mother (`momSafe`) |\n1475\t| S3-6 | 00:20 | B2↔B1 | Lonnie → Tee (only if Heat ≥ 70) | P | ★LONNIE: Count's moving to Saturday. He's feeling something. | Path B night shifts (dialogue only) |\n1476\t\n1477\t## Appendix E: Interrogation data\n1478\t**Corey \"Stash\" Lyle (Ep2 box).** Starts at Resolve 100, Fear 30, Trust 0, 12 exchanges.\n1479\t\n1480\t| Evidence (△) | Effect | Line |\n1481\t|---|---|---|\n1482\t| The package (if found) | Resolve −30 | DANA: Forty vials. Orange tops. Your prints on the bag. / COREY: That bag was on the ground. |\n1483\t| The pager | Resolve −15; **needed for B2** | LOU: Your pager's been busy, Corey. Real popular kid. |\n1484\t| A photo of Corey at the vacant (★Act `stash-access` or a `stash` read) | Resolve −25 | DANA: That's you going into fourteen-twelve. Again. And again. |\n1485\t| A photo of Tee | Resolve −10 | COREY: I don't know him. *(he does)* |\n1486\t| Anything irrelevant | Resolve +10, Fear +5 | COREY: That's a kid. Why you showing me a kid? |\n1487\t\n1488\t| Beat | Condition | Corey says | Board fact |\n1489\t|---|---|---|---|\n1490\t| B1 | Resolve ≤ 75 | \"Tee. Terrence. He run Gaither. I just… I just sit.\" | `stmt:corey:tee-lieutenant` |\n1491\t| B2 | Resolve ≤ 50 and pager shown | \"The numbers… it's the phone, man. You turn it. That's all I know.\" | `stmt:corey:code` |\n1492\t| B3 | Resolve ≤ 25 | \"Fourteen-twelve. Behind the radiator. There's a board loose.\" | `stmt:corey:stash` |\n1493\t| Flip | After B3 and Fear ≤ 60 → *Work for us* | \"If Tee finds out, I'm dead. You know that, right? …What I gotta do?\" | `coreyCI` |\n1494\t| Lawyer | Fear ≥ 80 | \"I-I want a lawyer. I know my rights. I want a lawyer.\" | session ends |\n1495\t\n1496\t**Approach lines** (2 variants each in the build; Corey's reply by Resolve band: high > 60, mid 30-60, low < 30):\n1497\t- **○ Lean.** LOU: \"You know what distribution in a school zone gets you? That court's a school zone, Corey. Look it up.\" COREY high: \"I ain't distributing nothing. I was sitting.\" · mid: \"Why y'all on me? I'm nobody.\" · low: \"Stop. Just… stop.\"\n1498\t- **✕ Offer.** DANA: \"You're nineteen. Tee's twenty-four. Who do you think takes the weight?\" COREY high: \"Tee look out for me.\" · mid: \"…Tee ain't gonna let me go down.\" · low: \"What happens to me? If I say something. What happens?\"\n1499\t- **Lean → Offer combo:** Lou slams the table and walks out. DANA: \"He's gone. It's just me. Talk to me, Corey.\"\n1500\t- **□ Bluff (fact known).** DANA: \"Pigeon told us you hold for them.\" COREY: \"Pigeon don't know nothing about— …man.\" **(Fact unknown):** DANA: \"Rook says you set up Felton.\" COREY: \"Rook don't talk to police. You making stuff up now.\"\n1501\t\n1502\t**Rook (Ep3, if the wall-off stop happened)**, a 3-exchange comic beat that can't be won:\n1503\t- DANA: \"Nice car.\" ROOK: \"Lawyer.\"\n1504\t- LOU: \"Taillight's out.\" ROOK: \"Lawyer.\"\n1505\t- DANA: \"Who's the hammer for, Ricky?\" ROOK: \"Law. Yer.\""}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01XnCMPJrdKsvgzZ1BF12Jst","agent_id":"af67e84b720105c7c","session_id":"e2aa65a8-ee1a-45c4-b8e6-f96cf188e23d","uuid":"70d9e445-deec-4a4c-848d-7f4c86aaad03","timestamp":"2026-11-03T18:57:20.123Z","tool_result_met