{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01V53W6Vacj5C7s2meR8ryCc","type":"tool_result","content":"1575\t- LOU: This ain't a whodunit, Dana. It's a who-cares.\n1576\t\n1577\t**The detail assembles (1.3):**\n1578\t- NAVARRE: The Sun put Mr. Felton on page one. So now the Deputy Commissioner cares. Six weeks. One corner. Arrests.\n1579\t- LOU: Arrests. Not a case.\n1580\t- NAVARRE: He said arrests. I heard case. We'll see who's right. Detective Szabo, Homicide.\n1581\t- LOU: Formerly. I said something true at a retirement party.\n1582\t- NAVARRE: Detective Pettiford, pawn unit.\n1583\t- HAL: Thirteen years. Nobody complained, because nobody knew I was there.\n1584\t- NAVARRE: Officer Ocasio, on loan from Southwest.\n1585\t- REN: I brought my own camera. The department's has a crack in the lens.\n1586\t- NAVARRE: Detective Whitlock, Western narcotics. She knows Ridley.\n1587\t- DANA: Ridley knows me. That might be the problem.\n1588\t- NAVARRE: The Major wants bodies by Friday. I want to know who pays for that corner. We'll try to give him both.\n1589\t\n1590\t**Pockets' shoes (1.4).** After each description, the player picks the matching photo. Photos show full bodies, shoes included (§5.3).\n1591\t- POCKETS: Pockets don't do faces, Detective. Faces get you a funeral. Shoes, though. Shoes don't talk back. Twenty for the shoes. Pockets don't do credit.\n1592\t- Wheat Timbs, laces tucked, not a scuff on 'em. That's a man who thinks he's a businessman. Terrence. Tee.\n1593\t- Black Air Force, red check, size thirteen. Ricky Batts. Rook. Don't let him see you looking.\n1594\t- Nikes with the duct tape on the left toe. Corey. He holds for 'em in the vacant. Nervous boy. Nervous boys live longer.\n1595\t- Little sneakers that light up when he runs. Junior. Miss Odessa's grandbaby. They call him Pigeon on account of the birds. He's fourteen. *(beat)* Fourteen.\n1596\t- And Dre ain't with 'em no more. Broke his ankle jumping the fence at the old Arundel station, running from y'all. They still meet out there. Ain't nobody fixed that fence.\n1597\t\n1598\t**Easy's back room (I3):**\n1599\t- EASY: Sit down, Terrence.\n1600\t- TEE: I'd rather stand.\n1601\t- EASY: I didn't ask what you'd rather. *(Tee sits.)* You lost my package to a man who drives a hearse.\n1602\t- TEE: Sunday hit the boy right after the drop. Nobody could've—\n1603\t- EASY: Somebody knew where the drop was. Somebody always knows. That's the cost of doing business outside.\n1604\t- EASY: You know why they call me Easy? Because I never make anything hard that doesn't have to be. Make it back, Terrence. By the count.\n1605\t- LONNIE: And the phones.\n1606\t- EASY: The phones. Lonnie says you like the payphones.\n1607\t- TEE: Payphones don't have names on 'em.\n1608\t- EASY: Everything has a name on it. Stop using them.\n1609\t- *(Tee leaves)* EASY *(to Lonnie)*: He's smart. Smart gets you so far.\n1610\t\n1611\t**The van dilemma (3.4):**\n1612\t- REN: He's got a gun on that kid. We have to do something.\n1613\t- LOU *(radio)*: We do something, the wire's dead by tonight, and that kid's still a corner kid tomorrow.\n1614\t- **Go in:**\n1615\t  - DANA: Police. Put it down.\n1616\t  - SUNDAY: Detective. Ain't Sunday, so it's business. But I don't do police. *(sets the bag on the hood)* Police do me. *(drives off in the hearse)*\n1617\t\n1618\t**The finale choice (5.2):**\n1619\t- PRUITT: Friday. A table. Dope, guns, cash. The Deputy's bringing Channel 11.\n1620\t- NAVARRE: Hit the re-up Friday, we get Mabry and a package. Wait for Thursday's count, we might get the man who owns the package.\n1621\t- PRUITT: \"Might\" doesn't fit on a stat sheet, Lieutenant.\n1622\t- LOU: Neither does a soul-food restaurant with a check-cashing license. But it should.\n1623\t\n1624\t**Montage cards** (11-13 shown; rules evaluated top to bottom, first match wins per person):\n1625\t| Who | Condition | Card |\n1626\t|---|---|---|\n1627\t| Corner (always first) | — | \"The corner at Gaither & Ridley: open for business by Monday.\" |\n1628\t| Tee | A + weight + Case high | \"Terrence Mabry: pleaded to twelve years. Never said Easy's name.\" |\n1629\t| | A + weight | \"Terrence Mabry: pleaded to six years. Out in four. Never said Easy's name.\" |\n1630\t| | A + talk | \"Terrence Mabry: agreed to testify. Moved to a prison in Pennsylvania under another name.\" |\n1631\t| | B + stay | \"Terrence Mabry: indicted with Darnell Booker eighteen months later.\" |\n1632\t| | B + run | \"Terrence Mabry: last seen boarding a Greyhound to Charlotte.\" |\n1633\t| | Shut Down | \"Terrence Mabry: runs three corners now.\" |\n1634\t| Easy | B + Case high | \"Darnell Booker: arrested at Mama B's on a Thursday. The count was light.\" |\n1635\t| | B | \"Darnell Booker: indicted. The case is still in discovery.\" |\n1636\t| | A | \"Darnell Booker: opened a second check-cashing store on Cathedral Row.\" |\n1637\t| | Shut Down | \"Darnell Booker: sponsored the church's back-to-school drive.\" |\n1638\t| Pigeon | `lossOn = pigeon` + `rookFree` + A | \"Nobody has seen Junior Hollis since October. His grandmother still feeds the birds.\" |\n1639\t| | `lossOn = pigeon` | \"Junior Hollis: back on the roof. The birds are gone.\" |\n1640\t| | `pigeonTrust ≥ 70` or (B and the runner wasn't Pigeon) | \"Junior Hollis: started ninth grade at a school in the county. Still keeps one bird.\" |\n1641\t| | otherwise | \"Junior Hollis: running for Tavon now. Fourteen.\" |\n1642\t| Corey | CI, not exposed | \"Corey Lyle: moved to an aunt's in Richmond. Calls Detective Whitlock on her birthday.\" |\n1643\t| | CI, exposed, rescued | \"Corey Lyle: relocated by the State's Attorney. Testified for two days.\" |\n1644\t| | CI, exposed, not rescued | \"Corey Lyle: found in a vacant on Harlow Street. No witnesses.\" |"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01XnCMPJrdKsvgzZ1BF12Jst","agent_id":"af67e84b720105c7c","session_id":"e2aa65a8-ee1a-45c4-b8e6-f96cf188e23d","uuid":"7a48194e-02f9-4eca-a54e-535e1445d38e","timestamp":"2026-11-03T18:58:16.750Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01V53W6Vacj5C7s2meR8ryCc","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review game plan for gaps"}
