{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0147MstY2FkBGPH18dPEb5FB","type":"tool_result","content":"149:3. viewport meta (`width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover`), hub tags (§9.6), `<meta name=\"hub:type\" content=\"Game\">`, `<meta name=\"hub:players\" content=\"1-4\">`, `<title>WIRETAP</title>`, `<style>` with `ui.css`\n200:- **In an AI Hub session** (`AIHub.active`), 99-start skips the title: `menu.quit = false`, `autoPause: false`, and goes straight into the versus round (§9.6).\n1324:| `court` | gate 17-18,46 · inside 11-24,47-52 · hoops 11,49.5 and 24,49.5 | Basketball court (burner handout in Ep4) |\n1720:| hal | 142 | .15 | 9.5 | sine | .95 | .12 | — |\n---\n---\n731:| 3.6 | **Session 2** | wire, 20:00-01:00 | Calls S2-1…S2-8. Rook asks for \"a hammer\" → **threat to life:** *Let it ride* vs *Wall-off stop* (a patrol car stops Rook's Monte Carlo for a broken taillight, finds the gun, arrests him: Brass +15, Heat +5; Rook in the box, 3 lines: \"Lawyer.\"). Lonnie: \"He wants to see you. Mama B's.\" → THE MONEY tier gets \"Boss ?\" and Mama B's. **Code flip** (known-plaintext page) | `wallOff`, `rookFree` |\n773:  - Pigeon (3 fates): by `lossOn`, `pigeonTrust`, Path B runner and `rookFree`\n1638:| Pigeon | `lossOn = pigeon` + `rookFree` + A | \"Nobody has seen Junior Hollis since October. His grandmother still feeds the birds.\" |\n1646:| Rook *(shown if `wallOff` or `rookFree`; otherwise the Sunday card)* | `wallOff` | \"Ricky Batts: eight years on a gun charge from a taillight stop.\" |\n1647:| | `rookFree` | \"Ricky Batts: shot in December over a parking space. His son got the shoes.\" |\n1749:           wallOff: false, rookFree: true, lossOn: null, pigeonTrust: 0, promise: false, canary: false, coreyExposed: false,\n---\n---\n568:| 1 | *Ask for the van*: the Ep3 stakeout uses Ren's van (normal van heat) · vs · *Ask for overtime*: the stakeout uses Dana's Chevy (heat ×1.5), but each Ep3 wire session gets one extra hour with one extra pertinent call (S1-OT: Tavon confirms the count spot, +4; S2-OT: Dink complains Tee is \"scared of phones now\", +4) |\n---\n638:| I1 | Ep1 | $2,400 | Tutorial; Dutch is $2 short (let it slide / turn him away / let Rook handle it); a patrol drive-by (call 5-0 in time); Pigeon asleep on the roof; page the re-up with the code card; Rook and Tee talk about Felton (\"who told you his name?\" → the 911 leak thread) | Dutch: `goodwill±`, `discipline±` |\n---\n633:- **Shortfall:** missing the target sets `teeShort`. Easy's scenes get colder and Tee's ending changes. There's no game over.\n1750:           coreyRescued: false, momSafe: false, path: null, i5: null, danaKnown: false, teeShort: false, rookDrew: false },","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01XnCMPJrdKsvgzZ1BF12Jst","agent_id":"af67e84b720105c7c","session_id":"e2aa65a8-ee1a-45c4-b8e6-f96cf188e23d","uuid":"ada1f4f4-4b17-480c-ab4c-aac992d86734","timestamp":"2026-11-03T19:01:44.868Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_0147MstY2FkBGPH18dPEb5FB","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review game plan for gaps"}
