{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CggXWwkraAGYcaPvnbKRg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":180777,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":180777,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01XnCMPJrdKsvgzZ1BF12Jst","agent_id":"af67e84b720105c7c","session_id":"e2aa65a8-ee1a-45c4-b8e6-f96cf188e23d","uuid":"69c7d6c3-6b0a-4806-ad76-a0b30920f85b","timestamp":"2026-11-03T19:15:39.264Z","request_id":"req_011CggXWwC8gEXyCz4MNsqJe","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review game plan for gaps"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CggXWwkraAGYcaPvnbKRg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I read all of PLAN.md (lines 1-1799), TASK.md, STAGE.md and the protocol README. Every finding below was checked against the text. Distances use the plan's own convention: 1 cell = 16 units, cells read from App. A.\n\n**High**\n\n1. **High, L801, L833 vs L603, L606, L798.** The Corner can never win versus. At 0.25 customers/s × about 2 vials × $10, a 5:00 round brings in about $1,500. Even with the night ×1.2 and fresh-package ×1.2 bonuses it's about $2,160, before shutdowns and seizures. So the $3,000 target is out of reach, and every online round ends in a Detail win or a draw. The bots-only test (L1192) still passes because it accepts a draw. **Fix:** work the target out from the rates (about $1,200 per 5 minutes, scaled by round length) and add a balance test where a competent Corner bot wins roughly half its rounds.\n\n2. **High, L430-436, L1344-1363, L1184.** The Ep2 chase, a required tutorial beat, is over in about 6 s.\n   - Corey's shortest escape (A→B→C→D→E→X1) is about 660 units, so at 118 u/s he is out in about 5.6 s. The longest path takes about 6.5 s.\n   - Dana sprints at 125, so she gains only 7 u/s. She has to start within about 60 units, and the plan never sets a starting gap.\n   - Lou's car block at 15 s, the 10-s ditch timer, the 45-s bike kid and the \"catch within 60 s\" test can never come into play.\n\n   **Fix:** set the starting gap and lower Corey's speeds (sprint about 100-105, jog about 80), or keep the exits closed until the car block. Then re-time the chase against the real path lengths.\n\n3. **High, L635-641, L606, L633, L1628-1633.** The interlude cash targets ($2,400-$3,600) can't be reached. Story rates give 0.12 × 1.2 × up to 1.2 × $20, about $3.50/s, which is roughly $830-$1,250 in a 4-6 minute shift. Every player ends up with `teeShort`. Also, no Tee montage card checks `teeShort`, so \"Tee's ending changes\" never happens. **Fix:** set the targets to about 75% of what the rates can produce, or define a time scale for the night shift, and add `teeShort` conditions to the endings.\n\n**Medium**\n\n4. **Medium, L151 vs L838-843.** The hub flow uses `await` directly inside the game's ordinary (non-async) IIFE. That is a SyntaxError, so the whole game script fails, inside a session and outside one. **Fix:** wrap the flow in `(async () => {…})()`.\n\n5. **Medium, L862, L867-871, L803.** `finish()` is underspecified against the protocol.\n   - The standings must exclude players who left (their characters became bots) and the server's own id.\n   - With one human player, which \"1-4\" allows, the standings `[[id]]` carry no outcome. Pass `won` in that case.\n   - The shape of `awards` (`[{id,title,detail}]`) isn't given.\n   - L803's \"1 player = Detail\" rule contradicts the alternating seat formula on the same line.\n\n   **Fix:** filter each side to `AIHub.players` minus the ids from `leave`, add `won` when only one side has humans, and spell out the stats and awards shapes.\n\n6. **Medium, L798, L846, L875.** Three protocol points are missing.\n   - The round length ignores `info.limitMs`, which the harness sets with `&limit=`.\n   - Nothing handles a hidden host tab. Its animation loop stops, the shared world freezes for everyone, and the hub voids the round after 20 s.\n   - The plan never says that hub names must be inserted as text, never as HTML.\n\n   **Fix:** make the round `min(5:00, limitMs − 5 s)`, keep the host simulation stepping on a timer while `document.hidden`, and render names only with `textContent` or canvas text.\n\n7. **Medium, L505, L512, L237 vs L210-216.** The box's input collides with the global key bindings.\n   - ○ (Pad1) is also `cancel`, and Esc is both `cancel` and `pause`, so pausing in the box would also \"Lean on him\".\n   - The box's number keys 1-4 collide with Digit2 and Digit3, which are bound to the □ and △ UI actions. Pressing 3 would trigger △ Show evidence while the screen says 3 is ○ Lean.\n   - \"A fourth approach appears\" (Work for us) would actually be a fifth, and it has no button.\n\n   **Fix:** give the box its own actions (Pad3/2/1/0 plus Digit1-4, with Esc kept for pause), and have \"Work for us\" replace ✕ Offer once it unlocks.\n\n8. **Medium, L743-745 vs L1473, L1512.** The kitchen scene is beat 4.5, but burner B5 is only subpoenaed at 4.6 and Session 3 is 4.7. So call S3-4's consequence and the kitchen's \"I heard your call\" option can never happen. **Fix:** move the kitchen after Session 3, or cut that option.\n\n9. **Medium, L797, L1336 vs L1329, L590, L1365, L809, L1332.** The versus zone (x 18-50, y 16-44) contradicts its own content.\n   - It is described as \"Ridley between Abbott and Harlow\", which would be x 10-55.\n   - The `trashGate` stash at (19,45) is outside it.\n   - The \"Dunmore corner\" vantage at (30,15) is outside it, despite \"all inside the zone\".\n   - The patrol loop that jump-outs need runs outside the zone's blocked edges.\n\n   **Fix:** change the zone to x 10-55, y 15-45 (or move those points), and say how police cars get into the zone.\n\n10. **Medium, L729, L1322, L1327 vs L374, L378.** In Ep3 the van has to photograph the re-up at the gas station pumps (62,47 and 62,50). Spot V2 (62.5,29) is about 288 units away and V3 (63,33) is about 225-272. Both are beyond the 220-unit face-photo range, and Watch mode only pans 7 tiles. Only V1 can identify Dale, so choosing a \"far/safe\" spot is a trap. **Fix:** give the van's long lens its own range (about 360 units, 14-tile pan), or move V2 and V3 within about 180 units of the pumps.\n\n11. **Medium, L1089 vs TASK L66.** The `testing` field in the exit interview and About screen is a placeholder that asks \"what you actually ran\". TASK.md defines the field as \"testing parameters allowed\". **Fix:** state the allowed parameters (lightweight, token-efficient testing; FPS and optimization out of scope), then what was actually run.\n\n**Low**\n\n12. **Low-medium, L1646-1650, L1749, L773-778.** `rookFree` starts true and only the wall-off stop clears it. So \"show Rook's card if wallOff or rookFree\" is always true, and the Sunday card (with the `dilemma` flag's effect on the ending) can never appear. Ren is listed as having an ending card but has none. \"Pigeon (3 fates)\" actually has 4 cards. **Fix:** show Sunday's card based on `dilemma`, and add a Ren card.\n\n13. **Low-medium, L521-532, L717, L1528.** The affidavit's pager-clone line has no way to score. The probable-cause points are for evidence \"tied to that number\", but pages are sent to the pager and never show its number. **Fix:** list what counts for that line (for example: the seized pager, decoded pages as direct items, Corey's statement about the code).\n\n14. **Low-medium, L900, L172.** The `attract` scene \"owns the clock\" but calls `game.go` into real scenes, which unloads it. **Fix:** run the demo reel from a global director with one global any-input exit hook.\n\n15. **Low, L618 vs L1332.** The two patrol loops disagree (one goes through Gaither, the other through Harlow). **Fix:** keep App. A's loop and correct §7.2.\n\n16. **Low, L149, L200.** Both lines refer to \"§9.6\", which doesn't exist. **Fix:** point them to §9.3.\n\n17. **Low, L568 vs L1462, L1470.** The overtime calls S1-OT and S2-OT have no lines in App. D. S1-OT (\"Tavon confirms the count spot\") also gives away the count before Mama B's is named (call S2-5) or the count is learned (call S3-1). **Fix:** write both calls and change what S1-OT reveals.\n\n18. **Low, L444 vs L1290-1291.** The garage door cells are already walkable in the map, yet the raid's breach \"opens the door cell\". **Fix:** draw them closed (`G`) and open them at the breach.\n\n19. **Low, L533 vs L1519-1529.** The judge has no question for a falsely ticked \"Grand jury subpoena\", even though false ticks are \"always asked\". **Fix:** add that question.\n\n20. **Low, L939 vs L729, L1614-1616, L640.** The gunshot sound is \"used exactly twice\", but neither the \"Go in\" warning shot nor Rook going after Sunday in interlude I3 exists in the scenes. **Fix:** write those moments or correct the sound note.\n\n21. **Low, L1189 vs L500, L560; L1181 vs L377-381.** Two tests contradict the spec. \"Heat thresholds flip the code\" is wrong, because the code flip is unconditional. \"230 units = blurry\" is wrong, because the focus and act stars have no range limit. **Fix:** align both tests with the spec.\n\n22. **Low, L504, L507, L509, L1478.** Interrogations have a Trust stat that is never displayed and has no effect. **Fix:** drop it or define what it does.\n\n23. **Low, L416-417; L1339.** The tail's distance band leaves 48-64 units undefined. Tee's route has a \"window: carryout\" stop at (30,44), but the carryout is at (34-37, 31-34). **Fix:** treat under 64 as too close, and move the stop to (33,31).\n\n24. **Low, L1326-1327 vs L1332-1333.** Dana's parked Chevy and van spot V2 sit in the same lane the bus and patrol drive. **Fix:** park them at the north curb (row 27).\n\n**Checked and correct:** the cipher tables and all 8 example pages (Corey's 5, the 2 live pages and the flip page), every POI I checked sits on the right kind of cell, the exit-interview shape matches TASK.md key for key, and the hub tags, client placement and the four harness URLs match the README.\n\n**Not verified:** engine API usage (E.Shell, `game.settings`, `drawPortrait`, `splitScreen`), because I was limited to the three files and the README. I also didn't machine-check the music bar lengths in App. H or the map row lengths.\n\n**Verdict:** a thorough, buildable plan, but the versus, interlude and chase numbers, the hub flow fixes (#4-6) and the Ep4 sequencing should be corrected before handoff."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":180777,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":180777,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01XnCMPJrdKsvgzZ1BF12Jst","agent_id":"af67e84b720105c7c","session_id":"e2aa65a8-ee1a-45c4-b8e6-f96cf188e23d","uuid":"ab7130a5-9685-4541-8c51-0ee7c360b397","timestamp":"2026-11-03T19:16:02.921Z","request_id":"req_011CggXWwC8gEXyCz4MNsqJe","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review game plan for gaps"}
