{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011jjXFMK4s53kpf7W861MiE","type":"tool_result","content":"  - `cutThrough`: through the 1412 vacant or the Courts breezeway at a jog (70).\n  - `phoneStop` (4 s): at a payphone.\n  - `wait` (n s): leans on a wall.\n- **Distance band** (HUD bar with zones):\n  - under 48: too close; suspicion ×1.8 whenever you're in his view\n  - 64-160: good\n  - 160-220: amber\n- **Code flip (Ep3):** after the robbery Tee **always** switches to counter-clockwise (the inverse), so every playthrough meets the puzzle. Old decodes stop matching (\"NO MATCH ×3\"). It's a **known-plaintext** puzzle: a page arrives right after Tee is overheard saying \"call me at the laundry\". The player turns the pad the other \n\n### 6.4 The box: interrogation (17-box.js; App. E)\n- **Scene:** `brawler` view of a small room: table, two chairs, one-way glass, a buzzing fluorescent light (flicker light plus a 120 Hz hum). The suspect sits (sit pose). Dana and Lou stand or sit.\n- **DOM side panel:** the suspect's **Resolve** (100 → 0), **Fear** (0 → 100) and a clock (\"Booking wants him at Central in 20 min\" = 12 exchanges). Each is a bar with a word, with no color-only meaning.\n- **Each exchange,** choose an approach. The four sit on a face-button diamond drawn in the dialog area (glyph + verb; keys 1-4; hover/click):\n  - **△ Show evidence:** opens a 6-card evidence picker. Relevant evidence = a big Resolve drop. Irrelevant = Resolve +10 (\"That's a picture of a corner, Detective.\").\n  - **□ Bluff:** \"Your boy already told us…\". Succeeds only if the bluffed fact is known on the Board (Resolve −25). Otherwise Resolve +20 and Trust −1.\n  - **○ Lean on him:** Resolve −12, Fear +15.\n  - **✕ Offer a way out:** Fear −15, Resolve −8. Right after a Lean (Lou plays bad cop, you play good cop) it combos: an extra Resolve −20 and Trust +1.\n- **Beats:** 3 info beats per suspect, unlocked at Resolve thresholds and/or specific evidence. Each adds facts to the Board.\n- **Lawyer:** Fear ≥ 80 → \"I want a lawyer.\" The session ends and you keep what you have.\n- **Flip:** when beat 3 is reached and Fear ≤ 60, a fourth approach appears: **\"Work for us\"**. Accept → CI flag (with consequences later).\n\n### 7.2 Police pressure (for crew-side play, versus and attract)\n- **Patrol car:** a sedan shape drives a lane loop (Ridley → Gaither → Dunmore → Abbott) at 70 u/s every 60-90 s, with a light bar off. It triggers shutdowns when seen.\n- **Knockers:** an unmarked car stops; 2 officers jump out and frisk the nearest crew member carrying product or cash. Seized if not stashed in time.\n- **Detectives** (AI plainclothes in interludes/attract, players in versus) behave like civilians but linger and raise cameras (a visible tell: the camera-raise pose for 0.6 s before a shot).\n| 4.3 | **The tail** | field, 20:00, rain | Tee's dry-cleaning route (App. J `teeDry`) with Lou hand-offs (§5.5). Ends at the basketball court: Tee hands phones to the crew (read = observation `burners`) | checkpoint |\n| 4.4 | **Trash** | field, 21:30, rain | The alley behind Ridley Wireless (§5.7): find the bag with 12 phone boxes | `serials` |\n| 4.5 | **Kitchen** | Odessa's kitchen (box scene variant, warm light) | Pigeon at the table, Odessa at the stove (§6.4 kitchen) | `pigeonTrust` |\n| 4.6 | Numbers | Annex | The subpoena returns B1-B5. Halloway amends by phone (\"Same rules, Detective.\"). Pin burners to people | |\n| 4.7 | **Session 3** | wire, 6 calls (App. D) | The count is Thursdays at Mama B's after close; Friday's truck goes to \"the garage behind the Courts\". Tee mentions Dana's mother → choice: *call your mother* (`momSafe`: she goes to her sister's in the county) / *stay on the wire* | |\n| 4.8 | **Interlude I4** | Tee | The canary trap | `canary` |\n\n| 4 | 9 | **THE CHASE**: Corey bolts | Sprint, vault the court fence, tackle, cuff |\n| 5 | 10 | **THE WIRE**: wire room | Grandma call → MINIMIZE; pertinent call → LOG; a page decodes with a keypad turn |\n| 6 | 7 | **THE BOARD**: corkboard | Cards fly onto slots; red string ties Tee to P1 |\n| 7 | 8 | **THE BOX**: Corey | Lean → Offer a way out → beat unlocked |\n| 8 | 10 | **THE GAME**: versus, split screen, bots | A call-out burns a detective; a stash photo |\n| 9 | 8 | **THE COUNT**: Tee's tally | Bills flick, the total ticks up, then the title card |\n\n- **Implementation:** each entry is `{ id, seconds, setup(), tick(dt), caption }`. `setup()` loads a mission/scene with `attract: true`: no saves, no tutorials, no autosave, quieter music, no HUD prompts. The attract scene owns the clock and calls `game.go` for the next entry with a short dissolve.\n======\n507:  - **□ Bluff:** \"Your boy already told us…\". Succeeds only if the bluffed fact is known on the Board (Resolve −25). Otherwise Resolve +20 and Trust −1.\n509:  - **✕ Offer a way out:** Fear −15, Resolve −8. Right after a Lean (Lou plays bad cop, you play good cop) it combos: an extra Resolve −20 and Trust +1.\n533:- **Necessity section:** checkboxes for techniques tried: *Physical surveillance*, *Confidential informant*, *Undercover purchase*, *Search warrant*, *Grand jury subpoena*. Only what STATE says you did is true. Ticking a technique you didn't use is **perjury**: hidden until the judge asks. It's \n568:| 1 | *Ask for the van*: the Ep3 stakeout uses Ren's van (normal van heat) · vs · *Ask for overtime*: the stakeout uses Dana's Chevy (heat ×1.5), but each Ep3 wire session gets one extra hour with one extra pertinent call (S1-OT: Tavon confirms the count spot, +4; S2-OT: Dink complains Tee is \"s\n773:  - Pigeon (3 fates): by `lossOn`, `pigeonTrust`, Path B runner and `rookFree`\n774:  - Corey (3 fates): `coreyCI`, `canary`, rescue\n939:| `gunshot` | noise 0.18 s vol .45 + `boom` tail + an echo at −10 dB after 130 ms. Used exactly twice in the game (Ep3 robbery warning shot if *Go in*, and offscreen in I3 if Rook goes after Sunday) |\n1023:  - `sedan`, `chevy` (Dana's beige Lumina)\n1089:    \"testing\": \"<fill in: what you actually ran>\",\n1181:| photo scoring | Fixture cases: back turned = no ★Face; 230 units = blurry; act window = ★Act; burned = 0 |\n1189:| meters | Brass 0 → shutdown scene; Heat thresholds flip the code and add lookouts |\n1326:| `chevy` | 22.5,29 facing east | Dana's car (Ep1 cover) |\n1327:| `vanV1` / `vanV2` / `vanV3` | 58,45 facing north · 62.5,29 facing west · 63,33 facing south | Ep3 van spots (close/risky · far/safe · inside the lot, middle) |\n1332:- **Patrol loop:** a closed `E.Path` through lane centers. Abbott x 7.5 → Ridley y 28.5 → Harlow x 57.5 → Dunmore y 13.5 → back to Abbott.\n1333:- **Bus:** Ridley eastbound (y 28.8), stopping 4 s at 42,29.\n1339:`30,32` → `30,26` → `28,26 [window 3]` → `20,26 [lookBack]` → `9,26` → `9,21` → `15,20 [doubleBack 48]` → `29,20` → `30,15 [wait 4]` → `44,15 [lookBack]` → `56,15` → `56,30` → `56,47` → `49,47 [cutThrough]` → `46.5,41` → `46.5,36 [lookBack]` → `55,36` → `56,36` → `56,30` → `42,30 [phoneStop 4]`\n1508:- **△ Be honest:** cite a Board fact (\"I know you watch from the roof. I know Tee pays you forty a day.\"). Trust +15 if it's known, −5 if not.\n1510:- **○ Push:** \"You want to end up like Corey?\" Fear +20, Trust −10. A second Push → ODESSA: \"That's enough. You can go now, Dana Lynn.\" (ends it)\n1646:| Rook *(shown if `wallOff` or `rookFree`; otherwise the Sunday card)* | `wallOff` | \"Ricky Batts: eight years on a gun charge from a taillight stop.\" |\n1648:| Sunday *(shown when Rook's card isn't)* | stay | \"Royal Odom: still drives the hearse. Still doesn't work Sundays.\" |","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e2aa65a8-ee1a-45c4-b8e6-f96cf188e23d","uuid":"4d076880-d186-4841-9824-fc0512654ab8","timestamp":"2026-11-03T19:18:41.110Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"  - `cutThrough`: through the 1412 vacant or the Courts breezeway at a jog (70).\n  - `phoneStop` (4 s): at a payphone.\n  - `wait` (n s): leans on 