{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CggY4iaFZhyYN82n2XLsZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013S3T55VQqY5fWeC4F5ramC","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cp PLAN.md /tmp/wireplan-scripts/PLAN.before-review.md && cat > /tmp/wireplan-scripts/patch_review.py <<'PYEOF'\nimport re\np = 'PLAN.md'; s = open(p).read()\ndef rep(old, new, count=1):\n    global s\n    n = s.count(old)\n    assert n == count, f'expected {count} match(es), found {n}: {old[:90]!r}'\n    s = s.replace(old, new)\n\n# ---------- #16 broken section refs\nrep(\"hub tags (§9.6)\", \"hub tags (§9.3)\")\nrep(\"\"\"- **In an AI Hub session** (`AIHub.active`), 99-start skips the title: `menu.quit = false`, `autoPause: false`, and goes straight into the versus round (§9.6).\"\"\",\n    \"\"\"- **In an AI Hub session** (`AIHub.active`), 99-start skips the title: `menu.quit = false`, `autoPause: false`, and §9.3's async flow calls `game.start` itself and goes straight into the versus round. The `game.start` call above is the non-session path.\"\"\")\n\n# ---------- #14 global per-step systems (architecture rule 8)\nrep(\"\"\"7. **One save state.** `STATE` (App. J) is the only thing `game.saves` writes. Systems rebuild themselves from it.\"\"\",\n    \"\"\"7. **One save state.** `STATE` (App. J) is the only thing `game.saves` writes. Systems rebuild themselves from it.\n8. **Global per-step systems run from a scene wrapper.** Engine timers and tweens end with each scene, so every scene is registered through `withGlobals(scene)`, whose `update` first runs `Globals.tick(dt)`: the idle timer, the attract director, the device/glyph watcher and the hub hooks.\"\"\")\n\n# ---------- #7 box actions in the preset\nrep(\"\"\"  tabPrev: ['KeyQ','Pad4'], tabNext: ['KeyE','Pad5'], uiAlt: ['Digit2','KeyT','Pad2'], uiInfo: ['Digit3','KeyI','Pad3'], uiFast: ['ShiftLeft','Pad7']\n};\"\"\",\n    \"\"\"  tabPrev: ['KeyQ','Pad4'], tabNext: ['KeyE','Pad5'], uiAlt: ['Digit2','KeyT','Pad2'], uiInfo: ['Digit3','KeyI','Pad3'], uiFast: ['ShiftLeft','Pad7'],\n  boxTop: ['Digit1','Pad3'], boxLeft: ['Digit2','Pad2'], boxRight: ['Digit3','Pad1'], boxBottom: ['Digit4','Pad0']   // the box's diamond (§6.4)\n};\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"On the Controls screen, hide `tabPrev`, `tabNext`, `uiAlt`, `uiInfo` and `uiFast` with\"\"\",\n    \"\"\"On the Controls screen, hide `tabPrev`, `tabNext`, `uiAlt`, `uiInfo`, `uiFast` and the four `box*` actions with\"\"\")\n\n# ---------- #10 / #21 photo range rule, van long lens\nrep(\"\"\"- **Enter.** Hold `watch`: zoom tween ×1.6 (0.25 s), a reticle at screen center, and the camera keeps the reticle in the central 60% (pans up to 7 tiles from Dana).\"\"\",\n    \"\"\"- **Enter.** Hold `watch`: zoom tween ×1.6 (0.25 s), a reticle at screen center, and the camera keeps the reticle in the central 60% (pans up to 7 tiles from Dana; 14 tiles with the van's long lens in Ep3).\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"  - **★ Face:** the target is within 220 units,\"\"\",\n    \"\"\"  - **Range rule:** beyond the camera's range (220 units; the van's long lens 360), every photo is Blurry (0 stars).\n  - **★ Face:** the target is in range,\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"Ren drives. Choose a spot (V1 Harlow curb, V2 Ridley east, V3 lot gap); van heat (§5.2); long lens (48 shots).\"\"\",\n    \"\"\"Ren drives. Choose a spot (V1 Harlow curb, V2 Ridley east, V3 lot gap); van heat (§5.2); long lens (48 shots, range 360, pans 14 tiles: every spot reaches the pumps).\"\"\")\n\n# ---------- #2 chase redesign (§5.6)\nrep(\"\"\"- **Runner AI:** at each node, pick the next node maximizing `dist(pursuer, node) − 0.5·alignment + rng·20`, never the edge blocked by Szabo's car (after 15 s the partner \"takes the car around\" and blocks one alley mouth: a parked car shape plus a blocked floor cell).\n- **Speeds:** runner sprints 118 for 9 s, then jogs 95 (no regen). Dana sprints 125 with stamina (§5.0).\"\"\",\n    \"\"\"- **Start:** the knockers' car pulls up and Corey bolts from the post with a **110-unit head start** (Dana is scripted at the bus shelter, P3).\n- **Runner AI:** the escape graph is a network of loops with no exits (App. A). At each node pick the next node maximizing `dist(pursuer, node) − 0.5·alignment + rng·20`, preferring edges that break line of sight. At 15 s Lou \"takes the car around\": his car blocks the edge Corey is about to take next (a car shape plus a blocked floor cell), forcing a reroute.\n- **Speeds and stamina:** Corey sprints 112 for 10 s, then runs 92, and recovers his sprint after 4 s out of Dana's sight. Dana sprints 125 on stamina (about 7 s from full, §5.0) and runs 85 otherwise. Sprinting from the start empties Dana before she closes the gap: the catch comes from routing (cut-throughs, the court gate instead of the fence), Lou's block and Corey tiring. **Target length: 20-45 s** for a competent player.\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"- **Win:** cuffed. **Lose:** the runner reaches the map-edge exit node; retry from the chase start.\"\"\",\n    \"\"\"- **Win:** cuffed. **Lose:** Corey stays out of Dana's sight for 8 s in a row (\"He's gone.\"). Retry from the chase start.\"\"\")\n\n# ---------- #22 box Rapport, #7 box keys and flip\nrep(\"\"\"- **Each exchange,** choose an approach. The four sit on a face-button diamond drawn in the dialog area (glyph + verb; keys 1-4; hover/click):\"\"\",\n    \"\"\"- **Each exchange,** choose an approach. The four sit on a face-button diamond drawn in the dialog area (glyph + verb + number key; hover/click). They use the box's own actions (`boxTop` △/1, `boxLeft` □/2, `boxRight` ○/3, `boxBottom` ✕/4), so the box never reads `cancel`, and Esc/Options still pause:\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"Succeeds only if the bluffed fact is known on the Board (Resolve −25). Otherwise Resolve +20 and Trust −1.\"\"\",\n    \"\"\"Succeeds only if the bluffed fact is known on the Board (Resolve −25). Otherwise Resolve +20 and Rapport −1.\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"it combos: an extra Resolve −20 and Trust +1.\"\"\",\n    \"\"\"it combos: an extra Resolve −20 and Rapport +1.\n- **Rapport** (0-3 pips, shown under the bars): each pip lowers the Fear a Lean adds by 3, and *Work for us* needs Rapport ≥ 1.\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"- **Flip:** when beat 3 is reached and Fear ≤ 60, a fourth approach appears: **\"Work for us\"**. Accept → CI flag (with consequences later).\"\"\",\n    \"\"\"- **Flip:** when beat 3 is reached, Fear ≤ 60 and Rapport ≥ 1, **\"Work for us\"** replaces ✕ Offer (same button). Accept → CI flag (with consequences later).\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"**Corey \"Stash\" Lyle (Ep2 box).** Starts at Resolve 100, Fear 30, Trust 0, 12 exchanges.\"\"\",\n    \"\"\"**Corey \"Stash\" Lyle (Ep2 box).** Starts at Resolve 100, Fear 30, Rapport 0, 12 exchanges.\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"| Flip | After B3 and Fear ≤ 60 → *Work for us* |\"\"\",\n    \"\"\"| Flip | After B3, Fear ≤ 60, Rapport ≥ 1 → *Work for us* (replaces ✕) |\"\"\")\n\n# ---------- #13 pager-clone line\nrep(\"\"\"  - A line needs **≥ 4 points including at least one direct item** (ACT photo or page).\"\"\",\n    \"\"\"  - A line needs **≥ 4 points including at least one direct item** (ACT photo or page).\n  - **The pager-clone line** targets the stash pager, **555-0110**. That number is on the label of Corey's seized pager, and the crew keeps it in service for whoever holds the stash. Direct items: the seized pager with its decoded memory (2) and each decoded page in evidence (+1, at most 2). Support: Corey's code statement B2 (1), Corey's face ID (1), an ★Act `stash-access` photo (1).\"\"\")\n\n# ---------- #1 / #3 economy\nrep(\"\"\"- Customer arrivals: Poisson λ = 0.12/s base (story), 0.25/s (versus); × night 1.2; × package freshness (1.2 fresh → 0.8 stale); × 0 while shut down.\"\"\",\n    \"\"\"- Customer arrivals (Poisson):\n  - **story field missions:** 0.12/s (observation pace)\n  - **interludes as Tee:** 0.35/s (a busy night)\n  - **versus:** 0.30/s\n\n  Story and interludes multiply by night 1.2 and package freshness (1.2 fresh → 0.8 stale); versus uses no multipliers; × 0 while shut down. At $10 a vial and 2 vials per customer on average, an interlude makes about $7-8/s and versus about $6/s at full uptime, before shutdowns.\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"- Re-up needed when the stash < 30 vials (versus: < 20).\"\"\",\n    \"\"\"- Re-up needed when the stash < 30 vials (versus starts with 60 and re-ups below 20).\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"### 7.4 Interludes (all at night, 4-6 min, CornerSim running)\"\"\",\n    \"\"\"### 7.4 Interludes (all at night, 5:00 of real time on a fast clock 22:00 → 02:00, CornerSim running; targets are about 70-80% of what the rates allow)\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"| I1 | Ep1 | $2,400 |\"\"\", \"\"\"| I1 | Ep1 | $1,500 |\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"| I2 | Ep2 | $2,800 |\"\"\", \"\"\"| I2 | Ep2 | $1,600 |\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"| I3 | Ep3 | $3,600 | Easy's summons at Mama B's back room (scene: Easy, Lonnie, Tee); double shift with Pigeon promoted to runner; the van event (if burned); Sunday's hearse rolls by (panic shutdown); Rook missing if arrested |\"\"\",\n    \"\"\"| I3 | Ep3 | $2,000 (a stretch: making back the loss) | Easy's summons at Mama B's back room (scene: Easy, Lonnie, Tee); double shift with Pigeon promoted to runner; the van event (if burned); Sunday's hearse rolls by (panic shutdown); Rook missing if arrested; **if the wall-off stop didn't happen:** two distant gunshots from Harlow at 01:10 (Rook went after Sunday's hearse; nobody hit) and a 40-s shutdown |\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"| I4 | Ep4 | $3,000 |\"\"\", \"\"\"| I4 | Ep4 | $1,700 |\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"  - **Corner win:** at time-up, Count ≥ **$3,000** and Evidence < 100.\"\"\",\n    \"\"\"  - **Corner win:** at time-up, Count ≥ the **quota: $1,200** for 5:00 ($240 per minute of round length) and Evidence < 100.\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"<meta name=\"hub:session-goal\" content=\"Cops: build a 100-point case. Corner: make $3,000 unseen.\">\"\"\",\n    \"\"\"<meta name=\"hub:session-goal\" content=\"Cops: build a 100-point case. Corner: make $1,200 unseen.\">\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"`cash` at Count ≥ $2,000 |\"\"\", \"\"\"`cash` once Count reaches 2/3 of the quota |\"\"\")\n\n# ---------- #5 seats exception\nrep(\"\"\"so players alternate sides between rounds. With 1 player: Detail vs bot Corner. With 3: two on one side.\"\"\",\n    \"\"\"so players alternate sides between rounds. **Exception:** a single human always plays Detail (vs a bot Corner). With 3: two on one side.\"\"\")\n\n# ---------- #9 versus zone\nrep(\"\"\"on the **versus zone** of the same map (cells 18-50 × 16-44: Ridley between Abbott and Harlow, Gaither, the two alleys, the Courts lane).\"\"\",\n    \"\"\"on the **versus zone** of the same map (cells 10-55 × 15-45: Ridley between Abbott and Harlow, Gaither from Dunmore to the strip, the two alleys, the strip, the Courts lane).\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"**Versus zone:** cells x 18-50, y 16-44. Every walkable cell outside it is blocked for players. Draw sawhorses and tape where streets leave the zone. Civilians spawn and leave at the zone's street edges.\"\"\",\n    \"\"\"**Versus zone:** cells x 10-55, y 15-45.\n- **Characters** (players, bots, civilians) can't leave it: a character-only boundary check, not `map.block`.\n- **Cars:** patrol cars drive the loop above and pass through the zone's edges on Ridley. Knockers drive in along Ridley or Gaither and stop at the curb nearest their target.\n- **Dressing:** sawhorses and tape where streets leave the zone. Civilians spawn and leave at its street edges.\"\"\")\n\n# ---------- #5 / #6 hub flow, finish and protocol gaps\nold_flow = \"\"\"```js\nif (window.AIHub && AIHub.active) {                      // straight into the round: no title, attract or menus\n  game.start({ scenes, scene: 'hubWait', boot });        // 'Connecting…' (no prompts)\n  const info = await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'shared-world', seats: [1, 4] });   // the hub's own card (no card: true)\n  if (!info) game.go('title');                           // no hub after all: the normal game\n  else { await Versus.buildRound(info); AIHub.ready(); } // roster from AIHub.rng('roster'); sides from seats + info.round\n}\nAIHub.on('start', () => Versus.countdown());             // overlay: role card + 3-2-1 until AIHub.time() >= 0\n```\"\"\"\nnew_flow = \"\"\"```js\nif (window.AIHub && AIHub.active) (async () => {         // async wrapper: the game's IIFE itself is not async\n  game.start({ scenes, scene: 'hubWait', boot });        // 'Connecting…' (no prompts): straight into the round, no title/attract/menus\n  AIHub.on('start', () => Versus.countdown());           // overlay: role card + 3-2-1 until AIHub.time() >= 0\n  const info = await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'shared-world', seats: [1, 4] });   // the hub's own card (no card: true)\n  if (!info) { game.go('title'); return; }               // no hub after all: the normal game\n  await Versus.buildRound(info);                         // roster from AIHub.rng('roster'); sides from seats + info.round\n  AIHub.ready();                                         // once, with no key press\n})().catch(e => { game.fail('hub', e); AIHub.fail(String((e && e.message) || e)); });\nelse game.start({ scenes, scene: 'title', boot });\n```\"\"\"\nrep(old_flow, new_flow)\nrep(\"\"\"  - `standings`: winners `[[winning side ids],[losing side ids]]`; draw `[[all ids]]`. Only hub player ids, never bots.\n  - `scores`: personal scores.\n  - `stats`: `{id:{Photos, Burns, Count}}`.\n  - `awards`.\"\"\",\n    \"\"\"  - `standings`: winners `[[winning side ids],[losing side ids]]`; draw `[[all ids]]`. Use only ids from `AIHub.players` that haven't left (left players may be omitted: the hub places them last). Never bots, never the server's own id.\n  - `won`: when only one side has humans (one player vs bots, or every human on one side), pass `won: true` or `false` for that side. Standings alone can't say it.\n  - `scores`: `{ id: personalScore }`.\n  - `stats`: `{ id: { Photos, Burns, 'Call-outs', Count } }` (numbers or short strings).\n  - `awards`: `[{ id, title, detail }]`, e.g. `{ id: 2, title: 'Eyes On', detail: '4 hand-to-hand photos' }`.\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"- **Session rules:**\n  - No other network use.\"\"\",\n    \"\"\"- **Session rules:**\n  - **Round length:** `min(300 s, info.limitMs − 5 s)`, so the host always finishes before the hub's hard limit (the harness sets it with `&limit=`).\n  - **Hidden host tab:** the engine's animation loop stops in a hidden tab. While `document.hidden` on the host, step the sim from a `setInterval` that calls `game.advance(elapsed)` (real elapsed time, capped at 1 s per call; browsers may throttle it to 1 Hz) and keep sending snapshots, so the other players don't freeze. Check that `advance` behaves while the loop is suspended. The hub voids the round after 20 s hidden anyway.\n  - **Names** from the hub are text: render them with `textContent` or canvas text (`E.font`), never as HTML.\n  - No other network use.\"\"\")\n\n# ---------- #8 Ep4 order: subpoena → Session 3 → kitchen\nrep(\"\"\"| 4.5 | **Kitchen** | Odessa's kitchen (box scene variant, warm light) | Pigeon at the table, Odessa at the stove (§6.4 kitchen) | `pigeonTrust` |\n| 4.6 | Numbers | Annex | The subpoena returns B1-B5. Halloway amends by phone (\"Same rules, Detective.\"). Pin burners to people | |\n| 4.7 | **Session 3** | wire, 6 calls (App. D) | The count is Thursdays at Mama B's after close; Friday's truck goes to \"the garage behind the Courts\". Tee mentions Dana's mother → choice: *call your mother* (`momSafe`: she goes to her sister's in the county) / *stay on the wire* | |\"\"\",\n    \"\"\"| 4.5 | Numbers | Annex | The subpoena returns B1-B5. Halloway amends by phone (\"Same rules, Detective.\"). Pin burners to people | |\n| 4.6 | **Session 3** | wire, 6 calls (App. D) | The count is Thursdays at Mama B's after close; Friday's truck goes to \"the garage behind the Courts\". Tee mentions Dana's mother → choice: *call your mother* (`momSafe`: she goes to her sister's in the county) / *stay on the wire* | |\n| 4.7 | **Kitchen** | Odessa's kitchen (box scene variant, warm light) | Pigeon at the table, Odessa at the stove (§6.4 kitchen). The \"I heard your call\" option exists only if Dana listened past S3-4's window | `pigeonTrust` |\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"| Box (4 approaches, evidence, combo, flip, lawyer) | 2.4 | 3.6 (Rook), 4.5 (kitchen variant) |\"\"\",\n    \"\"\"| Box (4 approaches, evidence, combo, flip, lawyer) | 2.4 | 3.6 (Rook), 4.7 (kitchen variant) |\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"| Affidavit + necessity honesty + judge | 2.6-2.7 | 4.6 (amendment) |\"\"\",\n    \"\"\"| Affidavit + necessity honesty + judge | 2.6-2.7 | 4.5 (amendment) |\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"| Wire: minimize, spot-check, log, voice ID, pages, fast-forward, legal | 3.2-3.3 | 3.6, 4.7 |\"\"\",\n    \"\"\"| Wire: minimize, spot-check, log, voice ID, pages, fast-forward, legal | 3.2-3.3 | 3.6, 4.6 |\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"| Moral choices (dilemma, threat to life, mother, canary, loss) | 3.4 | 3.6, 4.7, I3, I4 |\"\"\",\n    \"\"\"| Moral choices (dilemma, threat to life, mother, canary, loss) | 3.4 | 3.6, 4.6, I3, I4 |\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"Plan: tail Tee to the handout, get the packaging, subpoena the carrier. Ops choice 4. Gloria calls: \"Somebody was asking about you at the market.\" | Car scene |\"\"\",\n    \"\"\"Plan: tail Tee to the handout, get the packaging, subpoena the carrier. Ops choice 4. Gloria calls: \"Somebody was asking about you at the market.\" If Rook went after Sunday in I3, Lou: \"Somebody shot up a hearse on Harlow last night. Nobody hit. The church lost a window.\" | Car scene |\"\"\")\n\n# ---------- #11 exit interview testing field\nrep(\"\"\"\"testing\": \"<fill in: what you actually ran>\",\"\"\",\n    \"\"\"\"testing\": \"Lightweight, token-efficient testing as TASK.md allows (FPS targets and optimization out of scope). Run: <replace with what you actually ran, e.g. headless Node tests on the engine's fixed-step clock, engine check.mjs screenshots, Playwright gamepad/touch checks, the AI Hub harness, a viewport-matrix spot check>\",\"\"\")\n\n# ---------- #12 montage fixes\nrep(\"\"\"- **Three paths:** A (raid), B (money) or Shut Down. Each montage is 11-13 cards, picked by rules over the flags (App. G's card table).\"\"\",\n    \"\"\"- **Three paths:** A (raid), B (money) or Shut Down. Each montage is 14 cards (one per row group in App. G's table, in that order), each picked by rules over the flags.\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"  - Pigeon (3 fates): by `lossOn`, `pigeonTrust`, Path B runner and `rookFree`\n  - Corey (3 fates): `coreyCI`, `canary`, rescue\"\"\",\n    \"\"\"  - Pigeon (4 fates): by `lossOn`, `pigeonTrust`, Path B runner and `rookFree`\n  - Corey (4 fates): `coreyCI`, `canary`, rescue\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"reaches the montage with 11-13 valid cards |\"\"\", \"\"\"reaches the montage with all 14 cards valid |\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"**Montage cards** (11-13 shown; rules evaluated top to bottom, first match wins per person):\"\"\",\n    \"\"\"**Montage cards** (14, always in this order; for each person the first matching row wins):\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"| Tee | A + weight + Case high | \"Terrence Mabry: pleaded to twelve years. Never said Easy's name.\" |\"\"\",\n    \"\"\"| Tee | A + weight + `teeShort` | \"Terrence Mabry: pleaded to twelve years. Easy stopped paying his mother's rent in March.\" |\n| | A + weight + Case high | \"Terrence Mabry: pleaded to twelve years. Never said Easy's name.\" |\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"| | B + stay | \"Terrence Mabry: indicted with Darnell Booker eighteen months later.\" |\"\"\",\n    \"\"\"| | B + stay + `teeShort` | \"Terrence Mabry: cut loose by Easy, then indicted. Testified against him.\" |\n| | B + stay | \"Terrence Mabry: indicted with Darnell Booker eighteen months later.\" |\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"| Rook *(shown if `wallOff` or `rookFree`; otherwise the Sunday card)* | `wallOff` |\"\"\", \"\"\"| Rook (always) | `wallOff` |\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"| Sunday *(shown when Rook's card isn't)* | stay |\"\"\", \"\"\"| Sunday (always) | stay |\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"| Navarre | A / else |\"\"\", \"\"\"| Ren (always) | — | \"Renata Ocasio: transferred to the Tactical Section. Kept the camera.\" |\n| Navarre | A / else |\"\"\")\n\n# ---------- #15 patrol loop\nrep(\"\"\"a sedan shape drives a lane loop (Ridley → Gaither → Dunmore → Abbott) at 70 u/s\"\"\",\n    \"\"\"a sedan shape drives App. A's lane loop (Abbott → Ridley → Harlow → Dunmore) at 70 u/s\"\"\")\n\n# ---------- #17 overtime calls\nrep(\"\"\"(S1-OT: Tavon confirms the count spot, +4; S2-OT: Dink complains Tee is \"scared of phones now\", +4) |\"\"\",\n    \"\"\"(App. D calls S1-OT and S2-OT, +4 each) |\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"| S1-10 | 21:15 | pager | page `555-0769 33 07` | P | — | Decode → P1, \"the count\" |\"\"\",\n    \"\"\"| S1-10 | 21:15 | pager | page `555-0769 33 07` | P | — | Decode → P1, \"the count\" |\n| S1-OT | 22:10 | P1 | Tavon → Dink (only with ops choice *overtime*) | P | TAVON: Tee want it tight tonight. Extra man up on Harlow. / ★DINK: Package came in light, so we cutting the testers. / TAVON: Cut 'em. Ain't nobody gonna complain. | Crew structure + product handling (+4) |\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"| S2-8 | 00:30 | P1/P2 | drunk citizen → his ex | N | Sad, funny, about a dog he misses more than her | — |\"\"\",\n    \"\"\"| S2-8 | 00:30 | P1/P2 | drunk citizen → his ex | N | Sad, funny, about a dog he misses more than her | — |\n| S2-OT | 00:50 | P2 | Dink → Tavon (only with ops choice *overtime*) | P | DINK: Tee got scared of phones. Say after Friday nobody talk on these no more. / ★TAVON: Then how I'm supposed to reach the stash? / DINK: He say he got a plan. Everybody getting a new number. | Burner switch confirmed (+4) |\"\"\")\n\n# ---------- #18 garage doors\nrep(\"\"\"| `garage` | side door 50,50 · roll-up door 55,50-51 · inside 51-54,49-52 | The raid target |\"\"\",\n    \"\"\"| `garage` | side door 50,50 · roll-up door 55,50-51 · inside 51-54,49-52 | The raid target. Both doors are wall cells (`G`) in `ROWS`; scripts open them with `map.set(cx, cy, 0)` (the roll-up for the truck and at the breach, the side door at the breach) |\"\"\")\n\n# ---------- #19 judge grand jury question\nrep(\"\"\"| Q8 minimization | \"Who's monitoring, and do they know the rules?\" |\"\"\",\n    \"\"\"| Q9 grand jury | ticked falsely: \"Which grand jury? I'd like to see those returns.\" / not ticked: \"Why no grand jury subpoenas?\" | not ticked: \"Subpoenaed witnesses would warn the organization, and the people who know won't testify against it.\" | ticked falsely = denied |\n| Q8 minimization | \"Who's monitoring, and do they know the rules?\" |\"\"\")\n\n# ---------- #20 gunshot note\nrep(\"\"\"Used exactly twice in the game (Ep3 robbery warning shot if *Go in*, and offscreen in I3 if Rook goes after Sunday) |\"\"\",\n    \"\"\"Used in exactly one moment: two distant shots during I3 if the wall-off stop didn't happen (Rook goes after Sunday) |\"\"\")\n\n# ---------- #21 tests aligned with the spec; #1 balance test; #2 chase test\nrep(\"\"\"| meters | Brass 0 → shutdown scene; Heat thresholds flip the code and add lookouts |\"\"\",\n    \"\"\"| meters | Brass 0 → shutdown scene; Heat thresholds add the 3rd lookout and rotate payphones; the code flip happens in every Ep3 Session 2 |\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"| chase | Bot pursuer with good routing catches the runner within 60 s; the ditch happens; the kid takes it after 45 s if it's not searched |\"\"\",\n    \"\"\"| chase | A routing bot catches Corey in 20-45 s; a bot that sprints from the start along his exact path runs out of stamina and hasn't caught him by 15 s; out of sight 8 s → \"He's gone\"; the ditch happens; the bike kid takes the package after 45 s if it isn't searched |\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"| versus | A bots-only local match ends with a valid outcome;\"\"\",\n    \"\"\"| versus balance | 20 bots-only 5-minute rounds with competent bots on both sides: Corner wins 35-65%, Detail wins 35-65%, draws ≤ 20%. Tune the quota and evidence points until it holds |\n| versus | A bots-only local match ends with a valid outcome;\"\"\")\n\n# ---------- #23 tail band + route\nrep(\"\"\"  - under 48: too close; suspicion ×1.8 whenever you're in his view\"\"\",\n    \"\"\"  - under 64: too close; suspicion ×1.8 whenever you're in his view\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"`34,30` → `30,30` → `30,44 [window 3: carryout]` → `18,45` → `18,49` (END: the handout).\"\"\",\n    \"\"\"`34,30` → `33,31 [window 3: carryout]` → `30,32` → `30,44 [wait 3]` → `18,45` → `18,49` (END: the handout).\"\"\")\n\n# ---------- #24 Ridley lanes\nrep(\"\"\"- **Bus:** Ridley eastbound (y 28.8), stopping 4 s at 42,29.\"\"\",\n    \"\"\"- **Bus:** Ridley eastbound in row 28 (y 28.5), pulling into parking row 29 for 4 s at P3 (42,29).\n- **Ridley lanes:** westbound row 27, eastbound row 28, parking row 29 (south curb). Parked cars (the Chevy, van V2) use parking cells only. Keep P3's curb (x 40-44, row 29) clear for the bus.\"\"\")\n\nopen(p, 'w').write(s)\nprint('review patch applied')\nPYEOF\npython3 /tmp/wireplan-scripts/patch_review.py","description":"Apply all verified reviewer fixes to PLAN.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12273,"cache_read_input_tokens":542629,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":12273,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e2aa65a8-ee1a-45c4-b8e6-f96cf188e23d","uuid":"37f82fe2-f117-4cd5-a08f-f55bb2e5d612","timestamp":"2026-11-03T19:21:41.497Z","request_id":"req_011CggY4hktHqF6xPV7T8Ggz","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_013S3T55VQqY5fWeC4F5ramC":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-105319/work && cp PLAN.md /tmp/wireplan-scripts/PLAN.before-review.md && cat > /tmp/wireplan-scripts/patch_review.py <<'PYEOF'\nimport re\np = 'PLAN.md'; s = open(p).read()\ndef rep(old, new, count=1):\n    global s\n    n = s.count(old)\n    assert n == count, f'expected {count} match(es), found {n}: {old[:90]!r}'\n    s = s.replace(old, new)\n\n# ---------- #16 broken section refs\nrep(\"hub tags (§9.6)\", \"hub tags (§9.3)\")\nrep(\"\"\"- **In an AI Hub session** (`AIHub.active`), 99-start skips the title: `menu.quit = false`, `autoPause: false`, and goes straight into the versus round (§9.6).\"\"\",\n    \"\"\"- **In an AI Hub session** (`AIHub.active`), 99-start skips the title: `menu.quit = false`, `autoPause: false`, and §9.3's async flow calls `game.start` itself and goes straight into the versus round. The `game.start` call above is the non-session path.\"\"\")\n\n# ---------- #14 global per-step systems (architecture rule 8)\nrep(\"\"\"7. **One save state.** `STATE` (App. J) is the only thing `game.saves` writes. Systems rebuild themselves from it.\"\"\",\n    \"\"\"7. **One save state.** `STATE` (App. J) is the only thing `game.saves` writes. Systems rebuild themselves from it.\n8. **Global per-step systems run from a scene wrapper.** Engine timers and tweens end with each scene, so every scene is registered through `withGlobals(scene)`, whose `update` first runs `Globals.tick(dt)`: the idle timer, the attract director, the device/glyph watcher and the hub hooks.\"\"\")\n\n# ---------- #7 box actions in the preset\nrep(\"\"\"  tabPrev: ['KeyQ','Pad4'], tabNext: ['KeyE','Pad5'], uiAlt: ['Digit2','KeyT','Pad2'], uiInfo: ['Digit3','KeyI','Pad3'], uiFast: ['ShiftLeft','Pad7']\n};\"\"\",\n    \"\"\"  tabPrev: ['KeyQ','Pad4'], tabNext: ['KeyE','Pad5'], uiAlt: ['Digit2','KeyT','Pad2'], uiInfo: ['Digit3','KeyI','Pad3'], uiFast: ['ShiftLeft','Pad7'],\n  boxTop: ['Digit1','Pad3'], boxLeft: ['Digit2','Pad2'], boxRight: ['Digit3','Pad1'], boxBottom: ['Digit4','Pad0']   // the box's diamond (§6.4)\n};\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"On the Controls screen, hide `tabPrev`, `tabNext`, `uiAlt`, `uiInfo` and `uiFast` with\"\"\",\n    \"\"\"On the Controls screen, hide `tabPrev`, `tabNext`, `uiAlt`, `uiInfo`, `uiFast` and the four `box*` actions with\"\"\")\n\n# ---------- #10 / #21 photo range rule, van long lens\nrep(\"\"\"- **Enter.** Hold `watch`: zoom tween ×1.6 (0.25 s), a reticle at screen center, and the camera keeps the reticle in the central 60% (pans up to 7 tiles from Dana).\"\"\",\n    \"\"\"- **Enter.** Hold `watch`: zoom tween ×1.6 (0.25 s), a reticle at screen center, and the camera keeps the reticle in the central 60% (pans up to 7 tiles from Dana; 14 tiles with the van's long lens in Ep3).\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"  - **★ Face:** the target is within 220 units,\"\"\",\n    \"\"\"  - **Range rule:** beyond the camera's range (220 units; the van's long lens 360), every photo is Blurry (0 stars).\n  - **★ Face:** the target is in range,\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"Ren drives. Choose a spot (V1 Harlow curb, V2 Ridley east, V3 lot gap); van heat (§5.2); long lens (48 shots).\"\"\",\n    \"\"\"Ren drives. Choose a spot (V1 Harlow curb, V2 Ridley east, V3 lot gap); van heat (§5.2); long lens (48 shots, range 360, pans 14 tiles: every spot reaches the pumps).\"\"\")\n\n# ---------- #2 chase redesign (§5.6)\nrep(\"\"\"- **Runner AI:** at each node, pick the next node maximizing `dist(pursuer, node) − 0.5·alignment + rng·20`, never the edge blocked by Szabo's car (after 15 s the partner \"takes the car around\" and blocks one alley mouth: a parked car shape plus a blocked floor cell).\n- **Speeds:** runner sprints 118 for 9 s, then jogs 95 (no regen). Dana sprints 125 with stamina (§5.0).\"\"\",\n    \"\"\"- **Start:** the knockers' car pulls up and Corey bolts from the post with a **110-unit head start** (Dana is scripted at the bus shelter, P3).\n- **Runner AI:** the escape graph is a network of loops with no exits (App. A). At each node pick the next node maximizing `dist(pursuer, node) − 0.5·alignment + rng·20`, preferring edges that break line of sight. At 15 s Lou \"takes the car around\": his car blocks the edge Corey is about to take next (a car shape plus a blocked floor cell), forcing a reroute.\n- **Speeds and stamina:** Corey sprints 112 for 10 s, then runs 92, and recovers his sprint after 4 s out of Dana's sight. Dana sprints 125 on stamina (about 7 s from full, §5.0) and runs 85 otherwise. Sprinting from the start empties Dana before she closes the gap: the catch comes from routing (cut-throughs, the court gate instead of the fence), Lou's block and Corey tiring. **Target length: 20-45 s** for a competent player.\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"- **Win:** cuffed. **Lose:** the runner reaches the map-edge exit node; retry from the chase start.\"\"\",\n    \"\"\"- **Win:** cuffed. **Lose:** Corey stays out of Dana's sight for 8 s in a row (\"He's gone.\"). Retry from the chase start.\"\"\")\n\n# ---------- #22 box Rapport, #7 box keys and flip\nrep(\"\"\"- **Each exchange,** choose an approach. The four sit on a face-button diamond drawn in the dialog area (glyph + verb; keys 1-4; hover/click):\"\"\",\n    \"\"\"- **Each exchange,** choose an approach. The four sit on a face-button diamond drawn in the dialog area (glyph + verb + number key; hover/click). They use the box's own actions (`boxTop` △/1, `boxLeft` □/2, `boxRight` ○/3, `boxBottom` ✕/4), so the box never reads `cancel`, and Esc/Options still pause:\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"Succeeds only if the bluffed fact is known on the Board (Resolve −25). Otherwise Resolve +20 and Trust −1.\"\"\",\n    \"\"\"Succeeds only if the bluffed fact is known on the Board (Resolve −25). Otherwise Resolve +20 and Rapport −1.\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"it combos: an extra Resolve −20 and Trust +1.\"\"\",\n    \"\"\"it combos: an extra Resolve −20 and Rapport +1.\n- **Rapport** (0-3 pips, shown under the bars): each pip lowers the Fear a Lean adds by 3, and *Work for us* needs Rapport ≥ 1.\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"- **Flip:** when beat 3 is reached and Fear ≤ 60, a fourth approach appears: **\"Work for us\"**. Accept → CI flag (with consequences later).\"\"\",\n    \"\"\"- **Flip:** when beat 3 is reached, Fear ≤ 60 and Rapport ≥ 1, **\"Work for us\"** replaces ✕ Offer (same button). Accept → CI flag (with consequences later).\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"**Corey \"Stash\" Lyle (Ep2 box).** Starts at Resolve 100, Fear 30, Trust 0, 12 exchanges.\"\"\",\n    \"\"\"**Corey \"Stash\" Lyle (Ep2 box).** Starts at Resolve 100, Fear 30, Rapport 0, 12 exchanges.\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"| Flip | After B3 and Fear ≤ 60 → *Work for us* |\"\"\",\n    \"\"\"| Flip | After B3, Fear ≤ 60, Rapport ≥ 1 → *Work for us* (replaces ✕) |\"\"\")\n\n# ---------- #13 pager-clone line\nrep(\"\"\"  - A line needs **≥ 4 points including at least one direct item** (ACT photo or page).\"\"\",\n    \"\"\"  - A line needs **≥ 4 points including at least one direct item** (ACT photo or page).\n  - **The pager-clone line** targets the stash pager, **555-0110**. That number is on the label of Corey's seized pager, and the crew keeps it in service for whoever holds the stash. Direct items: the seized pager with its decoded memory (2) and each decoded page in evidence (+1, at most 2). Support: Corey's code statement B2 (1), Corey's face ID (1), an ★Act `stash-access` photo (1).\"\"\")\n\n# ---------- #1 / #3 economy\nrep(\"\"\"- Customer arrivals: Poisson λ = 0.12/s base (story), 0.25/s (versus); × night 1.2; × package freshness (1.2 fresh → 0.8 stale); × 0 while shut down.\"\"\",\n    \"\"\"- Customer arrivals (Poisson):\n  - **story field missions:** 0.12/s (observation pace)\n  - **interludes as Tee:** 0.35/s (a busy night)\n  - **versus:** 0.30/s\n\n  Story and interludes multiply by night 1.2 and package freshness (1.2 fresh → 0.8 stale); versus uses no multipliers; × 0 while shut down. At $10 a vial and 2 vials per customer on average, an interlude makes about $7-8/s and versus about $6/s at full uptime, before shutdowns.\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"- Re-up needed when the stash < 30 vials (versus: < 20).\"\"\",\n    \"\"\"- Re-up needed when the stash < 30 vials (versus starts with 60 and re-ups below 20).\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"### 7.4 Interludes (all at night, 4-6 min, CornerSim running)\"\"\",\n    \"\"\"### 7.4 Interludes (all at night, 5:00 of real time on a fast clock 22:00 → 02:00, CornerSim running; targets are about 70-80% of what the rates allow)\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"| I1 | Ep1 | $2,400 |\"\"\", \"\"\"| I1 | Ep1 | $1,500 |\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"| I2 | Ep2 | $2,800 |\"\"\", \"\"\"| I2 | Ep2 | $1,600 |\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"| I3 | Ep3 | $3,600 | Easy's summons at Mama B's back room (scene: Easy, Lonnie, Tee); double shift with Pigeon promoted to runner; the van event (if burned); Sunday's hearse rolls by (panic shutdown); Rook missing if arrested |\"\"\",\n    \"\"\"| I3 | Ep3 | $2,000 (a stretch: making back the loss) | Easy's summons at Mama B's back room (scene: Easy, Lonnie, Tee); double shift with Pigeon promoted to runner; the van event (if burned); Sunday's hearse rolls by (panic shutdown); Rook missing if arrested; **if the wall-off stop didn't happen:** two distant gunshots from Harlow at 01:10 (Rook went after Sunday's hearse; nobody hit) and a 40-s shutdown |\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"| I4 | Ep4 | $3,000 |\"\"\", \"\"\"| I4 | Ep4 | $1,700 |\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"  - **Corner win:** at time-up, Count ≥ **$3,000** and Evidence < 100.\"\"\",\n    \"\"\"  - **Corner win:** at time-up, Count ≥ the **quota: $1,200** for 5:00 ($240 per minute of round length) and Evidence < 100.\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"<meta name=\"hub:session-goal\" content=\"Cops: build a 100-point case. Corner: make $3,000 unseen.\">\"\"\",\n    \"\"\"<meta name=\"hub:session-goal\" content=\"Cops: build a 100-point case. Corner: make $1,200 unseen.\">\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"`cash` at Count ≥ $2,000 |\"\"\", \"\"\"`cash` once Count reaches 2/3 of the quota |\"\"\")\n\n# ---------- #5 seats exception\nrep(\"\"\"so players alternate sides between rounds. With 1 player: Detail vs bot Corner. With 3: two on one side.\"\"\",\n    \"\"\"so players alternate sides between rounds. **Exception:** a single human always plays Detail (vs a bot Corner). With 3: two on one side.\"\"\")\n\n# ---------- #9 versus zone\nrep(\"\"\"on the **versus zone** of the same map (cells 18-50 × 16-44: Ridley between Abbott and Harlow, Gaither, the two alleys, the Courts lane).\"\"\",\n    \"\"\"on the **versus zone** of the same map (cells 10-55 × 15-45: Ridley between Abbott and Harlow, Gaither from Dunmore to the strip, the two alleys, the strip, the Courts lane).\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"**Versus zone:** cells x 18-50, y 16-44. Every walkable cell outside it is blocked for players. Draw sawhorses and tape where streets leave the zone. Civilians spawn and leave at the zone's street edges.\"\"\",\n    \"\"\"**Versus zone:** cells x 10-55, y 15-45.\n- **Characters** (players, bots, civilians) can't leave it: a character-only boundary check, not `map.block`.\n- **Cars:** patrol cars drive the loop above and pass through the zone's edges on Ridley. Knockers drive in along Ridley or Gaither and stop at the curb nearest their target.\n- **Dressing:** sawhorses and tape where streets leave the zone. Civilians spawn and leave at its street edges.\"\"\")\n\n# ---------- #5 / #6 hub flow, finish and protocol gaps\nold_flow = \"\"\"```js\nif (window.AIHub && AIHub.active) {                      // straight into the round: no title, attract or menus\n  game.start({ scenes, scene: 'hubWait', boot });        // 'Connecting…' (no prompts)\n  const info = await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'shared-world', seats: [1, 4] });   // the hub's own card (no card: true)\n  if (!info) game.go('title');                           // no hub after all: the normal game\n  else { await Versus.buildRound(info); AIHub.ready(); } // roster from AIHub.rng('roster'); sides from seats + info.round\n}\nAIHub.on('start', () => Versus.countdown());             // overlay: role card + 3-2-1 until AIHub.time() >= 0\n```\"\"\"\nnew_flow = \"\"\"```js\nif (window.AIHub && AIHub.active) (async () => {         // async wrapper: the game's IIFE itself is not async\n  game.start({ scenes, scene: 'hubWait', boot });        // 'Connecting…' (no prompts): straight into the round, no title/attract/menus\n  AIHub.on('start', () => Versus.countdown());           // overlay: role card + 3-2-1 until AIHub.time() >= 0\n  const info = await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'shared-world', seats: [1, 4] });   // the hub's own card (no card: true)\n  if (!info) { game.go('title'); return; }               // no hub after all: the normal game\n  await Versus.buildRound(info);                         // roster from AIHub.rng('roster'); sides from seats + info.round\n  AIHub.ready();                                         // once, with no key press\n})().catch(e => { game.fail('hub', e); AIHub.fail(String((e && e.message) || e)); });\nelse game.start({ scenes, scene: 'title', boot });\n```\"\"\"\nrep(old_flow, new_flow)\nrep(\"\"\"  - `standings`: winners `[[winning side ids],[losing side ids]]`; draw `[[all ids]]`. Only hub player ids, never bots.\n  - `scores`: personal scores.\n  - `stats`: `{id:{Photos, Burns, Count}}`.\n  - `awards`.\"\"\",\n    \"\"\"  - `standings`: winners `[[winning side ids],[losing side ids]]`; draw `[[all ids]]`. Use only ids from `AIHub.players` that haven't left (left players may be omitted: the hub places them last). Never bots, never the server's own id.\n  - `won`: when only one side has humans (one player vs bots, or every human on one side), pass `won: true` or `false` for that side. Standings alone can't say it.\n  - `scores`: `{ id: personalScore }`.\n  - `stats`: `{ id: { Photos, Burns, 'Call-outs', Count } }` (numbers or short strings).\n  - `awards`: `[{ id, title, detail }]`, e.g. `{ id: 2, title: 'Eyes On', detail: '4 hand-to-hand photos' }`.\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"- **Session rules:**\n  - No other network use.\"\"\",\n    \"\"\"- **Session rules:**\n  - **Round length:** `min(300 s, info.limitMs − 5 s)`, so the host always finishes before the hub's hard limit (the harness sets it with `&limit=`).\n  - **Hidden host tab:** the engine's animation loop stops in a hidden tab. While `document.hidden` on the host, step the sim from a `setInterval` that calls `game.advance(elapsed)` (real elapsed time, capped at 1 s per call; browsers may throttle it to 1 Hz) and keep sending snapshots, so the other players don't freeze. Check that `advance` behaves while the loop is suspended. The hub voids the round after 20 s hidden anyway.\n  - **Names** from the hub are text: render them with `textContent` or canvas text (`E.font`), never as HTML.\n  - No other network use.\"\"\")\n\n# ---------- #8 Ep4 order: subpoena → Session 3 → kitchen\nrep(\"\"\"| 4.5 | **Kitchen** | Odessa's kitchen (box scene variant, warm light) | Pigeon at the table, Odessa at the stove (§6.4 kitchen) | `pigeonTrust` |\n| 4.6 | Numbers | Annex | The subpoena returns B1-B5. Halloway amends by phone (\"Same rules, Detective.\"). Pin burners to people | |\n| 4.7 | **Session 3** | wire, 6 calls (App. D) | The count is Thursdays at Mama B's after close; Friday's truck goes to \"the garage behind the Courts\". Tee mentions Dana's mother → choice: *call your mother* (`momSafe`: she goes to her sister's in the county) / *stay on the wire* | |\"\"\",\n    \"\"\"| 4.5 | Numbers | Annex | The subpoena returns B1-B5. Halloway amends by phone (\"Same rules, Detective.\"). Pin burners to people | |\n| 4.6 | **Session 3** | wire, 6 calls (App. D) | The count is Thursdays at Mama B's after close; Friday's truck goes to \"the garage behind the Courts\". Tee mentions Dana's mother → choice: *call your mother* (`momSafe`: she goes to her sister's in the county) / *stay on the wire* | |\n| 4.7 | **Kitchen** | Odessa's kitchen (box scene variant, warm light) | Pigeon at the table, Odessa at the stove (§6.4 kitchen). The \"I heard your call\" option exists only if Dana listened past S3-4's window | `pigeonTrust` |\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"| Box (4 approaches, evidence, combo, flip, lawyer) | 2.4 | 3.6 (Rook), 4.5 (kitchen variant) |\"\"\",\n    \"\"\"| Box (4 approaches, evidence, combo, flip, lawyer) | 2.4 | 3.6 (Rook), 4.7 (kitchen variant) |\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"| Affidavit + necessity honesty + judge | 2.6-2.7 | 4.6 (amendment) |\"\"\",\n    \"\"\"| Affidavit + necessity honesty + judge | 2.6-2.7 | 4.5 (amendment) |\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"| Wire: minimize, spot-check, log, voice ID, pages, fast-forward, legal | 3.2-3.3 | 3.6, 4.7 |\"\"\",\n    \"\"\"| Wire: minimize, spot-check, log, voice ID, pages, fast-forward, legal | 3.2-3.3 | 3.6, 4.6 |\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"| Moral choices (dilemma, threat to life, mother, canary, loss) | 3.4 | 3.6, 4.7, I3, I4 |\"\"\",\n    \"\"\"| Moral choices (dilemma, threat to life, mother, canary, loss) | 3.4 | 3.6, 4.6, I3, I4 |\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"Plan: tail Tee to the handout, get the packaging, subpoena the carrier. Ops choice 4. Gloria calls: \"Somebody was asking about you at the market.\" | Car scene |\"\"\",\n    \"\"\"Plan: tail Tee to the handout, get the packaging, subpoena the carrier. Ops choice 4. Gloria calls: \"Somebody was asking about you at the market.\" If Rook went after Sunday in I3, Lou: \"Somebody shot up a hearse on Harlow last night. Nobody hit. The church lost a window.\" | Car scene |\"\"\")\n\n# ---------- #11 exit interview testing field\nrep(\"\"\"\"testing\": \"<fill in: what you actually ran>\",\"\"\",\n    \"\"\"\"testing\": \"Lightweight, token-efficient testing as TASK.md allows (FPS targets and optimization out of scope). Run: <replace with what you actually ran, e.g. headless Node tests on the engine's fixed-step clock, engine check.mjs screenshots, Playwright gamepad/touch checks, the AI Hub harness, a viewport-matrix spot check>\",\"\"\")\n\n# ---------- #12 montage fixes\nrep(\"\"\"- **Three paths:** A (raid), B (money) or Shut Down. Each montage is 11-13 cards, picked by rules over the flags (App. G's card table).\"\"\",\n    \"\"\"- **Three paths:** A (raid), B (money) or Shut Down. Each montage is 14 cards (one per row group in App. G's table, in that order), each picked by rules over the flags.\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"  - Pigeon (3 fates): by `lossOn`, `pigeonTrust`, Path B runner and `rookFree`\n  - Corey (3 fates): `coreyCI`, `canary`, rescue\"\"\",\n    \"\"\"  - Pigeon (4 fates): by `lossOn`, `pigeonTrust`, Path B runner and `rookFree`\n  - Corey (4 fates): `coreyCI`, `canary`, rescue\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"reaches the montage with 11-13 valid cards |\"\"\", \"\"\"reaches the montage with all 14 cards valid |\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"**Montage cards** (11-13 shown; rules evaluated top to bottom, first match wins per person):\"\"\",\n    \"\"\"**Montage cards** (14, always in this order; for each person the first matching row wins):\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"| Tee | A + weight + Case high | \"Terrence Mabry: pleaded to twelve years. Never said Easy's name.\" |\"\"\",\n    \"\"\"| Tee | A + weight + `teeShort` | \"Terrence Mabry: pleaded to twelve years. Easy stopped paying his mother's rent in March.\" |\n| | A + weight + Case high | \"Terrence Mabry: pleaded to twelve years. Never said Easy's name.\" |\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"| | B + stay | \"Terrence Mabry: indicted with Darnell Booker eighteen months later.\" |\"\"\",\n    \"\"\"| | B + stay + `teeShort` | \"Terrence Mabry: cut loose by Easy, then indicted. Testified against him.\" |\n| | B + stay | \"Terrence Mabry: indicted with Darnell Booker eighteen months later.\" |\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"| Rook *(shown if `wallOff` or `rookFree`; otherwise the Sunday card)* | `wallOff` |\"\"\", \"\"\"| Rook (always) | `wallOff` |\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"| Sunday *(shown when Rook's card isn't)* | stay |\"\"\", \"\"\"| Sunday (always) | stay |\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"| Navarre | A / else |\"\"\", \"\"\"| Ren (always) | — | \"Renata Ocasio: transferred to the Tactical Section. Kept the camera.\" |\n| Navarre | A / else |\"\"\")\n\n# ---------- #15 patrol loop\nrep(\"\"\"a sedan shape drives a lane loop (Ridley → Gaither → Dunmore → Abbott) at 70 u/s\"\"\",\n    \"\"\"a sedan shape drives App. A's lane loop (Abbott → Ridley → Harlow → Dunmore) at 70 u/s\"\"\")\n\n# ---------- #17 overtime calls\nrep(\"\"\"(S1-OT: Tavon confirms the count spot, +4; S2-OT: Dink complains Tee is \"scared of phones now\", +4) |\"\"\",\n    \"\"\"(App. D calls S1-OT and S2-OT, +4 each) |\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"| S1-10 | 21:15 | pager | page `555-0769 33 07` | P | — | Decode → P1, \"the count\" |\"\"\",\n    \"\"\"| S1-10 | 21:15 | pager | page `555-0769 33 07` | P | — | Decode → P1, \"the count\" |\n| S1-OT | 22:10 | P1 | Tavon → Dink (only with ops choice *overtime*) | P | TAVON: Tee want it tight tonight. Extra man up on Harlow. / ★DINK: Package came in light, so we cutting the testers. / TAVON: Cut 'em. Ain't nobody gonna complain. | Crew structure + product handling (+4) |\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"| S2-8 | 00:30 | P1/P2 | drunk citizen → his ex | N | Sad, funny, about a dog he misses more than her | — |\"\"\",\n    \"\"\"| S2-8 | 00:30 | P1/P2 | drunk citizen → his ex | N | Sad, funny, about a dog he misses more than her | — |\n| S2-OT | 00:50 | P2 | Dink → Tavon (only with ops choice *overtime*) | P | DINK: Tee got scared of phones. Say after Friday nobody talk on these no more. / ★TAVON: Then how I'm supposed to reach the stash? / DINK: He say he got a plan. Everybody getting a new number. | Burner switch confirmed (+4) |\"\"\")\n\n# ---------- #18 garage doors\nrep(\"\"\"| `garage` | side door 50,50 · roll-up door 55,50-51 · inside 51-54,49-52 | The raid target |\"\"\",\n    \"\"\"| `garage` | side door 50,50 · roll-up door 55,50-51 · inside 51-54,49-52 | The raid target. Both doors are wall cells (`G`) in `ROWS`; scripts open them with `map.set(cx, cy, 0)` (the roll-up for the truck and at the breach, the side door at the breach) |\"\"\")\n\n# ---------- #19 judge grand jury question\nrep(\"\"\"| Q8 minimization | \"Who's monitoring, and do they know the rules?\" |\"\"\",\n    \"\"\"| Q9 grand jury | ticked falsely: \"Which grand jury? I'd like to see those returns.\" / not ticked: \"Why no grand jury subpoenas?\" | not ticked: \"Subpoenaed witnesses would warn the organization, and the people who know won't testify against it.\" | ticked falsely = denied |\n| Q8 minimization | \"Who's monitoring, and do they know the rules?\" |\"\"\")\n\n# ---------- #20 gunshot note\nrep(\"\"\"Used exactly twice in the game (Ep3 robbery warning shot if *Go in*, and offscreen in I3 if Rook goes after Sunday) |\"\"\",\n    \"\"\"Used in exactly one moment: two distant shots during I3 if the wall-off stop didn't happen (Rook goes after Sunday) |\"\"\")\n\n# ---------- #21 tests aligned with the spec; #1 balance test; #2 chase test\nrep(\"\"\"| meters | Brass 0 → shutdown scene; Heat thresholds flip the code and add lookouts |\"\"\",\n    \"\"\"| meters | Brass 0 → shutdown scene; Heat thresholds add the 3rd lookout and rotate payphones; the code flip happens in every Ep3 Session 2 |\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"| chase | Bot pursuer with good routing catches the runner within 60 s; the ditch happens; the kid takes it after 45 s if it's not searched |\"\"\",\n    \"\"\"| chase | A routing bot catches Corey in 20-45 s; a bot that sprints from the start along his exact path runs out of stamina and hasn't caught him by 15 s; out of sight 8 s → \"He's gone\"; the ditch happens; the bike kid takes the package after 45 s if it isn't searched |\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"| versus | A bots-only local match ends with a valid outcome;\"\"\",\n    \"\"\"| versus balance | 20 bots-only 5-minute rounds with competent bots on both sides: Corner wins 35-65%, Detail wins 35-65%, draws ≤ 20%. Tune the quota and evidence points until it holds |\n| versus | A bots-only local match ends with a valid outcome;\"\"\")\n\n# ---------- #23 tail band + route\nrep(\"\"\"  - under 48: too close; suspicion ×1.8 whenever you're in his view\"\"\",\n    \"\"\"  - under 64: too close; suspicion ×1.8 whenever you're in his view\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"`34,30` → `30,30` → `30,44 [window 3: carryout]` → `18,45` → `18,49` (END: the handout).\"\"\",\n    \"\"\"`34,30` → `33,31 [window 3: carryout]` → `30,32` → `30,44 [wait 3]` → `18,45` → `18,49` (END: the handout).\"\"\")\n\n# ---------- #24 Ridley lanes\nrep(\"\"\"- **Bus:** Ridley eastbound (y 28.8), stopping 4 s at 42,29.\"\"\",\n    \"\"\"- **Bus:** Ridley eastbound in row 28 (y 28.5), pulling into parking row 29 for 4 s at P3 (42,29).\n- **Ridley lanes:** westbound row 27, eastbound row 28, parking row 29 (south curb). Parked cars (the Chevy, van V2) use parking cells only. Keep P3's curb (x 40-44, row 29) clear for the bus.\"\"\")\n\nopen(p, 'w').write(s)\nprint('review patch applied')\nPYEOF\npython3 /tmp/wireplan-scripts/patch_review.py","description":"Apply all verified reviewer fixes to PLAN.md"}},"wire_ingest_context":{"toolu_013S3T55VQqY5fWeC4F5ramC":{"cwd":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-105319/work"}}}
