{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01D2E139iDXpwDaKm9WdSGW9","type":"tool_result","content":"### 5.6 Foot chase (12-chase.js)\n- **Escape graph** (data): nodes on cells with edges typed `run`, `vault` (a fence cell: 0.5 s for the runner, 0.7 s for Dana), `cut` (vacant or breezeway) and `gate`.\n- **Start:** the knockers' car pulls up and Corey bolts from the post with a **110-unit head start** (Dana is scripted at the bus shelter, P3).\n- **Runner AI:** the escape graph is a network of loops with no exits (App. A). At each node pick the next node maximizing `dist(pursuer, node) − 0.5·alignment + rng·20`, preferring edges that break line of sight. At 15 s Lou \"takes the car\n- **Speeds and stamina:** Corey sprints 112 for 10 s, then runs 92, and recovers his sprint after 4 s out of Dana's sight. Dana sprints 125 on stamina (about 7 s from full, §5.0) and runs 85 otherwise. Sprinting from the start empties Dana \n- **Vault:** a context prompt at fence cells, when moving toward the fence and within 14 units. `✕` triggers a jump arc over the blocked `fence` floor cell. Fences are floor-tagged and blocked (App. A), so walkers stop and jumpers pass.\n- **Ditch:** when Dana gets within 90 units, or after 10 s, the runner throws the package into the nearest ditch spot within 40 units: trash can, under a parked car, storm drain (lost) or vacant window. Cues: throw animation, a soft \"plink\"\n- **Tackle:** within 14 units while sprinting, the prompt `✕ Tackle`. The paired action `E.ACTIONS.tackle` is written like the engine's `takedown` (lunge 0.25 s, both bodies fall). A miss means a stumble of 0.8 s. A hit means the runner is \n- **Search:** ditch spots within 30 units show \"Search\" (2 s each). After 45 s a kid on a bike rides in and takes the package if it's still there (no drugs charge, Heat +5). A storm drain is gone.\n- **Win:** cuffed. **Lose:** Corey stays out of Dana's sight for 8 s in a row (\"He's gone.\"). Retry from the chase start.\n\n### 5.7 Stealth search (trash, Ep4) and the long lens (Ep5B)\n....\n218:  boxTop: ['Digit1','Pad3'], boxLeft: ['Digit2','Pad2'], boxRight: ['Digit3','Pad1'], boxBottom: ['Digit4','Pad0']   // the box's diamond (§6.4)\n509:- **Each exchange,** choose an approach. The four sit on a face-button diamond drawn in the dialog area (glyph + verb + number key; hover/click). They use t\n514:- **Rapport** (0-3 pips, shown under the bars): each pip lowers the Fear a Lean adds by 3, and *Work for us* needs Rapport ≥ 1.\n882:  - `won`: when only one side has humans (one player vs bots, or every human on one side), pass `won: true` or `false` for that side. Standings alone can't \n887:  - **Round length:** `min(300 s, info.limitMs − 5 s)`, so the host always finishes before the hub's hard limit (the harness sets it with `&limit=`).\n888:  - **Hidden host tab:** the engine's animation loop stops in a hidden tab. While `document.hidden` on the host, step the sim from a `setInterval` that call\n1646:| Tee | A + weight + `teeShort` | \"Terrence Mabry: pleaded to twelve years. Easy stopped paying his mother's rent in March.\" |\n1650:| | B + stay + `teeShort` | \"Terrence Mabry: cut loose by Easy, then indicted. Testified against him.\" |\n1674:| Ren (always) | — | \"Renata Ocasio: transferred to the Tactical Section. Kept the camera.\" |","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e2aa65a8-ee1a-45c4-b8e6-f96cf188e23d","uuid":"9a016ed8-508c-4094-8bf6-ac3043dbc9fb","timestamp":"2026-11-03T19:23:37.832Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"### 5.6 Foot chase (12-chase.js)\n- **Escape graph** (data): nodes on cells with edges typed `run`, `vault` (a fence cell: 0.5 s for the runner, 0.7 s for Dana), `cut` (vacant or breezeway) and `gate`.\n- **Start:** the knockers' car pulls up and Corey bolts from the post with a **110-unit head start** (Dana is scripted at the bus shelter, P3).\n- **Runner AI:** the escape graph is a network of loops with no exits (App. A). At 