{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CggYNJkHT21KQ9hmGAhXN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"PLAN.md is finished: about 1,820 lines in `work/`. An independent reviewer read it against TASK.md, STAGE.md and the AI Hub protocol and reported 24 problems; all 24 were real and are fixed. I also fixed four more problems my own checks turned up:\n- the map grid was missing its closing `];`\n- two schema examples weren't valid JavaScript\n- the chase start distance was wrong\n- one chase node sat on a fence cell\n\nEvery code block parses, the map is exactly 72×56, and every route point and point of interest sits on a walkable cell.\n\n**Title:** WIRETAP, tagline \"Somebody's always listening.\" I brainstormed 50 riffs on The Wire and a cryptographic random number picked #7. The single file will be `Wiretap-TheWire-claude-opus-5-5-max-20261103-105319.html`.\n\n**The game:** a stealth investigation crime drama in isometric 2.5D, set in a fictional West Baltimore neighborhood in October 2004. It plays both sides of one corner.\n- **As Det. Dana Whitlock:** watch the corner without getting \"made\", photograph deals, put faces and numbers on the Board, crack the crew's pager code, write an affidavit honest enough for a judge, and work the wire room, where you must stop listening to personal calls or lose the wire.\n- **As Tee, the crew's lieutenant:** run one night shift between episodes. How well you play him makes Dana's next day harder.\n- **Pressure:** four meters drive the choices and the endings: the Major's patience, the crew's wariness, legal risk and case strength.\n\n**Content:**\n- **Story:** five short episodes plus four crew-side interludes, about 60-75 minutes. The finale splits into a raid or a \"follow the money\" path, then a 14-card epilogue montage picked from your choices.\n- **Versus:** 1-4 players, cops against the corner, where the detectives hide among civilians. It runs locally (split screen or against bots) and online through the AI Hub's shared-world mode.\n- **Attract mode:** after 10 seconds idle, a bot-played reel of nine scenes from the game.\n- **Other requirements:** controller-first TV interface with PlayStation glyphs by default and an Xbox option, toggles to invert each stick axis, a \"Controller or keyboard required\" notice on touch-only devices, and an About/Credits screen fed from the same file that produces `exit-interview.json`.\n\n**For the builders:**\n- **Architecture:** rules that let one set of systems serve bots, network play and headless tests; content kept as data.\n- **Build order:** 12 milestones, each with a \"done when\" test.\n- **Risks:** a table with how to reduce each.\n- **Testing:** lightweight, as TASK.md asks: fast headless tests, a few screenshots, a fake-gamepad check and the AI Hub harness.\n- **Appendices:** the map, routes, cipher tables, wire-call scripts, interrogation data, the judge's questions, key scenes, music scores, voice profiles and data schemas, so nothing has to be invented to get started.\n\nNothing has been built or run yet; this stage was planning only."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1044,"cache_read_input_tokens":580800,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1044,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e2aa65a8-ee1a-45c4-b8e6-f96cf188e23d","uuid":"baf72c29-2737-4c6b-8de4-58678f9fa981","timestamp":"2026-11-03T19:24:40.431Z","request_id":"req_011CggYNJKzDV65LjiGd5TEy"}
